PVD("philippines_ndp_2017-2022",{"docs":["","PDP 2017 2022"],"s":{"1":[[1,"65","1","Government Security Mechanisms Against Cybercrime and Cyberattacks","Relatedly, these online platforms demand that the government establish security mechanisms against incidences of cybercrimes and cyberattacks.",""],[1,"70","4","ICT Privacy and Data Protection Framework","Develop and implement a framework for privacy, personal data protection, and security in the use and application of ICT.",""],[1,"273","22","Secure and Resilient Philippine Cyberspace Initiative","Establish a secure and resilient Philippine Cyberspace",""],[1,"276","3","National Cybersecurity Plan Implementation","The Department of Information and Communications Technology will ensure the successful implementation of the National Cybersecurity Plan (NCSP) 2022","Department of Information and Communications Technology"],[1,"276","3","Cybersecurity Resilience Enhancement Measures","The strategic initiatives of the NCSP will include enhancing security resilience of critical information infrastructure, and government, public, and military networks to deal with sophisticated attacks",""],[1,"276","3","Cybersecurity Adoption and Skills Expansion Programme","promoting the adoption of cybersecurity measures among individuals and businesses, and enhancing and expanding the pool of local cybersecurity experts",""],[1,"276","4","Strategic Defensive Cybersecurity Posture","a strategic defensive posture within the Office of the President will be established.",""],[1,"276","4","National Critical Information Infrastructure Protection and Cyber Resilience Program","This will be complemented by the strengthening of the country's capability to protect the National Critical Information Infrastructures and improve its cyber resiliency through cybersecurity assessment and compliance and national drill exercises.",""],[1,"276","4","National Cybersecurity Capacity and Awareness Initiative","The government will build the skills and capabilities of local cybersecurity experts; strengthen cooperation between law enforcement, cybersecurity experts, academe, and the private sector; and improve cybersecurity awareness through the conduct of National Cybersecurity Awareness Month, engagements with non-government organizations and other stakeholders, and employing social media as means for disseminating information.",""],[1,"277","4","Cybercrime Detection and Investigation Modernization","Law enforcement capability on cybercrime detection and investigation will be improved and modernized.",""],[1,"277","4","Public Cybercrime Awareness Campaign","This also calls for efforts to increase the general public's awareness on the detection of cybercrimes to protect themselves and avoid being a victim, especially at the height of a pandemic and other crisis situations.",""]],"2":[[1,"169","2","Integrated and Interoperable Health Information System","Institute a fully integrated and interoperable health information system and database.",""],[1,"220","4","Reliable Digital Infrastructure and Cybersecurity Support","All these need to be supported by a reliable digital infrastructure system with strong cybersecurity protection.",""],[1,"220","4","Production Sector Automation and Digitalization","In the production sector, there will be increased demand for automation and digitalization to supplement manual labor in the immediate term.",""],[1,"231","1","Deployment of Trained CIOs in Government Agencies","processes will also be advanced through the deployment of trained CIOs in government agencies, assigned to lead in the development of internal digital transformation strategies and business continuity plans.",""],[1,"232","2","Digital Transactions Infrastructure and Regulation Strengthening","Strengthen infrastructure for and regulation of digital transactions.",""],[1,"232","2","National Broadband Program Acceleration","The implementation of DICT's National Broadband Program will be fast-tracked to provide the national ICT backbone to support government services delivery, including the use of digital transactions and the linking of digital transformation and research laboratories as part of the STI ecosystem.","DICT"],[1,"235","13","National eHealth System Development and Regulation","This aims to establish, institutionalize, and regulate a coherent, coordinated, and collaborative National eHealth System, guided by a national policy and strategic framework.",""],[1,"235","14","Whole-of-Government Digital Innovation and Transformation Approach","This aims to adopt a whole-of-government approach in promoting digital innovation and transformation in business and government.",""]],"3":[[1,"8","22","National Digital ID System","The PhilSys Act establishes a national digital ID system that will provide every Filipino with proof of identity.",""],[1,"66","8","Expanded Access to Government Services through PhilSys","increase the people's access to these services through reconfigured government systems pursuant to the PhilSys Act",""],[1,"72","1","PhilSys Acceleration and Registration Expansion","Accelerate the implementation of the PhilSys.",""],[1,"72","1","PhilSys Use-Case Expansion for Public Services and Digital Economy","Use cases for the issued identification (ID) called the PhilSys ID, will be identified, particularly in facilitating more efficient provision of key services (e.g., pension, conditional cash transfer, farmer assistance, health coverage, among others).",""],[1,"191","36","PhilSys Fast-Track Implementation and Listahanan Synchronization","Fast-track implementation of the PhilSys, and synchronize the Listahan with the PhilSys",""],[1,"191","39","Registry of Vulnerable Groups","Create a registry of vulnerable groups and address data constraints",""],[1,"191","41","Digitalization of Social Protection Delivery","Digitalize the delivery of SP assistance and services",""],[1,"198","2","Integration of Safeguards into Development Interventions","Integrate safeguards into development interventions and establish funding mechanisms for these safety nets.","NEDA"],[1,"198","2","Funding Mechanisms for Safety Nets","The NEDA, DOF, and the Department of Budget and Management will identify funding mechanisms that may be tapped by national agencies and local government units to assist the adversely affected population groups.","NEDA | DOF | Department of Budget and Management"],[1,"198","3","Protective Services for Persons of Concern","Engagements and partnerships of concerned agencies such as the Department of Justice and DSWD will continue to provide POCs with access to protective services.","Department of Justice | DSWD"],[1,"198","3","POC Database Management System","A database management system for the POCs will be developed to efficiently assess and monitor their concerns.",""],[1,"198","4","Social Protection Code Development","The NEDA-SCSP will develop a Social Protection Code to aid stakeholders, especially LGUs, in developing responsive and effective social protection programs and projects.",""],[1,"198","5","Social Protection Floor Institutionalization","Institutionalize a Social Protection Floor.",""],[1,"198","6","Household Resilience and Financial Literacy Campaign","Information and education campaign to encourage households to prepare for emergencies will be strengthened, through the financial literacy and advocacy program of the Bangko Sentral ng Pilipinas, among others.",""],[1,"198","6","Household Savings Mobilization and Bank Account Access","An important element in this strategy is encouraging households to have a bank account so that they can save and improve their resilience in coping with shocks.",""],[1,"199","1","PhilSys National ID Fast-Track Implementation","Fast-track the implementation of the PhilSys and synchronize the Listahanan with the PhilSys.","Philippine Statistics Authority | DSWD"],[1,"199","1","PhilSys Digital Payment Linkage for Social Assistance","Concerned agencies such as the PSA and the DSWD will explore linking the PhilSys ID cards to a digital payment system that will allow for more efficient transfer of government assistance in times of crisis, pandemics, or disasters.","Philippine Statistics Authority | DSWD"],[1,"199","1","PhilSys-Enabled Bank Account Opening for Cash Transfers","Part of the plan for the registration process for the PhilSys national ID, is to allow registrants to open a bank account with Land Bank of the Philippines through which cash transfers can be made.","Land Bank of the Philippines"],[1,"199","2","Listahanan-PhilSys Database Synchronization","The Listahanan database needs to be synchronized with the PhilSys to include information found in PhilSys such as biometrics, use of PhilSys Number (PSN), tokenized PSN, among others.",""],[1,"199","3","Registry of Vulnerable Groups Development Initiative","the DSWD, in cooperation with the concerned councils and/or commissions, will develop a registry of vulnerable groups, especially for the street children, older persons, persons with disabilities, workers in the informal and gig economy, and those affected by development interventions.","DSWD"],[1,"199","4","Digitalization of Social Protection Delivery","Digitalize the delivery of social protection assistance and services.","DSWD | DOLE | SSS | DICT"],[1,"199","5","Social Protection Monitoring and Evaluation System","social protection programs will be regularly assessed and monitored by the SDC-SCSP to ensure that program and project objectives are met.",""],[1,"200","1","Legislative Action for Universal Social Protection","the following legislative action will be pursued to achieve universal and transformative social protection program for all Filipinos.",""]],"4":[[1,"15","25","Digital Transformation Program","this updated PDP contains five major programs designed to build the resilience of individuals, families, business, government, and society under the new normal: (4) digital transformation",""],[1,"16","5","Digital Government Transactions Platform","More and more government transactions will be enabled using the digital platform",""],[1,"16","5","Business Digitalization Support Programs","there will be technical and financial assistance programs to help businesses, especially the MSMEs, to transition towards greater digitalization",""],[1,"16","6","Digital Transaction Security and Consumer Protection Framework Review","government will ensure safety and security of digital transactions, including digital payments.",""],[1,"59","2","Digital Economy Support Reforms","The government will prioritize reforms to support the digital economy as these are essential elements for the new normal.",""],[1,"61","2","Inclusive Digital Finance and Consumer Protection Reform","It seeks to foster a resilient and inclusive financial system amid the COVID-19 pandemic through targeted supervisory actions and reforms particularly in developing a more inclusive digital finance ecosystem, encouraging innovation in microfinance and microinsurance, and expanding consumer protection.",""],[1,"133","21","E-Commerce Industry Development","Develop the Philippines' e-commerce industry",""],[1,"138","2","E-commerce Development Support Measures","Hasten growth of e-commerce by focusing on building up digital speed, security, and structure to expand the market and increase sales.",""],[1,"138","2","E-commerce Policy, Awareness, Payment, and Infrastructure Package","Establish necessary policies, advocacy, awareness campaigns, payment systems, and infrastructure to support its growth.",""],[1,"138","3","Update the Philippine E-Commerce Roadmap to Include Digital Trade Strategies","Incorporate digital trade in the updating of the Philippine E-Commerce Roadmap 2016-2020.",""],[1,"138","5","E-commerce Industry Data Portal","Generate official industry data to monitor and measure the contribution of e-commerce and digital trade to the economy.",""],[1,"145","11","Digital Platform Adoption for Technology Access","Increase access to appropriate technology including adoption of digital platforms",""],[1,"149","4","Enterprise Digital Platform Adoption Support","the government, through the RIICs, will assist enterprises in adopting applicable digital platforms",""]],"5":[[1,"252","15","Local Government Income Classification Reform","Institute the income classification of provinces, cities, and municipalities, to make it reflective of LGUs' financial capability, particularly their ability to generate locally-sourced revenues.",""],[1,"252","16","LGU Property Insurance Bill","Key legislative measures that will improve local government finance such LGU Property Insurance Bill (see Chapter 19) and Amendment to the Local Government Code of 1991 (see Chapter 5).",""],[1,"252","16","Amendment to the Local Government Code of 1991","Key legislative measures that will improve local government finance such LGU Property Insurance Bill (see Chapter 19) and Amendment to the Local Government Code of 1991 (see Chapter 5).",""]],"6":[[1,"64","2","Citizen Feedback and Responsive Governance Reform","reforms will focus on: (a) proactively seeking citizens' perspectives to ensure the responsiveness of government interventions;",""],[1,"67","7","Transparent Strategic Risk Communication","Ensure public access to transparent, strategic risk communication",""],[1,"68","2","Civil Society Representation in Local Development Councils","adequate and genuine representation of civil society in local development councils and other advisory bodies will be ensured.",""],[1,"68","2","Localized Response and Feedback Mechanisms","Response and feedback mechanisms will also be localized and expanded.",""],[1,"68","3","Inclusive Development Planning and Stakeholder Participation","Government programs, projects, and public policies will be made more inclusive and responsive to the needs of the different sectors.",""],[1,"68","3","Participation of Overseas Filipinos, MSMEs, and Vulnerable Groups in Development Planning","The government will ensure that overseas Filipinos; micro, small, and medium enterprises; and the vulnerable and marginalized sectors, such as indigenous groups and disabled individuals, are involved in development planning.",""],[1,"68","3","Human Rights-Based Development Planning Training for Frontline Agencies","Frontline agencies will be trained on mainstreaming human rights based approach to development planning to enable them to assist and provide the public with better government services.",""],[1,"68","4","Citizen Engagement for Responsive Government Interventions","Agencies will proactively solicit comments and suggestions from citizens using a three-pronged approach: (a) providing adequate venues for engagement; (b) communicating in clear language; and (c) collaborating with other sectors.",""],[1,"68","4","Outside-In Public Service Design Approach","The \"outside-in\" approach5 will be adopted by actively listening to the people and understanding their needs and expectations.",""],[1,"68","4","Citizen Participation Platforms for Public Resource Management","Several platforms will be provided to enable ordinary citizens to take an active role in information sharing, public resource management, policy and regulation review, and other related processes.",""],[1,"68","4","Whole-of-Society National and Local Planning","A whole- of-society approach in national and local planning will be instilled.",""],[1,"68","5","Citizen Empowerment Participation Platforms","The government will develop programs for people to participate in the promotion of citizen empowerment in their respective locality.",""],[1,"68","5","Citizen and CSO Participation Platforms for Local Governance","Platforms will be provided to enable citizens and CSOs to participate in local government processes such as development planning, budgeting, implementation, and M&E.",""],[1,"68","5","Digital Participation Tools for Local Governance","Development of mobile apps, utilization of media platforms, and application of geotagging technologies will also be implemented to facilitate broader participation such as Development Live or DevLive.",""],[1,"68","5","Citizen Participatory Audit Institutionalization and Capacity Building","With the institutionalization of the Citizen Participatory Audit (CPA), citizens and LGUs will be capacitated on the auditing process and the importance of CPA in minimizing corruption and enhancing public accountability.",""],[1,"68","7","DevLive Citizen Reporting Mobile Application","DevLive is a mobile application where citizens can report status of projects in their communities that allows greater transparency, accountability, and efficiency in the implementation of government infrastructure projects.","DILG | United Nations Development Programme"],[1,"69","2","Volunteerism Promotion and Strengthening Initiative","The government will reinforce and strengthen the practice of volunteerism in the delivery of social services, provision of technical assistance, response to disaster, and undertaking humanitarian efforts, especially in remote and unserved areas.",""],[1,"69","2","Volunteerism Criterion for the Seal of Good Local Governance","Encouraging volunteerism will also be explored as a criterion in the Seal of Good Local Governance (SGLG).",""],[1,"69","3","Civil Society Organization Accreditation and Local Special Bodies Strengthening","Further advocacy will be conducted to encourage more CSOs to apply for accreditation, as outlined in the Department of the Interior and Local Government's (DILG) Memorandum Circular No. 2019-72.","Department of the Interior and Local Government"],[1,"69","3","Harmonization of CSO Accreditation Guidelines","Existing guidelines of other agencies on CSO accreditation will also be harmonized.",""],[1,"69","3","Upgrade of CSO Member Selection and Representation Criteria","The selection process and criteria for CSO members will be upgraded to ensure unbiased and fair representation in local special bodies.",""],[1,"69","3","Capacity Building and Evaluation of Local Special Bodies","Further, DILG will capacitate and evaluate the functionality of these bodies to ascertain the legitimacy of representatives and sectoral concerns in the planning process.","Department of the Interior and Local Government"],[1,"69","4","Open and Participatory Governance Reform Scale-Up","The government will continue to implement and upscale efforts in fulfilling the commitments to the Open Government Partnership Action Plans and Participatory Governance Cluster Performance and Projects Roadmap (2017-2022).",""],[1,"69","4","Regular Online Peer Learning for Governance Best Practices","Best practices from the Partnership will be shared with other government agencies through the conduct of regular, online peer learning sessions.",""],[1,"69","4","Unified Citizen Engagement Policy","The national government will also develop and issue a unified policy on citizen engagement in governance to consolidate fragmented guidelines, institutionalize best practices, and ensure sustainability of existing open and participatory governance reforms.",""],[1,"69","4","Transparency Seal Compliance Maintenance","national agencies will sustain compliance with the Transparency Seal.",""],[1,"69","5","Freedom of Information Bill Passage","The government will continue to pursue the passage of the Freedom of Information Bill to enable the public to have access to government data through online means, among others, free of charge and in an open format.",""],[1,"69","6","Citizen Engagement Technology Mainstreaming","Mainstream the use of technology in informing, consulting, involving, collaborating, and empowering citizens.",""],[1,"70","2","Citizen Feedback and Public Consultation Platforms","the government will utilize other platforms to reach a wider audience and engage citizens to generate more feedback on the quality of government services.",""],[1,"70","2","Crowdsourcing-Based Public Consultation","Crowdsourcing will also be explored as another form of public consultation, while collaboration with non-government sectors will be facilitated.",""],[1,"70","2","Complaint Feedback Loop Improvement Mechanism","Mechanisms will also be improved and simplified to ensure that the feedback loop is closed - citizens who submit complaints must be given real-time updates on their issues to show that their concerns matter.",""],[1,"71","1","Co-created Service Delivery Programmes","Better service delivery strategies and new programs will be co-created among related agencies, relevant stakeholders, and citizens.",""],[1,"76","6","Citizen Empowerment and Public Accountability Capacity-Building Program","Citizen empowerment efforts and capacity-building activities for non-government organizations and other volunteers on monitoring and public accountability will also be strengthened and expanded through open and participatory governance programs.",""],[1,"76","6","Bantay Korapsyon Anti-Corruption Program","The DILG's Bantay Korapsyon Program will mobilize citizens and utilize various anti-corruption mechanisms at the local level to ensure that erring local officials will be held accountable for committing corrupt practices and for failure to perform their mandated functions.","DILG"],[1,"77","5","Government Data Transparency and E-Participation Initiative","This will address transparency issues on government data, thereby promoting meaningful and increased participation of the people in government decision- making and public accountability.",""]],"7":[[1,"264","5","Support for the Bangsamoro Transition Authority","Support the Bangsamoro Transition Authority (BTA) as the interim government of the Bangsamoro Autonomous Region in Muslim Mindanao (BARMM)",""],[1,"264","17","Support for the Bangsamoro Transition Authority","Support the Bangsamoro Transition Authority (BTA) as the interim government of the Bangsamoro Autonomous Region in Muslim Mindanao (BARMM).",""],[1,"264","17","Priority Legislation Enactment for BARMM Transition","Foremost are the enactment of priority legislations, the determination of parliamentary districts for the first regular elections of the Parliament members, the organization of its own civilian bureaucracy, and the full transfer of powers and properties of the dissolved ARMM regional government to the BARMM.",""],[1,"264","17","Bangsamoro Government Intergovernmental Relations Mechanism","A critical component in the implementation of the peace agreement is the immediate organization of all mechanisms under the National Government-Bangsamoro Government Intergovernmental Relations Body (IGRB),",""],[1,"265","1","Intergovernmental Relations Mechanisms","Aside from the Intergovernmental Fiscal Policy Board and the Intergovernmental Energy Board, other intergovernmental relations mechanisms that will be organized are: (a) Philippine Congress-Bangsamoro Parliament Forum; (b) Joint Body for the Zones of Joint Cooperation (Sulu Sea and Moro Gulf); (c) Intergovernmental Infrastructure Development Board; (d) Bangsamoro Sustainable Development Board, and the (e) Council of Leaders.",""]],"8":[[1,"68","2","Electoral Reform Intensification","Electoral reforms will be intensified while observing risk mitigation protocols for the citizenry.",""],[1,"70","5","Political and Electoral Reform Package","the government will push for political and electoral reforms to integrate new election protocols such as, but not limited to, automation and online system of voter registration, digitization of voters' list, enhancement of voting measures for senior citizens and persons with disabilities, and establishment of additional polling places for indigenous groups","Commission on Elections (COMELEC)"],[1,"70","5","Party-List, Anti-Dynasty, and Campaign Finance Regulation","Rules and regulations on party-list development, anti-political dynasty, and campaign financing will also be pursued.",""],[1,"70","6","Election Pandemic Risk Mitigation Measures","appropriate risk mitigation measures against COVID-19, or any other pandemic, will be developed for the 2022 elections.",""],[1,"70","6","Voter Education and Safety Protocol Information Campaign","Voter education activities will be intensified to include information on safety protocols during elections.",""],[1,"70","6","Partnership with Universities for Voter Education Modules","there will be partnership with state universities and colleges (SUCs) and open universities for the development of education modules and dissemination of information.",""],[1,"70","6","Online Voter Information Platform","Online platforms will also be utilized to inform voters.",""],[1,"77","5","Online Election Registration and Voting System","This will allow for online registration and online voting, and facilitate risk mitigation procedures for the 2022 National and Local Elections.",""]],"9":[[1,"8","23","Ease of Doing Business and Regulatory Streamlining Reform","The Ease of Doing Business and Efficient Government Service Delivery Act, meanwhile, directs all agencies in government to streamline government processes, particularly those concerning business (B2G) and consumers (C2G), and rationalize or even harmonize regulations.",""],[1,"64","2","Ease of Doing Business and Efficient Government Service Delivery Act Implementation","expediting the implementation of the Ease of Doing Business and Efficient Government Service Delivery (EODB EGSD) Act of 2018 (Republic Act No. 11032) and the Philippine Identification System (PhilSys) Act (RA 11055);",""],[1,"71","4","Ease of Doing Business and Efficient Government Service Delivery Act Implementation","Expedite implementation of the EODB and EGSD Act.",""],[1,"72","4","Regulatory Impact Assessment Institutionalization","The EODB and EGSD Act institutionalizes the regulatory impact assessment (RIA) in the bureaucracy, which mandates the thorough review of regulations prior to their issuance.",""],[1,"72","4","Regulatory Burden Reduction and Process Simplification Reforms","Other reforms will also be intensified to reduce unnecessary regulatory burden while simplifying processes:",""],[1,"72","5","Expansion of Program NEHEMIA","Expand the National Effort on the Harmonization of Efficient Measures of Interrelated Agencies (Program NEHEMIA) for the pursuit of a whole-of-government approach to service delivery.",""],[1,"73","1","Administrative Burden Reduction and Government Process Rationalization","To support remote government operations, oversight agencies such as the Department of Budget and Management (DBM), the Government Procurement Policy Board, the COA, and the Civil Service Commission (CSC), among others, will review and rationalize their rules, regulations, and requirements to allow for electronic transactions, alternative work arrangements, and procurement of off-the-shelf software9 in the public sector.","Department of Budget and Management | Government Procurement Policy Board | COA | Civil Service Commission"],[1,"73","2","Review and Amendment of Government Procurement and Audit Regulations","Pre-existing issues with the IRR of the Government Procurement Reform Act (RA 9184) (e.g., tedious process) and COA rules (e.g., uniform application) will be addressed through the review and amendment of these regulations, as necessary, while making these responsive to the new normal.",""],[1,"73","3","Agency and Sector Policy Review for Efficiency","There will also be a review of agency-specific and sector-wide policies to improve internal and sectoral efficiency.",""],[1,"73","4","Regulatory Impact Assessment Framework Development and Training Programme","Priority will be given to the development of a national and sectoral framework for RIA, including the drafting of proportionality analysis guidelines.",""],[1,"73","4","RIA Capacity-Building for Regulatory and Local Authorities","Regulatory agencies, the legislative branch, LGUs, and decision-makers will be trained to undertake RIA.",""],[1,"73","4","RIA Compliance Cost and Public Consultation Training","Courses on compliance cost assessment and public consultation will also be conducted to support an effective RIA implementation.",""],[1,"73","4","Online RIA Training and Assessment Platform","Online training and assessment platforms will be developed in this regard.",""],[1,"73","6","Return to Regular Procurement Rules","Regular procurement rules will apply after the Bayanihan Act lapses in effectivity.",""],[1,"126","3","Regulatory Permitting and Licensing Streamlining","Address regulatory bottlenecks by streamlining permitting and licensing processes across industries.",""],[1,"134","5","Business Environment Streamlining and Regulatory Simplification Measures","Further improve the business environment with the full implementation of the Ease of Doing Business and Efficient Government Service Delivery Act of 2018 and the Philippine Business Registry and the Business Permit Licensing System to minimize, if not eliminate, redundancies and overlaps in requirements and reduce transactions costs.",""],[1,"134","5","Business One Stop Shop and Central Business Portal","In addition, the implementation of the Business One Stop Shop (BOSS) and the creation of the Central Business Portal to streamline procedures will be prioritized.",""],[1,"134","5","Project Repeal Regulatory Review","Continuation of \"Project Repeal\" will also be pushed to further eliminate irrelevant laws and regulations.",""],[1,"134","8","Regulatory Impact Assessment of Existing Regulations","Undertake a comprehensive regulatory impact assessment of existing regulations to ensure that these do not impose unnecessary burden on businesses.",""],[1,"141","2","Easy-Access Business Verification System","Establish an easy-access business verifier containing an online database of duly registered businesses with valid licenses to operate.",""],[1,"146","4","Regulatory Streamlining for Firms","Streamline the regulatory environment to reduce compliance costs for all firms.",""],[1,"146","6","Startup-Friendly Business Climate Reform","The government will enhance business incubation support and accelerate services for startups, lessen administrative burdens and complexity of regulatory procedures for startups, and reduce, if not eliminate, the regulatory protection of incumbents (see Chapter 16).",""],[1,"146","6","Streamlining of Business Registration and Permit Processes","Further, national and local governments will speed up streamlining of agency processes and requirements for business registrations and permit issuances47 and will be streamlined through digital platforms (see also Chapters 5 and 9A).",""],[1,"146","6","One-Stop-Shop for Startups and Startup Green Lane","A One-Stop-Shop for Startups and a Startup Green Lane with ARTA will be created.",""],[1,"147","3","Streamlined LGU Business Registration and Permit Processing for BMBEs","Streamline LGU processes and requirements for registration and securing business permits of barangay micro business enterprises (BMBEs) targeting informal sector operators.","Department of the Interior and Local Government | Anti-Red Tape Authority"],[1,"147","6","Business Permit Fee Streamlining and Registration Leniency","streamlining can be done by setting more reasonable standard business permit fees for micro and small enterprises and granting leniency, particularly to informal sector operators who will register for the first time.",""],[1,"256","15","Business Registration and Permitting Streamlining","Streamline business registration and permitting processes",""],[1,"256","17","Philippine Business Data Bank Establishment","Establish the Philippine Business Data Bank (PDB)",""],[1,"260","2","Business Registration and Permitting Streamlining","Streamline business registration and permitting processes.","ARTA | Department of Information and Communications Technology"],[1,"260","3","Regulatory Management Strengthening","ARTA will be strengthened in terms of regulatory management practices to include reducing unnecessary regulatory burdens and requirements.",""],[1,"260","3","Program NEHEMIA Interagency Process Streamlining","To achieve this, ARTA will continue coordinating with relevant government agencies for the implementation of Program NEHEMIA (National Effort for the Harmonization of Efficient Measures of Inter-related Agencies), which commenced in the first quarter of 2020.",""],[1,"260","4","Philippine Business Databank Establishment","Establish the Philippine Business Databank (PBD).",""]],"10":[[1,"80","2","Judicial Human Resources and Court Expansion","further increasing human resources and courts to enhance access to justice",""],[1,"80","2","Penal Facility Decongestion and Justice Process Acceleration","addressing congestion in penal facilities through infrastructure development and expedient criminal justice processes.",""],[1,"80","12","Jail Decongestion and Correction Reform","· Pursue jail decongestion and correction reforms",""],[1,"83","1","Jail Decongestion and Corrections Reform","Pursue jail decongestion and corrections reform.",""],[1,"83","2","Penal Facility Health and Safety Protocols","the government will put in place necessary health and safety protocols to ensure humane living conditions of PDL.",""],[1,"83","3","Correctional Facility Modernization and Prison Management Reform","Security facilities will be modernized to prevent escapes, violence, and illegal activities.",""],[1,"83","4","Legal Assistance and Paralegal Support for Persons Deprived of Liberty","Access to legal assistance for pre-sentence and sentenced PDL will be provided and facilitated.",""],[1,"83","4","BJMP Paralegal Program Improvement and Expansion","The Bureau of Jail Management and Penology (BJMP) will continuously improve and update its paralegal program for PDL in local jails, which the Bureau of Corrections (BUCOR) can adopt for national penitentiaries.","Bureau of Jail Management and Penology (BJMP) | Bureau of Corrections (BUCOR)"],[1,"83","4","Expansion of e-Dalaw Family Contact Facility","The e- Dalaw facility will be sustained and introduced in more jails and prisons to enable off-site interface of PDL and their families, subject to appropriate security protocols and available resources.",""],[1,"83","5","Task Force Katarungan at Kalayaan Expansion","The Judiciary will sustain and expand its lead role in the Task Force Katarungan at Kalayaan as an inter- agency forum to address jail congestion and facilitate timely resolution of cases involving pre-sentence detainees.",""],[1,"83","5","Innovative Trial Facilitation Measures for PDL","Innovative approaches on facilitating the conduct of trial for PDL will also be explored and pursued including transfer of venue in authorized cases for valid grounds and on-site trial.",""],[1,"83","6","Operationalization of the Interim National Preventive Mechanism Against Torture","The CHR will likewise continue its efforts in operationalizing the Interim National Preventive Mechanism (NPM) against torture pursuant to the State obligation under the United Nations (UN) Optional Protocol to the Convention against Torture and Other Cruel, Inhuman, or Degrading Treatment or Punishment.",""],[1,"83","7","Legal Assistance and Case Monitoring for Qualified PDL","In partnership with other organizations, the CHR will provide legal assistance to PDL and conduct regular case monitoring to facilitate early and timely release of qualified PDL.",""],[1,"84","1","Penal System and Restorative Justice Framework Reform","The DOJ and DILG will also coordinate with Congress to revisit and improve the country's legal and policy framework relating to the penal system and restorative justice, taking into consideration the state obligations on the rights of PDL, offenders, and victims; public safety, and national security.","DOJ | DILG | Congress"],[1,"84","2","Strict Implementation of the Revised IRR of the GCTA Law","With the revised IRR of RA 10592, also referred to as the Good Conduct Time Allowance (GCTA) Law, strict implementation will be ensured particularly on the exclusion of heinous crime offenders and inclusion of transparency and accountability mechanisms.",""],[1,"84","2","Expansion of Non-Custodial Measures","Non-custodial measures will be maximized, including release on recognizance and community service for arrested and charged persons, and probation, parole, and executive clemency for convicted persons.",""],[1,"84","2","Review and Improvement of Probation, Parole, and Executive Clemency Rules","Rules and guidelines relative to probation, parole, and executive clemency will be reviewed and improved in the interest of restorative justice for the offender and the victim.",""],[1,"86","8","GCTA Eligibility Clarification and Safeguards Reform","Clarify the applicability to heinous crime offenders; include transparency procedures; establish the checks and balances, including the role of higher and court authorities (i.e., apart from jail and prison authorities); and provide for corrective measures in cases of erroneous grant of GCTA and release on account thereof.",""],[1,"86","15","Unified Penology and Corrections System","Establishment of a Unified Penology and Corrections System",""],[1,"86","16","Penology and Corrections Institutional Framework Reform","Address the fragmentation on the institutional framework of the penology and corrections system.",""]],"11":[[1,"21","3","WHO Solidarity Vaccine Trials Participation","The Philippines is participating in the WHO Solidarity Vaccine Trials, with 12 hospitals around the country designated as trial sites.",""],[1,"21","3","Review of Vaccine Clinical Trial Results","Aside from these, the country is also studying results of clinical trials of vaccines from six companies from China, Russia, Australia, and Taiwan.",""],[1,"21","3","Phase 3 Vaccine Clinical Trials","Phase 3 vaccine clinical trials are set to begin in November 2020.",""],[1,"131","2","Integration of Health and Sanitary Protocols in Daily Activities","the government now has to establish the integration of necessary health and sanitary protocols in daily activities to ensure that the public remains safe in light of the current pandemic.",""],[1,"132","3","Immigration Control and Health Screening Measures","For those allowed to travel, immigration controls will be stricter and health checks will be carried out frequently.",""],[1,"132","3","Sanitation and Disinfection Services for Public Facilities and Transport","There is a heightened need for regular sanitation or disinfection of accommodation, public establishments, and transport services, as well as a stable provision of sanitation or disinfecting devices in these areas.",""],[1,"156","5","COVID-19 Containment and Vaccination Preparedness","the sector will be able to effectively implement its programs and provide quality services both at the national and local levels, in pursuit of improving nutrition and health care outcomes, while maintaining efforts to contain and prevent the spread of COVID-19 including preparations for massive vaccination.",""],[1,"165","1","Emerging Infectious Disease Control Programs","DOH will also develop or strengthen programs to address emerging and re-emerging infectious diseases such as dengue.","DOH"],[1,"165","1","National Immunization Program Expansion","Moreover, government will aggressively implement the National Immunization Program, including measures to encourage demand and secure the supply of vaccines and other implements.",""],[1,"165","1","COVID-19 Vaccine Procurement and Distribution Plan","the government will also guarantee effective delivery of the COVID-19 vaccine once available through the development and implementation of a vaccine procurement and distribution plan, which includes crafting of appropriate vaccine allocation framework, readying logistics channels and cold chain facilities, ensuring communication strategies, and setting-up monitoring mechanisms.",""],[1,"191","21","Equitable COVID-19 Vaccine Access","Ensure equitable access to the COVID-19 vaccine once available",""],[1,"195","6","COVID-19 Vaccine Acquisition Strategy","The sTWG will likewise explore multiple avenues (i.e. WHO Solidarity trials; COVAX facility, bilateral or multilateral agreements) to acquire the vaccines.",""],[1,"195","6","National COVID-19 Vaccine Procurement and Distribution Plan","In anticipation, a procurement and distribution plan will be developed to prepare budgetary and logistical requirements, among others, and ensure equitable access nationwide.",""]],"12":[[1,"167","3","Public Health Facility Construction and Upgrade Programme","more public health facilities will be constructed and upgraded, especially primary health care facilities",""],[1,"167","3","Hospital Equipment and Capacity Upgrade Programme","Hospitals will be equipped with multi-specialty training capabilities, reference laboratories, and advanced medical equipment.",""],[1,"167","3","Isolation and Critical Care Expansion","There will also be an increased number of fully equipped isolation rooms and critical care beds in hospitals.",""],[1,"167","3","Quarantine Facility Improvement at Ports and Airports","quarantine facilities in major ports and airports need to be improved to enable the Bureau of Quarantine (BOQ) to better perform its mandate on ensuring health surveillance and security.",""],[1,"167","3","Health Facility Procurement and Supply Chain Reform","Budget for construction and rehabilitation of public health facilities will be effectively utilized through improved procurement processes and supply chain management.",""],[1,"182","13","Health Facility Capacity Rationalization Legislation","This aims to rationalize the distribution of capacity and capability of health facilities.",""],[1,"183","2","Health Facility Licensing and Regulatory Reform","This proposed measure aims to make licensing standards responsive to the needs of the health systems.","DOH"],[1,"292","3","Healthcare Facility and System Upgrading","Additional investments will be pursued in affording new priorities for social infrastructure services under the new normal, particularly given the heightened importance of advancing our healthcare systems and the capacities of our healthcare facilities;",""],[1,"309","3","Health Facilities Enhancement Program","DOH will conduct a comprehensive needs assessment of critical health facilities involved in service delivery networks, especially with respect to those that are vital in dealing with COVID-19.","DOH"],[1,"309","4","Integrated Health Data Management System","there is a need to establish an integrated health data management system that tracks and links patient referrals and laboratory testing and monitors the supply of available equipment, medicines, and blood, among others.",""],[1,"309","4","Regional Level 2 Biosafety Laboratory Construction","Further, there may be a need to construct and establish an operational Level 2 Biosafety laboratory with adequate number of test kits in every region.",""]],"13":[[1,"9","1","Sagip Saka Assistance for Farmers and Fisherfolk","Farmers and fisherfolk are expected to benefit from the Sagip Saka Act which provides various forms of assistance to improve (a) production and productivity; (b) access to financing and better technologies; and (c) business support and development services.",""],[1,"9","1","Agricultural Free Patent Reform","Access to finance is further increased with the Agricultural Free Patent Reform Act which makes agricultural free patents tradable and bankable instruments.",""],[1,"9","2","Rice Tariffication Reform","A major reform in the agriculture sector is the Rice Tariffication Law.",""],[1,"14","3","Agricultural Credit, Inputs, and Training Support","Assistance will also be given to the agriculture sector in the form of credit, farm inputs, and training; and skills training, particularly on digital skills, to the displaced workers.",""],[1,"15","25","Food Security and Resiliency Program","this updated PDP contains five major programs designed to build the resilience of individuals, families, business, government, and society under the new normal: (2) food security and resiliency",""],[1,"16","2","Food Value Chain Policy and Program Framework","Over the next two years, policies and programs will be guided by a food value chain approach - from farm to plate.",""],[1,"16","2","Agricultural Productivity Improvement Programs","In addition to programs to improve agricultural productivity, there will be investments in storage facilities, postharvest, cold chain, and even technologies that prolong the shelf-life of food.",""],[1,"16","2","Food Storage, Postharvest, and Cold Chain Investments","there will be investments in storage facilities, postharvest, cold chain, and even technologies that prolong the shelf-life of food.",""],[1,"59","1","Agriculture, Forestry, and Fisheries Support Services Expansion","The first half of the Plan implementation was focused on improving the delivery of support services prioritizing small farmers and fisher folks on financing, insurance, technologies, and intensified market matching, complemented with major policy reforms that created opportunities to pursue diversification and overall rural development.",""]],"14":[[1,"99","13","Holistic Value Chain Approach for AFF Sector","In the remaining Plan implementation period, the AFF sector will adopt a holistic value chain approach, guided by science-based decision support tools, towards ensuring sustainable and resilient production and food availability, expanding access to markets by SFFs, and improving access of consumers to nutritious, affordable, and safe food.",""],[1,"100","11","Efficient Transport and Logistics Systems for Agricultural and Food Market Access","Provide efficient transport and logistics systems to link production areas to markets and ensure unhampered movement of A&F goods and services",""],[1,"100","19","AFF Sector Linkage Strengthening Scheme","Strengthen AFF sector linkage to industry sector through innovative production, processing, value adding, and marketing schemes",""],[1,"106","1","Agricultural Transport and Logistics Infrastructure Development","Provide efficient transport and logistics systems to link production areas to markets and ensure unhampered movement of A&F goods and services.",""],[1,"106","2","Community Fish Landing Centers Expansion","more Community Fish Landing Centers (CFLCs) will be established in strategic areas that will serve as landing and fish trading hubs.",""],[1,"106","3","International Trade Process Streamlining for Agricultural and Food Goods and Services","international trade processes for A&F goods and services will be streamlined and enhanced to ensure non-disruption of flow of goods and services",""],[1,"107","1","Small Farmer and Fisherfolk Organization and Consolidation Programme","Organize small farmers and fisherfolk into formal groups, and promote farm and fishery consolidation and clustering arrangements to bring about economies of scale.",""],[1,"107","1","Small Farmer and Fisherfolk Support Services Access Expansion","By organizing SFFs into formal groups, SFFs will increase access to support services (e.g., formal credit, modern farm technologies and machinery, capacity building, livelihood projects, etc.), and enable them to meet the demand of larger agribusiness enterprises and institutional buyers.",""],[1,"107","2","Link Small Farmers and Fisherfolk to Government Nutrition and Relief Procurement","Link small farmers and fisherfolk groups to government nutrition programs (e.g., supplemental feeding programs, etc.), hospitals, and other facilities, as suppliers.",""],[1,"107","4","Agribusiness Linkage and Market Access Programme","Strengthen AFF sector linkage to industry sector through innovative production, processing, value- adding, and marketing schemes.",""],[1,"108","3","Agricultural Market Information System Expansion","Establish and/or update, and increase access of SFFs and other AFF stakeholders to timely and reliable agricultural market information systems.",""],[1,"108","4","Supply Chain Analytics Tool Adoption","The utilization of ICT tools such as the Supply Chain Analytics (SCAn) Dashboard and SCAn Reporter should also be encouraged among AFF stakeholders to ensure the unhampered flow of goods and inputs.",""],[1,"108","5","Private Sector Investment Promotion in Agri-Based Enterprises","Encourage the private sector to invest in agri-based enterprises.",""],[1,"108","5","Agro-Industrial Hubs and Business Incubators Development","Public-private partnerships will be employed to pursue the establishment of agro-industrial hubs, A&F business incubators, and regional technology parks to support an environment that would foster innovation and technology transfer to facilitate a vibrant A&F technology-based entrepreneurial system.",""],[1,"108","6","Fast-Tracked Sagip Saka Act Implementation","The implementation of the Sagip Saka Act of 2019 (RA 11321) will also be fast-tracked to provide SFFs with greater opportunities to engage in entrepreneurial activities through the implementation of the Farmers and Fisherfolk Enterprise Development Program under the law.",""],[1,"108","6","Farmers and Fisherfolk Enterprise Support Services","Aside from providing various forms of assistance to SFFs (e.g., improvement of production and productivity, improvement of producers' and entrepreneurs' access to financing, access to better technologies, and provision of business support and development services), RA 11321 also encourages private sector partnership or alliances between farmers and fisherfolk to engage in enterprise development and improve market access of producer groups.",""],[1,"110","4","Joint Planning, Monitoring, and Budgeting for Priority Programs and Projects","Strengthen coordination and convergence of government agencies in undertaking joint planning, monitoring, and budgeting for priority programs and projects.",""],[1,"110","4","Commodity and Industry Roadmap Formulation","the DA, DTI, and other related agencies in consultation with AFF/industry players, will work together in the formulation of commodity/industry roadmaps to complete the linkage between the AFF sector and the industry.","DA | DTI"],[1,"118","2","Efficient Supply Chain Distribution and Network Support","Ensure efficient supply chain distribution and network across regions.",""]],"15":[[1,"100","25","AFF Extension System Strengthening and Farmer Capacity Building","Strengthen AFF extension system and enhance the capacity of farmers and fisherfolk to adopt to new and better technologies",""],[1,"101","2","Science-Based Agricultural Decision Support Tools Expansion","Optimize the use of science-based decision support tools and methodologies to improve resilience and productivity within ecological limit, and increase the income of farmers and fisherfolk.",""],[1,"101","6","AgriDoc Farm Management App","The AgriDoc App developed by PhilRice is a farm management tool which can keep records on expenses and farm activities.",""],[1,"101","6","MOET Soil Diagnostic Mobile Application","The Minus-One Element Technique application (MOET App) is an Android-based app developed to complement the soil diagnostic tool MOET kit.",""],[1,"104","2","Farmer and Fisherfolk Technology Adoption Capacity-Building Programme","Enhance the capacity of farmers and fisherfolk to adopt new and better technologies.",""],[1,"104","3","Agriculture Extension System Strengthening","Strengthen the AFF extension system as a whole.","DA | TESDA | LGUs"],[1,"111","4","Agribusiness Education and Training Programme","Promote agribusiness courses and training programs (e.g., farm tourism, enterprise development, etc.) under collaborative schemes with the academe, government, and business sector;",""],[1,"111","4","Agriculture Curriculum Integration Initiative","integrate agriculture, including the use of modern technologies (e.g., drones, smart greenhouses, and smartphone applications) in the elementary and high school curriculum to encourage the youth to engage in agriculture and fisheries (See Chapter 10).",""],[1,"111","7","Climate- and Shock-Resilient Agricultural Extension Services","Intensify AFF extension services that will increase adoption of climate- and shock-resilient technologies (e.g., smart greenhouses, varieties that are short-maturing, high-yielding, flood/drought-tolerant, and stress-resilient, etc.), animal breeds, and best practices (e.g., AWD technology, integrated pest management, diversified/integrated farming, etc.);",""],[1,"111","8","Weather and Climate Advisory Decision Support Enhancement","Enhance the decision support tools of concerned agencies by providing timely and site-specific weather and climate advisories and utilize advanced and appropriate ICT to make it more available and accessible to stakeholders;",""],[1,"112","1","Early Warning and Anticipatory Mechanisms Development","Develop and mainstream the use of early warning systems and other anticipatory mechanisms (e.g., PRISM, etc.) that can help anticipate potential hazards and disturbances which can disrupt production operations.",""],[1,"112","1","Drone-Based Disaster Information and Response Enhancement","the use of drones and the subsequent information generated by the DA, before, during, and after disasters will be further enhanced and promoted to increase preparedness and response efficiency","DA"]],"16":[[1,"100","30","Affordable Formal Credit Access","Provide access to affordable formal credit",""],[1,"100","32","Low-Interest and Flexible-Term Credit Programs for SFFs and AFF-Based Enterprises","Continue to implement credit programs with low interest and flexible terms for the SFFs and AFF-based enterprises",""],[1,"100","33","Agricultural Insurance Expansion","Expand agricultural insurance coverage",""],[1,"109","2","Affordable Formal Credit Access for Livelihoods and MSMEs","Provide access to affordable formal credit to start, restore, sustain, and expand AFF-based livelihood activities and businesses.",""],[1,"109","3","Affordable Credit Programs for Small Farmers and Fisherfolk Enterprises","Continue to implement credit programs with low interest and flexible terms for SFFs and AFF-based enterprises.","DA"],[1,"109","3","Innovative and Affordable Financing Facilities","The government will continue to develop and implement innovative and affordable financing facilities, such as the Production Loan Easy Access and Survival and Recovery Assistance programs of the DA, which prioritizes loans for marginalized SFFs at low-interest rates, minimal or no collateral, and fewer documentary requirements.","DA"],[1,"109","3","KAYA Financing Expansion for Young Agripreneurs","Moreover, the DA can also expand the Kapital Access for Young Agripreneurs (KAYA) to finance the capital requirements of start-up or existing projects of young agripreneurs which intend to reach out and convince Filipino youth to engage in AFF ventures.","DA"],[1,"109","3","Awareness and Promotion of Credit Programs","SFF's awareness of available innovative and affordable credit programs will be increased through marketing and promotion activities (e.g. radio and TV plugs and guestings and brochures and pamphlets).",""],[1,"109","4","Expansion of Agricultural Insurance Coverage","Despite this, the PCIC will continue to expand coverage by engaging in partnership agreements with more LGUs, with the latter paying the insurance premium of farmers and fisherfolk not covered by RSBSA while the registry is being updated.",""],[1,"109","4","Innovative Index-Based Agricultural Insurance Development","In terms of facilitating faster payouts of indemnity claims, the PCIC will continue to develop and commercialize the implementation of innovative index-based insurance programs.",""],[1,"111","4","Youth Agripreneur Financing Support","Support in terms of financing of start-up or existing agri- based projects of young entrepreneurs and agri-fishery graduates will be provided to transform them into agripreneurs.",""],[1,"112","6","Coconut Farmers and Industry Trust Fund","Establishment of the Coconut Farmers and Industry Trust Fund",""],[1,"112","7","Coconut Farmers and Industry Trust Fund","The bill17 aims to consolidate all assets and benefits emanating from the coconut levy and create a Coconut Farmers and Industry Trust Fund to exclusively benefit coconut farmers and farmworkers.",""],[1,"112","9","PCIC Reorganization and Capitalization Increase","There is a need to reorganize the PCIC and increase its authorized capital stock to cater to the demands of SFFs more effectively.",""],[1,"113","2","Amendment of the Agri-Agra Reform Credit Act","This bill aims to amend the Agri-Agra Reform Credit Act of 2009 (RA No. 10000) by expanding the list of eligible projects and activities that can be funded by banks, as well as broaden the existing modes of alternative compliance, to allow banks to comply with their agricultural lending obligations.",""]],"17":[[1,"100","20","Food Safety and Quarantine Enforcement","Strictly implement food safety measures, quarantine procedures, and other existing rules and regulations in managing risks and addressing food safety and quality standards",""],[1,"110","1","Food Safety and Quality Regulatory Strengthening","Strictly implement food safety measures, quarantine procedures, and other existing rules and regulations in managing risks and addressing food safety and quality standards.",""],[1,"126","6","One-Stop Food Safety Certification Processing Venue","Operationalize a one-stop processing venue for the various certifications required by various food safety regulatory agencies (FSRAs) utilizing online platforms and digital payment channels;",""],[1,"126","6","Streamlining of Food Safety Regulatory Clearance Processes","Shorten turn-around periods of processing and issuing clearances, permits, or other required certifications to address regulatory compliance including a thorough review to streamline the FSRA processes;",""],[1,"126","6","Update Food Regulation Standards and Protocols","Update current standards and protocols for food regulation aligned with internationally recognized standards and protocols to address product safety and quality concerns of consumers.",""],[1,"127","4","Targeted Accreditation Awareness and Standards Compliance Promotion","Intensify targeted awareness and information dissemination on the benefits of accreditation for firms engaged in essential sectors and emerging industries.",""],[1,"128","1","Institutional and Human Capacity Strengthening for Product Safety Enforcement","Strengthen institutional and human capacities of key agencies to enforce regulations and enhance consumer awareness on the safety and quality of products and services.","Department of Health (DOH) | Department of Agriculture (DA) | Department of Trade and Industry (DTI)"],[1,"128","5","Food, Drug, and Cosmetics Standards Setting","The DOH through the Food and Drug Administration (FDA), establishes standards for processed food, drugs, and cosmetics.","DOH | Food and Drug Administration (FDA)"],[1,"128","6","Agricultural and Fisheries Product Standards Development","The DA's Bureau of Agriculture and Fisheries Product Standards develops standards for agriculture and agriculture-related products including fruits and vegetables and grains.","DA's Bureau of Agriculture and Fisheries Product Standards"],[1,"128","7","National Standardization and Standards Development Program","The DTI's Bureau of Philippine Standards (BPS) formulates standards for food and other categories including building, construction, and transport products; electrical and electronic products; and chemical and consumer products.","DTI's Bureau of Philippine Standards (BPS) | DOH | DA"],[1,"330","8","Sanitary and Phytosanitary Border Measures","It aims to strengthen the protection of the country's wildlife resources by: (a) increasing the fees and penalties for violators and (b) define and implement sanitary and phytosanitary measures to address possible entry of zoonotic infectious disease into the country (e.g., standards and protocols for crops, livestock, fisheries, and wildlife).",""]],"18":[[1,"100","14","Small Farmer and Fisherfolk Organization and Farm Consolidation Programme","Organize small farmers and fisherfolk into formal groups and promote farm consolidation and clustering arrangements",""],[1,"100","15","Intercropping and Integrated Farming Systems Promotion","Strengthen the promotion of intercropping and integrated farming systems",""],[1,"102","2","Intercropping and Integrated Farming Systems Promotion","Strengthen the promotion of intercropping and integrated farming systems.",""],[1,"102","3","Urban Agriculture and Community Gardening Promotion","The DA, in partnership with other government agencies, LGUs, and the private sector, shall intensify the promotion of urban agriculture, subsistence backyard/household gardening and animal raising, and community gardening through the establishment of community gardens in barangays and schools with vacant areas.","DA | other government agencies | LGUs | the private sector"],[1,"102","3","Urban Agriculture Start-Up Inputs and Skills Training","Production inputs such as seeds/seedlings, soil, compost, and initial stock (e.g., small ruminants, chicken, ducks, etc.) will be provided as start-up kits, complemented with skills training on sowing of seeds and proper management, composting, and pest disease management, among others.",""],[1,"102","3","Urban Agriculture Registration and Reporting Streamlining","Registration processes and reporting requirements will need to be streamlined for more efficient assistance to investors/firms pursuing urban agriculture, particularly modern methods of growing plants and fish such as hydroponics, aeroponics, and aquaponics.",""],[1,"108","1","Capacity Building for High-Value Commodity Diversification","To support this, capacity building activities for diversifying into commodities with high- value adding and market value will be provided to SFFs and MSMEs.",""],[1,"109","1","Community-Based Enterprise Support in Upland Areas","The government will continue to implement and monitor programs and projects that foster community-based enterprises in upland areas.",""],[1,"109","1","Farmer-to-Farmer Training and Extension Support","Provision of training and extension support services in these areas will be through a farmer-to-farmer approach where farmers serve as extension agents and are part of technology generation and dissemination.",""],[1,"112","11","Young Farmers Support and Representation Programme","This measure aims to promote and protect the rights of young farmers, establish programs for young farmers, and institutionalize young farmers' representation in agricultural decision-making and policy-making processes.",""]],"19":[[1,"9","5","Pantawid Pamilyang Pilipino Conditional Cash Transfer Program","The Pantawid Pamilyang Pilipino Act institutionalizes the Pantawid Pamilyang Pilipino Program to reduce the vulnerabilities of children in poor families.",""],[1,"13","7","Unconditional Cash Transfer Program","This was done by providing transfers to low-income families (estimated at 10 million) through the Unconditional Cash Transfer program, which has been implemented for three years.",""],[1,"187","5","CCT Household Replacement Policy Institutionalization","Institutionalizing replacement policy allowing for continuous replacement of CCT households.","DSWD"],[1,"191","16","Cash-for-Work Programs","Continue cash-for-work programs",""],[1,"193","4","Cash-for-Work Program Continuation","Continue cash-for-work programs.","DSWD | Department of Labor and Employment (DOLE)"],[1,"193","5","Wage Subsidy for Worker Retention","The Employment Recovery Plan of the DOLE will continue to help establishments retain their workers amidst temporary closures and adoption of flexible work arrangements.","DOLE"]],"20":[[1,"10","2","Social Security System Strengthening","The Social Security Act of 2018 strengthens the Social Security System, which is an important institution in building resilience.",""],[1,"10","2","Economic Support for Involuntarily Displaced Workers","It also provides economic support to workers who have been involuntarily displaced.",""],[1,"60","2","Vulnerable Sector Registry Setup","the government will focus on proactively minimizing Filipinos' exposure to risks and increasing their capacities to manage shocks, such as setting up registries for vulnerable sectors",""],[1,"60","2","Social Security System Coverage Expansion","expanding coverage of the Social Security System",""],[1,"60","2","Employment Insurance Scheme Introduction","instituting employment insurance schemes",""],[1,"183","8","Pandemic Social Assistance","It may also cover establishing medical reserve corps for disasters and health emergencies; and providing social assistance (i.e., social amelioration) during pandemics.",""],[1,"186","1","Social Protection System Strengthening","the sector will focus on proactively minimizing Filipinos' exposure to risks and increasing their capacities to manage shocks so that they can continue to achieve their full potential and pursue their aspirations.",""],[1,"186","1","Responsive Social Protection for Emergencies and the New Normal","The proposed initiatives will guarantee that the country's social protection system is responsive to keep the country healthy and resilient as it adjusts to the changes brought about by emergencies and adapt to the new normal.",""],[1,"186","2","Social Protection Financing and Institutional Arrangements","The government has improved social protection financing and institutional arrangements during the first three years of Plan implementation.",""],[1,"188","2","Social Protection for Emergency Food Access and Risk Management","Strategies under the social protection sector of the Philippine Development Plan 2017-2022 aim to ensure access to nutritious food even during emergencies, reduce each type of risk, and enable people to manage individual, economic, natural and human-induced disasters, and governance and political risks.",""],[1,"190","13","Vulnerability Reduction and Coping Capacity Enhancement","Strategies that reduced the vulnerability of Filipinos and built the capacity of individuals and families to manage and cope with various risks and shocks will be enhanced.",""],[1,"191","29","Safeguards Integration and Safety Net Funding Mechanisms","Integrate safeguards into development interventions and establish funding mechanisms for these safety nets",""],[1,"191","30","Social Protection Floor Institutionalization","Institutionalize a SP Floor",""],[1,"191","38","Disaster and Emergency Social Protection Program Menu","Establish a menu of social protection programs to be implemented during disasters and emergencies",""],[1,"191","42","SP Policy and Programme Monitoring and Evaluation","Monitor and evaluate SP policies and programs",""],[1,"192","1","Poverty Reduction and Resilience Policy and Service Upgrading","The government will continue to implement policies and programs that will empower and build the resilience of Filipinos, and further reduce poverty and vulnerability.",""],[1,"196","2","Social Protection Access and Assistance for GIDAs","Working with the LGUs, the NEDA-SDC Subcommittee on Social Protection (SCSP) will determine and address the barriers that prevent Filipinos, especially those living in GIDAs from accessing social protection programs.","NEDA-SDC Subcommittee on Social Protection (SCSP) | LGUs"],[1,"196","2","Emergency Assistance Measures for GIDA Residents","the SDC-SCSP shall also identify appropriate assistance measures to be provided to individuals living in GIDAs during pandemics and emergency situations.","SDC-SCSP"],[1,"196","3","Expanded SSS Coverage and Benefits Access","The SSS aims to broaden its coverage by ensuring simple registration, payment, and benefit application processes through physical and online platforms.",""],[1,"196","3","SSS Information Campaigns and Informal Sector Outreach","It will also continue conducting information campaigns and providing programs such the AlkanSSSya and KaltaSSS, which help workers, especially those in the informal sector - gain SSS coverage.",""],[1,"196","3","Gig Economy Social Security Partnership Framework","To facilitate coverage, partnerships will be established between gig economy platforms (i.e. Grab, Angkas, Lalamove, FoodPanda, Transportify, among others) and government social security agencies (SSS, PhilHealth, and Employees' Compensation Commission).",""],[1,"196","3","Expanded Employment Compensation Program Coverage","With this, the coverage of the Employment Compensation Program may also be expanded.",""],[1,"197","5","Disaster and Emergency Social Protection Menu","the SDC- SCSP will develop a menu of social protection programs which can be readily implemented upon the occurrence of such events.",""]],"21":[[1,"197","4","Safe Evacuation and Transition Housing Provision","the National Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Council (NDRRMC) will ensure the provision of safe evacuation and transition houses, which will have women and child-friendly spaces","National Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Council (NDRRMC)"],[1,"197","4","Mental Health and Psychosocial Support in Disasters","The DSWD and DOH will also make available appropriate and adequate mental health and psychosocial support services during disasters","DSWD | DOH"]],"22":[[1,"332","2","Support and Assistance for Repatriated and Displaced Overseas Filipinos","The government will continuously support and assist repatriated and displaced OFs and seek to address the increased vulnerability of those who remain abroad.",""],[1,"332","2","Socioeconomic Reintegration Support for Returning Overseas Filipinos","For those who have decided to return to the Philippines permanently, their successful socioeconomic reintegration will be prioritized.",""],[1,"336","7","Support and Assistance for Repatriated and Displaced Overseas Workers","Enhance government support and assistance for repatriated and displaced OFWs",""],[1,"336","10","Socioeconomic Reintegration Support for Overseas Filipinos and Families","Ensure successful socioeconomic reintegration of OFs and their families",""],[1,"336","19","Anti-Trafficking Protection Measures for Overseas Filipinos","Strengthen measures to protect OFs against human trafficking",""],[1,"337","1","Government Support for Repatriated and Displaced Overseas Filipino Workers","Enhance government support for repatriated and displaced OFWs.",""],[1,"337","2","Repatriated Overseas Filipino Worker Employment and Skills Retooling Program","Moreover, the government will explore hiring repatriated OFs as healthcare workers, contact tracers, personnel for the Build, Build, Build projects, the National ID System (PhilSys), and Community-Based Monitoring System (CBMS), among others.",""],[1,"337","2","Skills Retooling and Upgrading for Displaced and Repatriated OFWs","Along with these initiatives, the government will intensify the skills retooling and upgrading programs for displaced and repatriated OFWs (especially for telecommuting and e-commerce-friendly jobs) to keep them competitive whether in the domestic or international labor markets.",""],[1,"338","3","Assistance-to-Nationals Service Expansion","Provide sufficient assistance-to-nationals (ATN) services.",""],[1,"338","3","Support for Repatriation of Undocumented Filipino Migrants","In addition, agencies' capacity to provide assistance to undocumented Filipino migrants who wish to be repatriated will be strengthened.",""],[1,"338","3","Pre-Deployment Documentation and Protection Measures for OFWs","Proper documentation before the deployment of OFWs will strengthen protection and lessen the risk of OFWs becoming undocumented (see Chapter 18).",""],[1,"338","4","Migrant Agency Crisis Preparedness and Contingency Planning Capacity Building","there is a need to enhance the capability of migrant-serving agencies and consular officers on crisis preparedness and contingency planning.",""],[1,"338","4","Regular Updating of Foreign Service Contingency Plans","All Philippine Foreign Service Posts will be enjoined to regularly update their respective contingency plans.",""],[1,"338","4","One Country Team Approach for Overseas Crisis Response","The One Country Team Approach, where overseas representatives of various government agencies act together under the leadership of the Head of Post, will be strictly observed.",""],[1,"338","4","Overseas Preparedness Response Team Coordination and Relief Mechanism","The Overseas Preparedness Response Team (OPRT) will ensure that coordination with relevant agencies is sustained and rapid response and relief measures are implemented efficiently (see Chapter 18).",""],[1,"339","2","Migrant Worker Anti-Trafficking Protection Measures","Strengthen measures to protect OFs against human trafficking and exploitation.",""],[1,"339","2","Technology-Enabled Anti-Trafficking Information Platform","Trafficking and illegal recruitment schemes will be abated with effective use of technology-enabled platforms for information dissemination.",""],[1,"339","2","Local Government Anti-Trafficking Capacity Building","There is also a need to capacitate more LGUs to invest in anti-trafficking interventions.",""],[1,"339","2","Grassroots Anti-Trafficking Seminars for Duty Bearers","This includes seminars for duty bearers and stakeholders at the grassroots level on how, when, and where to report violations and other related laws.",""],[1,"339","2","Inter-Agency Trafficking Referral and Feedback System Improvement","The Inter-Agency Council Against Trafficking's referral and feedback system among duty bearers and stakeholders will be improved.",""],[1,"339","2","Updated Service Directories and Referral Pathways for OFs","Service directories will be regularly updated and effective referral pathways for essential services (including healthcare, policing and justice services, psychosocial support, reporting and complaints mechanisms, and other necessary support) will be made available and accessible to all OFs.",""],[1,"339","2","Strengthened Law Enforcement Coordination Against Trafficking","Moreover, coordination among local and international law enforcement agencies will be strengthened.",""],[1,"339","2","International Cooperation on Combatting Trafficking in Persons","The government will continue to explore ways to cooperate with other countries on combatting trafficking in persons (see Chapter 18).",""],[1,"340","2","Comprehensive OFW Reintegration Program","The Comprehensive OFW Reintegration Program will be implemented fully and continuously to realize its objectives: (a) incorporation of a gender-responsive reintegration preparedness program in all phases of migration, involving both OFWs and their families left behind; (b) initiation of reintegration pathways for different OFW segments, particularly domestic workers, less-skilled workers, sea-based workers, and professionals; and (c) convergence of initiatives and harmonization of reintegration programs and services of all government agencies and organizations to ensure a comprehensive approach to reintegration.",""],[1,"340","3","Expanded Loan Guarantee Fund for Enterprise Development and Loan Program","The budget for the loan guarantee fund of the Overseas Workers Welfare Administration (OWWA) for the Enterprise Development and Loan Program (EDLP), which is administered by the agency in partnership with the Land Bank of the Philippines and the Development Bank of the Philippines, will be increased.",""],[1,"340","3","Financial and Livelihood Assistance for Returning Filipinos","All financial and livelihood assistance initiatives, including grants and loans, will be promoted to reach a greater number of returning Filipinos.",""],[1,"340","3","Employment Facilitation Services for Returning Workers","For those seeking local employment, the government will strengthen employment facilitation services through proactive job matching, competency assessment, and certification.",""],[1,"340","3","Integrated Skills Registry for Employer-Worker Matching","The convergence of DOLE's enhanced National Skills Registration Program and the National Reintegration Center for OFWs' OFW Skills Registry will facilitate matching of employers and employees based on the former's needs and the latter's background and skills.",""]],"23":[[1,"191","17","Social Pension Expansion","Increase social pension and expand its coverage",""],[1,"195","2","Social Pension Expansion and Targeting Improvement","Increase the social pension and expand its coverage.",""],[1,"200","5","Foster Care Quality Improvement for Abandoned and Neglected Children","The bill will improve the quality of foster care for abandoned and neglected children, particularly those with special needs.",""],[1,"200","6","Anti-Senior Citizen Abuse Act and Expanded Social Pension Coverage","Anti-Senior Citizen Abuse Act Increasing amount and coverage of social pension",""],[1,"200","7","Senior Citizens Protection and Social Pension Expansion","The bill will protect senior citizens from all forms of abuse.",""],[1,"205","4","Resettlement Emergency Assistance Program","A resettlement emergency assistance program (REAP) by the DHSUD will, likewise, be implemented to ensure that families affected by unanticipated events are provided with emergency financial assistance for the construction or rehabilitation of their houses.","DHSUD"]],"24":[[1,"191","12","Emergency Food and Essential Supplies Support","Facilitate the provision of food and other necessities to vulnerable and high-risk individuals during emergencies",""],[1,"191","14","Designated Service Time for Vulnerable Groups","Provide designated service time for older persons and other groups highly-susceptible to infection",""],[1,"191","20","Vulnerable Individuals Access and COVID-19 Protection Measures","Implement measures to improve access of vulnerable individuals to necessities and support services and protect them from COVID-19",""],[1,"193","2","Emergency Food and Basic Necessities Assistance","Facilitate the provision of food and other necessities to vulnerable and high-risk individuals during emergencies.","DSWD | NNC | LGUs"],[1,"193","3","Designated Service Hours for Vulnerable Groups","Provide designated service time for older persons and other groups highly susceptible to infection.",""],[1,"195","5","Protection and Support Measures for Vulnerable Individuals During COVID-19","Implement measures to improve access of vulnerable individuals to necessities and support services and protect them from COVID-19.",""]],"25":[[1,"191","10","Holistic Child Labor Reduction Approach","Implement a holistic approach in addressing child labor",""],[1,"194","2","Holistic Child Labor Reduction Strategy","Implement a holistic approach in addressing child labor.",""],[1,"194","2","Employer Compliance Enforcement on Employment Standards","Aside from initiatives to address poverty and ensure employers' compliance to employment standards, the government as led by the National Council Against Child Labor, will also implement specific programs that will strategically help end child labor.",""],[1,"194","2","Child Labor Prevention and Support Programs","These include engaging non-government organizations and community members, addressing the needs of both children and their parents, and gathering and sharing data.",""],[1,"194","2","Parent Education on Child Labor","Educating parents on child labor through the Family Development Sessions of the 4Ps (under the DSWD) and Parents-Teachers Associations (under the DepEd) will be a central strategy in this endeavor.",""],[1,"194","3","Child Labor Registry Rollout","DOLE and DSWD will roll out the child labor registry, which lists all profiled child laborers and the appropriate services for the child and their parents.","DOLE | DSWD"]],"26":[[1,"7","1","Infrastructure Development Acceleration Programme","accelerate infrastructure development;",""],[1,"10","8","Build, Build, Build Infrastructure Program","Government has embarked on the Build, Build, Build program, which is an ambitious infrastructure program that increases spending for infrastructure from 4 percent of GDP in 2016, based on actual disbursement, to 5.5 percent in 2021, and 4.3 percent in 2022.",""],[1,"17","2","Build, Build, Build Infrastructure Program","The Build, Build, Build (BBB) program will remain a major strategy for economic recovery.",""],[1,"18","2","Public-Private Partnership Infrastructure Delivery","public-private partnerships will remain an option to address infrastructure gaps in various social and economic sectors",""],[1,"45","2","Metro Cebu Priority Infrastructure Project Package","It has also identified its priority project packages such as the Mega Cebu expressway, Cebu bus rapid transit, the new Cebu international container port, the third Cebu-Mactan bridge, and coastal road.",""],[1,"45","3","Mindanao Railway Project, Phase 1 Construction","This role will be enhanced by the construction of the first phase of the Mindanao Railway project in the first quarter of 2021.",""],[1,"48","11","Metro Manila Transport Infrastructure Development Roadmap","The Roadmap for Transport Infrastructure Development for Metro Manila and its Surrounding Areas and the Urban Transport Master Plan of Metro Cebu and the Davao City Infrastructure Development Plan and Capacity Building Project (IM4Davao) in Metro Davao are being implemented to reduce traffic, enhance competitiveness, improve safety and disaster response, and contribute to sustainable urban development of the areas covered.",""],[1,"49","4","Rural Connectivity Improvement","Linking rural areas to urban areas physically through transportation systems or virtually through information and communications technology (ICT) will enable people in rural areas to gain more access to alternative opportunities for employment, and bigger markets for their products.",""],[1,"50","3","Transport Network Improvement for Settlement Connectivity","the strategy is to establish better transport networks that will enable urban centers with high growth potentials to further expand growth while providing better access to opportunities to lagging areas",""],[1,"50","4","Connectivity and Infrastructure Development Policy Implementation","Flesh out and swiftly implement policies and plans for promoting connectivity and guiding infrastructure development in the country.",""],[1,"50","4","Transport Infrastructure Project Completion Acceleration","Timely completion of transport infrastructure projects under the BBB program will be pursued by addressing implementation bottlenecks under the new normal (see Chapter 19).",""],[1,"295","1","Transport Infrastructure Maintenance and Network Expansion","Ensure the upkeep of existing infrastructure while expanding the transport network.",""],[1,"295","1","Flagship Project Monitoring Mechanism","Projects that are implemented, especially those identified as flagship projects, will be monitored closely to ensure the quality and timely delivery of output.",""],[1,"295","3","Land-Based Transport Network Improvement","Prioritize mobility of people and goods over private vehicles by improving land-based transport network through engineering, enforcement, and education.",""],[1,"296","2","Philippine High Standard Highway Network Program Phase II","Future developments will be pursued for the national road network with the planned implementation of the Philippine High Standard Highway Network Program Phase II, which will add about 1,044.6 kilometers (km) of high standard national roads and expressways across metropolitan areas (884.7 km in Luzon, 73.8 km in Metro Cebu, and 86.1 km in Metro Davao).",""],[1,"296","2","Interoperable Contactless Toll Collection System","Toll expressways will be equipped with interoperable contactless toll collection systems for greater mobility and limiting person-to-person contact.",""],[1,"296","3","Local Roads Improvement and Maintenance Programme","local roads will continuously be improved by upgrading, expanding, and providing adequate maintenance.",""],[1,"296","3","Road Network Capacity and Design Optimization","Road capacity should be optimized while maximizing the design speed in the road network.",""],[1,"296","3","Innovative Road Intersection and Interchange Design","Innovative designs of intersections and interchanges will also be adopted and temporary bridges will be made permanent.",""],[1,"296","3","Road Safety and Resilience Standards Enforcement","Design standards that ensure the safety of users and resiliency of roads and bridges will be strictly enforced noting the road network should remain functional for humanitarian logistics.",""],[1,"296","4","Transport Corridor Decongestion and Road Clearance Program","the Department of the Interior and Local Government (DILG), together with the Philippine National Police (PNP) and respective LGUs, will sustain directives for all concerned units to clear all roads from illegal structures and abandoned construction materials, and rehabilitate damaged road facilities.","Department of the Interior and Local Government (DILG) | Philippine National Police (PNP)"],[1,"296","4","Local Roads Inventory and Road Network Database Development","To complement the ongoing inventory of national roads by the DPWH and to establish a complete database and monitoring of the Philippine road network, LGUs will also be required to prepare an inventory of all roads within their jurisdiction as part of their geographic information system-based Local Roads Network Development Plan and their respective Local Public Transport Route Plans as part of their CLUPs.",""]],"27":[[1,"8","19","Transport Policy and IRR Implementation","National Transport Policy and its IRR",""],[1,"10","9","National Transport Policy and Implementing Rules and Regulations","A National Transport Policy (NTP), together with its Implementing Rules and Regulations (IRR), has also been adopted.",""],[1,"35","5","National Transport Policy Implementation","The approved National Transport Policy (NTP), which envisions a Philippine transport system that is \"safe, secure, reliable, efficient, integrated, intermodal, affordable, cost-effective, environmentally sustainable, and people-oriented\", will be an important instrument in achieving this goal.",""],[1,"35","5","Transport System Master Plan Formulation","The subsequent formulation of a transport system master plan will guide the rational development of an intermodal transport network in the country.",""],[1,"50","5","Integrated Transport Planning and Project Implementation","An integrated approach to transport planning and project implementation will be pursued through closer engagement between national transport agencies and LGUs.","Department of Public Works and Highways | Department of Transportation"],[1,"50","5","Local Transport and Traffic Management Program Support","the Department of Public Works and Highways and the Department of Transportation can provide assistance in coming up with their local transport and traffic management programs that are aligned with national priorities","Department of Public Works and Highways | Department of Transportation"],[1,"50","6","Public Transport Accessibility and Route Rationalization","Ensure the accessibility, availability, affordability, convenience, and reliability of public transport (e.g., railway, bus, etc.). This will involve rationalization of the public transport design or transport routes to serve new and emerging origins and destinations.",""],[1,"50","6","Integrated Public Transport Terminal Development","Public transport terminals that integrate different modes of public transportation will be established in strategic locations.",""],[1,"293","4","National Transport Policy Enforcement and Legislative Strengthening","Enforce the National Transport Policy (NTP) and strengthen it through legislation.",""],[1,"293","4","Independent Transport Regulatory Bodies Establishment","a law adopting it and creating independent regulatory bodies for the railways, airports, and seaports, among others, will establish a more streamlined transport sector",""],[1,"293","5","National Transport Policy Compliance and Oversight","the NEDA Board Committee on Infrastructure (INFRACOM) and the Inter-Agency Technical Committee on Transport Planning will continuously ensure that the NTP and its implementing rules and regulations (IRR) will be adhered to in planning, programming, implementing, operating, and maintaining transport projects and in operationalizing strategies and intended policy reforms.",""],[1,"293","6","Technical Assistance for Local Mobility Planning and Management","To this end, the Department of Transportation (DOTr) and the Department of Public Works and Highways (DPWH) will extend technical assistance to LGUs in the field of transport planning, transport and land use integration, program and project implementation and monitoring, and traffic engineering and management.","Department of Transportation (DOTr) | Department of Public Works and Highways (DPWH)"],[1,"294","1","Unified Transport Data and Modeling System","baseline transport data and information will have to be consolidated and a unified database and transport model will be maintained.",""],[1,"294","1","Local Traffic Flow Data Collection and Sharing Arrangement","At the local level, regional agencies of DOTr, DPWH, Land Transportation Office, and Land Transportation Franchising and Regulatory Board, together with LGUs will be responsible for collecting traffic flow data across different transport modes, which will be shared with the central transport database.","DOTr | DPWH | Land Transportation Office | Land Transportation Franchising and Regulatory Board | LGUs"],[1,"294","2","Integrated Land Use and Transport Planning","National transport agencies and LGUs will implement an integrated approach to land use and transport planning in the provision of transport infrastructure and services.",""],[1,"294","2","Local Transport Sector Planning Requirement","LGUs will be required to prepare local transport sector plans such as the Local Public Transport Route Plan as part of their Comprehensive Development Plans (CDPs).",""],[1,"294","2","Regular Updating of Comprehensive Development Plans","The CDPs will be regularly updated to account for new and significant developments in land use and transport networks.",""],[1,"294","2","Critical Infrastructure Requirements in Land Use Plans","Critical infrastructure in times of disasters, calamities, and future pandemics will be required in the Comprehensive Land Use Plans (CLUPs) of LGUs.",""],[1,"311","5","National Transport Policy Enactment","Enactment of the National Transport Policy",""],[1,"311","5","Independent Railway and Maritime Regulatory Bodies Law","Enactment of a law creating independent regulatory bodies for the railway and maritime transport sectors",""],[1,"311","7","Agency-Level Transport Planning Framework","This policy will provide the parameters for planning at the agency level, e.g., the formulation of the Philippine Transport System Master Plan.",""],[1,"311","9","Transport Sector Regulatory Body Creation Bill","The proposed law is for filing/endorsement to the 18th Congress.",""]],"28":[[1,"51","1","RORO Port Improvement and Expansion Programme","be strengthened through the improvement of existing RORO ports and the establishment of new ones.",""],[1,"51","1","National Airport Facilities Improvement and Expansion Programme","Improvements and expansion of airport facilities across the country will also be continued to meet the demand and improve the quality of air travel",""],[1,"51","2","Efficient Logistics System Development","Develop an efficient logistics system.","Department of Agriculture | Department of Trade and Industry"],[1,"297","4","Airport Operational Efficiency and Capacity Expansion Strategy","Improve the operational efficiency of airports and address constraints to optimal capacity utilization.",""],[1,"297","5","Optimal Airports System Expansion Strategy","Implement an optimal airports system strategy to expand airport capacities at pace with growing demand.",""],[1,"297","5","Provincial Airport Rehabilitation Programme","Existing provincial airports will be rehabilitated, while smaller or community airports will be upgraded to standard Principal Class 2 classification to cater to commercial flights for better connectivity with various tourist destinations.",""],[1,"297","5","Airport Night Operations Upgrade","Aeronautical Lighting System and Instrument Landing System, can be installed in airports with appropriate facilities complying with the existing civil aviation regulations to enable night-time operations and improve accessibility, especially for those identified to readily accommodate said technology.",""],[1,"297","5","Regional Airport Night-Landing Assessment and Design Measures","The remaining regional airports will be assessed to determine night- landing viability.",""],[1,"297","6","Air Transport Facilities Modernization and New Investment Program","Facilities and equipment will be modernized (e.g., night-rating) in compliance with International Civil Aviation Organization (ICAO) and International Air Transport Association standards, especially those that serve island provinces in Visayas and Mindanao.",""],[1,"297","6","Air Transport Security Integration in Facility Planning","Security features/aspects should be integrated in the planning and design stages of development and/or rehabilitation of air transport facilities, to ensure allotment of sufficient space for security equipment (technology), processes (passenger and baggage throughput), and personnel (ergonomics).",""],[1,"298","1","Airport Development for Tourism Connectivity","Airport development in regional areas and island provinces will follow a hub-and-spoke model, where the gateway airport will connect to feeder airports providing access to areas of destination with natural and cultural tourism sites.",""],[1,"298","2","Airport-Led Growth Center and Smart City Development Exploration","The role of airports as a catalyst for new growth centers and smart cities will be explored, taking off from the experience in CRK where demand growth complements and is reinforced by various ongoing mixed- use developments in Northern and Central Luzon, e.g., the New Clark City.",""],[1,"298","3","Air Transport Regulatory Reform and Airport Modernization","Strengthen and rationalize air transport regulations, policies, and protocols and modernize facilities to enhance air passenger experience.",""],[1,"298","4","Airport Equipment Modernization and Training Enhancement","Equipment inventory will be modernized and airport training modules will be further enhanced.",""],[1,"298","4","Passenger Compensation and Public Assistance Deployment","more public assistance officers will also be deployed.",""],[1,"298","6","Port Facilities Improvement and RORO Network Expansion","Improve port facilities to ensure that inter-island shipping, including a stronger roll-on/roll-off (RORO) network, will remain a viable option for transporting people and cargo.",""],[1,"298","6","Port Expansion to International Standards","International standards will be followed in the expansion of port facilities.",""],[1,"298","6","Navigation Channel Installation for Larger Vessels","In addition, navigation channels to accommodate larger vessels will be installed to ensure the sustainability and efficiency of ports.",""],[1,"299","3","Coastal and Inland Waterways Transport System Development","the government will develop the Coastal and Inland Waterways Transport System to further reduce urban traffic congestion and pollution, expand the intermodal transport network, increase regional connectivity, and create new business opportunities.",""],[1,"299","4","Maritime Industry Development Plan Implementation","Implement the Maritime Industry Development Plan (MIDP).",""],[1,"299","4","Nautical Highway Development Program","These include the Nautical Highway Development Program, Maritime Tourism Program, and National Fishery Industry Development Program",""],[1,"299","4","Maritime Tourism Program","These include the Nautical Highway Development Program, Maritime Tourism Program, and National Fishery Industry Development Program",""],[1,"299","4","National Fishery Industry Development Program","These include the Nautical Highway Development Program, Maritime Tourism Program, and National Fishery Industry Development Program",""],[1,"299","5","Global Maritime Hub and Eco-Maritime Industrial Park Development","A global maritime hub for SBSRs and related ancillary businesses with a world-class research and training center in the country will be developed to bring together all maritime-related companies in one eco- maritime industrial park.",""]],"29":[[1,"130","7","E-Vehicle Production and Usage Incentive Scheme","Support and grant for time-bound and performance-based incentives for the manufacture, assembly, conversion, and sale of hybrid and other fuel-alternative vehicles and the establishment of charging stations, will be pursued in accordance with the provisions under the Corporate Recovery and Tax Incentives Reform Act (CREATE) bill (see Chapter 15).",""],[1,"130","7","Public Utility Vehicle Modernization Program Support","This is also in support of the Public Utility Vehicle (PUV) Modernization Program of the government to make the country's public transportation system efficient and environment friendly.",""]],"30":[[1,"294","3","National Supply Chain Network Development","Develop efficient and resilient national supply chain network system.",""],[1,"294","3","Transport Agency Convergence Programs","Transport agencies will continue to formulate convergence programs with concerned agencies to ensure that economic sectors are provided with adequate transport infrastructure support and services.",""],[1,"294","3","Farm-to-Market and Farm-to-Mill Road Support","Agricultural areas will continue to be supported through the provision of farm-to-market and farm-to-mill roads in accordance with the standards set for both design and construction.",""],[1,"294","3","Tourism Transport Infrastructure Development","Transport infrastructure supporting tourist destinations will continuously be developed to boost tourism activities that were affected by the COVID-19 pandemic.",""],[1,"294","4","Mindanao Logistics Infrastructure Network Road Projects","To support development in Mindanao, road projects under the Mindanao Logistics Infrastructure Network will be pursued",""],[1,"294","4","Improving National Roads for Inclusive Growth in Mindanao Projects","along with the implementation of the Improving National Roads for Inclusive Growth in Mindanao Projects in Western Mindanao",""],[1,"294","4","BIMP-EAGA Road Network Capacity Expansion","The capacity of the Brunei Darussalam-Indonesia-Malaysia- Philippines East ASEAN Growth Area (BIMP-EAGA) road network will also be increased",""],[1,"294","5","Multimodal Transport Terminal Development","multimodal transport terminals complete with ancillary facilities will be established to provide smooth transition for passengers and freight from one mode to another.",""],[1,"294","6","National Logistics Estates and Hubs Development","Logistics estates and hubs will be developed at critical locations nationwide to support not only regional economic activities, but also humanitarian logistics in times of pandemics and disasters.",""],[1,"296","6","Passenger and Freight Railway Transport Interconnectivity Development","Tourism, trade, and commerce will be supported through enhanced interconnectivity of passenger and freight railway transport development to generate opportunities for local area development, as well as expansion of local markets to promote productivity and trade competitiveness.",""],[1,"299","1","Port Capacity Optimization and Logistics Network Integration","The government commits to optimize the utilization of existing ports.",""],[1,"299","2","Cavite Gateway Terminal and Domestic Port Connectivity Enhancement","The direct connection between Manila and Batangas Ports, through the Cavite Gateway Terminal, will be further enhanced, and co-loading (modified cabotage) will be promoted to encourage shipment between domestic ports.",""],[1,"299","2","Dry Port Improvement and Expansion Programme","Existing dry ports will be improved and new ones will be built to provide support to manufacturers, importers, and exporters.",""],[1,"299","2","Logistics Hub Development for Industrial and Agro-industrial Connectivity","Logistics hubs will be developed, where applicable, to connect industrial and manufacturing zones and agro-industrial areas to major port areas.",""],[1,"299","2","BIMP-EAGA Transit Transport Route Capacity Improvement","Further, the capacity of the BIMP-EAGA Transit Transport Route in Mindanao will be improved to facilitate swift intra-EAGA transport.",""]],"31":[[1,"129","6","Customs Modernization and Tariff Act Implementation","Address bureaucratic hurdles to reduce trade costs pertinent to logistics by fully implementing the Customs Modernization and Tariff Act (CMTA).",""],[1,"129","6","24/7 Customs Port Service and Decongestion Measures","the Bureau of Customs (BOC) must ensure uninterrupted 24/7 service in the ports including weekends and must accredit more off-dock Container Yards and Container Barge Terminals as part of its decongestion measures.","Bureau of Customs (BOC)"],[1,"129","6","Prompt Truck Franchise and Permit Issuance","The Land Transport and Franchising Regulatory Board (LTFRB), for its part, will ensure prompt issuance of franchises and Permit to Operate (PTO) to truck drivers.","Land Transport and Franchising Regulatory Board (LTFRB)"],[1,"129","6","Regulation of Port and Shipping Fees","the DTI's issuance of a policy to regulate port and shipping fees for shippers and Full Container Load (FCL) shipments must be fast- tracked.",""],[1,"129","10","Digital Permitting Streamlining for Exporters and Importers","Adopt digitalization with the view of harmonizing and streamlining permitting requirements of exporters and importers pursuant to the implementation of the EODB-EGSD Act, as enforced by the Anti-Red Tape Authority (ARTA)","Anti-Red Tape Authority (ARTA)"],[1,"129","10","Inter-agency Taskforce for Ecozone Coordination","establish an Inter-agency Taskforce to strengthen coordination among IPAs, including the establishment of a one-stop shop to respond to all concerns regarding ecozone development, investment requirements, and applicable incentives, among others",""],[1,"132","3","Supply Chain Bottleneck Reduction Measures","For logistics, bottlenecks in achieving a seamless, uninterrupted supply chain that is efficient and reliable needs to be addressed.",""],[1,"133","22","Logistics Services Improvement","Improve logistics services",""],[1,"139","1","Port Development Near Export-Processing Zones","Develop ports near export-processing zones to provide businesses with the necessary infrastructure to facilitate shipment of goods and services to export markets at a lower cost.",""],[1,"139","1","Regulation on International Shipping Rates","Immediate promulgation and implementation of regulation on international shipping rates will be critical in addressing high shipping costs.",""],[1,"139","1","Utilization of Ports Outside Metro Manila","Increased utilization of ports outside Metro Manila (e.g., Batangas and Subic ports), as well as deterrence of smuggling activities, will be crucial in eliminating logistical inefficiencies.",""],[1,"139","2","Customs Procedure Improvement under Lateral Attrition Act Review","Revisit the Lateral Attrition Act (RA 9335) to include improvement in current customs procedures as part of the assessment of performance indicators used by the Bureau of Customs.",""],[1,"139","3","Customs Procedure Streamlining and Port Decongestion Reform","Accelerate streamlining of customs procedures in terms of speed, simplicity, and predictability to avoid congestion in ports.",""],[1,"139","3","Shipment Tracking and Tracing System","An efficient system of tracking and tracing shipments must be in place using the latest available technology.",""],[1,"139","3","Warehouse, Cold Storage, and Paperless Transaction Investment Programme","Investments in warehouses, cold storage facilities, and paperless transaction systems need to be increased.",""],[1,"139","4","Port Management and Regulation Reform","Revisit the management and regulation of ports to improve efficiency of port operations and encourage competition among ports.",""],[1,"139","5","TradeNET Full Operationalization","Pursue efforts towards the full operationalization of the TradeNET in line with the country's commitment to the ASEAN Single Window.",""],[1,"139","6","National Logistics Master Plan Upgrade and Implementation Strengthening","Upgrade the National Logistics Master Plan 2017-2022 to include innovation and strengthen its implementation to improve the efficiency of the national logistics system.",""],[1,"139","6","Smart Logistics Technology Development and Diffusion","Development and diffusion of smart logistics technology (e.g,, drones, automation) are essential to keep abreast of the changing logistics landscape.",""],[1,"139","6","Supply Chain Analytics Dashboard Promotion","Use of the Supply Chain Analytics (SCAn) Dashboard and SCAn Reporter, which aim to troubleshoot problems in the supply chain for goods and production inputs and in planning supply chain-related interventions, will be promoted.",""],[1,"139","6","Logistics Fee and Regulation Rationalization","Fees and regulations imposed by local and national governments will be rationalized to reduce the burden for logistics industry players.",""],[1,"139","6","Transport Infrastructure Upgrades for Logistics Hubs","Infrastructure upgrades, particularly the construction of transport systems connected to logistics hubs, are critical in coping with the increasing demand for logistics services.",""],[1,"139","7","National Multimodal Transport Body","Create a competent national body for multimodal transport.",""],[1,"139","7","Transport Policy Coordination and Function Rationalization","In the interim, close policy coordination, deeper integration, and information sharing towards potential rationalization of functions should be developed by the Department of Transportation (DOTr), Maritime Industry Authority (MARINA), and Land Transport Franchising Regulatory Board (LTFRB) to ensure greater interconnectivity among different modes of transport and land uses.","Department of Transportation (DOTr) | Maritime Industry Authority (MARINA) | Land Transport Franchising Regulatory Board (LTFRB)"],[1,"139","7","Automated Multimodal Franchise and Permit Processing","Provision of franchises and permits for multi-modal operations (land, sea, and air) should be automated and streamlined.",""],[1,"139","8","Review of the Foreign Ships Co-Loading Act","Review the existing Foreign Ships Co-Loading Act for possible amendments.",""],[1,"139","9","Support for Maritime Industry Development Plan Programs","Support the adoption of the programs under the Maritime Industry Development Plan (MIDP) 2019-2028",""],[1,"140","1","Philippine Ship Registration Act","Pursue the passage of the Philippine Ship Registration Act, which will enhance and rationalize the Philippine maritime industry through the establishment of a ship registry system compliant with international maritime convention regulations and practices.",""],[1,"142","6","Standardized Destination and Shipping Charges Regulation","Mandates MARINA to promote standardized destination and shipping charges among freight forwarders and agents of international shipping lines operating in the Philippines.","MARINA"],[1,"142","6","Inter-agency Competition and Revenue System Support","Will also mandate DTI, PCC, BOC, BIR, and other relevant agencies to assist MARINA in facilitating competition, commerce, and an honest revenue system, among others.","DTI | PCC | BOC | BIR | MARINA"]],"32":[[1,"295","3","Public Transport Reform and Fleet Modernization","For a more efficient use of road infrastructure, high-quality public transport modes will be pursued, such as public transport reform, fleet modernization, route rationalization, and environmentally sustainable urban transport systems, among others, so that commuters will prefer public over private vehicles and more people can be moved with less road space, thereby addressing traffic congestion.",""],[1,"295","3","High-Capacity Mass Transit Prioritization","In high passenger density corridors, high capacity mass transit systems such as rail will be prioritized over buses and jeepneys.",""],[1,"296","5","Rail Network and Mass Transit Expansion","Expand the rail network and other mass transit systems and ensure their accessibility, affordability, convenience, and reliability.",""],[1,"296","7","Interregional Railway Project Completion and Rail Freight Connectivity","the completion of planned interregional railway projects will be prioritized",""],[1,"296","7","Rail-Based Connectivity to Ports and Airports","The establishment of rail-based connection to seaports, dry ports, inland container depots, and airports will also be pursued",""],[1,"296","8","Integrated Fare Collection System","Transport network operators, both private and public, will continue to forge convergence undertakings to achieve integrated fare collection systems.",""],[1,"297","1","Expansion of Contactless Public Transport Fare Payment","migration from physical stored value cards to mobile, contactless payment will be expanded to other public transport modes to reduce the risk of spreading diseases as part of health and safety protocol in the public transport sector.",""],[1,"297","2","Railway Procurement Policy Customization","Policies and guidelines on procurement activities in the railway sector will be customized to ensure the availability of highly specialized spare parts and supplies.",""],[1,"297","3","Rail and Mass Transit Skills Upgrading Programme","capacities of skilled workers in mass transit systems, especially rail, will be upgraded.",""],[1,"297","3","Philippine Railway Training Center Technical Training","the Philippine Railway Training Center will continue to provide comprehensive technical training for train drivers and other rail professionals.",""]],"33":[[1,"165","5","Road Traffic Injury Prevention Measures","To prevent road traffic injuries, stricter enforcement of laws and standards to mitigate risks factors (i.e., vehicle standards, speeding, drunk driving, wearing of seatbelts or helmets), safer infrastructure, enhanced post-crash care will be continuously promoted to avoid these accidents.",""],[1,"299","6","Universal Transport Security Structure","Adopt a universally-accepted security structure to improve safety and security of the public transport system.",""],[1,"299","6","Transport Accident Investigation Body","An independent body will be created to investigate transport accidents and provide transport safety recommendations to minimize activities that may cause injury, death, loss, or damage to property.",""],[1,"299","6","Transport Security Compliance Monitoring Activities","the Office of Transportation Security (OTS) will continue to conduct compliance monitoring activities (CMA) such as security audit, inspection, and test in public and private transport terminals to ensure that the security measures and procedures are implemented and in compliance with the standard presented in their respective security plans.",""],[1,"300","1","Advanced Security Systems Procurement and Installation","Advanced security systems for land-based terminals, airports, and seaports will be procured and installed.",""],[1,"300","1","Philippine Coast Guard Capability-Building Programme","The Philippine Coast Guard (PCG) will continue its capability- building programs to ensure presence and control over the country's vast maritime domain.",""],[1,"300","1","Marine Navigation Aids Installation Programme","To ensure safety in marine navigation, the PCG will continue the installation of aids to navigation such as buoyage systems, lighthouses, and other related facilities.",""],[1,"300","1","Maritime Floating and Air Assets Procurement","New floating and air assets will be procured and a sufficient well- trained personnel complement will be provided.",""],[1,"300","1","Strategic Maritime Base and Station Development","To serve the growing tourism and maritime industry, new bases or stations will be developed in strategic locations.",""],[1,"300","2","Road Safety Measures for Public Transport and National Roads","Strictly implement road safety measures.",""],[1,"300","3","Risk-Based Health Protocols at Gateways","Mainstream risk-based health protocols at the country's gateways.",""],[1,"312","1","Transport Safety and Security Authority Law","Enactment of a law creating an independent body for transport Safety and Security",""],[1,"312","2","Independent Transport Safety and Security Authority","This places all transport safety and security matters under a single independent body that will, among others, investigate transport accidents and provide transport safety recommendations, thereby eliminating conflicting and overlapping functions of existing agencies or entities.",""]],"34":[[1,"295","2","Universal Accessibility in Transport Infrastructure and Services","universal accessibility design and principles will be considered in the implementation of all transport infrastructure facilities and services to ensure an inclusive and people-oriented national transport system.",""],[1,"295","2","Revival of the Task Force on Accessibility","The Task Force on Accessibility created in 2007 will be revived to develop initiatives that will address the unique needs of persons with disabilities, elderly, women, and children in terms of mobility within the transport network, particularly in public transport systems.",""],[1,"295","4","Adoption of Accessible Public Utility Vehicle Standard","the DOTr and its attached agencies will adopt the Philippine Standard for Accessible Public Utility Vehicles formulated by the Department of Trade and Industry - Bureau of Philippine Standards.","Department of Transportation | Department of Trade and Industry - Bureau of Philippine Standards"],[1,"295","5","Non-Motorized Transport Infrastructure Integration","Non-motorized transport (e.g., bicycle and pedestrian infrastructure) will be integrated into the existing network through retrofitting.",""],[1,"295","5","Walkability and Cycling Design Standards for New Transport Projects","The design of new projects will also consider features to encourage more walking and cycling trips.",""],[1,"295","5","Mainstreaming of Bicycle and Pedestrian Infrastructure Standards","Standardized designs for bicycle and pedestrian infrastructure will be mainstreamed in projects of national transport agencies and LGUs.",""],[1,"295","5","Multimodal Mobility Support Facilities","Existing and future transportation facilities will have infrastructure supporting non-motorized transport modes (e.g., bicycle racks, adequate pedestrian lighting) to promote multimodal mobility.",""],[1,"312","4","Active and Sustainable Transport Law","Enactment of a law institutionalizing the use of bicycles and other active and sustainable modes of transportation",""],[1,"312","5","Non-Motorized and Active Transport Integration Programme","This will be done by providing the necessary infrastructure and support services, establishing safety and design standards, and increasing public awareness on road safety and road sharing among motorists, cyclists, and pedestrians.",""],[1,"325","16","Mass Transport System Reform and Ride-Sharing Expansion","Support reforms on mass transport system, including the expansion of ride-sharing services to reduce proliferation of vehicles, and promote the production and utilization of eco-friendly",""],[1,"326","1","Bicycle Lane and Bike-Sharing Expansion","the use of non-motorized transport through the establishment of bicycle lanes and replication of local bike-sharing systems",""],[1,"326","2","Walkable Cities and Urban Green Infrastructure Development","Encourage development of walkable cities and major urban areas to improve built-up systems of urban environment, and expand green and open urban spaces and green infrastructure to improve health and well-being of people and the environment (e.g., reduce carbon emissions).",""],[1,"331","7","Pedestrian and Non-Motorized Transport Infrastructure Network","This intends to provide safe and convenient pathways for pedestrians and non- motorized vehicles (e.g., walkways and bike lanes) and integrate these in the infrastructure development agenda.",""],[1,"331","7","Pop-up Bicycle Lane Network","The Bill intends to create a network of pop-up bicycle lanes to connect users to essential destinations (e.g., medical facilities), designate a network of people-oriented emergency pathways, and mandate the provision of adequate parking spaces for bicycles and other non-motorized vehicles, as far as practicable, among others.",""]],"35":[[1,"249","2","Continuous Structural Reform for Business Environment Improvement","Continuous structural reforms will serve as the backbone of ongoing efforts to develop a better business environment and create development opportunities.",""],[1,"250","3","Alternative Work Arrangements Amendment","Further, incorporating amendments related to provisions that will address alternative work arrangements may also be considered.",""],[1,"250","6","Ease of Doing Business and Efficient Government Service Delivery Act Implementation","Full implementation of the Ease of Doing Business and Efficient Government Service Delivery Act will be pursued to streamline processes or regulations that impede exports.",""],[1,"250","6","Public Service Act Reform for Foreign Investment Liberalization","The Public Service Act will also be pushed, which will allow foreign investments in transport and communication, this in turn can help reduce shipping costs (see Chapter 9).",""],[1,"250","6","Foreign Investment and Retail Trade Liberalization Measures","Other legislations that will allow foreign competition and improve the competitive environment such as the Foreign Investments Act and the Retail Trade Liberalization shall also be pursued.",""],[1,"253","11","Telecommuting and Work-from-Home Regulatory Provisions","Consider relaxing export requirements and incorporate provisions which will address telecommuting and work from home arrangements as a response to the pandemic",""],[1,"253","12","National Quality Infrastructure Bill","Key legislative measures that will promote a sustainable and resilient external sector include measures listed under Chapter 9 such as National Quality Infrastructure Bill, Amendment to the Foreign Investment Act, and Amendment to the Retail Trade Liberalization Act.",""],[1,"253","12","Amendment to the Foreign Investment Act","Key legislative measures that will promote a sustainable and resilient external sector include measures listed under Chapter 9 such as National Quality Infrastructure Bill, Amendment to the Foreign Investment Act, and Amendment to the Retail Trade Liberalization Act.",""],[1,"253","12","Amendment to the Retail Trade Liberalization Act","Key legislative measures that will promote a sustainable and resilient external sector include measures listed under Chapter 9 such as National Quality Infrastructure Bill, Amendment to the Foreign Investment Act, and Amendment to the Retail Trade Liberalization Act.",""],[1,"259","5","Services Sector Liberalization and Professional Practice Reform","the government will open sectors to foreign players and consider the enactment of legislation that will ease requirements for the practice of professions in the country",""],[1,"259","5","Telecommunications Sector Opening and Digitalization Support","Opening the telecommunications sector, for instance, will ensure more reliable internet services in the country and digitalization of businesses, especially of small business players and MSMEs in the new normal.",""],[1,"261","4","Foreign Equity Liberalization for Service Sectors","The measure will lift foreign equity restrictions in certain sectors that offer services not under the scope of public utilities such as those engaged in the telecommunication services.",""],[1,"261","6","Foreign Investment Act Liberalization","The measure will ease restrictive provisions in the Foreign Investment Act to address procurement restrictions and lengthy procedures that hamper foreign investment and participation of foreign bidders in local procurement.",""]],"36":[[1,"126","1","Supportive Policy Environment for Entrepreneurs and Startups","Provide a supportive policy environment for entrepreneurs and startups.",""],[1,"126","2","Convergence of Government Startup and SME Initiatives","Pursue convergence among various government initiatives and flagship programs for startups, micro, and small enterprises and cooperatives.",""],[1,"145","8","Startup and MSME Growth Incentive Programme","Facilitate growth of startups and MSMEs by incentivizing their expansion and subsequent upgrade",""],[1,"145","9","Support Transition of Micro and Small Enterprises to the Formal Economy","Support transition to the formal economy of micro and small enterprises",""],[1,"145","21","Coordination of Productivity-Enhancing Government Initiatives","Ensure that all government agencies with productivity-enhancing initiatives are coordinated",""],[1,"145","23","Startup, MSME, and Cooperative Statistics System","Establish relevant statistics for startups, MSMEs, and cooperatives",""],[1,"146","1","Startup and MSME Growth Incentive Reform","Facilitate growth of startups and MSMEs by incentivizing their expansion and subsequent upgrade.",""],[1,"146","1","Regulatory Incentive and Disincentive Restructuring for MSMEs","In restructuring the incentives (and disincentives) in the regulatory framework, facilitating the growth of MSMEs to eventually become globally competitive will be a key goal.",""],[1,"146","3","Time-Bound and Performance-Based Grant and Assistance Provision","Ensure that provision of grants and other financial or technical assistance, are time-bound and performance-based, as provided under the Corporate Recovery and Tax Incentives Reform Act (CREATE);",""],[1,"146","6","Startup-Friendly Business Climate Reform","The government will enhance business incubation support and accelerate services for startups, lessen administrative burdens and complexity of regulatory procedures for startups, and reduce, if not eliminate, the regulatory protection of incumbents (see Chapter 16).",""],[1,"146","6","Philippine Startup Development Program","the Philippine Startup Development Program will support incubators, accelerators and makerspaces by creating opportunities for innovative startups to gain access to marketing and technical support as well as linkage to potential collaborators locally and globally (see",""],[1,"150","5","Coordination of Productivity-Enhancing Initiatives","Ensure that all government agencies with productivity-enhancing initiatives are coordinated.",""],[1,"150","5","Agency Coordination for Startup, MSME, and Cooperative Productivity","Close coordination of relevant agencies concerned with enhancing productivity, efficiency, and resilience of startups, MSMEs, and cooperatives will be pursued.",""],[1,"150","5","Productivity Toolbox Partnership Expansion","The National Wages and Productivity Commission (NWPC) and its Regional Tripartite Wages and Productivity Boards (RTWPBs) will strengthen and expand partnerships with concerned government agencies, industry associations, employer groups, and labor groups to foster synergy in the deployment of the Productivity Toolbox63 (see Chapter 10).","National Wages and Productivity Commission (NWPC) | Regional Tripartite Wages and Productivity Boards (RTWPBs)"],[1,"150","8","MSME Productivity Training and Technical Assistance Package","This package of training and technical assistance services is designed to help MSMEs identify and address productivity gaps through appropriate and needs-based productivity tools and technologies.",""],[1,"150","8","Productivity-Based Incentive Scheme Design and Implementation","It also helps MSMEs design and implement productivity-based incentive schemes to ensure growth in workers' income commensurate to their productivity.",""],[1,"151","2","Startup, MSME, and Cooperative Statistics System","Regular collection and publication of relevant statistics on startups, MSMEs64, and cooperatives will be pursued.",""],[1,"151","2","MSME Financial Statistics Survey","As part of establishing comprehensive MSME financial statistics, the BSP, in partnership with the ADB, is exploring the design and conduct of the MSME survey to generate more granular data on MSME access to finance.",""],[1,"219","2","Startup and MSME Support Services Expansion","Various government support services for startups and micro, small, and medium enterprises (MSMEs) will also be ramped up to help them become more innovative and resilient in times of crisis.",""],[1,"223","9","Innovative Financing Mechanisms and Private Sector Investment Promotion","Encourage more innovative financing mechanisms and private sector investments",""],[1,"223","14","Startup and MSME Support Mechanisms in the Regions","Provide support mechanisms for startups and MSMEs in the regions",""],[1,"224","2","Innovation Hubs and Business Support Outreach","Utilize innovation hubs, business support mechanisms, state universities and colleges (SUCs), private HEIs, and LGUs to promote technologies and government support to innovation activities.",""],[1,"227","1","Startup and Innovation Financing Mechanisms","Establish and expand the funding mechanisms provided under the Philippine Innovation Act and the Innovative Startup Act.",""],[1,"227","2","Innovative Start-up Act Implementation","Fast-track the implementation of the newly enacted \"Innovative Start-up Act\" (RA 11337).",""],[1,"227","2","Philippine Startup Development Program","The Philippine Startup Development Program will be formulated to provide monetary and operational support to innovative and technology start-ups.",""],[1,"227","2","MSME Innovation Development Program","In addition, the MSME Innovation Development Program will be mobilized to enable government agencies to work hand in hand with private organizations and academic institutions to provide technical and/or financial support programs for the development training of entrepreneurs.",""],[1,"227","2","Regulatory Sandbox for Start-up Technologies","A regulatory sandbox6 approach will be used by the government for unimpeded roll out of start-up technologies.",""],[1,"227","3","MSME and Startup Innovation Support Programs","Bolster government support to MSMEs and startups to enhance their innovation activities.",""],[1,"227","3","Food Innovation Center Service Upgrading","the services of the Food Innovation Centers (FICs) will be upgraded from product prototyping or pilot scale processing into toll processing.",""],[1,"227","3","Startup Philippines Digital Support Portal","the Startup Philippines website will provide a centralized platform for news and information on government startup support programs and networking and learning opportunities, as well as a one-stop-shop for startup registration and support program applications.",""],[1,"227","4","DTI Startup and MSME Program Reconfiguration","Continue reconfiguring the Department of Trade and Industry's (DTI) lineup of programs and projects available for startups and MSMEs in response to the COVID-19 pandemic.","Department of Trade and Industry"],[1,"227","4","DTI New Normal Program and Project Reconfiguration","In response to the pandemic, DTI will reconfigure its lineup of projects and programs to make it compatible to the minimum public health standards under the new normal.","Department of Trade and Industry"],[1,"227","4","Regional Inclusive Innovation Centers Expansion","The establishment of Regional Inclusive Innovation Centers (RIICs) will be continued and replicated in other key areas around the country (e.g., Batangas City [Region 4A], Iloilo [Region 6], and Zamboanga [Region 9]).",""],[1,"227","4","Startup and MSME Capacity Building, Financing, and Matching Support","These programs include, but are not limited to, capacity- building activities for eligible and qualified startups or MSMEs affected by the pandemic, funding assistance/credit programs, and matching needs of MSMEs with startup solutions providers.",""],[1,"228","1","Online Delivery of Innovation and Business Support Services","Some services of the innovation hubs and TBIs, innovation centers, among others, will be conducted online (e.g., mentoring, training, and consultancy services), if applicable, to comply with social distancing measures.",""],[1,"228","1","Online Promotion of Innovation Support Mechanisms","Furthermore, these innovation support mechanisms will also promote their services online to entice beneficiaries.",""],[1,"228","1","Strengthening Government Online Business Support Portals","Government agencies with existing online portals on business support mechanisms will be enhanced and strengthened.",""],[1,"231","8","Startup Visa and Incentive Promotion","Promote startup visas and other benefits and incentives under the Innovative Startup Act (RA 11337).",""],[1,"231","8","National Startup Ecosystem Marketing Campaign","The government will strategically market the country's startup ecosystem to experienced startup founders, investors, and other enablers.",""],[1,"243","3","Regulatory Sandbox for Emerging Industries","it is important for the government to utilize a regulatory sandbox approach to help develop supportive regulatory frameworks for emerging industries under the new normal",""]],"37":[[1,"123","2","Access to Finance Improvement","Improve access to finance (see Chapters 9C and 15 for detailed strategies).",""],[1,"126","1","Blended Finance for Sustainable Development","Blended finance or the strategic use of development finance to mobilize additional funding for sustainable development will be tapped.",""],[1,"126","1","Gender Lens Investing Plan","For instance, blended finance that offers \"gender lens investing plan\" - encouraging investment in activities that positively affect women - will be explored and scaled-up.",""],[1,"126","1","Innovative Financing Expansion for Startups and MSMEs","Access to other types of innovative financing for startups and MSMEs, as well as cooperatives will also be expanded to enable them to operate under the new normal.",""],[1,"126","5","Emerging Markets Impact Investment Fund","The EMIIF intends to invest in funds for SMEs, or in financial intermediaries such as banks who, in turn, will lend to SMEs.",""],[1,"145","13","Access to Finance Support for Start-ups, MSMEs, and Cooperatives","Facilitate access to finance of start-ups, MSMEs, and cooperatives",""],[1,"147","4","Access to Low-Cost Financing for Competitive and Export-Oriented MSMEs","Access to low-cost financing will also be provided to competitive and export-oriented MSMEs, if merited under the CREATE/SIPP framework.",""],[1,"147","4","Blended Finance Mobilization for Social Benefit Projects","Blended finance or the strategic use of development finance to mobilize funding for projects with societal benefits but also provide financial returns to the investor, will also be tapped.",""],[1,"147","5","Fintech and Innovative Financing Development","Promote the development of fintech and innovative financing alternatives.",""],[1,"147","5","Support for Non-traditional MSME Financial Products","Other non-traditional initiatives from the private sector and startups to develop appropriate financial products and services for MSMEs and cooperatives will also be supported.",""],[1,"147","5","Startup Venture Financing Access Facilitation","Government will also facilitate access of startups to venture financing and angel",""],[1,"148","1","Movable Collateral Security System","a system for the use of movable collateral as security for loans will be put in place.",""],[1,"148","1","Credit Surety Funds Expansion","The CDA with BSP will promote the establishment of Credit Surety Funds across local governments to enable more MSMEs, particularly those hit hard by the pandemic, to gain access to finance53","CDA | BSP"],[1,"148","2","Agriculture Value Chain Financing Pilot Project","The Bangko Sentral ng Pilipinas (BSP), in partnership with the Asian Development Bank (ADB), is implementing a pilot agriculture value chain financing (AVCF) project54, which aims to demonstrate the viability of AVCF and encourage more banks to lend to the agriculture sector using this approach.","Bangko Sentral ng Pilipinas | Asian Development Bank"],[1,"148","2","Supply Chain Financing Promotion and Market Development Study","The BSP also aims to promote supply chain financing (SCF) in the banking sector as an innovative financing approach to improve access to financing of smaller enterprises.","Bangko Sentral ng Pilipinas"],[1,"148","3","Startup, MSME, and Cooperative Grants and Soft Loan Support","Extend grants and soft loans to startups, MSMEs, and cooperatives to sustain business operations.",""],[1,"148","3","MSME Loan Guarantee Fund","On top of providing a loan guarantee fund, existing government programs targeting MSMEs will continue to be implemented and monitored.",""],[1,"148","5","Personal Property Security Framework and Registry","This will be operationalized through the establishment of a unified and modern legal framework for securing obligations with personal property.","Land Registration Authority"],[1,"148","6","CSF Cooperative Registration and Supervision Unit","the Cooperative Development Authority (CDA) has created a CSF unit that will register, regulate, and regularly monitor and supervise the operations of CSF cooperatives.",""],[1,"152","8","Institutionalization of the Pondo sa Pagbabago at Pag-asenso (P3) Program","Institutionalization of the Pondo sa Pagbabago at Pag asenso (P3) Program",""],[1,"152","9","Pondo sa Pagbabago at Pag-Asenso Program Institutionalization","Institutionalizing the Pondo sa Pagbabago at Pag Asenso Program of government that aims to develop entrepreneurship and contribute to inclusive economic growth and provide accessible and reasonably-priced financing to micro entrepreneurs to help them avoid usurious rates.",""],[1,"152","16","Central Online Warehouse Receipts Registry","The proposed House Bill No. 4413 proposes to establish a central online Registry for all Warehouse Receipts, which shall be eventually integrated with other existing registries.",""]],"38":[[1,"9","3","Revised Corporation Code Business Facilitation Reform","the Revised Corporation Code of the Philippines eliminates barriers to entry of both small and large enterprises by permitting the formation of one-person corporations and by allowing stockholders or members to exercise their rights through remote communication and in-absentia voting, among others.",""],[1,"61","2","Export Diversification and Sector Support Packages","As for the external sector, it promotes sustainability and resiliency through scaled up and diversified products and markets, and targeted comprehensive packages of support for specific products and services sectors.",""],[1,"236","2","Trade Diversification and Market Expansion Initiative","Trade partnerships will be intensified, while products and markets will be diversified and scaled up to take advantage of shifts in business processes and consumer preferences under the New Normal.",""],[1,"242","11","Product and Market Diversification Initiative","Scale up and diversify products and markets",""],[1,"247","3","Trade Integration and FTA Utilization Strategy","Strategically participate in bilateral, regional, and global integration, and optimize the utilization of existing free trade agreements (FTAs).",""],[1,"247","3","Export and Market Diversification Strategy","The pandemic has also highlighted the significance of diversifying products and markets to reduce vulnerability to supply constraints and shifts in production chains.",""],[1,"247","4","Preferential Market Access Utilization Advocacy and Analytics Programme","To ensure that utilization of existing preferential market access is enhanced and facilitated, the reach of advocacy programs will be expanded through information sessions and greater use of data-driven analytics.",""],[1,"247","4","FTA Utilization Database and Assessment Tool Development","This will be complemented by the development of a database for utilization of FTA agreements and an assessment tool to identify gaps and formulate initiatives to enhance utilization.",""],[1,"247","4","FTA Compliance Monitoring Mechanism","The compliance of partner countries with their FTA commitments will be closely monitored.",""],[1,"247","4","Preferential Trade Negotiation Expansion Initiative","The government will pursue negotiations to expand or lock-in current preferential concessions, such as the review of the Philippines-Japan Economic Partnership Agreement and ASEAN+1 Free Trade Agreement.",""],[1,"247","4","Active Trade Agreement Negotiation Programme","In addition, active negotiations will be carried out with existing trading partners, such as in the proposed Regional Comprehensive Partnership Agreement, the Philippines-Korea Free Trade Agreement, the Philippines-EU Free Trade Agreement, and the proposed agreements with the USA.",""],[1,"248","1","Investment Promotion for Relocating Manufacturing Firms","The government is presenting the Philippines as a complementary host country for the production of health products, electrical equipment and appliances, metal products, automotive and auto parts, machinery and equipment, optical lenses, and furniture to firms that were either affected by the COVID-19 pandemic in China or the trade tension between China and the USA.",""],[1,"248","1","Preferential Market Access Utilization Strategy","The government will also leverage the country's preferential access to the US and EU (through the Generalized System of Preferences [GSP] scheme).",""],[1,"248","2","Economic and Technical Cooperation with Trading Partners","Enhance economic and technical cooperation with trading partners and pursue strategic partnerships with other non-traditional trading partners.",""],[1,"248","2","Dialogue Mechanisms and Trade Agreements with Non-Traditional Partners","The country will also engage non-traditional partners in Eastern Europe, Northern and Central Asia, Middle East, Latin America, and Africa through dialogue mechanisms or possible trade agreements.",""],[1,"248","3","Digital Export Promotion and Online Trade Matching","Intensify promotion of Philippine exports in digital platforms and targeted marketing efforts for international leads.",""],[1,"248","4","Trade Feedback and Market Information Platform Enhancement","DTI and DFA will likewise bolster a feedback mechanism with diplomatic posts, trade, and agricultural attaches to obtain accurate information on market access opportunities, especially in non-traditional but strategic markets, and provide market relevant and timely information in a single website.","DTI | DFA"],[1,"248","4","Philippine Trade Repository and TradeLine User-Friendliness Upgrade","Platforms such as the Philippine Trade Repository and the TradeLine will be made more user-friendly and refocused on practical content for exporters and potential buyers.",""],[1,"248","5","National Branding Strategy for Goods, Services, and Investment","Consistent national branding strategies will be utilized across goods, services, and investment sectors to ensure maximum recall and effectivity.",""],[1,"248","5","Promotion of Design-Centric and Quality-Driven Products","Design-centric and quality-driven products will be promoted in niche markets.",""],[1,"249","1","Investment Promotion Events and Outbound Missions","Participation in investment promotion events or high-level outbound missions to Korea, Japan, China, Taiwan, and the US may be timed with bilateral FTA negotiations or meetings.",""],[1,"249","4","Digital Trade Promotion and Non-Traditional Export Diversification","The digitalization of these operations will enable the Philippines to increase the reach of its products, develop product lines that respond to consumer demand, promote trade through virtual tours, discover better marketing leads, and reallocate other resources to diversify and develop non-traditional exports.",""],[1,"251","4","Exporter Support Package for Product Development, Research, Capacity Building, and Marketing","A comprehensive package of support measures related to product development, research, capacity building and marketing approaches will be provided to assist exporters in restarting operations in a calibrated manner while maintaining minimum health standards.",""],[1,"251","4","Exporter Capacity Building for Digital Trade and Online Promotion","To improve the response to product demand shifts in the long-term, capacity building programs through education and training activities for exporters shall be implemented to fully tap technology-enabled business-to-business (B2B) / e-commerce platforms and engage in trade marketing activities despite the pandemic.",""],[1,"251","6","Export Development and Marketing Coordination","The DTI under the Regional Interactive Platform for the Philippine Exporters Plus (RIPPLES Plus) and Philippine Halal Export Development and Promotion Program (PHEDPP) shall likewise continue to coordinate with other trade promotion agencies and the private sector to undertake export development and marketing activities","DTI"]],"39":[[1,"18","3","Intellectual Property Rights Protection Capacity Improvement","the Philippines needs to improve its capacity for intellectual property right protection.",""],[1,"18","3","Knowledge Ecosystem Strengthening for Health and Resilience","increasing knowledge and improving the knowledge ecosystem to improve health and building resilience should be prioritized to improve education and health outcomes.",""],[1,"19","1","National Quality Infrastructure Strengthening","Prescribing the country's National Quality Infrastructure covering standardization, metrology, testing analysis, quality management, certification, and accreditation is an important step to gain access to markets, especially global markets.",""],[1,"19","1","Decentralized Testing Laboratory Network","the testing laboratories need to be strategically dispersed across the country in order to provide MSMEs easy access to the facility.",""],[1,"117","21","National Quality Infrastructure System Development","Develop the National Quality Infrastructure (NQI) system",""],[1,"121","8","Intellectual Property Technical Support Office Network","IPOPHL, in recent years, developed a network of 100 ITSOs composed of higher education and research development institutions.",""],[1,"121","8","Intellectual Property Support for Academe, Researchers, MSMEs, and Local Inventors","This program seeks to foster creation of intellectual property (IP) in the academe and research sectors, particularly in invention and utility models, to increase the national innovative output and to push the presence of Filipino inventions in the international patent system.",""],[1,"121","8","MSME and Local Inventor Technical Assistance for IP Searches and Drafting","It is set up to also strengthen support for MSMEs as the ITSOs extend technical assistance to MSMEs and local inventors as regards trademark and patent searches as well as drafting of patents, utility models, and industrial design documents.",""],[1,"122","4","Intellectual Property Rights Enforcement","Strongly enforce intellectual property (IP) rights to encourage firm innovation.",""],[1,"125","5","Geographic Indication Policy Framework and Capacity Building","Adopt a policy framework to promote geographic indication (GI) system to boost production of local agricultural products with unique characteristics attributable to its geographic origin, human factors, or indigenous knowledge (e.g., pili nuts of Bicol, Guimaras mangoes, etc.).",""],[1,"125","8","Geographic Indication and Trademark Registration Examination","The Bureau of Trademark under the Intellectual Property Office of the Philippines (IPOPHL) is in-charge of the \"search and examination of the applications for the registration of marks, geographic indications and other marks of ownership and the issuance of the certificates of registration.\"","Intellectual Property Office of the Philippines (IPOPHL) | Bureau of Trademark"],[1,"127","2","National Quality Infrastructure Law Passage","Pursue Passage of the National Quality Infrastructure Law.",""],[1,"127","5","National Quality Infrastructure Assessment and Capacity Support","An assessment of the NQI in the Philippines and the corresponding support for institutional capacity of both government and the private sector will be pursued to ensure harmonization of domestic standards and regulations at par with global standards.",""],[1,"127","6","Cooperation Framework for NQI Institutions and Regulatory Authorities","This will include the establishment of effective cooperation amongst the NQI institutions and the national regulatory authorities, and also with their regional and international counterparts.",""],[1,"128","8","ASEAN Periodic Exchange Programmes for Capacity Building","Periodic exchange programmes among ASEAN Member States (AMS), for instance, will build national capacity and encourage these agencies to pursue a higher standard of quality awareness and consumer protection in ASEAN.",""],[1,"130","9","National Quality Infrastructure Policy","An NQI policy will raise quality consciousness of both suppliers and consumers as NQI institutions introduce, promote, and maintain a culture of safety and quality of goods produced.",""],[1,"136","6","Intellectual Property Promotion, Protection, Regulation, and Enforcement","Strengthen IP promotion, protection, regulation, and enforcement.",""],[1,"145","16","MSME Conformity Assessment Promotion","Promote the use of accredited certification, testing, inspection, verification, and calibration among MSMEs to ensure safety, reliability, and quality of their products and services",""],[1,"150","3","MSME Certification and Laboratory Services Expansion","Promote the use of accredited certification, testing, inspection, verification, and calibration among MSMEs to ensure safety, reliability, and quality of their products and services.","DOST"],[1,"223","13","Intellectual Property Rights Culture Development Initiative","· Develop a vibrant intellectual property rights culture",""],[1,"225","5","Expansion and Capacity Enhancement of Innovation and Technology Support Offices","Expand the network of Innovation and Technology Support Offices (ITSOs) and enhance and develop its capacities to do online transactions.","Intellectual Property Office of the Philippines (IPOPHL)"],[1,"225","6","Innovation Portal Development Support","The preparation of the Innovation Portal is being supported by the Global Innovation Policy Accelerator.",""],[1,"226","1","Online Service Capacity Building for ITSOs","the IPOPHL will capacitate the ITSOs to do their transactions/services online in order for them to assist clients (e.g. inventors) remotely.",""],[1,"226","2","Administrative and Registration Procedure Streamlining for Innovation","To encourage and improve innovation, the IPOPHL, in coordination with the National Innovation Council (NIC), will streamline and rationalize administrative and registration procedures.",""],[1,"226","2","MSME Intellectual Property Registration Assistance Program","It will also undertake programs to assist MSMEs in the registration of patents, layout designs, registration of trademarks, and geographical indications and other marks of ownership, industrial designs, utility models, and deposit of copyrights.",""],[1,"226","2","Digitalization of IPOPHL Services and Processes","The IPOPHL will develop and provide the necessary IT infrastructure so that bulk of its services, processes, and procedures can be done online.",""],[1,"226","2","IP Enforcement on Virtual Platforms","Under the new normal, e-commerce platforms are expected to be on the rise, thus, the IPOPHL will also strengthen IP enforcement on virtual platforms.",""],[1,"226","3","National Intellectual Property Strategy Awareness Campaigns","Hence, the IPOPHL, in coordination with the NIC, will conduct various awareness campaigns/programs to promote the NIPS.","IPOPHL | NIC"],[1,"226","3","Intellectual Property Curriculum Integration in Science and Engineering Courses","Furthermore, the IP process (e.g., from application to commercialization) will also be made part of the curriculum in science and engineering courses to increase awareness and encourage participation.",""],[1,"228","2","Online IP Training and Digital Payment Expansion","The IPOPHL will also conduct training online through webinars such as the LEAP IP Webinar Project and expand its online payment options for clients.",""],[1,"234","7","IPOPHIL Institutional Strengthening and Service Modernization","This seeks to strengthen the IPOPHIL as the lead government agency in IP.",""]],"40":[[1,"127","3","Expanded Common Service Facilities for MSMEs","Provide more dispersed access points for common service facilities including laboratories, calibration, and testing facilities for MSMEs especially in the regions (see Chapter 9C).",""],[1,"148","8","Shared Service Facilities and Fabrication Laboratories Project","Some of these programs which target micro and small enterprises are: (b) Shared Service Facilities Project/Fabrication laboratories;",""]],"41":[[1,"129","7","Temporary Export Threshold Reduction for PEZA Export-Oriented Industries","Temporarily reduce export threshold for COVID-19-affected economic zone export-oriented industries, as prescribed by the PEZA Board subject to terms and conditions as the latter may determine (RA 791639).",""],[1,"145","17","SME Integration into Global Value Chains Support","Support integration of SMEs into GVCs",""],[1,"149","3","SME Integration into Global Value Chains Support Programme","Support integration of SMEs into GVCs.",""],[1,"149","3","Exporter Capacity Building and Technical Support","Support will be provided to enhance capacities of exporters in sectors where the country has significant comparative advantage through technical support.",""],[1,"149","3","Exporting SME Market Access and Trade Facilitation Measures","The government will also scale up efforts to facilitate access of exporting SMEs to information on foreign distribution networks and foreign regulations, enhance access to business and trade finance, streamline customs procedures, further address logistics costs, and reduce tariffs (see box article 94.1, Chapters 9B and 15).",""],[1,"149","7","Low-Cost Financing and Loan Guarantees for Overseas Construction Projects","construction firms who are ready to tap global and regional opportunities will need low-cost financing or loan guarantees to undertake overseas construction projects.",""]],"42":[[1,"62","3","Security Forces Capability Strengthening","Moving forward, the government will continue to strengthen the capabilities of its security forces to ensure that the Philippine territory and sovereignty is defended.",""],[1,"62","3","Campaign Against Criminality, Illegal Drugs, Trafficking, and Violent Extremism","It also remains committed in its campaign against all forms of criminality, illegal drugs, transnational crimes, trafficking-in-persons, and violent extremism.",""],[1,"62","3","Security Sector Mobilization for Health Emergencies","During times of health emergencies, the whole of the security sector will be mobilized to adequately respond to the needs of the people, including the provision of support to sectors that bring food, basic necessities, and essential services to them.",""],[1,"271","3","Campaign Against Criminality, Drugs, Trafficking, and Violent Extremism","It also remains committed in its campaign against all forms of criminality, illegal drugs, transnational crimes, trafficking-in-persons, and violent extremism.",""],[1,"271","3","Public Order and Safety Systems Upgrade","Furthermore, the government will upgrade its systems and operations to conform to the new normal in keeping public order and safety.",""],[1,"273","7","Intensified Law Enforcement Operations","Sustain the intensified law enforcement operations, including military support to fight criminality, trafficking, and terrorism",""],[1,"273","10","Police Visibility and Professionalization Reform","Increase police visibility, professionalize the police ranks, and conduct internal cleansing in law enforcement",""],[1,"273","12","Community-Oriented Law Enforcement Partnership","Strengthen the partnership between law enforcement agencies, local peace and order institutions, and communities",""],[1,"273","13","Internal Security Enforcement Capacity Enhancement","Enhance the capability of police, coastguard, military and other law enforcers to address internal security threats",""],[1,"273","20","Crime and Emergency Response Systems Expansion","Sustain and expand systems for responding to crime and emergencies",""],[1,"274","1","Public Safety Institutions Capacity-Building Programme","The government will continue to exert efforts in building the capabilities of public safety institutions to respond to all hazards, including pandemics, that pose risks to the safety of the people.",""],[1,"274","1","Violent Extremism Prevention Interventions","This will include interventions in preventing the spread of radicalization resulting in violent extremism.",""],[1,"274","1","Public Safety Standards Improvement Measures","The following strategies will be implemented to raise the standards for public safety.",""],[1,"274","2","Police Presence Expansion and Professionalization","Increase police presence and professionalize police ranks.",""],[1,"274","2","Construction of Additional Police Stations","the government will pursue the construction of additional police stations in every community",""],[1,"274","2","Community-Based Policing Support Programs","various programs and activities, such as Pulis Nyo Po sa Barangay, Barangay Peacekeeping Action Teams, and Barangay Information Networks, will be organized and empowered as force multipliers for the PNP.",""],[1,"274","2","Community and Service-Oriented Policing System Strengthening","the Community and Service-Oriented Policing System will be strengthened",""],[1,"274","3","Revitalized Internal Cleansing Strategy","The PNP will continue its efforts in sustaining internal discipline within their ranks through the implementation of the Revitalized Internal Cleansing Strategy, with particular focus on getting rid of incompetent and corrupt police personnel.",""],[1,"274","3","Integrity Monitoring and Enforcement Group Hotline","Reporting platforms such as the Integrity Monitoring and Enforcement Group Hotline aimed at receiving complaints and information from the public about erring police officers will also be sustained.",""],[1,"274","3","Strict Disciplinary Sanctions for Corruption and Unlawful Activities","Disciplinary actions and sanctions will be strictly imposed on those involved in corruption and other unlawful activities.",""],[1,"274","4","Mandatory Police Training and Continuing Education Programme","The Philippine Public Safety College and PNP will continue to institutionalize a highly efficient, competent, credible, and professionalized corps of peace and order and public safety personnel through the conduct of mandatory courses, specialized and in-service training, and continuing quality education and training to PNP uniformed personnel.",""],[1,"274","5","Police Operational Logistics and PPE Support","the police force will be equipped with adequate logistical support for its operations and be provided with sufficient PPE.",""],[1,"274","6","Local Peace and Order Institution Strengthening","LGUs will continuously strengthen local peace and order institutions to effectively address criminality and illegal drugs within communities.",""],[1,"274","6","LGU Official Capacity Building for COVID-19 Response","To this end, the government will capacitate LGU officials, especially those at the barangay level, as force multipliers and frontliners in the fight against COVID-19.",""],[1,"274","6","Community Quarantine Protocol Development","Capacity-building interventions will include developing protocols on checkpoints and enforcement of community quarantine guidelines.",""],[1,"274","6","PNP Supply Chain Support","The PNP will support other sectors, particularly those involved in supply chains, to ensure",""],[1,"275","1","Rules of Engagement Development for Civilian Counterparts","Together with the DILG, the PNP will also develop a concise rules of engagement with their civilian counterparts.","DILG | PNP"],[1,"275","2","911 Emergency Hotline Service Expansion","The implementation of the 911 Emergency Hotline Service, which serves as the direct access of the people to the government, will be sustained.","DILG"],[1,"275","2","Telecommunicator and Responder Training Programme","Moreover, training programs for telecommunicators and responders will be provided.",""],[1,"275","3","Internet and Mobile-Based Reporting Channel Expansion","the DILG, the DOH, and other relevant security sector agencies will expand the utilization of internet and mobile-based reporting channels.","DILG | DOH"],[1,"276","5","Campaign Against Criminality and Illegal Drugs","The government remains committed to its campaign against all forms of criminality and illegal drugs.",""],[1,"276","5","Counter-Radicalization and Counter-Extremism Measures","Likewise, the government recognizes the need to address the spread of radicalization and violent extremism that leads to terrorism, transnational crimes, and other non-traditional threats that pose risks to public safety.",""],[1,"276","5","Pandemic-Responsive Law Enforcement Operations","The conduct of law enforcement operations will need to consider new challenges brought about by the current pandemic.",""],[1,"277","1","Intensified Law Enforcement Operations","Sustain the intensified law enforcement operations, including military support, to fight criminality, trafficking, and terrorism.",""],[1,"277","1","Law Enforcement Policy and Procedure Updating","This will involve updating of existing and/or developing new policies, manuals, and procedures to ensure compliance with pertinent laws and human rights standards, particularly on crime investigations including those for missing persons, case documentation and filing, and harmonization of inter-agency procedures.",""],[1,"277","1","Enhanced Coordination Between Law Enforcers and Military","Coordination between law enforcers and military, especially during conduct of operations, will also be enhanced.",""],[1,"277","2","Revision and Updating of Law Enforcement Procedures","standard procedures for law enforcement and anti-illegal drug operations will be revised and updated.","Department of Health (DOH)"],[1,"277","2","Use of Non-Lethal Weapons and Police Equipment","The PNP will also consider using non-lethal weapons and other police equipment in the conduct of police operations, delivery of public safety services, and other law enforcement functions","PNP"],[1,"277","3","Core Competency-Based Training Program for Investigators","Rollout of the Core Competency-Based Training Program for investigators will strengthen the PNP's investigative capability and contribute to the success of law enforcement operations.",""],[1,"277","3","Police Personnel Capability Enhancement","Capabilities of police personnel in case recording and tracking, case filing and arrest, operational readiness, and disaster and emergency response will also be enhanced.",""],[1,"277","3","Secure Mobile AI-Driven Policing Modernization","Moreover, the current pandemic brought the need to utilize advanced information and communications technology in the performance of PNP's mandate, such as the adoption of secured, mobile, artificial intelligence-driven, and real-time policing.",""],[1,"277","3","Criminal Justice Information System Harmonization","This will harmonize information systems and improve data sharing and coordination within the criminal justice system.",""],[1,"277","5","Crime Monitoring and Reporting Information Technology Solutions","The PNP will ensure timely and accurate crime monitoring and reporting through information technology solutions and initiatives.","PNP"],[1,"277","5","Periodic Nationwide Crime Victimization Survey","The conduct of a periodic nationwide Crime Victimization Survey will be pursued to augment administrative-based data.",""],[1,"277","5","Survey on Perception of Criminality and Law Enforcement","In addition, a survey on the perception of criminality and law enforcement will be carried out.",""],[1,"277","6","Law Enforcement Modernization and Capability Enhancement Program","Development and full implementation of the modernization programs of the PNP, AFP, Philippine Coast Guard (PCG), Bureau of Fisheries and Aquatic Resources (BFAR), and other law enforcement agencies is critical in addressing threats posed by local and transnational terrorists and criminal groups, and emerging security threats such as cybercrimes.",""]],"43":[[1,"11","3","Expanded National Integrated Protected Areas System (ENIPAS) Implementation","The Expanded National Integrated Protected Areas System or ENIPAS Act expands the coverage of the country's national protected areas (3.1 million hectares), strengthens institutional arrangements for the management of protected areas, and streamlines the process for accessing the Integrated Protected Area Fund (IPAF) for additional financial resources and economic opportunities in the sites.",""],[1,"63","1","Environmental and Natural Resources Improvement Programme","the government will continue to improve the state of the environment and natural resources.",""],[1,"314","3","Environmental Rehabilitation and Protected Area Reform Measures","For the first three years of Plan implementation, stakeholders have increasingly been participating in transformative actions toward bringing back the benefits that Filipinos enjoy from environment and natural resources while improving resilience to climate and disaster risks.",""],[1,"318","1","Natural Resource Protection, Conservation, and Rehabilitation","the government will intensify the protection, conservation, and rehabilitation of natural resources",""],[1,"318","7","Natural Resources Protection, Conservation, and Rehabilitation","Intensify protection, conservation, and rehabilitation of natural resources",""],[1,"319","2","Natural Resources Protection, Conservation, and Rehabilitation Scale-Up","demonstration effects from natural resources protection, conservation, and rehabilitation efforts will be replicated and scaled up by building on the increased multi-stakeholder involvement and existing opportunities for inter-agency convergence.",""],[1,"319","3","Ecosystem-Based Conservation and Habitat Rehabilitation","Ecosystem-based actions and area-based management will continue to be prioritized to protect terrestrial and coastal and marine ecosystems while supporting the natural and assisted rehabilitation of degraded habitats.",""],[1,"319","3","Sustainable Natural Resource Management Strengthening","Conservation and sustainable use of natural resources will also be strengthened to ensure continuous provision of essential ecosystem goods and services to optimize their contribution to the economy, food security, and overall well-being of people.",""],[1,"319","4","Forest Protection and Reforestation in Critical Watersheds","Prioritize interventions and investments to accelerate and improve forest protection and reforestation activities in critical watersheds.",""],[1,"319","4","Forest Landscape Restoration Programme","Integrated and science-based restoration approaches, such as forest landscape restoration, will be used to rehabilitate the remaining unproductive, denuded, and degraded forest areas, including critical watersheds.",""],[1,"319","4","Community-Based Forest and Watershed Management","Local government units (LGUs), private sector, and communities will, once more, be engaged for community-based forest and watershed management to ensure that the remaining natural forests and reforested areas remain intact and protected.",""],[1,"320","1","Forestland Zoning and Management Arrangements","Delineate production and protection forests.",""],[1,"320","2","NIPAS Act Implementation Optimization for Protected Area Management","Optimize the implementation of the NIPAS Act, as amended, to improve the management of terrestrial protected areas.","Department of Environment and Natural Resources (DENR)"],[1,"320","2","Regular Protected Area Management Monitoring","conduct regular monitoring of protected area management to gauge effectiveness","Department of Environment and Natural Resources (DENR)"],[1,"320","2","Biodiversity Assessment and Management System","implement a biodiversity assessment and management system starting with determining baseline conditions of habitats and species (e.g., species richness and abundance).","Department of Environment and Natural Resources (DENR)"],[1,"320","3","Inland Wetlands Conservation and Sustainable Use Program","Improve the management and sustainable use of inland wetlands and their resources.","DENR"],[1,"320","4","Sustainable Cave Management and Protection Scale-Up","Scale up sustainable management of caves and cave systems.","DENR"],[1,"320","4","Cave Ecotourism Policy and Visitor Management Framework","Policies to develop caves as ecotourism attractions and monitor/manage visitor impact, while ensuring compliance with safety and sanitation standards, will be formulated and implemented by the DENR, Department of Tourism, and LGUs.","DENR | Department of Tourism | LGUs"],[1,"320","5","Terrestrial Ecological Connectivity Research and Biodiversity Corridor Development","Conduct research on terrestrial ecological connectivity to support biodiversity corridors.",""],[1,"325","12","Sustainable Land Management Promotion","Promote sustainable land management (SLM) to arrest land degradation.",""],[1,"325","13","Integration of Sustainable Land Management Practices into Development Plans","Integrate SLM practices into national and local development plans;",""],[1,"325","14","Land Resources Planning and Management Capacity Building","Improve local capacities and skills for planning and management of land resources, and strengthen awareness and advocacy campaigns;",""],[1,"325","15","Sustainable Land Management Scale-Up Programme","Scale up and promote SLM in production landscapes and within multiple-use zones, among others.",""],[1,"330","2","Integrated Land Use Planning Institutional Mechanism","It aims to provide an institutional mechanism for integrating existing sector-specific land use laws and institutionalize land use planning as basis for the rationalization, management, and development of the country's land resources",""],[1,"330","9","Forestland Delineation for Forest Resource Conservation and Development","It intends to delineate the specific limits of forestlands for the conservation, protection, and development of the country's forest resources.",""],[1,"330","11","Sustainable Forest Management Strategy Institutionalization","It will institutionalize the development of sustainable forest management strategy enhancement of private sector participation, and forest certification, monitoring, assessment, and reporting system.",""]],"44":[[1,"7","1","Environmental Concerns Response Measures","and address environmental concerns.",""],[1,"18","6","Philippine Action Plan for Sustainable Consumption and Production","NEDA has formulated the Philippine Action Plan for Sustainable Consumption and Production which consists of a package of actions with respect to policy and regulation, research and innovation, infrastructure, and education and promotion.","NEDA"],[1,"318","14","Natural Capital Accounting and Ecosystem Services Valuation","Upscale natural capital accounting including valuation of ecosystem services in national and local planning and programming",""],[1,"318","15","Sustainable Finance Framework for Green and Climate Finance","Streamline green and climate finance through the creation of a sustainable finance framework that aims to support and accelerate the development of a green and sustainable economy",""],[1,"318","16","Sustainable Consumption and Production Implementation Acceleration","Accelerate implementation of sustainable consumption and production",""],[1,"322","5","Bioprospecting and Biotechnology Program","Develop a bioprospecting and biotechnology program to facilitate discovery and development of novel compounds and derivatives for pharmaceutical purposes.",""],[1,"328","5","Natural Capital Accounting Scale-Up","Upscale natural capital accounting (NCA) including valuation of ecosystem services in national and local planning and programming.",""],[1,"329","1","Sustainable Finance Framework and Roadmap","Streamline green and climate finance in the financial sector through the formulation of a sustainable finance framework and roadmap that will support and accelerate the development of a green and sustainable economy.",""],[1,"329","2","Philippine Action Plan for Sustainable Consumption and Production Rollout","In the remaining Plan period, the Philippine Action Plan for Sustainable Consumption and Production (PAP4SCP) will be rolled out to guide the government and stakeholders' programmatic actions in the short term (2020-2022), medium term (2022-2030), and long term (2030-2040).",""],[1,"329","2","Natural Resource Valuation and Accounting Measures","The PAP4SCP5 calls for a) the valuation of economic, social, and environmental costs and benefits of production and consumption processes by accounting the stock of natural resources and flow of ecosystem services, and (b) a set of interventions, schemes, and innovative technologies, as well as enhanced environmental education, to ensure efficient use and equitable allocation of natural resources.",""],[1,"329","2","Sustainable Consumption and Production Interventions and Environmental Education","The PAP4SCP5 calls for a) the valuation of economic, social, and environmental costs and benefits of production and consumption processes by accounting the stock of natural resources and flow of ecosystem services, and (b) a set of interventions, schemes, and innovative technologies, as well as enhanced environmental education, to ensure efficient use and equitable allocation of natural resources.",""],[1,"331","4","Green Public Procurement Strengthening","It aims to strengthen green public procurement by enhancing compliance of procuring entities in integrating green criteria in the procurement guidelines, including bidding documents and technical specifications, and in setting clear LGU involvement based on market readiness.",""]],"45":[[1,"313","5","Creation of Local Environment and Natural Resources Offices and Dedicated Solid Waste Management Units","the proposed amendments include, among others, the mandatory creation of a local environment and natural resources offices and identification of dedicated focal SWM units with corresponding organization structure, powers, and functions.",""],[1,"314","2","Environmental and Natural Resources Governance and M&E Improvement","the government will continue to improve the state of the environment and natural resources (ENR) and increase resilience of resource-dependent and vulnerable communities against the converging risks arising from natural and biological hazards under a changing climate.",""],[1,"318","1","Environmental Compliance and Safeguards Enforcement Strengthening","Law enforcement will be further strengthened to enhance compliance with environmental standards and safeguards and consequently improve environmental quality",""],[1,"318","10","Environmental Compliance Enforcement and Monitoring","Strengthen enforcement, regulation, and monitoring of environmental compliance and management interventions",""],[1,"318","13","Environmental and Natural Resources Policy Codification and Streamlining","Review, codify, and streamline existing ENR policies, rules, and regulations to improve compliance, address conflicting provisions, and promote transparency and accountability",""],[1,"323","3","Environmental Law Enforcement and Compliance Monitoring Intensification","The enforcement, regulation, and monitoring of compliance with existing environmental laws and regulations will be intensified to implement the necessary operational mechanisms to address the impact of the COVID-19 pandemic, rapid urbanization, and climate change on environmental quality.",""],[1,"328","4","Environmental Policy Review and Codification Reform","Review, codify, and streamline existing ENR policies, rules, and regulations to improve compliance, address conflicting provisions, and promote transparency and accountability.",""],[1,"328","4","Environmental Governance Institutional Review","An institutional review and assessment of the agencies' existing mandates vis-a-vis the human resources, as well as technical and financial capacity required, will be conducted.",""],[1,"330","18","Department for Climate Change and Disaster Risk Reduction and Management","It aims to provide a clear operational framework to address the fragmented institutional functions and actions among concerned agencies on climate change and disasters by establishing a Department that will serve as the primary agency responsible for leading the coordination, implementation, monitoring, and reporting on climate change and disaster risk reduction and management.",""],[1,"330","18","Environmental Impact Statement System Strengthening","This will also strengthen the use of the Environmental Impact Statement System as a planning and monitoring tool.",""],[1,"331","1","Environmental Legislation Amendment Package","Amendment of the Ecological Solid Waste Management Act, Clean Water Act, Clean Air Act, and Toxic Substances, Hazardous and Nuclear Wastes Control Act",""]],"46":[[1,"309","5","Local Government Solid Waste Management Capacity Support","Enhance technical and financial capacities of LGUs in implementing solid waste management (SWM) initiatives in compliance with the Ecological Solid Waste Management Act of 2020 (RA 9003).","Department of Environment and Natural Resources-Environmental Management Bureau | National Solid Waste Management Commission | DILG"],[1,"309","6","Local Government Unit Clustering for Solid Waste Management Facilities and Services","Facilitate clustering or pooling of resources of LGUs for common SWM facilities and services for enhanced economies of scale;",""],[1,"309","7","Innovative Financing for Local Government Solid Waste Management Programs","Explore innovative financing and improve access of LGUs to financing windows, such as those being provided by government financing institutions and through PPP arrangements, to finance SWM programs;",""],[1,"309","8","Alternative Waste-to-Energy Technology Adoption","Adopt alternative technologies, including waste-to-energy, considering institutional, legal, and technical limits;",""],[1,"310","1","Solid Waste Management Innovation and R&D Support","Support knowledge management through increased investments in SWM-related innovation and R&D of appropriate technologies;",""],[1,"310","2","National Solid Waste Management Fund Operationalization","Operationalize the National SWM Fund and study the re-institutionalization of the national government-LGU cost-sharing scheme for SWM;",""],[1,"310","3","Solid Waste Management Act Amendment","Revisit the SWM Act of 2020 and make necessary amendments towards facilitating and expediting the provision of SWM facilities.",""],[1,"318","1","Waste and Pollution Abatement Measures","Innovative waste and pollution abatement measures will also be implemented to address the increasing waste and other pollutants generated from COVID-19 response measures, among others",""],[1,"325","1","Local Solid Waste Management Plan Implementation","the LGUs will need to prioritize the (a) approval and/or implementation of their approved 10-year solid waste management plans",""],[1,"325","1","Dumpsite Closure Initiative","the LGUs will need to prioritize the (b) closure of dumpsites",""],[1,"325","1","Inter-LGU Waste Facility Clustering Partnership","the LGUs will need to prioritize the (c) clustering of waste management facilities through inter-LGUs partnership",""],[1,"325","2","Fast-Track Waste Management Measures","Fast-track the implementation of waste management measures for solid, toxic, and hazardous wastes, including electronic waste, especially at the local level through:",""],[1,"325","3","Materials Recovery Facilities Maintenance and Operational Training Programme","Engagement among solid waste management (SWM) regulators, users, service providers, and intermediaries to ensure that cities, municipalities, and barangays have fully-functional materials recovery facilities (MRFs) by conducting regular onsite maintenance and operational trainings;",""],[1,"325","4","Local Government Solid Waste Monitoring and Reporting Capacity Development","Capacity development of LGUs to implement a proper monitoring and reporting scheme on solid waste management, development of methodology for estimation of waste diversion, and strengthening the monitoring and evaluation of effectiveness of SWM programs by the National Solid Waste Management Commission (NSWMC);",""],[1,"325","5","Community-Based Composting and Compost Market Linkage","Implementation of community-based composting of food wastes and other biodegradable materials and linking households to composting market/industry for commercial viability;",""],[1,"325","6","E-Waste Management and Extended Producer Responsibility Policy","Formulation of a policy on the management and monitoring of e-wastes and institutionalization of extended producer responsibility (EPR);",""],[1,"325","7","Health Care and Infectious Waste Management Streamlining","o Streamlining the management of health care and infectious wastes, especially at the community and household levels by:",""],[1,"325","8","Healthcare Facility and Treatment Technology Compliance with Hazardous Waste Standards","Ensuring compliance of healthcare facilities2 and treatment technologies3 with the standards for hazardous waste management and handling new pathogens or viruses;",""],[1,"325","9","Treatment Storage and Disposal Facility Expansion","Modernizing and increasing the number of Treatment Storage and Disposal (TSD) facilities for handling infectious healthcare wastes.",""],[1,"325","10","Household and Barangay Healthcare Waste Disposal Improvement","Improving disposal of healthcare wastes at the household or barangay level, especially in areas with limited access and capacity to transport to TSD facilities;",""],[1,"325","11","Partnerships for Healthcare Waste Containment","Establishing partnerships between and among LGUs and TSD accredited facilities to ensure that untreated healthcare wastes do not reach MRFs and SLFs.",""],[1,"325","18","Environmental Technology Verification and Compliance Testing","New and existing technologies need to undergo Environmental Technology Verification of the DOST-Industrial Technology Development Institute and comply with the applicable environmental standards and the DOH-required level of microbial destruction or inactivation to eliminate bacteria/virus.","DOST-Industrial Technology Development Institute | DOH"],[1,"330","16","Electronic Waste Management Standards and Guidelines","It aims to institutionalize mechanisms and guidelines/standards for proper collection, handling/storage, and disposal of electronic wastes.",""],[1,"331","2","Hazardous Waste Management and Enforcement Reform","It also intends to bridge the policy gap between municipal waste management and health care waste management by streamlining protocols on the management of hazardous wastes, particularly infectious wastes, at the community and household levels.",""],[1,"331","2","Waste Segregation, Composting, and Landfill Enforcement Measures","These bills will also contain better enforcement against mixed waste collection and biodegradables in landfills and incentives for home composting as well as LGU support for at-source segregation and composting.",""],[1,"331","6","Extended Producer Responsibility for Post-Consumer Product Disposal","It aims to enhance product stewardship among producers/manufacturers nationwide, who will be made responsible for the disposal and treatment of post-consumer products and help minimize pollution, especially from packaging materials of the food and beverage sector at source.",""]],"47":[[1,"273","26","West Philippine Sea Marine Protected Area Declaration","Declare the West Philippine Sea as a marine protected area pursuant to domestic laws, and other bilateral and multilateral cooperation agreements",""],[1,"281","4","West Philippine Sea Marine Protected Areas Declaration","Declaration of some parts of the West Philippine Sea as marine protected areas (MPAs).",""],[1,"321","12","Coastal and Marine Habitat Stocktaking and Biodiversity Assessment","Complete stocktaking of coastal and marine habitats and species diversity.",""],[1,"321","13","Marine Protected Area Networking and Management Measures","Optimize the increased coverage of marine protected areas (MPAs) as a habitat of biologically and economically important species through MPA networking.",""],[1,"321","13","Marine Ecological Connectivity Studies","To scale up MPA networking, more ecological connectivity studies will be undertaken to effectively protect and conserve the entire life cycle of fish and other marine species.",""],[1,"321","14","Pilot Testing of Innovative Coastal Habitat Rehabilitation Technologies","Pilot-test existing innovative technologies for rehabilitation of coastal habitats.",""],[1,"322","1","Municipal Waters Delineation and Spatial Planning Support","Continuous support and technical assistance from the National Mapping and Resource Information Authority (NAMRIA) will be provided to LGUs to fast-track municipal water delineation, while the guidelines for delineation of municipal waters with offshore islands will be finalized by the Bureau of Fisheries and Aquatic Resources of the Department of Agriculture (DA-BFAR).","National Mapping and Resource Information Authority | Bureau of Fisheries and Aquatic Resources of the Department of Agriculture"],[1,"322","2","Multi-stakeholder Coastal and Marine Resource Management Coordination","Enhance multi-stakeholder coordination and capacity on coastal and marine resources management aligned with the country's international commitments and related sector initiatives (e.g., Coral Triangle Initiative on Coral Reefs, Fisheries, and Food Security).","DA | DENR | Department of the Interior and Local Government (DILG)"],[1,"322","4","Access and Benefit Sharing Policy Framework","The national policy framework on ABS will be finalized and adopted to enhance regulatory measures and facilitate sharing of economic benefits from the use of genetic resources and traditional knowledge.",""],[1,"322","4","Marine Scientific Research Permitting Protocol Strengthening","Permitting protocols on marine scientific research will also be strengthened.",""],[1,"322","6","Private Sector and Civil Society Biodiversity Participation Mechanism","Establish a clear mechanism for encouraging private sector investment and civil society participation in biodiversity conservation and sustainable use.","DENR"],[1,"323","2","Collective Environmental Protection Action","Government, private and business, and individuals will be enjoined to take collective and concrete actions to achieve a clean and healthy environment.",""],[1,"328","1","Sustainable Fish and Marine Industries Development","Sustainable fish- and marine-based industries4 will be developed and promoted using innovative technologies and practices and with proper sanitary and safety protocols.",""],[1,"328","1","Climate-Resilient Post-Harvest Facilities for Coastal Communities","Climate-resilient post- harvest facilities will be provided to support value-adding activities in coastal communities.",""],[1,"328","1","Operationalization of Community Fish Landing Centers","Existing community fish landing centers will be operationalized by the BFAR to cater to the needs of coastal communities for cold storage and other related support services.",""],[1,"328","1","Ocean Economy Satellite Accounts","The overall economic contribution of the blue economy will be accounted through the ocean economy satellite accounts of the Philippine Statistics Authority.","Philippine Statistics Authority"],[1,"328","2","Ecotourism and Cultural Sites Development Programme","Develop and promote ecotourism and cultural sites within ecological limits, and sanitary and safety standards.",""],[1,"330","4","Access and Benefit-Sharing Policy Framework","It aims to provide and institutionalize a policy framework on access and benefit- sharing from the utilization of genetic resources aligned with the country's commitments to the Nagoya Protocol.",""],[1,"330","6","Integrated Coastal Management National Strategy","It aims to adopt ICM as a national strategy to ensure the sustainable development of the coastal and marine environment and establish supporting mechanisms for its implementation.",""],[1,"330","12","Maritime Zone Delimitation and Management Framework","It intends to define the limits of the different maritime zones over which the country can exercise sovereignty (i.e. Territorial Sea) and sovereign rights (i.e. exclusive economic zone).",""],[1,"330","14","Archipelagic Sea Lanes Delimitation","It intends to define the limits of Archipelagic Sea Lanes.",""],[1,"331","9","Maritime Code Implementation and Enforcement","This intends to provide a Maritime Code that will implement and enforce international maritime instruments, of which the country is a state-party.",""]],"48":[[1,"129","8","Medical Waste Disposal Facility and Equipment Incentive Registration","Include the establishment of Medical Waste Disposal Facility and production of medical waste disposal equipment among the eligible and priority products/activities for registration with incentives, pursuant to DTI-DOF JMC No. 2020-02.",""],[1,"129","9","Wastewater Discharge Monitoring and Compliance Rationalization","Rationalize the strict implementation of DAO 2016-08 which provides additional parameters for monitoring and compliance for wastewater discharge, with DENR to undertake cost-benefit study on the additional environmental parameters.","DENR"],[1,"323","4","Vehicle Emission-Testing and No-Contact Apprehension Enforcement","The air quality compliance monitoring activities of the DENR will be complemented by more aggressive implementation of the vehicle emission-testing program and no-contact apprehension policy of the Department of Transportation (DOTr) and Land Transportation Office.","Department of Transportation (DOTr) | Land Transportation Office | DENR"],[1,"323","4","Airshed Attainment and Non-Attainment Area Designation and Action Plans","The DENR will also designate attainment and non-attainment areas in existing airsheds and implement necessary action plans to comply with the National Ambient Air Quality Guidelines Values.","DENR"],[1,"323","5","Air Pollution Control and Emission Regulatory System Upgrade","Upgrade air pollution control and emission regulatory systems",""],[1,"323","6","Strengthened Motor Vehicle Emissions Inspection and Compliance","the actual inspection of new imported motor vehicles will be strengthened to ensure compliance with the EURO IV Emission Limits requirement.","DENR"],[1,"323","6","National Motor Vehicle Inspection and Maintenance Program Guidelines","The DENR, DOTr, and Department of Trade and Industry will expedite the issuance of procedural guidelines on the National Motor Vehicle Inspection and Maintenance Program (NMVIMP) for public and private vehicles, and implement the public utility vehicle (PUV) modernization program.","DENR | DOTr | Department of Trade and Industry"],[1,"323","6","CORSIA Implementation for International Aviation","The Civil Aviation Authority of the Philippines, in cooperation with the International Civil Aviation Organization, will implement the Carbon Offsetting and Reduction Scheme for International Aviation (CORSIA);","Civil Aviation Authority of the Philippines"],[1,"323","7","Industrial Emission Management Program","Streamlining the stack emission testing, installation of Continuous Emission Monitoring, System (CEMS), permitting, and inspection of industries will be reinforced through the implementation of Industrial Emission Management Program (IEMP).","DENR"],[1,"323","8","Support for Local Enforcement of Environmental Ordinances","the DENR will provide support to the LGUs to strengthen the implementation of environmental local ordinances","DENR | LGUs"],[1,"324","1","Air Quality Monitoring System Modernization","Modernize air quality monitoring systems of the DENR-EMB","DENR-EMB"],[1,"324","2","Air Quality Standards and Monitoring Framework","Develop a more stringent air quality index for PM2.5, standard for regulating and :unselected: monitoring black carbon (i.e., PM1), and ambient air quality standards/guideline values for Hazardous Ambient Air Pollutants.",""],[1,"324","3","Air Quality Monitoring Station Upgrade and Maintenance Programme","Repair, upgrade, and increase the number of air quality monitoring stations and install :unselected: backup systems to ensure adequate data capture, including regular preventive maintenance to lessen equipment breakdown.",""],[1,"324","4","Digital Air Pollution Monitoring System","Develop and utilize digital, modelling, and remote sensing technologies for air pollution monitoring in partnership with the DOST.","DOST"],[1,"324","5","Local Air Pollution Control Technology Development and Use","Develop and/or utilize locally-available technologies for ambient and indoor air pollution control.",""]],"49":[[1,"124","8","National Ecolabelling Programme - Green Choice Philippines","The NELP-GCP is a voluntary, third-party ecolabelling programme that follows the guidelines set by ISO 14020 and ISO 14024.",""],[1,"128","2","Green and Sustainable Public Procurement","Prioritize procurement of environmentally-preferable products and services that are domestically produced and at par with international quality and standards.",""]],"50":[[1,"18","5","Development of New Drinking Water Sources","New sources of drinking water need to be developed.",""],[1,"18","5","Water Sector Apex Coordination Body","There is a need to create an apex body that will act as the single lead agency to oversee/coordinate overall policy and project / program implementation.",""],[1,"18","5","Water Regulatory Commission","The creation of a Water Regulatory Commission is also proposed to harmonize regulatory practices, processes, and fees in the water sector.",""],[1,"286","2","Health and Water Infrastructure Expansion","the government will have to continue and step up efforts to address: increasing demand for infrastructure, especially health and water facilities, which have been and continue to be critical in the fight against COVID-19; right-of-way issues; lack of updated and integrated infrastructure data; and regulatory environment issues.",""],[1,"286","2","Water Resources Apex Body and Economic Regulator Reform","the remainder of the reform agenda will still be pursued: creation of an apex body for water resources and an independent economic regulator for water supply and sanitation; and amendments to the National Economic and Development Authority (NEDA) Joint Venture (JV) Guidelines.",""],[1,"292","3","Safe Water Supply and Sanitation Expansion","Access to safe and adequate water supply and sanitation will be given priority with the ever increasing water demand and consumption, especially to help mitigate the spread of COVID-19 and other diseases through proper hygiene.",""],[1,"300","4","Water Supply and Sanitation Reform Agenda","Pursue water supply and sanitation (WSS) policies, plans, and programs in accordance with the key reform agenda identified in the Philippine Water Supply and Sanitation Master Plan.",""],[1,"300","5","Apex Water Resources Body Establishment","The creation of an apex body for water resources and the establishment of an independent economic regulatory body for WSS will remain as priority reforms in the sector.",""],[1,"300","5","Independent Economic Regulatory Body for WSS","The creation of an apex body for water resources and the establishment of an independent economic regulatory body for WSS will remain as priority reforms in the sector.",""],[1,"301","1","Independent Water Regulatory Body for WSS Regulation","The independent water regulatory body, on the other hand, will harmonize regulatory practices, processes, and fees, among others, to facilitate and rationalize the expansion, improvement, and efficient provision of WSS services in the country.",""],[1,"301","2","Strengthening of the National Water Resources Board","the government will also continue to push for an executive issuance that will strengthen the National Water Resources Board (NWRB) to address fragmentation in the water sector and provide the overarching framework for an integrated and coordinated policy-making, planning, and implementation of programs and projects.",""],[1,"301","3","Fast-Track Water Supply and Sanitation Infrastructure Expansion","the government will fast-track the implementation and expansion of WSS infrastructure and services",""],[1,"301","3","Water Demand Management Program","a water demand management program will likewise be implemented through: (a) conduct of intensive public education campaign on water demand management; (b) formulation of policies and strategies for efficient water supply system; and, (c) conduct of researches on water storage and collection systems",""],[1,"301","4","New Water Source Development and Surface Water Prioritization","Thus, the government will continue to support the development of new water sources and prioritization of surface water development, where feasible.",""],[1,"301","4","Groundwater Recharge Integration for Surface Water Development","Groundwater recharge system in the development of the surface water source for critical areas will be incorporated, wherever possible, in accordance with prescribed standards.",""],[1,"301","4","Water Efficiency, Conservation, and Eco-efficient Infrastructure Promotion","Measures on efficient water utilization and conservation, as well as the use of eco-efficient water infrastructure such as, but not limited to, rainwater harvesting, water reuse, proper agricultural and agronomic planning for irrigation, and other emerging technologies on WSS will continue to be promoted to avert water shortage.",""],[1,"301","5","El Niño Impact Response Roadmap Update","With the reactivation and reconstitution of the El Niño Task Force4 pursuant to Memorandum Order No. 38, s. 2019, NEDA, as overall head, will revise and update the Roadmap for Addressing the Impacts of El Niño.","NEDA | NWRB"],[1,"301","5","National Water Security Roadmap Action Facilitation","NEDA will also facilitate action on the pertinent recommendations emanating from the National Roadmap for Water Security currently being prepared by NWRB.","NEDA | NWRB"],[1,"301","5","Water Crisis Preparedness Roadmap Integration","Said roadmap will incorporate the possible impacts of future epidemics, pandemics, and climate change or variability to address the impending water crisis.",""],[1,"301","6","Common Unified Resource Allocation Framework for WSS","Adopt a common/unified framework for resource allocation for WSS and review the National Sewerage and Septage Management Program (NSSMP) to accelerate the provision of WSS services.",""],[1,"301","6","Sewerage and Septage Management Project Implementation","Likewise, in accordance with the Clean Water Act (RA 9275), sewerage and septage management projects will be implemented.",""],[1,"301","6","NSSMP Expansion or Restructuring","Given this, the government will explore the expansion or restructuring of the NSSMP, in line with principles of the common/unified framework for resource allocation for WSS to accommodate more beneficiaries other than sewerage or septage",""],[1,"302","1","NSSMP Expansion and Restructuring","Such expansion and restructuring of the NSSMP may include the review and restructuring of the cost-sharing scheme with the LGUs on the basis of absorptive capacities and performance, as well as technical assistance and revision of cost-sharing schemes in the preparation of feasibility studies.",""],[1,"312","7","Water Resources Apex Body Establishment Law","Enactment of a law creating an apex body for the water resources subsector;",""],[1,"312","8","Water Resources Subsector Coordination and Oversight Mechanism","The apex body will act as the lead agency to oversee/coordinate overall policy and project/program implementation to address the weak and fragmented institutional set-up of the water resources subsector.",""],[1,"312","10","Independent Water Supply and Sanitation Regulatory Authority","an independent economic regulator for the water supply and sanitation is envisioned to harmonize the regulatory practices, processes, fees, and standards on water supply and sanitation while addressing the overlapping functions or jurisdictions of existing regulatory entities.",""]],"51":[[1,"58","4","Sustainable Cultural Development Mechanisms","Moving forward, the government will ensure that the initial gains will be sustained to eventually establish sustainable mechanisms for cultural development from the national to local levels.",""],[1,"58","4","Whole-of-Government Cultural Awareness and Recovery Response","The Filipino spirit of bayanihan will be invoked to enable the whole-of-government and whole-of- society response and recovery from the pandemic by promoting cultural awareness and understanding, inculcating values for the common good, advancing creativity for social impact, and strengthening culture-sensitivity in governance and development.",""],[1,"75","4","National Values Formation Program","A whole-of-government and whole-of-society National Values Formation Program will be implemented by the government to address the anticipated changes in behavior and level of social trust.",""],[1,"75","4","Civil Service Values Training Harmonization","Values-related training programs for civil servants such as the Alay sa Bayan, Public Service Ethics and Accountability, and values orientation workshop will be harmonized to ensure consistency and quality of trainings.",""],[1,"75","4","Values Module Development and Survey Cross-Referencing","Development of these modules will also be cross-referenced with the results of the National Values Survey commissioned by the National Commission for Culture and the Arts to ensure that Filipino values are integrated in all levels of civil service.","National Commission for Culture and the Arts"],[1,"75","4","Public Service Values Program Revision","The Public Service Values Program will be revisited to strengthen inculcation of patriotism, integrity, excellence, and spirituality in public servants and officials (see also Chapter 7).",""],[1,"75","4","Accredited Learning Institution Engagement for Values Training","The CSC will tap accredited learning and development institutions in the conduct of these values-oriented interventions.",""],[1,"75","4","Technology-Enabled Civil Service Values Awareness Platforms","Technology-enabled platforms will be widely used to raise awareness on civil service values and norms.",""],[1,"87","2","National Values Formation Program","Under the Malasakit pillar, this Chapter invokes the Filipino spirit of bayanihan to enable the whole-of-government and whole-of-society response and recovery from the pandemic by promoting cultural awareness and understanding, inculcating values for the common good through a National Values Formation Program, advancing creativity for social impact, and strengthening culture-sensitivity in governance and development.",""],[1,"87","2","Cultural Awareness and Understanding Promotion","Under the Malasakit pillar, this Chapter invokes the Filipino spirit of bayanihan to enable the whole-of-government and whole-of-society response and recovery from the pandemic by promoting cultural awareness and understanding, inculcating values for the common good through a National Values Formation Program, advancing creativity for social impact, and strengthening culture-sensitivity in governance and development.",""],[1,"87","2","Creativity for Social Impact Initiative","Under the Malasakit pillar, this Chapter invokes the Filipino spirit of bayanihan to enable the whole-of-government and whole-of-society response and recovery from the pandemic by promoting cultural awareness and understanding, inculcating values for the common good through a National Values Formation Program, advancing creativity for social impact, and strengthening culture-sensitivity in governance and development.",""],[1,"87","2","Culture-Sensitivity in Governance and Development","Under the Malasakit pillar, this Chapter invokes the Filipino spirit of bayanihan to enable the whole-of-government and whole-of-society response and recovery from the pandemic by promoting cultural awareness and understanding, inculcating values for the common good through a National Values Formation Program, advancing creativity for social impact, and strengthening culture-sensitivity in governance and development.",""],[1,"89","6","National Values Formation Program","implementing a National Values Formation Program based on our shared values",""],[1,"89","6","Cultural Awareness and Understanding Campaign","This will be done by raising awareness and understanding of our diverse cultures",""],[1,"89","6","Filipino Creativity for Social Impact Initiative","nurturing Filipino creativity for social impact",""],[1,"89","6","Culture-Sensitivity Mainstreaming in Governance and Development","mainstreaming culture-sensitivity in governance and development",""],[1,"90","7","National Values Formation Program","Implement a whole-of-government and whole-of-society National Values Formation Program",""],[1,"91","1","National Values Formation Program","Implement a whole-of-government and whole-of-society National Values Formation Program.",""],[1,"91","2","Values Formation Partnership Initiative","Concerted action on values formation by all levels of government, in partnership with various sectors such as mainstream media, LGUs, and civil society organizations, will ensure greater societal impact.",""],[1,"91","3","Civil Service Values and Ethics Development Program","Under this Program, the Civil Service Commission through its Civil Service Institute, will work toward ensuring that public officials and civil servants not only embody Filipino core values, but exemplify the highest standards of patriotism, integrity, excellence, and spirituality to increase public trust in institutions (see Chapter 5).","Civil Service Commission"],[1,"91","4","National Values Inculcation Campaign","Values of malasakit, bayanihan, resilience and pakikipagkapwa, will likewise be emphasized through the use of various channels for values inculcation all throughout the country such as formal and informal education systems, information campaigns, and values orientation seminars, among others.",""],[1,"91","4","Volunteerism Promotion Initiative","Volunteerism across various aspects of community life will be vigorously promoted and pursued, in collaboration with LGUs.",""],[1,"91","5","Culture and Values Mainstreaming in Education Curriculum","Hence, under this Program, culture and values will be mainstreamed in the curriculum within the basic, technical-vocational, and higher education systems.",""]],"52":[[1,"9","4","Universal Access to Quality Tertiary Education Support","the Universal Access to Quality Tertiary Education Act provides free tuition in state universities and colleges, free technical and vocational education and training, tertiary- education subsidy, and student loans.",""],[1,"9","4","Philippine Qualifications Framework Recognition System","the Philippine Qualifications Framework Act reinforces and strengthens the recognition of knowledge and skills acquired outside the formal education systems through a system of pathways, equivalencies, and credit transfers.",""],[1,"9","4","Tulong Trabaho Training and Financial Aid Program","the Tulong Trabaho Act provides free training fees and additional financial aid to qualified beneficiaries enrolling in selected training programs (STPs).",""],[1,"14","3","Digital Skills Training for Displaced Workers","Assistance will also be given to the agriculture sector in the form of credit, farm inputs, and training; and skills training, particularly on digital skills, to the displaced workers.",""],[1,"15","25","Learning Continuity Program","this updated PDP contains five major programs designed to build the resilience of individuals, families, business, government, and society under the new normal: (3) learning continuity",""],[1,"16","4","Inclusive Quality Education Delivery Mechanisms","Education sector agencies will thus design inclusive mechanisms that deliver quality education.",""],[1,"16","4","Lifelong Learning and Digital Skills Training","Lifelong learning will remain a priority strategy, but especially focusing on digital skills training.",""],[1,"18","3","Knowledge Economy Development Initiative","it is important to begin developing the country's knowledge economy.",""],[1,"136","9","Implementation of the Transnational Higher Education Act","Implement provisions of the Transnational Higher Education Act (RA 11448), which allows foreign higher education institutions to establish a commercial presence or provide educational services in various modes or arrangements with local partner educational institutions.",""],[1,"153","1","K to 12 Program Implementation","Implementation of the K to 12 Program and the Universal Access to Quality Tertiary Education Law will also enable Filipinos to continuously develop their skills towards achieving their full potential as productive members of a rapidly changing society.",""],[1,"153","1","Universal Access to Quality Tertiary Education Law","Implementation of the K to 12 Program and the Universal Access to Quality Tertiary Education Law will also enable Filipinos to continuously develop their skills towards achieving their full potential as productive members of a rapidly changing society.",""],[1,"157","3","Foreign Investment and Transnational Higher Education Liberalization","The passage of the 11th Regular Foreign Investment Negative List (RFINL) and Transnational Higher Education Act (RA 1148) is expected to improve competitiveness of education and training institutions by bringing international quality standards and expertise into the country.",""],[1,"161","12","Sulong EduKalidad Reform Implementation","Aggressively implement reforms under Sulong EduKalidad",""],[1,"161","26","Student Financial Assistance Program Implementation Enhancement","Enhance the implementation of Student Financial Assistance Programs",""],[1,"161","47","Internationalization of Education Guidelines","Formulate guidelines on internationalization of education",""]],"53":[[1,"158","11","Flexible Learning Continuity Measures","As flexible learning will need be adopted to continue delivery of education services during the COVID-19 pandemic, issues of expensive, slow, and unreliable internet connection, and added expenses for devices needed to access online learning resources are major challenges.",""],[1,"158","11","Teacher Reskilling for Online Teaching","This shift will also require adjustment measures to reskill teachers on online teaching and re-orient parents and guardians towards homeschooling, distance education, and other modes of flexible learning.",""],[1,"161","16","Basic Education Learning Continuity Plan","Implement the Basic Education Learning Continuity Plan (BE-LCP)",""],[1,"161","33","Distance Learning Expansion","Intensify distance learning methods to promote learning continuity and retooling",""],[1,"161","42","Learning and Teaching Materials Modernization","Upgrade/modernize learning and teaching materials, and methods",""],[1,"172","11","Alternative Learning Modalities for Physical Distancing","other learning modalities will be carried out to maintain physical distancing.",""],[1,"173","1","Basic Education Learning Continuity Plan","Implement the Basic Education Learning Continuity Plan (BE-LCP).",""],[1,"174","4","Distance Learning Expansion for Higher Education and TVET","Intensify distance-learning methods to promote learning continuity and retooling.",""],[1,"175","3","Modernization of Learning and Teaching Materials and Methods","Modernize learning and teaching materials and methods.",""],[1,"175","3","Teacher, Parent, and Guardian Training for Flexible Learning","Training activities will be provided to teachers, parents, and guardians to enable them to adjust to flexible learning.",""],[1,"185","1","Flexible Learning System Bill and Blended Learning Support","Flexible Learning System Bill and support for blended learning systems",""],[1,"185","2","Flexible Learning Systems Funding Support","The proposed legislative measure will allow for funding to support and promote flexible learning systems in public and private schools, as well as in HEIs.",""],[1,"215","3","Early Childhood Care and Development Strengthening Program","A key strategy will be strengthening early childhood care and development programs in line with the Global Nurturing Care Framework through early stimulation and early intervention from birth to three years old to prepare them for basic education.",""],[1,"215","3","Inclusive Basic Education through the Alternative Learning System","Basic education programs will be inclusive for vulnerable groups and those not covered by formal education through the Alternative Learning System.",""],[1,"215","3","Higher Education Curriculum Update and New Program Development","Activities such as the updating of higher education curriculum and the development of new programs (e.g., data science, nanotechnology, machine learning, green/renewable energy engineering, etc.) will be initiated to increase responsiveness to the demands of the Fourth Industrial Revolution.",""],[1,"215","3","Flexible Learning Expansion and Institutionalization","The use of flexible learning options4 will be expanded and institutionalized to reach more Filipino learners and to reduce contact and COVID-19 transmission (see Chapter 10).",""],[1,"215","5","Flexible Learning Options Expansion","Flexible learning options include open distance learning, blended learning, homeschooling, television- and radio-based instruction, and satellites for off-grid areas.",""],[1,"230","6","Curriculum Updating","CHED will lead the updating of the curriculum.","CHED"],[1,"231","3","Adult Learning through Online and Blended Learning","Pursue adult learning through online, distance, and/or blended learning.",""],[1,"231","4","Health, Food, and Well-Being Education Strengthening","Strengthening formal and informal education on health, food, and well-being will also be pursued to equip Filipinos with the fundamental education and preparedness on sound practices in staying healthy and well.",""],[1,"233","1","Creativity Integration in Education","creativity will be strongly nurtured as a vital skill of students at all levels and will also be integrated into all disciplines (e.g., science and engineering courses).",""],[1,"233","1","DepEd STEM to STEAM Transformation","The transformation of the DepEd's STEM Program to science, technology, engineering, arts, and math (STEAM) will serve as a starting point (see also Chapter 7).",""],[1,"308","5","Blended Learning System for Formal Education","the DepEd has adopted the blended learning system starting SY 2021-2022, which includes online distance learning, television and radio-based instruction, and distribution of printed learning modules to students, to ensure that quality learning opportunities are made available to public school students.",""],[1,"308","5","Universal Education Internet Access Expansion","universal access to reliable and affordable internet connection for the education sector will be prioritized.",""],[1,"308","5","ICT Equipment Support for Teachers and Students","DepEd may consider providing its faculty and students access to necessary ICT equipment (both hardware and software) to enable them to access virtual classes and other online learning modules.","DepEd"],[1,"308","5","Interagency Coordination for Blended Learning Implementation","cooperation among concerned national government agencies and LGUs should be ensured for the successful implementation of the blended learning program.",""]],"54":[[1,"172","6","Sulong EduKalidad Basic Education Reform Program","Aggressively implement reforms under Sulong EduKalidad.","DepEd"],[1,"172","7","K to 12 Curriculum Review and Update","Review and update of the K to 12 curriculum in close coordination with relevant institutions towards a world-class curriculum that prepares learners for the future.",""],[1,"172","7","Futures Thinking Unit Institutionalization","A Futures Thinking Unit will be institutionalized within DepEd to foresee and make the curriculum responsive and adaptive to the needs of learners in the future.","DepEd"],[1,"173","2","Participation in International Large-Scale Assessments","Participate in international large-scale assessments (ILSAs).",""],[1,"183","16","Timely Textbook Provision and Local Publishing Support","This legislation aims to ensure timely provision and adequacy of quality textbooks in basic education without compromising the standards set by the DepEd.",""]],"55":[[1,"172","9","Teacher Upskilling and Reskilling Program","Upskilling and reskilling of teachers through a transformed professional development program that will equip teachers with 21 st century knowledge and skills and reinforce their competencies through the National Educators Academy of the Philippines Transformation",""],[1,"175","4","Graduate Scholarships and Teacher Training Programme","Promote graduate scholarships and teacher training programs.",""],[1,"178","7","Workforce Upskilling and Reskilling Programme","The government will take an active role in upskilling and reskilling its workforce through comprehensive and coordinated skills development and training programs.",""],[1,"178","7","Flexible and Blended Skills Retooling Expansion","Skills retooling programs through flexible and blended training arrangements will be expanded to build skills critical to current and emerging industry demand.",""],[1,"178","7","TESDA Online Program Expansion","For instance, courses and modules offered under the TESDA Online Program will be expanded to respond to in-demand skills in the new normal, with particular focus on ICT skills.",""],[1,"178","7","Targeted Training Modules for Priority Groups","Targeted training modules will be developed to cater to the needs of youth, displaced workers and repatriated OFWs, new entrants to the labor force, and the vulnerable sector (e.g., informal sector workers, workers in hard-hit industries, casual and gig workers).",""],[1,"178","7","Training Voucher Subsidy Scheme","To facilitate efficient and wider reach of training and retooling assistance, provision of subsidies through issuance of training vouchers to individuals, in partnership with the private sector through institution-based, enterprise-based, community-based, or online modalities is envisioned.",""],[1,"178","7","TESDA Scholarship Access Reform","Procedures for availing TESDA scholarship programs will also be revisited to improve accessibility and reduce difficulties in application requirements.",""],[1,"178","7","Mobile Training Laboratory Expansion","The Mobile Training Laboratory Program will also be expanded to better serve far-flung areas.",""],[1,"178","7","Tulong Trabaho Fund Acceleration","Implementation of the Tulong Trabaho Fund will be accelerated to help fund such interventions.",""]],"56":[[1,"122","5","Industry 4.0 Workforce Capacity Development","Enhance labor capacities to equip the future workforce to be Industry 4.0-ready.",""],[1,"122","6","National Human Resource Development Blueprint","A human resource development (HRD) strategy for the entire country will be formulated starting with priority sectors.",""],[1,"122","6","Human Capital Development and Skills Training Cooperation Roadmap","The crafting of a Human Capital Development and Skills Training Cooperation Roadmap consistent with the Philippine Inclusive Innovation Industrial Strategy (i3s) and its Inclusive Filipinnovation and Entrepreneurship Roadmap will lay a unified blueprint, incorporating various initiatives on human resource development and capacity building.",""],[1,"122","7","Innovative Talent and Digital Skills Development","Build innovative talent focusing on the acquisition of soft and hard skills with focus on science, technology, engineering, arts, and mathematics (STEAM), ICT, and digital-related competencies.",""],[1,"122","7","Remote On-the-Job Training and Apprenticeship Programs","In the immediate term, TESDA and other relevant government agencies, including LGUs, will proactively collaborate with the private sector to design remote on-the-job-training and apprenticeships programs to support the creation of digital careers.","TESDA"],[1,"122","7","Early Childhood Development and Lifelong Learning Support","For the future workforce, critical support in the early stages of childhood development through the acquisition of essential life skills and foundational abilities with a focus on lifelong learning will be prioritized.",""],[1,"136","7","Worker Reskilling and Upskilling Programme","Pursue reskilling and upskilling of workers and invest in human capital development based on the transformation of jobs, facilities, processes, and future skills needs.",""],[1,"136","7","Training Curriculum Update for Higher Value-Added Services","Update course offerings and training programs to include skills needed to cater to higher value-added services and to diversify labor skill sets to encourage specialization.",""],[1,"136","7","Skilled Trainer Availability Initiative","Skilled trainers must also be readily available to ensure the quick adaptation of the labor force to current and emerging trends.",""],[1,"136","8","Industry-Education Skills Alignment Initiative","Address mismatch in industry needs and education/skills through strengthened linkages between industry, government, and academe; review of curricula and courses offered in consultation with MSMEs and industries; and a study to address the industry needs and matching of education/skills.",""],[1,"149","8","Capacity-Building Support for Local Suppliers","Technical support can also be provided through capacity-building programs.",""],[1,"149","8","AS9100 Aerospace Quality Management Training Program","the AS9100 Training Program (Aerospace Quality Management System) will enable local auto parts and electronics suppliers to supply the technical requirements of the aerospace industry.",""],[1,"150","1","Digital Technology Adaptation Training for MSMEs and Cooperatives","The government will provide appropriate support through training programs that will help MSMEs and cooperatives adapt to new digital technologies and platforms, as relevant to their needs (see Chapter 9A).",""],[1,"161","9","Skills Development and Retooling Programme","Further advance skills development and retooling through continuing education, training, and digital learning",""],[1,"161","17","Internship, Apprenticeship, and Dual Training Expansion","Strengthen and expand internship, apprenticeship, and dual training programs",""],[1,"161","24","Joint TVET Quality Assurance Bodies","Set up joint industry and government bodies for technical and vocational education and training (TVET) quality assurance",""],[1,"161","31","Roadmap for Academic and Technical Programs","Develop a roadmap for academic and technical programs responsive to the demands of FIRE",""],[1,"161","39","Future-Ready Adult Learning Interventions","Develop future-ready adult learning interventions",""],[1,"161","44","Graduate Scholarships and Teacher Training Programme","Promote graduate scholarships and teacher training programs",""],[1,"161","46","Government-Academe-Industry Collaboration and International Partnership Initiative","Maximize government-academe-industry collaborations and international partnerships to ensure alignment of competencies and labor requirements",""],[1,"161","48","Philippine Qualifications Framework Operationalization Action Plan","Develop an action plan to operationalize the Philippine Qualifications Framework",""]],"57":[[1,"174","2","SUC Promotion System for Research and Innovation","The Commission on Higher Education (CHED) will enhance policies to establish a promotion system in state universities and colleges (SUCs) that incentivizes research and innovation;","Commission on Higher Education (CHED)"],[1,"174","2","Higher Education Quality Assurance and Accreditation Mechanism","a quality assurance mechanism (e.g., SUC levelling and granting of autonomous/deregulated status) will also be institutionalized for both private and public institutions to reward international competitiveness.",""],[1,"174","2","Support for Centers of Excellence and International Accreditation","Support will be provided to quality programs deemed centers of excellence and HEIs ready for international accreditation.",""]],"58":[[1,"174","3","Higher Education Curriculum Roadmap and Program Update","Develop a roadmap for academic and technical programs responsive to the demands of FIRe.",""],[1,"174","3","Local Training Centers and Community Colleges Establishment","Further, training centers and/or community colleges will be established at the local level to address regional human resource development requirements.",""],[1,"174","3","Graduate Employability Data Mechanism","Government agencies will also put in place mechanisms to ensure that regular data on the employability of graduates are available to guide students, educational planners, and industry.","Government agencies"]],"59":[[1,"175","2","Future-Ready Adult Learning Interventions","Develop future-ready adult learning interventions.",""],[1,"179","1","Online-Based Continuing Professional Development Platform","the Professional Regulation Commission will need to strengthen the Continuing Professional Development programs through online-based platforms.","Professional Regulation Commission"]],"60":[[1,"223","1","Technology Adoption and Innovation Acceleration","This will be done by scaling-up technology adoption and accelerating innovation to address the potential challenges ushered in by the new normal.",""],[1,"223","1","Expanded STI Applications and Investment Support","To scale-up technology adoption, STI application in the agriculture, industry, services, and health sectors, as well as investments in STI-based start-ups, enterprises and spin-offs, will be increased.",""],[1,"223","1","STI Ecosystem Collaboration and Capacity Strengthening","To accelerate innovation, the creative capacity for knowledge and technology generation, acquisition, and adoption will be enhanced, and open collaboration among actors in the STI ecosystem will be strengthened.",""],[1,"230","1","Frontier Technology Prioritization and RD&E Integration","The government, through the NIC, will identify the priority frontier technologies7 that are relevant to the country's development setting and incorporate these in the RD&E themes that will be developed by the government.","NIC"],[1,"230","1","FIRe Skills Support and Worker Retraining","The NIC will also provide support (e.g., training programs to build new skills) to those that will be adversely affected (e.g., workers) by the emergence of the FIRe.","NIC"],[1,"230","1","FIRe Curriculum Development and Approval","Accelerating curriculum development related to FIRe and its approval by the Commission on Higher Education (CHED) will also be critical.","Commission on Higher Education (CHED)"],[1,"230","1","Industry 4.0 Technology Absorption and Startup Development Programs","The DTI - Competitiveness and Innovation Group will continue the implementation of its programs related to the absorption of industry 4.0 technologies and startup development.","DTI - Competitiveness and Innovation Group"],[1,"230","2","STEM Curriculum Reform and Lifelong Learning Skills Development","Moreover, the government will implement changes to the STEM curriculum8 and include life-long learning skills development to enable workers to respond to the requirements of the FIRe.",""],[1,"230","2","Innovation Leadership Training for Government Officials","Government officials' leadership capacities for innovation will also be enhanced by conducting regular training programs / management seminars that will enable the government to lead relevant stakeholders (e.g., industries and academe) towards becoming innovative (see also Chapter 10).",""],[1,"230","4","Digital Skills Development Programs for Government Employees and Public School Teachers","Expand digital skills development programs for government employees and public school teachers.","Department of Information and Communications Technology | Department of Education | CHED | TESDA"],[1,"231","2","Digital Workforce Capacity Building Program","The Digital Workforce program of the DICT will also be launched as a capacity building program to enable the broader use of digital technologies in critical sectors such as education, finance, health, agriculture, and logistics","DICT"]],"61":[[1,"201","4","Urban Environmental Risk Safeguards","Safeguards families and communities from environmental risks and negative impacts of urbanization, with particular attention to children, women, elderly people, and persons with disability.",""],[1,"203","1","Integration of Public Health Goals in Human Settlement Design","First, public health goals in the design of human settlements will be integrated.",""],[1,"203","7","Building and Design Standards Enforcement","Enforce strict compliance with building and design standards that consider public health goals",""],[1,"203","12","Risk-Based Public Health Standards Monitoring","Strictly monitor the implementation of risk-based public health standards in housing and urban development-related activities",""],[1,"204","1","Integration of Public Health into Building and Shelter Planning Standards","public health goals will need to be considered in building and design standards as well as in shelter planning.",""],[1,"204","2","Housing Building and Design Standards Enforcement","Enforce strict compliance with building and design standards that consider public health goals.","DHSUD | POPCOM | NGAs | LGUs"],[1,"204","3","Health and Hazard Standards Integration in Land Use Planning","Specific health measures include incorporating hazard and health standards in the CLUPs and zoning ordinances.",""],[1,"204","3","Open Space and Walkability Planning for Social Distancing","Such measures are aimed at reducing infectious and communicable diseases and enhancing the well-being of the population, especially those who face additional risks due to poverty (i.e., women, children, elderly, and other marginalized groups); prioritizing more open and green spaces and better walkability that allow for social distancing in CLUPs; and exploring the inclusion of an open or public space, which may be used for isolation and/or quarantine or other similar purposes, in the design of housing and resettlement packages.",""],[1,"205","3","Urban Greening and Inclusive Community Planning","With lessons from the past two decades, the recent iteration of the NUDHF provides a more cohesive framework with emphasis on making urban spaces greener and more inclusive.",""],[1,"206","1","Risk-Based Public Health Standards Monitoring in Housing and Urban Development","Strictly monitor the implementation of risk-based public health standards in housing and urban development-related activities.","DHSUD"],[1,"207","4","Safety Standards and Health Protocols for Participatory Settlement Planning","Specifically, the DHSUD and its attached corporations will provide guidelines for the strict observance of safety standards and health protocols in the conduct of peoples' planning and other community- led/participatory approaches in human settlements development.","DHSUD | its attached corporations"],[1,"207","4","Community Capacity Building for Disaster-Related Activities","This is to aid in (a) strengthening community cohesion; (b) improving community competencies for pre- and post-health action activities, and other disaster-related activities; (c) upgrading community areas through site development and provision of infrastructure (e.g., utilities, small roads/access roads, sewage systems); and (d) capacitating community associations such as homeowners associations (HOAs), housing cooperatives, and neighborhood associations on estate management in a truly participatory and sustained manner.",""]],"62":[[1,"122","1","Comprehensive and Integrated Strategic Environmental Assessment for Public Infrastructure","Particularly for public infrastructure programs and projects, applying the Comprehensive and Integrated Strategic Environmental Assessment will be advocated.",""],[1,"122","1","Research and Development on Sustainable Construction Materials","R&D in the use of alternative sustainable materials in the construction sector will also be pursued.",""],[1,"125","4","Fast-Tracking Build Build Build Infrastructure Projects","Boost infrastructure development by fast-tracking implementation of Build Build Build projects aimed towards improving the country's healthcare system, digital and power infrastructure, among others.",""],[1,"130","13","Construction Sector Market Access Reform","This will provide a level playing field and expand opportunities to eligible and qualified domestic and foreign contractors by reducing barriers to entry of new players in the construction sector.",""],[1,"130","13","Quality and Climate-Resilient Infrastructure Investment Facilitation","This will facilitate potential investments in quality and climate-resilient infrastructures.",""],[1,"285","1","Build, Build, Build Infrastructure Program","The Build, Build, Build (BBB) Program managed to overcome several implementation challenges in the first half of Plan period, having increased infrastructure spending to more than five percent of the gross domestic product (GDP) in 2018, twice more than the average spending over the past five decades.",""],[1,"285","3","BBB Program Rollout Resumption","The resumption of rollout of activities under the BBB Program and the continuous investment in infrastructure are vital to stimulating the economy and facilitating recovery with their potential multiplier effects on creating jobs and stimulating growth.",""],[1,"285","3","Continuous Infrastructure Investment","The resumption of rollout of activities under the BBB Program and the continuous investment in infrastructure are vital to stimulating the economy and facilitating recovery with their potential multiplier effects on creating jobs and stimulating growth.",""],[1,"285","3","Strategy and Target Reassessment for the Remaining Plan Period","Accordingly, the government reassessed its strategies and targets for the remaining Plan period to ensure that these remain relevant and achievable in the face of the \"new normal\" and in pursuit of a healthy and resilient Philippines.",""],[1,"285","3","Early Interventions for Long-Term Development Goals","Even while facing constraints brought about by the pandemic, government will remain mindful of the longer-term development goals requiring early interventions.",""],[1,"290","10","Infrastructure Investment for the New Normal","Invest in necessary infrastructure under the new normal",""],[1,"290","11","Operations and Maintenance Capacity Strengthening","Strengthen technical and financial capabilities for operations and maintenance",""],[1,"290","12","Public-Private Partnerships for Infrastructure Development","Pursue PPPs in infrastructure development",""],[1,"290","13","Reform and Convergence Programs","Continue to push for reforms and convergence programs",""],[1,"290","14","Climate Change Adaptation and Disaster Resilience Measures for Infrastructure","Incorporate climate change adaption and disaster resilience measures and ensure the security of infrastructure facilities",""],[1,"290","15","Infrastructure Data Management Improvement","Improve the collection, management, and utilization of infrastructure data across all subsectors for planning, programming, and policy-making",""],[1,"291","1","Resumption of the BBB Program","the government will prioritize the continuous resumption of the BBB Program",""],[1,"291","1","Infrastructure Reprogramming for the New Normal","re-programming for the new normal",""],[1,"291","1","Strategic Infrastructure Implementation","implement strategic infrastructure for the various infrastructure subsectors",""],[1,"291","1","Asset Preservation Initiative","ensure asset preservation",""],[1,"291","1","Infrastructure Research, Development, and Monitoring Initiative","intensify infrastructure-related research and development (R&D) on technologies, including monitoring and evaluation of critical outcome indicators",""],[1,"291","2","Infrastructure Program Rollout and Monitoring","the government will thus continue to closely monitor progress and make adjustments on an annual basis or as necessary",""],[1,"291","2","Project Preparation and Implementation Support Measures","Important projects that form part of master plans and are expected to yield significant benefits in the long-term will still be pursued by starting pre-procurement activities, capacity building, social preparation, coordination among agencies and LGUs, anticipating and resolving right of way problems and other regulatory issues, which are common and recurring causes of implementation delays",""],[1,"291","2","Build, Build, Build Program Resumption","the resumption of the BBB Program is intended to put the Philippines in a good position to drive its recovery and resiliency program",""],[1,"291","3","Infrastructure Investment for Economic Recovery","Invest in necessary infrastructure under the new normal.",""],[1,"291","4","Infrastructure Development Program Review and Reprioritization","The government has an ambitious infrastructure development program in place that has undergone review and reprioritization.",""],[1,"292","1","Revision and Prioritization of the BBB Program and Infrastructure Flagship Projects","Thus, the government has carefully revisited the BBB Program and the Infrastructure Flagship Projects (IFPs) to take into account emerging priorities under the new normal and prioritize projects with high economic impact with due consideration for project readiness, implementation capacity of line agencies, job-generation potential, and interest and risk level of the private sector.",""],[1,"292","4","Public-Private Partnerships for Infrastructure Development","Pursue PPPs in infrastructure development.",""],[1,"292","5","PPP Regulatory Framework Enhancement","the government will continue to enhance the regulatory framework for PPP to address various issues and challenges and fast-track the implementation of priority projects and programs.",""],[1,"292","6","Convergence Programs and Inter-Agency Collaboration Intensification","convergence programs and inter-agency collaborations will be further intensified, such that the needed reforms that the government has initiated can be finally realized and implemented.",""],[1,"293","1","BBB Program Coordination and Budget Alignment","To smoothly carry out the BBB Program, NEDA will work closely with DBM and other member agencies of the NEDA Board Committees to strengthen the alignment and synergy among planning, programming, and budgeting.","NEDA | DBM"],[1,"293","1","Priority Program Delivery and Bottleneck Resolution","Moreover, the government will continue to champion the timely movement and completion of priority programs, activities, and projects by identifying operational issues hampering project implementation under the new normal and aiming for the early resolution of bottlenecks.",""],[1,"293","1","Infrastructure Rollout Coordination and Utility Service Provider Engagement","To minimize road disruptions in the rollout of infrastructure, the government (e.g., DWPH, DOTr, DICT, among others) will form convergence programs and agreements for coordination of planning permission and civil works, and in the process, to also work towards transparency and better coordination with utility service providers.","DWPH | DOTr | DICT"],[1,"293","2","Public Investment in Strategic Infrastructure Sectors","Public investment will be focused on transport, water resources, energy, information and communications technology (ICT), and social infrastructure, which are strategic and crucial in achieving development goals, especially in transitioning into the new normal.",""],[1,"310","4","Infrastructure Asset Management and Innovative Maintenance Programme","asset management planning and innovative maintenance strategies will be implemented to improve the infrastructure system's performance.",""],[1,"310","4","Critical Infrastructure Vulnerability and Risk Assessment","The conduct of comprehensive vulnerability and risk assessment of critical infrastructure, particularly in areas considered as COVID-19 hot spots - including buildings that may serve as isolation or treatment facilities - is deemed urgent and significant.",""],[1,"310","5","Operations and Maintenance Capacity Strengthening","Strengthen technical and financial capabilities for operations and maintenance.",""],[1,"310","5","Technical and Managerial Skills Training Facilities","Training facilities will be established for the upgrading of the technical and managerial skills of the country's workforce and building their capacity to innovate.",""],[1,"310","5","Planning Rationalization and Project Streamlining Reform","National and local level planning will be rationalized and processes will be streamlined to expedite program and project implementation.",""],[1,"310","5","Value Engineering and Value Analysis for Infrastructure Projects","To optimize the use of funds for infrastructure development, value engineering and value analysis techniques at different stages of project development will continue to be applied.",""],[1,"310","6","Regional Development Budget Rationalization","The country's regions will be developed through better rationalization of the budget allocation that takes into account the geographic location of infrastructure projects and programs.",""],[1,"310","6","Masterplan and Roadmap Preparation and Updating","This effort will be guided by masterplans and roadmaps being formulated, maintained, and updated by pertinent agencies.",""],[1,"310","7","Climate Change Adaptation and Disaster Resilience Measures","Incorporate climate change adaptation and disaster resilience measures and ensure the security of infrastructure facilities.",""],[1,"310","7","Infrastructure Security Technology Upgrades","To mitigate risks that threaten essential infrastructure services, there will be coordinated efforts to enhance the security of infrastructure facilities through the adoption of appropriate technologies, e.g., surveillance systems, satellite-based navigation systems, among others.",""],[1,"310","7","National Disaster Risk Reduction Operations Center Data Infrastructure Upgrade","Existing data infrastructure in the National Disaster Risk Reduction Management Operations Center will be upgraded.",""],[1,"310","7","Disaster Response Protocol Exercises and Stakeholder Engagement","Joint exercises in disaster response protocols and engagement of stakeholders in disaster risk reduction and climate change adaptation will be conducted with the end view of meeting international sustainability standard rating systems for construction.",""],[1,"310","7","Sustainability Incentive Programs","Sustainability incentive programs will be promoted and the comprehensive and integrated strategic environmental assessment will be undertaken.",""],[1,"311","1","Renewable Energy and Clean Technology R&D Programme","the government will pursue R&D on renewable energy and technologies to meet the growing need for clean and affordable energy",""],[1,"311","1","Waste Management Technology R&D Programme","cost-efficient technologies for the management of wastewater and solid, hazardous, and healthcare wastes to protect public health and the environment",""],[1,"311","1","Climate-Resilient Infrastructure Design R&D","climate change- and disaster-resilient infrastructure designs",""],[1,"311","1","Science-Based Data Management Methodologies","new methodologies for gathering and managing science-based data",""],[1,"311","1","Research and Development Facilities Support","the establishment of R&D facilities will be supported",""],[1,"311","2","Infrastructure Data Management and Database Development","Improve the collection, management, and utilization of infrastructure data across all subsectors for planning, programming, and policy-making.",""]],"63":[[1,"191","35","Disaster-Resilient Infrastructure Promotion","Promote disaster-resilient infrastructure",""],[1,"197","3","Disaster-Resilient Infrastructure Assessment","The Department of Public Works and Highways will conduct an assessment of the structural integrity of existing structures to ensure safety and resilience to natural hazards, particularly during earthquakes.","Department of Public Works and Highways"],[1,"197","3","Building Permit Enforcement Review","Stringent implementation of policies on the issuance of permits for buildings, especially residential, will also be assessed",""]],"64":[[1,"304","4","Implementation of Remaining Renewable Energy Policy Mechanisms","Expedite the implementation of remaining policy mechanisms under the Renewable Energy Act of 2008 (RA 9513) to further encourage RE development in the country.",""],[1,"304","4","Renewable Portfolio Standards and Green Energy Option Implementation","Policy issuances on the Renewable Portfolio Standards and the Green Energy Option will be implemented to require mandated electric power industry participants to source a certain percentage of their power mix from eligible RE sources such as biomass, geothermal, solar hydropower, ocean, and wind.",""],[1,"304","4","Renewable Energy Certificate Trading Market Establishment","Establishment of the RE market will facilitate the trading of RE Certificates.",""],[1,"304","4","Affiliated Renewable Energy Centers Expansion","Affiliated Renewable Energy Centers will continue to be established.",""],[1,"304","5","Water-Energy-Food Nexus Integration in Energy Project Design","The water-energy-food nexus will be incorporated in the design and facilitation of all the energy projects to conserve water, ensure energy security, and maximize food production.",""],[1,"304","5","Renewable Energy and Energy Storage for Agricultural Processing","Instead of competing with the water and food sectors, complementation will be targeted through the introduction of RE and energy storage technologies in farming and crop processing methods and machineries, such as, but not limited to, pump or drip irrigation, rice hulling, and milling.",""],[1,"304","7","Net Metering Pricing and Financing Review","In implementing the net metering policy,6 the government will review the current pricing methodology and financing mechanisms that will help in the adoption of Photo Voltaic (PV) in the country.",""],[1,"304","7","Renewable Energy Policy Studies","DOE will continue to conduct policy studies to accelerate the positioning of RE in the country.","DOE"],[1,"305","1","Electric Cooperative-Owned Distributed Generation Facility Program","the Electric Cooperative-owned Distributed Generation Facility Program will be implemented.",""]],"65":[[1,"133","17","Tourism and Travel Industry Recovery Initiative","Accelerate the recovery of the tourism and travel industry",""],[1,"135","5","Tourism Plan Revision and Competitiveness Enhancement","Revisit the National Tourism Development Plan 2016-2022, local tourism plans, as well as the Tourism Industry Training Plan, to ensure the development and marketing of competitive products and destinations; intensify improvement of market access, connectivity, transport, and infrastructure; and enhance tourism institutional governance and human resources in line with the new normal.",""],[1,"135","5","Tourism Health and Safety Protocol Enhancement","In particular, the enhancement of health and safety protocols in all tourism establishments will be prioritized.",""],[1,"135","5","Tourism Personnel Infectious Disease Training and Reporting System","Trainings on initial handling of possible infectious disease cases should be given to tourism personnel and a reporting system for suspected cases should be established.",""],[1,"135","6","Local Tourism Statistics System Institutionalization","Strengthen tourism data collection and management through the institutionalization of the Department of Tourism's Local Tourism Statistics System.",""],[1,"135","7","National Tourism Enterprise Accreditation Standards Amendment","Amend the National Accreditation Standards for all tourism enterprises to include additional measures related to regular sanitation, disinfection, promotion of proper hygiene, and responsible information sharing.",""],[1,"135","8","Tourism Business Continuity Planning Support","Encourage tourism businesses, especially MSMEs, to craft business continuity plans to take into account resilience to risks and health-related outbreaks, epidemics, and disasters due to natural and human induced hazards.",""],[1,"135","9","Review of Shipping Services for Maritime Tourism Program","Revisit the Maritime Industry Development Plan (MIDP) 2019-2028 Program 2 on the Development of Shipping Services for Maritime Tourism.",""],[1,"138","1","Expansion of ASEAN Mutual Recognition Arrangements Coverage for Tourism Qualifications","Intensify benchmarking and comparability of qualifications under the Philippine Qualifications Framework by expanding the coverage of the ASEAN Mutual Recognition Arrangements (MRA) for Tourism Professionals, among others.",""]],"66":[[1,"320","6","Rapid Land Tenure Appraisal and Free Patent Issuance","Complete Rapid Land Tenure Appraisal (RLTA) to identify patentable lands and facilitate issuance of free patents (i.e., residential and agricultural).",""],[1,"320","6","Land Agency and LGU Coordination for Land Titling","Partnership and coordination among land-related agencies and LGUs will be intensified and land titling processes will be streamlined.",""],[1,"320","6","Local Zoning Ordinance Adoption Support","LGUs will also be encouraged to adopt their zoning ordinances based on best-use assessment of land assets and enable implementation of their Comprehensive Land Use Plans (CLUPs).",""],[1,"320","7","Indigenous Peoples Mapping and Ancestral Domain Titling Support","Pursue the mapping of Indigenous Cultural Communities/Indigenous Peoples (ICCs/IPs) to facilitate the recognition of ancestral lands/domains.",""],[1,"320","8","FPIC Process Rationalization and Enhancement","Rationalize and enhance the free, prior, and informed consent (FPIC) process for the protection of indigenous peoples' rights and interests in their ancestral domains.","National Commission on Indigenous Peoples"]],"67":[[1,"58","2","Acceleration of Digital Government Platforms","the government will accelerate its shift to digital platforms for citizen engagement, service delivery, capacity building, and accountability and anti-corruption mechanisms.",""],[1,"64","1","Government Digital Platform Shift","the government will expedite its shift to digital platforms for citizen engagement, service delivery, capacity building, and accountability mechanisms.",""],[1,"64","3","Government Process Automation Initiatives","Initiatives to automate processes are also being implemented for transactions between government and businesses, government and citizens, and government and government",""],[1,"64","3","Public Investment Program Online Submission System","the National Economic and Development Authority (NEDA) has developed the Public Investment Program Online System for submission of programs and projects",""],[1,"66","7","Technology Mainstreaming Across Public Service Subsector Outcomes","The framework has been expanded to mainstream technology across all subsector outcomes and to improve the agility of the government to adapt to the new normal.",""],[1,"66","8","Government Process Automation for Service Delivery","the government will: (a) sustain the automation of government processes for corrupt-free, people-centered delivery of services through the full implementation of the EODB and EGSD Act",""],[1,"67","6","Whole-of-Government Service Delivery Strengthening","Strengthen whole-of-government approach in delivery of key services",""],[1,"70","1","Online Public Information and Government Services Platform","National agencies and LGUs will maximize the use of online platforms to provide timely and responsive public information including policies, advisories, statistics, and other government data.",""],[1,"71","1","E-Governance Transition and Service Delivery Reform","All of government will be engaged in streamlining policies, processes, and procedures, while ensuring interoperability to facilitate the shift towards e-governance.",""],[1,"71","2","Whole-of-Government Service Delivery Integration","Strengthen the whole-of-government approach in the delivery of key services.",""],[1,"71","2","Government Process and Systems Interoperability","A whole-of-government approach entails interoperable government processes and systems in delivering key services (e.g., provision of healthcare, access to basic social services, and utilization of the PhilSys, among others).",""],[1,"71","2","Intergovernmental Service Coordination and Automation","Coordination among the national government, LGUs, private sector, and civil society will be enhanced by automating systems and linking government services.",""],[1,"71","5","Digital Frontline Services and Contactless Transactions","Fast-track the digitalization of frontline services and contactless transactions with the government.",""],[1,"71","5","ICT Investment for Remote Government Operations","The government will invest in ICT to enable remote government operations and to strengthen and harmonize existing online platforms.",""],[1,"71","5","Digital Government Program Implementation","the DICT will also fast-track the implementation of its Digital Government Program to develop key solutions for national government agencies and LGUs that will enable them to remotely perform their mandates and implement their programs, projects, and activities.","DICT"],[1,"71","5","Government Digital Infrastructure and Tools Provision","These include providing reliable and secure connectivity, collaboration tools, videoconferencing applications, cloud platforms, cloud hosting, and digital signatures.",""],[1,"71","5","Philippine e-Government Interoperability Framework Enforcement","Moreover, the DICT will enforce the Philippine e-Government Interoperability Framework (PeGIF) which defines a common language, principles, and standards that national government agencies should adopt in designing their technology-enabled platforms to ensure cohesion of ICT systems for the whole of government.","DICT"],[1,"122","3","Public Sector Cybersecurity and Data Protection Mainstreaming","Strengthen cybersecurity and data privacy measures in the public sector and build efficient digital infrastructure (hard and soft).",""],[1,"122","3","Efficient Digital Infrastructure Investment Programme","Ramping up investment on efficient digital infrastructure and pushing for structural reforms to allow greater competition in these key sectors will also be prioritized.",""],[1,"122","8","Unified Cybersecurity Support Platform","A unified platform with which the DICT and its cybersecurity partners from the private sector may be able to assist government agencies with cybersecurity threats, attacks, and other issues.","DICT"],[1,"126","4","Government Digitalization and E-Governance Acceleration","Fast-tracking the implementation of e-governance projects, especially in terms of Government to Business (G2B) electronic services, is paramount in supporting the shift to the new normal (see Chapter 5).",""],[1,"126","4","TradeNet Full Implementation","Full implementation of TradeNet, the online platform for the Philippine National Single Window, will digitize trade processes, including online payment systems, simplifying trade (see Chapter 15).",""],[1,"126","4","Electronic Business Permits and Licensing System Implementation","The government will likewise fully implement the electronic Business Permits and Licensing System (eBPLS) project, providing LGUs across the country with software that digitizes the application of business permits and licenses.",""],[1,"126","4","Online Business Registration Fast-Tracking","The shift to online business registration for SEC, DTI, and other relevant NGAs will also be fast-tracked.","SEC | DTI"],[1,"126","4","Government Digital Platform Interoperability and Cybersecurity","Government digital platforms will consider interoperability for shared access by relevant national and local government units while ensuring appropriate cybersecurity protocols.",""],[1,"126","4","E-Payment Channel Prioritization for Government Transactions","Utilizing e-payment channels for government transactions will be prioritized.",""],[1,"136","5","TradeNet Full Implementation","Pursue the full implementation of the TradeNet to facilitate contactless trade and to expedite the processing of documents.",""],[1,"146","8","Electronic Business Process Licensing System Rollout","the Electronic Business Process Licensing System (eBPLS) is being rolled out to the LGUs nationwide.",""],[1,"307","4","Government Network (GovNet) Expansion","The physical infrastructure that will interconnect government offices via the Government Network (GovNet) can facilitate communication, address data gaps in various infrastructure subsectors, and allow better sharing and collaboration of the different units of government for coherence of initiatives.",""],[1,"307","4","ICT-Enabled Local Government Service Delivery","This aims to enable more LGUs to offer ICT-enabled government services to the public.",""],[1,"307","4","Government Cyber Resiliency and Security Measures","Alongside this are cyber resiliency and security measures for the protection of government data and infrastructure.",""]],"68":[[1,"58","2","Capacity Building for Mandanas Ruling Implementation","Local government units (LGUs) will be capacitated for the implementation of the Supreme Court ruling on the Mandanas case.",""],[1,"64","2","Local Government Capacity Building for Mandanas Case Implementation","building the capacities and preparing systems of local government units (LGUs) for the implementation of the Supreme Court ruling in the Mandanas case (General Register No. 199802, July 3, 2018);",""],[1,"64","4","Expanded Local Government Tax Revenue Sharing","The ruling significantly expands the tax base for LGUs' share in national taxes to include not only national internal revenue taxes but also customs duties and fees.",""],[1,"66","8","LGU and Stakeholder Capacity Building for Mandanas Implementation","strengthen the capacities of LGUs, civil society organizations (CSOs), and other local stakeholders to ensure readiness for the implementation of the Mandanas case ruling in the midst of other multidimensional risks",""],[1,"67","10","Local Government Unit Capacity-Building for Frontline Service Delivery","Boost capabilities of LGUs as first responders and frontline service delivery units",""],[1,"71","2","LGU Capacity Building for Devolved Service Delivery","Complementing efforts at the national level, LGU capacities on the implementation of infrastructure projects and the delivery of devolved services will also be enhanced to take advantage of the increase in their resources following the Mandanas case ruling.",""],[1,"71","2","Devolved Services Transition Roadmap and Standards Development","A communication, outreach, standards development for devolved services and roadmap to manage the transition will be formulated and implemented by the time the ruling takes effect in 2022.",""],[1,"74","1","LGU Capacity Building and Devolution Change Management","Boost capacities of LGU as first responders and frontline service delivery units.",""],[1,"74","2","Mandanas Ruling Transition Plan","The government will craft the transition plan for implementing the Supreme Court ruling in the Mandanas case, which, upon its rollout, will provide LGUs greater access to funds to implement devolved services.",""],[1,"74","2","Revision of IRA Guidelines for Development Projects","Guidelines on the use of the Internal Revenue Allotment for development projects will also be revisited to facilitate investments in community health programs and facilities.",""],[1,"74","3","LGU Capacity Development for Planning and Service Delivery","LGU capacities on forward planning, budgeting, implementing, monitoring and evaluating government projects such as infrastructure projects and the delivery of devolved services will be enhanced.","NEDA | DILG | DAP | different SUCs | the Local Government Academy (LGA)"],[1,"74","3","Inter-Agency Training and Capacity Development Support","NEDA will take on a bigger role by working with DILG, DAP, different SUCs, the Local Government Academy (LGA), and other training institutions to deliver the necessary training and other capacity development interventions.","NEDA | DILG | DAP | different SUCs | the Local Government Academy (LGA) | other training institutions"],[1,"74","3","LGU Accountability and Capacity Support Program","The DILG will also ensure that LGUs are provided with necessary capacity development to prepare them for bigger responsibilities and accountability given their increased share from the national wealth.","DILG"],[1,"75","3","Alternative Learning and Technology-Enabled Capacity Building for Local Chief Executives","Various forms of alternative learning and technology-enabled platforms in enhancing capacities and competencies of local chief executives will be explored in preparation for the increase in LGU expenditure responsibilities due to the full implementation of the Mandanas case ruling in 2022.",""],[1,"75","3","Training Program on Devolved Service Delivery and Local Governance","The DILG and LGA will work with NEDA in conducting training programs on policy, planning, programming, budgeting, implementation, and M&E of devolved services and the basic standards of service delivery.","DILG | LGA | NEDA"],[1,"243","2","LGU Devolution Transition Planning","Implement transition plans for fully devolved functions to LGUs, including capacity development and intensive public information campaign.",""],[1,"243","2","Intergovernmental Cost-Sharing Scheme for Multi-LGU Projects","Cost-sharing schemes between the national government and LGUs for projects that are local in nature but benefit multiple LGUs, will also be explored.",""],[1,"243","6","Transition Plan Development for Full Devolution","The crafting of these transition plans will be guided by the framework being developed by the Core Technical Working Group (TWG) on Full Devolution Efforts.",""]],"69":[[1,"56","7","Family Income and Expenditure Survey Implementation","The Family Income and Expenditure Survey (FIES) used to estimate poverty will be conducted in 2021 and will be done every two years thereafter.",""],[1,"67","19","National Governance Index Development and Institutionalization","At the national level, the National Economic and Development Authority (NEDA) and the Philippine Statistics Authority (PSA), with other agencies, will develop and institutionalize a National Governance Index (NGI).","National Economic and Development Authority (NEDA) | Philippine Statistics Authority (PSA)"],[1,"67","20","Sector Monitoring and Evaluation System Institutionalization","a monitoring and evaluation (M&E) system for the sector will also be institutionalized to track the accomplishments and challenges in the sector and to formulate strategies that will address bottlenecks",""],[1,"67","20","Standardized Indicator Collection and Analysis Framework","A standard way of collection, organization, and analysis of indicators will also be developed and prescribed so that indicators for each program, project, and initiative can be mined for higher-level analysis (if possible) and future planning",""],[1,"68","1","Ex-post Evaluation of Quarantine Interventions","the government will conduct ex-post evaluation of the various interventions rolled out during the imposition of the enhanced community quarantine and general community quarantine to determine lessons learned, share best practices across different agencies and LGUs, and influence future policies.",""],[1,"70","3","Report Card Survey Expansion and Harmonization","The Report Card Survey (RCS), now under the Anti-Red Tape Authority's (ARTA) purview, will be expanded and revamped to incorporate more measures of citizen satisfaction using a leaner, simpler tool.","Anti-Red Tape Authority"],[1,"70","3","Cross-Referenced Citizen Satisfaction Survey Harmonization","The RCS will be cross-referenced and, if possible, harmonized into a single survey with other existing stakeholder satisfaction surveys such as the Development Academy of the Philippines' Customer/Business/Stakeholder Satisfaction Surveys and the DILG's Citizen Satisfaction Index System.","Anti-Red Tape Authority | Development Academy of the Philippines | DILG"],[1,"71","2","Evidence-Based Service Quality Standards Initiative","To increase public satisfaction and confidence in the government, initiatives will be implemented on the use of evidence-based service quality standards, performance excellence, and best practices in citizen-centered public service delivery.",""],[1,"72","2","Community-Based Monitoring System Implementation","Implement the community-based monitoring system (CBMS).",""],[1,"73","3","Standard LGU Service Compliance Checklist","At the local level, a standard checklist will be developed containing the services that must be complied with by LGUs based on existing laws and issuances.","DILG | constitutional bodies | Congress"],[1,"79","1","Governance Indicator Monitoring Framework","The country's performance in the World Governance Indicator and World Justice Project Rule of Law (WJP-ROL) Index will continuously be monitored.",""]],"70":[[1,"65","1","Revision of Government Rules for Alternative Work and Digital Transactions","Physical distancing measures necessitate the adoption of alternative work arrangements and digital transactions, which require the revision of existing government rules and regulations.",""],[1,"67","17","Risk-Informed Human Resources Policy Integration","Integrate risk assessment and anticipatory response in HR policies, programs and systems",""],[1,"74","4","Smart Public Sector Capacity-Building and HR Modernization","The government will enable smart and resilient public sector organizations as well as develop and sustain a corps of smart and future-ready public servants by supporting capacity-building interventions and infusing technology in human resource (HR) management.",""],[1,"74","4","Government HR Process Automation and Systems Integration","The advent of the Fourth Industrial Revolution entails the automation of HR processes and the integration of HR systems that are aligned with government masterplans.",""],[1,"74","4","Bureaucracy-Wide Human Resource Management Information System","Essential to these will be the development of a bureaucracy-wide HR Management Information System, propelling a shift from transactional to strategic HR management.",""],[1,"74","5","Public Sector Innovation and Futures Thinking Capacity Building","To ensure productivity of the public sector, initiatives will focus on fostering innovation and futures thinking.",""],[1,"74","5","Design Thinking and Strategic Foresight Support for Public Sector Organizations","Public sector organizations will be assisted in applying design-thinking principles and strategic foresight tools.",""],[1,"74","5","Public Sector Knowledge Management and Interagency Collaboration Initiative","These interventions will be complemented with institutionalizing better knowledge management practices and encouraging knowledge sharing and collaboration between agencies.",""],[1,"74","5","Civil Servant Risk Management and Emergency Response Training","Online modules and training on risk management and emergency response will be developed and provided to civil servants to cope with the new normal.",""],[1,"75","1","Public Management Development Program","Initiatives will also include the provision of comprehensive and multimodal learning opportunities for public managers, high-level officials, and local chief executives through DAP's Public Management Development Program.",""],[1,"75","1","Capability Building on Innovative Leadership for Legislative Staff Program","The DAP will likewise continue its Capability Building on Innovative Leadership for Legislative Staff Program, which aims to capacitate senior executives, managers, and technical staff members of the legislative branch.",""],[1,"75","2","Reactivation of the Philippine Civil Service Academy","the Philippine Civil Service Academy (CSA) will be fully reactivated",""],[1,"75","2","Government Scholarship Policy Framework","The CSA will also formulate policies that will govern all locally- and foreign-funded scholarship programs in the government.",""],[1,"75","6","Human Resource Policy Review and Modernization","Current HR policies, programs, and systems will be reviewed and revised to ensure responsiveness to current times.",""],[1,"75","6","Flexible Work Arrangements Institutionalization","Alternative or flexible work arrangements will be institutionalized, with appropriate control and performance management mechanisms.",""],[1,"75","6","CSC HR Management System Modernization","HR management systems of the CSC will also be modernized to adapt to the transformation to digital economy.",""],[1,"75","6","Single Comprehensive HR Management Information System","This entails establishment of a single comprehensive HR management information system that will utilize digital tools for HR data analytics and support decision-making by the CSC.",""],[1,"77","12","Flexible and Alternative Working Arrangements for Public Sector Employees","This will institutionalize flexible and alternative working arrangements for employees in the public sector providing non-frontline public services.",""]],"71":[[1,"64","2","Technology-Enabled Anti-Corruption Mechanisms","tapping technologies to strengthen anti-corruption mechanisms.",""],[1,"67","14","Citizen Anti-Corruption Engagement Initiative","Engage citizens in anti-corruption drives",""],[1,"67","15","Integration of Anti-Corruption Measures into Disaster Risk Management Framework","Integrate anti-corruption measures in risk reduction and management framework for disasters and other forms of crisis",""],[1,"67","18","Monitoring and Enforcement Mechanisms for Accountability","Strengthen monitoring and enforcement mechanisms for accountability",""],[1,"76","1","Anti-Corruption Education, Prevention, and Enforcement Effort","The remaining Plan period will focus on intensified inter-agency and whole-of-society efforts in reducing corruption through education, prevention, and enforcement.",""],[1,"76","2","Citizen Anti-Corruption Engagement and Reporting Mechanism","Public awareness will be enhanced through continuous collaboration with the non-government sector (e.g., academe, media, civil society) and the use of technology-enabled platforms (e.g., social media).",""],[1,"76","2","Hotline 8888 Reporting Platform Reinforcement","To this end, the mobile and web platforms of Hotline 8888 will be reinforced, while reporting tools will be simplified.",""],[1,"76","2","Quick Response System for Corruption Reports","A quick response system will also be established to build public trust by providing simplified reporting tools in various delivery modes, channels, and platforms.",""],[1,"76","2","Agency Whistleblowing Program Strengthening","Whistleblowing programs of agencies will also be strengthened by increasing incentives and protection for whistleblowers.",""],[1,"76","3","Corruption Risk Assessment for Disaster and Crisis Preparedness and Response","The government will conduct corruption risk assessments of disaster and crisis preparedness and response.",""],[1,"76","3","Capacity Building for Internal Audit Service Units","Internal Audit Service units of government agencies will be capacitated to ensure effective control systems in the bureaucracy.",""],[1,"76","3","Integrity Safeguards for Resource Disbursement Systems","Safeguards will be installed to protect the integrity of systems and mechanisms, such as utilizing technology for the disbursement of resources.",""],[1,"76","4","Anti-Corruption and Transparency Initiatives","Previous prevention measures will be continued such as the country's commitment to the United Nations Convention against Corruption; other anti-corruption programs (e.g., Integrity Management Program); and existing transparency initiatives (e.g., Full Disclosure Policy, Transparency Seal, Citizen's Charter).",""],[1,"76","5","Anti-Corruption Law Enforcement and Case Management Automation","Anti-corruption laws and issuances will be fully enforced, especially with the enactment of the EODB and EGSD Act that penalizes civil servants found guilty of bribery.",""],[1,"76","5","Digital Complaints Filing and Corruption Case Management System","To expedite processing of cases and other administrative processes for corruption incidents and allegations, agencies will utilize technologies to automate complaints filing and evaluation, case management, and case inventory, to name a few.",""],[1,"76","5","Streamlined Administrative Investigations for Corruption Cases","Administrative investigations for corruption incidents and allegations will also be streamlined.",""]],"72":[[1,"6","11","Swift and Fair Justice Administration Reform","Pursue swift and fair administration of justice",""],[1,"6","22","People-Centered Governance and Justice Reform","The strategies aim to build the foundations for a high-trust society by ensuring a clean, efficient, and people-centered governance; guaranteeing swift and fair administration of justice; and increasing awareness of the different cultures and values across Philippine society.",""],[1,"58","3","Justice Sector Process Streamlining and Harmonization","the Plan aims to adopt a sector approach from a fragmented mode of delivering justice, thus streamlining and harmonizing processes across the different agencies in the executive and judiciary branches of the government.",""],[1,"58","3","Justice Sector Coordination and Process Improvement","Coordination and cooperation among justice sector agencies will further be strengthened and the agencies will continuously streamline and improve processes within the different pillars of the justice system.",""],[1,"78","1","Justice System Institutional, Policy, and Process Reform","the Philippine Development Plan (PDP) 2017- 2022 outlines strategies aimed at enhancing the country's civil, criminal, commercial, and administrative justice systems; and improving efficiency and accountability in the justice sector.",""],[1,"78","3","Justice Sector Coordination and Process Streamlining","It will further strengthen the coordination and cooperation among justice sector agencies, and continuously streamline and improve processes within the different pillars of the justice system.",""],[1,"80","2","Justice Sector Coordination and Program Convergence","The government will sustain current reforms being undertaken, and strengthen existing structures and systems.",""],[1,"80","2","Alternative Dispute Resolution Expansion","expanding and maximizing the use of Alternative Dispute Resolution (ADR)",""],[1,"80","7","Judicial Case Resolution Process Streamlining","Streamline processes for speedy resolution of criminal and civil cases",""],[1,"80","8","Justice Sector Coordination Strengthening","Strengthen justice sector coordination",""],[1,"84","3","Justice Sector Coordination Strengthening","Coordination within the justice sector at the national and local levels will be strengthened through the Justice Sector Coordinating Council (JSCC) and its Justice Zones.",""],[1,"84","4","Justice Sector Convergence Program","Respective justice sector agencies will implement the Justice Sector Convergence Program, under the leadership of the JSCC within the agreed strategic framework.",""],[1,"85","1","Justice Sector Participation in Inter-Agency Coordination Mechanisms","the justice sector agencies will continue to participate in other established inter-agency mechanisms at the national, regional, and local levels",""],[1,"85","2","Justice Sector Systems and Procedures Improvement","Justice sector agencies will continue to review and improve their systems and procedures, in the context of the government's quality and performance management policies, and in compliance with RA 11032.5",""],[1,"85","2","Continuity of Justice Service Delivery During Public Emergencies","Sustained administration of justice and delivery of services will be ensured amid public emergency situations.",""],[1,"85","3","Justice Sector Staffing and Resource Management Strengthening","Efforts will be undertaken to improve the staffing structure and increase the number of investigators, prosecutors, public attorneys, judges, jail and prison personnel, parole and probation officers, support, and other personnel, especially at the regional and local levels.",""],[1,"85","4","ICT-Enabled Competency Framework and Development Program","Justice sector agencies will establish sustained and ICT-enabled competency framework and development programs in accordance with civil service policies, especially for prosecution, law enforcement, court, legal service, frontline, management, and vital support personnel.",""],[1,"85","4","Harmonized Justice Sector Capacity Building and Legal Education","Specialized trainings and other capacity building activities will be harmonized among justice sector agencies to align with their functional mandates and competencies.",""],[1,"85","4","Mandatory Continuing Legal Education Harmonization","For the lawyers, these will be harmonized with their mandatory continuing legal education.",""],[1,"85","5","Sector Coordination and Infrastructure Management Improvement","Coordination within the sector and with infrastructure oversight and land management agencies will be improved specifically on planning, development, funding, project implementation, and maintenance of agency infrastructure.",""],[1,"85","7","Justice Sector Multi-Sectoral Coordination and Public Information Mechanism","Justice sector agencies will continue to participate in multi-sectoral mechanisms such as established committees, councils, and engagements with civil society organizations, for purposes of planning and policy development.",""],[1,"86","1","Governance Measurement and Crime Victimization Surveys","The National Economic and Development Authority and the Philippine Statistics Authority will develop and implement governance measurement and crime victimization surveys, incorporating national and local surveys to engage the citizens in measuring the performance of the justice system.","The National Economic and Development Authority | the Philippine Statistics Authority"]],"73":[[1,"58","3","Justice Sector Digital Platform Expansion","The COVID-19 pandemic emphasized the need for justice sector agencies to maximize the use of digital platforms in ensuring swift, fair, and humane administration of justice amidst such disruptions.",""],[1,"78","3","Digital Justice Administration Platform Expansion","the government will maximize the use of digital platforms to ensure swift, fair, and humane administration of justice.",""],[1,"78","4","ICT-Enabled Justice Sector Access and Procedures","With the onset of the COVID-19 pandemic, justice sector agencies will increasingly rely on ICT to facilitate access to justice particularly on the conduct of judicial and investigation procedures.",""],[1,"80","2","ICT-Enabled Justice Process Modernization","pursuing ICT-enabled systems to streamline or harmonize processes and facilitate information sharing",""],[1,"80","5","ICT-Enabled Justice Process Streamlining","Criminal, civil, and economic justice processes ICT-enabled and streamlined",""],[1,"81","1","Justice Sector ICT-Enabled Case Resolution Systems","The justice sector agencies will maximize the use of available technologies for the speedy resolution of criminal and civil cases, and community and economic disputes.",""],[1,"81","1","Expanded ICT-Enabled Investigation, Prosecution, and Adjudication Systems","The use of ICT-enabled systems will be expanded for investigation, prosecution, and adjudication, harmonization of procedures, and improving evidence management.",""],[1,"81","2","Criminal Investigation Process Streamlining Reform","These include legislation being proposed by the Department of Justice to streamline the criminal investigation processes among prosecutors and law enforcers, as well as improvements in existing Court rules and procedures on criminal investigation and better coordination with the Supreme Court (SC).","Department of Justice | Supreme Court (SC)"],[1,"81","3","Justice Sector Policy and Specialized Procedure Strengthening","As such, the government will establish and/or improve appropriate policies, interventions, coordination, and specialized procedures.",""],[1,"82","1","Judicial Procedure and E-Courts Modernization","The SC will sustain the review and enhancement of judicial rules and procedures including the continuous trial system, and ICT-enabled systems such as teleconferencing and the e-Courts system.",""],[1,"82","1","Amendment of Evidence and Civil Procedure Rules","New amendments to the Rules on Evidence and Rules on Civil Procedure will also be implemented.",""],[1,"82","1","Online Court Filing and Electronic Testimony Institutionalization","Initiatives on online filing of cases, petition for bail, and electronic testimony will also be institutionalized.",""],[1,"86","4","ICT-Enabled Justice Process Streamlining","Criminal, civil, and economic justice processes ICT-enabled and streamlined",""],[1,"86","6","Prosecutorial Role and Criminal Case Filing Reform","Redefine the role of prosecutors in relation to case buildup by law enforcers and preliminary investigation in relation to the courts; and increase the threshold for filing criminal cases in court.",""]],"74":[[1,"17","1","Review of Comprehensive Land Use and Local Development Plans","All these underscore a need to review the different comprehensive land use plans and local development plans.",""],[1,"18","4","National Land Use Framework","A national land use framework needs to be established to define the indicative priorities for land utilization and allocation across residential, infrastructure, agricultural, and protective uses.",""],[1,"18","4","Land Use Monitoring and Policy Guidance Mechanism","The framework will also guide efforts, monitor developments related to land use, and evolve policies, regulations, and directions of land use planning processes.",""],[1,"35","1","National Spatial Strategy","The Philippine Development Plan (PDP) 2017-2022 incorporates a national spatial strategy (NSS) that sets the direction of the physical development of the country.",""],[1,"35","3","Regional Agglomeration Support Strategy","Strategies will thus aim to expand and improve social services, fast-track investments in transportation infrastructure, and promote \"smart city\" principles in urban development.",""],[1,"36","2","National Spatial Strategy Implementation","the government will continue to pursue the NSS to promote inclusive and sustainable growth",""],[1,"44","1","Strategic Solutions for Regional Growth Centers","This guides the identification and development of strategic solutions such as the location of transportation linkages, high- quality urban services, as well as social development programs to improve the quality of life of Filipinos.",""],[1,"44","2","National Spatial Strategy Coordination and Planning Framework","Implementing the NSS requires cooperation across national and local governments to ensure coherence of development plans and efforts.",""],[1,"44","5","New Clark City Major Business District Development","Notable of these is the New Clark City in Region III, which is proposed to be a major business district with complete facilities for offices, housing, and sports and leisure.",""],[1,"44","5","National Government Administrative Center Establishment","EO 119 dated 17 November 2020 mandated the establishment of the national government administrative center in Capas, Tarlac to serve as an integrated government",""],[1,"45","3","Metro Davao Development Authority Institutionalization","Furthermore, the institutionalization of the Metro Davao Development Authority will strengthen coordination among the component cities and municipalities in the planning, implementation and monitoring of priority projects.",""],[1,"46","1","Regional Agglomeration and Connectivity Strategy","Considering the network of settlements listed below, the PDP 2017-2022 will continue to pursue regional agglomeration, connectivity, and vulnerability reduction.",""],[1,"48","11","Integrated Urban Planning and Master Plan Implementation","To this end, master plans have been formulated to address urban inefficiencies and guide sustainable urban development.",""],[1,"48","12","City Master Plan Formulation for Sustainable Infrastructure Development","Other master plans are now being formulated for 11 cities which will guide the preparation and implementation of programs and projects for sustainable infrastructure development (see Chapter 19).",""],[1,"53","3","Agri-industrial Area Siting and Development","These will inform more detailed planning and analysis of BP2 interventions such as the possible locations of agri-industrial areas, housing projects and infrastructure facilities that will address the immediate needs of communities, the connectivity among urban centers and production centers and other critical spatial functions that will determine comparative advantages of specific areas.",""],[1,"53","3","Housing Projects and Infrastructure Facilities","These will inform more detailed planning and analysis of BP2 interventions such as the possible locations of agri-industrial areas, housing projects and infrastructure facilities that will address the immediate needs of communities, the connectivity among urban centers and production centers and other critical spatial functions that will determine comparative advantages of specific areas.",""],[1,"77","9","Policy Coherence and Plan-to-Investment Translation Mechanism","This will strengthen horizontal and vertical coherence of policies, plans, and programs among agencies and across administrative units, as well as the functional translation of plans into investment programs, budget, and implementation.",""]],"75":[[1,"11","2","Free Internet in Public Places Act","The Free Internet in Public Places Act aims to provide free, secure and reliable internet service in public places across the country.",""],[1,"11","2","National Broadband Infrastructure Investment","the National Broadband Plan (NBP) was approved in 2017, which called for the government to also initiate investments in broadband infrastructure to complement private sector efforts in the delivery of universal, fast, reliable broadband internet services towards a digital economy.",""],[1,"16","5","National Broadband Plan Implementation","Government will accelerate its digital transformation agenda, beginning with the implementation of the National Broadband Plan",""],[1,"16","5","Free Wi-Fi Program","Government will accelerate its digital transformation agenda, beginning with the implementation of the National Broadband Plan and the Free Wi-Fi program",""],[1,"50","3","Telecommunications and Innovation Investment for Lagging Areas","investments in telecommunications, technology, and innovation will ensure that even lagging or conflict-affected areas will have access to services and employment opportunities",""],[1,"51","3","ICT Infrastructure Investment Expansion","Increase investment in ICT infrastructure.",""],[1,"130","11","Digital Economy Infrastructure and Regulatory Reform","This will require enhancing the foundation of the digital economy through greater investment in ICT infrastructure and connectivity and setting up a sound regulatory environment that promotes digital adoption.",""],[1,"132","4","Enhanced Broadband Connectivity","Consequently, enhanced broadband connectivity will be needed to respond to the increased demand.",""],[1,"136","2","Digital Skills and ICT Infrastructure Expansion","Improve digital skills, ICT infrastructure, and digital connectivity to ensure reliable and affordable broadband and internet services.",""],[1,"145","19","Broadband Access and Affordability Improvement for MSMEs","Improve access, quality, speed, and affordability of broadband communications technology for MSMEs",""],[1,"150","4","Broadband Communications Improvement for MSMEs","Improve access, quality, speed, and affordability of broadband communications technology for MSMEs.",""],[1,"292","3","Digital Infrastructure and Broadband Expansion","The changing patterns in the way people work and do business provide an impetus for the government to fast-track its efforts in shifting into the digital economy and contactless society, which require enhancing the country's digital infrastructure and broadband internet.",""],[1,"307","1","Digital Connectivity and Infrastructure Expansion","Digital infrastructure will need to be provided to address the digital divide that has been heightened due to the pandemic.",""],[1,"307","1","Digital Transformation Policy Reforms","Policy reforms will also be introduced to facilitate digital transformation.",""],[1,"307","2","Digital Connectivity Program Fast-Tracking","Fast-track the government's digital connectivity program.",""],[1,"307","2","Digital Infrastructure Investment Review","Investments in digital infrastructure will need to be reviewed to support current demand for broadband internet access to enable telecommuting (work from home set-up), distance learning, telehealth, business for micro, small, and medium enterprises, online financial services, and as support to the Balik Probinsya, Bagong Pag-asa Program.",""],[1,"307","3","Digital Connectivity Program Acceleration","The digital connectivity program, which encompasses the National Broadband Program and the Free WiFi in Public Places Program, will be prioritized and fast-tracked to accelerate the deployment of the needed digital infrastructure that can serve the government, businesses and industries, and the public, especially those in the countryside.",""],[1,"307","5","Public Broadband and Free WiFi Expansion","the broadband connection will also be provided to public segments of the country including public hospitals, rural health units, public schools, state universities and colleges, and other public places.",""],[1,"307","6","ICT Policy Reform for Digital Connectivity","Pursue ICT policy reforms to support the digital connectivity agenda.",""],[1,"307","6","ICT Sector Policy Interventions","the government will need to pursue the necessary policy reforms and interventions in the ICT sector.",""],[1,"307","7","Open Access Broadband Network Policy","The open access policy removes barriers to the entry of multiple, competing, and independent players in various layers of the broadband network.",""],[1,"307","8","Broadband Permit Streamlining and Harmonization","Streamlining and harmonizing broadband-related permits, fees, and processes will hasten the rollout of broadband infrastructure.",""],[1,"308","1","ICT Infrastructure Sharing for Broadband Rollout","Infrastructure sharing encourages the shared use of passive ICT infrastructure to reduce the associated costs in the broadband rollout.",""],[1,"313","1","Open Access in Data Transmission Enactment","Enactment of the Open Access in Data Transmission",""],[1,"313","2","Open Access Data Transmission Reform","This aims to lower the barriers to entry and allow participation of more diverse set of providers to compete in the various segments of the data transmission industry.",""]],"76":[[1,"10","1","Universal Health Care Reform Package","The Universal Health Care Act aims to provide health care coverage to all Filipinos, when and where needed, without having to bear huge financial burden.",""],[1,"10","1","Network-Based Health Care Provision Reform","Among others, it replaces the fragmented system of health care provision with a network approach.",""],[1,"15","25","Health System Improvement Program","this updated PDP contains five major programs designed to build the resilience of individuals, families, business, government, and society under the new normal: (1) health system improvement",""],[1,"15","27","Universal Health Care Reform","The Universal Health Care Act provides a comprehensive framework for health system improvement.",""],[1,"16","1","Medium-Term Health Care Improvement Investment Program","there needs to be a careful assessment of the current state of health care promotion and provision in the country, and a plan and investment program over the medium term on how to improve it to become better prepared for any future health crisis",""],[1,"166","4","Universal Health Care Act Implementation","The passage of UHC Act will ensure that every Filipino has immediate eligibility and access to preventive, promotive, curative, rehabilitative, and palliative care for medical, dental, emergency, and mental health services.",""],[1,"166","4","Hospital Public Health Unit Requirement","Moreover, the DOH will require all hospitals to establish a public health unit that will provide navigation support to the patients within the health facility; support the national health public programs' implementation; and institutionalize coordination mechanism with the primary care provider networks.","DOH"],[1,"168","3","Additional Funding for Universal Health Care Implementation","provide additional resources to sustain the implementation of the UHC Act",""],[1,"168","3","Integrated Health Financing Complementation Framework","promote complementation of health financing among national government, local government, development partners, and other stakeholders (e.g., private insurance, health maintenance organizations)",""],[1,"168","3","Progressive PhilHealth Premium Increase and Benefit Expansion","progressively increase the PhilHealth premium contribution with corresponding increase in benefits and improvement in premium payment protocols",""],[1,"168","3","High-Impact Nutrition and Health Resource Allocation","focus on financial resources for nutrition and health with high impact interventions",""],[1,"168","3","Nutrition and Health Sector Recovery Funding","ensure funding for nutrition and health sector recovery activities and programs, especially at the local/community level",""],[1,"168","3","Health Emergency Contingency Budget Revision","the Implementing Rules and Regulations (IRR) of the National Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Council Act will be revisited to ensure higher contingency budget for the management of health-related emergencies",""],[1,"168","4","Sin Tax and Excise Tax Expansion","Sin tax or excise tax levied on goods deemed harmful to society and individuals will be implemented continuously to curb the practice or, at least, augment funding for health interventions under the UHC Act.",""],[1,"168","4","Higher Excise Taxes on Alcohol, Tobacco, and Nicotine Products","In this regard, increased tax on alcohol products, heated tobacco products (HTP), and Electronic Nicotine Delivery Systems, which include electronic cigarettes or vapor products, will be pursued, along with continued imposition of excise tax on sweetened beverages and tobacco products.",""],[1,"168","5","Universal Health Insurance Coverage Expansion","Expand health insurance coverage and improve nutrition and health packages.",""],[1,"169","1","Provider Payment Mechanism Enhancement","PhilHealth will enhance provider payment mechanisms to ensure cost-effective quality health care services.",""],[1,"169","1","Hospital Claims Processing and Reimbursement Acceleration","the processing and reimbursement of hospital claims will be monitored and fast-tracked.",""],[1,"170","3","Local Health System Integration under the UHC Act","under the UHC, all local health systems will be integrated into the province-wide health system to be composed of municipal and component city health systems; and citywide health systems to refer to highly urbanized city-, and independent component city- wide health systems.","DOH | DILG"],[1,"170","3","Special Health Fund Creation","a \"Special Health Fund\" will be created to pool and manage health resources, including income from PhilHealth and province-wide and city-wide health systems.",""]],"77":[[1,"14","3","Health System Capacity Strengthening for Pandemic Response","Bayanihan 2 will sustain the efforts to improve health system capacity, particularly on contact tracing, testing and isolation protocols.",""],[1,"19","1","Personal Protective Equipment Ecosystem Development","Currently, the need is to develop the personal protective equipment (PPE) ecosystem to afford the country's health care system a reasonable level of security over the supply of PPEs.",""],[1,"52","4","Disease Outbreak and Pandemic Preparedness Capacity Building","Build capacities to mitigate and respond to disease outbreaks and pandemics.",""],[1,"52","4","Provision of Equipment and Medical Supplies for Disaster Agencies","Disaster management agencies such as the Office of Civil Defense and LGUs will be adequately provided with equipment and medical supplies; and evacuation centers and quarantine facilities that will be designed and constructed to meet the varying requirements of such hazard events.",""],[1,"60","4","COVID-19 Mitigation Programs","the government will implement programs that will mitigate the pandemic's long and short term effects while continuing to address persistent issues on malnutrition, access to health services, and quality of graduates for employment.",""],[1,"61","1","Health and Resilience Technology Rollout","Moving forward, the government will focus the sector's efforts towards health and resiliency.",""],[1,"72","3","National and Local Pandemic Preparedness and Response Frameworks","Formulate and enforce national and local preparedness and response frameworks for disease outbreaks and pandemics.",""],[1,"153","3","Human Capital Strengthening Strategy","Efforts will focus on strengthening strategies that transform the country's human capital towards greater agility, for a healthy and resilient Philippines.",""],[1,"156","5","Telemedicine Expansion","Moving forward, the sector will expand its use of innovative delivery mechanisms, such as telemedicine, enhance outreach programs by improving the capacity of target beneficiaries for home-based care and use of other media to deliver information, education and communication services on proper nutrition and health.",""],[1,"156","5","Home-Based Care Outreach Programmes","Moving forward, the sector will expand its use of innovative delivery mechanisms, such as telemedicine, enhance outreach programs by improving the capacity of target beneficiaries for home-based care and use of other media to deliver information, education and communication services on proper nutrition and health.",""],[1,"156","5","Health and Nutrition Information, Education and Communication Services","Moving forward, the sector will expand its use of innovative delivery mechanisms, such as telemedicine, enhance outreach programs by improving the capacity of target beneficiaries for home-based care and use of other media to deliver information, education and communication services on proper nutrition and health.",""],[1,"156","5","Efficient Health Spending and Financing for Key Health Laws","Moreover, amid competing demands for resources, it is also important to ensure efficient spending and to secure enough funds for the full implementation of key legislations such as the Universal Health Care (UHC) Act and the Kalusugan at Nutrisyon ng Mag- Nanay Act.",""],[1,"161","19","Health Facility Upgrade and Equipping Programme","Upgrade and equip health facilities",""],[1,"161","20","Human Resources for Health Strengthening","Improve the status and supply of Human Resources for Health (HRH)",""],[1,"161","23","Epidemiological and Surveillance Capacity Improvement","Improve epidemiological and surveillance capacities",""],[1,"161","35","Integrated Health Information System and Database","Institute a fully-integrated and interoperable health information system and database",""],[1,"161","37","Health Research and Evidence-Based Decision-Making Strengthening","Strengthen health research and development, and evidence-based decision making",""],[1,"161","43","Transparency, Accountability, and Regulatory Measures in Nutrition and Health Sector","Ensure transparency, accountability and regulatory measures in nutrition and health sector",""],[1,"162","1","Life-Course Care Services Guarantee","the government (a) guarantees to provide care services at all life stages",""],[1,"162","1","Responsive and Resilient Health System Strengthening","ensures responsive and resilient health system",""],[1,"162","1","Equitable Financing for Nutrition and Health Services","sustains equitable financing of nutrition and health services",""]],"78":[[1,"59","1","Nutritious Food Availability and Accessibility Initiative","Thus, to contribute to the goal of achieving a healthy and resilient Philippines, the agriculture, forestry, and fisheries sector will focus on ensuring availability, accessibility, and affordability of nutritious food while continuously addressing persistent challenges faced by the sector.",""]],"79":[[1,"10","3","Human Settlements and Urban Development Policy Reorientation","The creation of the Department of Human Settlements and Urban Development (DHSUD) reorients housing policies and programs towards building communities, in addition to building houses.",""],[1,"49","5","Social Services Expansion and Quality Improvement","Increase investments and spending efficiency to expand and improve the quality of social services to meet growing demand.",""],[1,"49","5","Urban Facilities and Human Resources Expansion","the government will expand and improve facilities and provide additional human resources in the sectors of housing, health, sanitation, and education",""],[1,"50","2","Local Government Social Service Delivery Improvement","Improve social service delivery of local government units (LGUs).",""],[1,"60","3","Human Settlements and Urban Development Department Reform","The creation of the Department of Human Settlements and Urban Development through Republic Act 11201 is a major reform to effect better policy and program coordination, reform advocacy, and implementation.",""],[1,"60","3","BALAI Program for Safe and Inclusive Communities","Moving forward, the housing and urban development sector will pursue building safe, resilient, and sustainable communities through the Building Adequate, Livable, Affordable, and Inclusive Filipino Communities (BALAI) program, in partnership with the private sector, LGUs, and the communities.",""]],"80":[[1,"49","1","Smart City Principle Adoption","These plans also adopt the smart city principle in urban mobility, natural and built environment, sustainable energy, and economic competitiveness.",""],[1,"49","1","Government Institutional Retooling for Urban Planning","The implementation of these plans will require retooling of current government institutions and advancements in planning approaches and urban management practices.",""],[1,"49","5","Urban Waste Reduction and Management","hence, the need to promote waste reduction and management.",""],[1,"49","7","Smart City Capacity Building and Urban Renewal Programme","Adopt \"smart city\" principles and increase technical, managerial, and financial capability of national and local institutions to implement such.",""],[1,"49","7","Urban Renewal and Redevelopment Projects","Improved urban environment and quality of life will be pursued through urban renewal and urban redevelopment projects.",""],[1,"49","7","Healthier and More Sustainable Urban Design Promotion","the aspect of livability will be given more emphasis by promoting healthier lifestyles, environmental consciousness, and sustainable urban design.",""],[1,"50","1","Smart City Capacity Building Partnerships","Capacity building will therefore be encouraged through partnerships with academic and training institutions, private sector, and international development agencies.",""]],"81":[[1,"49","6","Transport Infrastructure Investment and Traffic Management Measures","The government will continue to fast-track investment in transportation infrastructure to reduce traffic congestion and shorten distance and travel times between business and industrial centers, tourism areas, services, and residential areas.",""],[1,"49","6","Traffic Law Enforcement and Demand Management Scheme","The immediate remedial measures will be the enforcement of traffic laws, traffic management measures, and transport demand management schemes.",""],[1,"49","6","Intelligent Transportation Systems for Traffic Flow Management","Application of intelligent transportation systems will also be explored to help manage traffic flow in growth centers efficiently, minimize accidents, and provide transport and traffic information to passengers and decision-makers (see Chapter 19).",""],[1,"295","6","Traffic Management and Intelligent Transport Systems Deployment","Appropriate traffic management measures will also be enforced and updated to be responsive to prevailing situations.",""],[1,"295","6","Intelligent Transport Systems Installation","Traffic engineering solutions, such as the use of intelligent transport systems (e.g., signalized intersections, advanced detection systems, incident detection), will be installed, particularly in urban areas.",""],[1,"295","7","Road Overloading Enforcement Measures","Anti-overloading measures, including penalties will be strictly enforced and strengthened to prevent the rapid deterioration of roads.",""],[1,"295","7","Weighbridge and Portable Weighing Device Expansion","Additional weighbridges and portable weighing devices will be set up to broaden the scope of implementation.",""],[1,"295","7","Motor Vehicle Type Approval and Inspection System","To ensure compliance with international standards on vehicle safety and environmental impact, the Motor Vehicle Type Approval System and Motor Vehicle Inspection System will be implemented.",""],[1,"296","1","Driver and Traffic Enforcer Training Programme","Training of drivers and traffic enforcers will be continued to ensure that investments in transport facilities and other assets are preserved through proper use.",""]],"82":[[1,"50","5","Redundant Road Network Construction in Hazard-Prone Areas","For hazard-prone areas, road networks for redundancy have to be constructed to establish alternative routes for disaster response and evacuation.",""],[1,"51","4","Vulnerability Reduction and Disaster Mitigation Measures","This involves instituting prevention and mitigation measures to reduce the impact of climate change and disasters.",""],[1,"294","6","Climate- and Pandemic-Resilient Critical Transport Infrastructure Development","priority will be on the development and enhancement of critical transport infrastructure",""],[1,"294","6","Resilient Energy and Communications Infrastructure Development","These efforts will be complemented and supported by a resilient energy and communications infrastructure development.",""],[1,"294","6","Adoption of Resilient and Environment-Friendly Transport Standards","Applicable standards and best practices on the adoption of resilient, efficient, and environment-friendly designs and technologies will be adopted.",""],[1,"298","4","Airport Disruption Response Protocol Review","existing intervention protocols between airlines and airport authorities will be reviewed.",""],[1,"298","5","CORSIA Phase 2 Readiness and Implementation Preparation","The Civil Aviation Authority of the Philippines and other airport authorities (e.g., Manila International Airport Authority, Mactan-Cebu International Airport Authority, etc.) will ensure that airports will be ready for the implementation of the Second Phase of Carbon Offsetting and Reduction Scheme for International Aviation (CORSIA).","Civil Aviation Authority of the Philippines | Manila International Airport Authority | Mactan-Cebu International Airport Authority"],[1,"298","6","Port Breakwater Construction for Wave Protection","Breakwater facilities will be constructed for wave protection in order to prevent ports from deteriorating.",""],[1,"298","7","CORSIA Participation and Action Plan Submission","The Philippines has voluntarily applied to take part in the CORSIA and has submitted an action plan to ICAO.",""],[1,"299","3","Support for Local Seaport Establishment","Support for low-income LGUs and coastal and island communities in establishing their own seaports will be continued to promote local trade, tourism, livelihood, and disaster preparedness.",""]],"83":[[1,"10","4","National Innovation Council and STI Ecosystem Framework","Four landmark laws were recently enacted to help establish the ecosystem.",""],[1,"10","4","Innovation and Technology Startup Support Act","The Innovative Startup Act which provides incentives, monetary, and operational support to innovative and technology startups to foster an innovative entrepreneurial culture",""],[1,"10","4","National Space Technology Framework","The Philippine Space Act which provides the institutional framework to enable the country to reap the benefits from the development and use of space technologies",""],[1,"10","4","Balik Scientist Knowledge Return Programme","The Balik Scientist Act which further encourages Filipino experts, scientists, inventors, and engineers who are currently abroad to share their knowledge and expertise in the country",""],[1,"59","2","Inclusive Innovation and Industrial Strategy Operationalization","the sector will operationalize the Inclusive Innovation and Industrial Strategy to boost capacity of local enterprises, adopt inclusive business models, and strengthen the start-up ecosystem.",""],[1,"59","3","Services Sector Investment Attraction and Competitiveness Reforms","the necessary reforms to attract investments and push relevant services sub-sectors to become more competitive will be prioritized.",""],[1,"59","4","Implementation of Business Inclusion Reforms for Startups, MSMEs, and Cooperatives","Moving forward, the government and the business sector will pursue the full implementation of these reforms while addressing the adverse impacts of the pandemic, by providing assistance to enable enterprises to reconfigure business operations and build their resiliency to address the constraints of operation under the new and better normal.",""],[1,"61","1","Startup and MSME Innovation Support Expansion","Various government support services for start-ups and MSMEs will also be ramped up to help them become more innovative and resilient in times of crisis.",""],[1,"61","1","National Innovation Council Establishment","The establishment of the National Innovation Council, which is seen to guide the country towards long-term STI development, will also be fast-tracked.",""],[1,"69","4","Multi-Stakeholder Service Innovation and R&D Partnerships","Agencies will also engage and partner with the private sector, academe, civil society, and other stakeholders for service innovations, technologies, and research and development.",""],[1,"119","7","ASEAN Business Incubator Network Startup Linkage Support","Startups from the Philippines may reach out to the ASEAN Business Incubator Network (ABINet) which enables startups to network with other startups in ASEAN, and even provides potential contact with venture capitalists.",""],[1,"120","1","Manufacturing R&D and Technology Upgrading Support","Support Research and Development (R&D) applications in the manufacturing sector as part of the shift in business processes.",""],[1,"120","5","R&D Support for Semiconductor Firms","R&D support is needed by semiconductor firms to be able to customize electronic components in order to supply automobile spare parts needed by domestic producers of e-vehicles.",""],[1,"120","6","Patent Analytics and Search Services Capacity Expansion","IPOPHL's patent analytics and landscaping efforts, and patent information search initiatives are means of assisting innovative enterprises and research and development institutions as well as government agencies that create policies and grant science and technology funding.",""],[1,"121","1","Industry-Academe RD&I Linkage and Commercialization Initiative","Strengthen industry-academe linkage by prioritizing market-driven research, development, and innovation (RD&I) activities and accelerating commercialization of R&D investments.",""],[1,"121","1","Streamlined Procurement for RD&I Laboratory Equipment","the procurement conditions set in the Government Procurement Act (GPRA) will be streamlined to fast-track procurement of laboratory equipment needed for RD&I activities of state universities and colleges (SUCs) and research and development institutions (RDIs).",""],[1,"121","1","Technology Manager Capacity-Building for Technology Transfer","Technology managers from the public sector will be capacitated to promote, negotiate transfer of technologies particularly for government-funded R&Ds, and spot anti-competitive clauses in technology transfer agreements (TTAs).",""],[1,"121","1","ITSO 2.0 Scale-Up Program","The Innovation and Technology Support Offices (ITSOs) within the universities, other higher education institutes (HEIs), and research and development institutes (RDIs) under the ITSO 2.0 program18 of the IPOPHL will also be scaled up.",""],[1,"121","1","Patent Cooperation Treaty International Patent Access Facilitation","IPOPHL's designation as an international authority under the Patent Cooperation Treaty will facilitate the entry of Filipino innovations to the global patent system.",""],[1,"121","2","Regional Inclusive Innovation Center Scale-Up","Monitor and scale-up efforts to support innovation capacities of startups and MSMEs in the regions by expanding the Regional Inclusive Innovation Center (RIIC) pilot areas.",""],[1,"121","3","Industry Technology Adoption Support","Facilitate industry adoption of appropriate technologies including local R&D solutions and technology-enabled business models.",""],[1,"121","4","Inventory and Scale-Up of Approved Production Technologies","Conduct an inventory of existing DOST-approved or government-funded production technologies for possible scale-up.",""],[1,"123","3","Philippine Inclusive Innovation Industrial Strategies Implementation","Strengthen the implementation of the Philippine Inclusive Innovation Industrial Strategies (i3s).",""],[1,"123","4","Operationalization of the Innovation Memorandum of Understanding","Developing these priority sectors will increase the country's competitiveness amid global market uncertainties by operationalizing the Innovation Memorandum of Understanding (MOU) between relevant NGAs22 and closer coordination and collaboration with the academe and the private sector.",""],[1,"123","5","Industry 4.0 Technology Adoption Support","Provide assistance and facilitate funding for industries and enterprises as they create smart factories, adopt automation, and shift to Industry 4.0 technologies.",""],[1,"124","1","Industry 4.0 Pilot Factory and SME Academy","Establishment of an Industry 4.0 pilot factory and Industry 4.0 SME Academy that will serve as learning facilities providing Industry 4.0 training and technical support to companies transitioning to utilize Industry 4.0 technologies;",""],[1,"124","2","Digital Transformation Funding and Incentive Support","Allocation of funding programs (e.g., soft loans) and appropriate incentives to support companies' digital transformation plans and investments consistent with the CREATE provisions; and",""],[1,"124","3","Industry 4.0 Assessment Technical Support","Provision of technical support in conducting Industry 4.0 assessment through the Smart Industry Readiness Index (SIRI)23.",""],[1,"125","6","Regulatory Sandbox for New Technologies and Industries","Allow firms in new technologies and industries to test their products and business models through regulatory sandbox.",""],[1,"125","9","Regulatory Sandboxes for Emerging Industries","Regulatory sandboxes or testing grounds for emerging industries will require a high degree of regulatory flexibility, market openness, and a competitive policy environment.",""],[1,"145","15","Innovation Capacity Strengthening for Startups, MSMEs, and Cooperatives","Strengthen innovation capacities of startups, MSMEs, and cooperatives",""],[1,"146","2","Fiscal and Non-Fiscal Support for Innovative Enterprises","Provide appropriate fiscal and non-fiscal assistance to innovative and growth-oriented enterprises (e.g., tech-based startups and micro and small enterprises that are innovation-driven, etc.) appropriate with the stage of business operations;",""],[1,"147","4","Innovation Enterprise Technical Assistance and Finance Support","In line with the Philippine Innovation Act, the government will provide technical assistance grants and facilitate access to finance.",""],[1,"150","2","Innovation Capacity Strengthening for Startups, MSMEs, and Cooperatives","Strengthen innovation capacities of startups, MSMEs, and cooperatives.",""],[1,"161","34","Research and Innovation Initiatives","Boost cutting-edge research and innovation initiatives",""],[1,"174","5","National Research and Innovation Ecosystem Development","The government will build a robust national ecosystem for knowledge production and innovation",""],[1,"175","1","Implementation of the Magna Carta for Scientists and Researchers","implementing the Magna Carta of Scientists, Engineers, Researchers, and Other Science and Technology Personnel in the Government (RA 11312).",""],[1,"175","1","Review of Scientific Career System Eligibility for SUC Faculty","The exclusion of SUC faculty from the Scientific Career System will also be re-evaluated to incentivize research productivity among faculty member.",""],[1,"175","1","Balik Scientist Engagement and Research and Development Support","HEIs will be encouraged to tap Balik Scientists and engage in research and development initiatives supportive of the National Harmonized Research and Development Agenda and the country's science, technology, and innovation priorities, which will be outlined in the National Innovation Agenda and Strategic Development (see Chapter 14).",""],[1,"175","1","Strengthening University-Community-Industry Research Partnerships","Productive partnerships between HEIs and stakeholders in the community and industry will also be intensified to integrate formal research and innovation efforts with informal grassroots knowledge and innovation.",""]],"84":[[1,"4","5","Accelerated Reform Implementation","the country has been benefitting from the reforms enacted and already implemented (e.g., Rice Tariffication Law, Sin Tax Reform Law, Ease of Doing Business and Efficient Government Service Delivery Act, Tax Reform for Acceleration and Inclusion, Telecommuting Act, Social Security Act of 2018, Balik Scientist Act, etc.)",""],[1,"4","5","Accelerated Reform Timeline for Resilience","A more accelerated timeline concerning the other reforms would have substantially built up the country's resilience (e.g., PhilSys Act, Universal Health Care Act, Philippine Innovation Act, entry of a third telecommunications provider, Free Internet in Public Spaces Act, etc.)",""],[1,"4","5","Financial Institutions Strategic Transfer and GUIDE Laws","the proposed Financial Institutions Strategic Transfer (FIST) and Government Financial Institutions Unified Initiatives to Distressed Enterprises for Economic Recovery (GUIDE) laws are designed to manage such risks",""],[1,"7","1","Macroeconomic Stability and Competition Policy Package","Supporting these pillars are policies and programs to ensure sound macroeconomic fundamentals and promote healthy competition.",""],[1,"17","4","Financial Institutions Strategic Transfer Bill","the Financial Institutions Strategic Transfer' [FIST] bill, which seeks to create special purpose vehicles to help financial institutions offload their COVID19-induced nonperforming assets",""],[1,"17","4","GUIDE Special Investment Vehicle","the Government Financial Institutions Unified Initiatives to Distressed Enterprises for Economic Recovery (GUIDE), which creates a special investment vehicle that would infuse capital into key enterprises while preserving employment (and talents) therein",""],[1,"18","1","Corporate Recovery Tax Incentives for Enterprises","The Corporate Recovery Tax Incentives for Enterprises (CREATE), meanwhile, will usher in a more competitive tax and incentive regime for businesses - corporate income tax rate will be reduced (by 10 percentage points for small businesses and by 5 percentage points for all others); incentive structure can be nuanced depending on the type of investment, location and subject to agreed performance targets.",""],[1,"57","14","Strategic Trade and Responsive Fiscal Policy","Implement strategic trade and responsive fiscal policy",""],[1,"61","2","Responsive Fiscal Policy and Revenue Reform","Ensuring sound macroeconomic policy (Chapter 15) aims to promote a responsive fiscal policy by enabling budget policies and revenue measures, enhanced LGU capacity, improved private sector participation, and recalibrated debt and contingent liability management.",""],[1,"61","2","Corporate Recovery and Tax Incentives Reform","Furthermore, key reforms such as the Corporate Recovery and Tax Incentives for Enterprises Act (CREATE), the Financial Institutions Strategic Transfer Act (FIST), and the Government Financial Institutions Unified Initiatives to Distressed Enterprises for Economic Recovery Act (GUIDE) will be actively pursued and implemented.",""],[1,"61","3","National Competition Policy Implementation","With the recent issuance of the National Competition Policy through Joint Memorandum Circular No. 1 by NEDA and Philippine Competition Commission on July 30, 2020, the government will ensure that its responses and interventions follow competition principles to address market failures.","NEDA | Philippine Competition Commission"],[1,"61","3","Competition Law Enforcement and Regulatory Reform","Promoting competition (Chapter 16) reinforces the Philippine Competition Act through strategies that aim to foster an environment that penalizes anti-competitive practices, facilitates entry of players and creates an economic playing field where these players operate and grow, supports regulatory reform to address restrictive laws and regulations that hamper competition, and improves trade policies to stimulate investments and innovation and boost competitiveness.",""],[1,"77","7","Expansionary Fiscal Policy Support Measures","This will support the expansionary fiscal policy of the government in response to COVID-19 through (a) streamlining the cash budgeting system; (b) strengthening the Bureau of the Treasury's oversight function over government bank accounts; (c) providing the legal basis for upholding the validity of online financial transactions; (d) giving DBM the power over internal audit standards; and (e) instituting participation in government budgeting.","Bureau of the Treasury | DBM"],[1,"130","5","Foreign Investment Law Amendment Package","The current law needs to be updated to attract more foreign investments in manufacturing and other priority sectors.",""],[1,"131","2","Investment Attraction and Business Environment Reform","reforms to attract investments, increase competitiveness, and further improve the country's business environment are needed to boost the recovery and strengthen the economy's resilience.",""],[1,"133","13","Trade in Services Market Access Expansion","Maximize opportunities that expand access of trade in services to existing and new markets under the ASEAN Free Trade Agreement and other preferential agreements with key trading partners",""],[1,"134","3","Market Access Expansion under Preferential Trade Agreements","Maximize opportunities that expand access to existing and new markets under the ASEAN Free Trade Agreements and other preferential agreements with key trading partners.",""],[1,"134","4","Services Sector Liberalization and Competition Reform","Continue efforts to ease or remove restrictions in the services sector and pursue reforms to open the sector to foreign participation and encourage competition.",""],[1,"134","6","Enforcement Rules for Liberalized Sectors","Prioritize the establishment of clear enforcement rules for sectors/economic activities liberalized under the 11th RFINL in line with easing foreign equity restrictions",""],[1,"134","7","National Competition Policy Implementation","Implement the National Competition Policy to enhance the competitiveness of the services sector by ensuring that regulations promote fair competition and level the playing field, particularly in the transportation, energy, and telecommunication sectors.",""],[1,"134","9","Sector-Specific Services Trade Data Development","Develop sector-specific services trade data, including indices, to measure the country's services regulatory environment.",""],[1,"135","4","Air Services Agreement Expansion Initiative","Aggressively pursue new air services agreements to increase access and connectivity to new markets and potentially benefit the travelling public, tourism industry, and airline carriers, among others.",""],[1,"141","5","Foreign Equity Liberalization in Key Service Sectors","This will enable higher foreign equity participation (over 40%) in other key areas such as telecommunication and transportation services.",""],[1,"141","6","Retail Sector Foreign Investment Liberalization","the relaxation of barriers to foreign investments in the retail sector through lowering the minimum paid-up capital to USD 200,000 from USD 2.5 million and removing the USD 250,000 paid-up capital per store for enterprises engaged in high-end or luxury products, among others.",""],[1,"141","7","Foreign Investment Act Amendment for SME Hiring and Professional Access","Proposed amendments in the Act aim to reduce the minimum employment requirement from 50 to 15 direct local hires for small- and medium-sized domestic enterprises established by foreign investors with paid-in capital of at least USD 100,000.",""],[1,"141","7","Removal of Professional Services from Foreign Investment Negative List","The proposed amendments also exclude the practice of professions from the coverage of the foreign investment negative list.",""],[1,"141","9","Data Transmission and Telecommunications Market Liberalization","The objective is to level the playing field in the data transmission and telecommunications market.",""],[1,"145","12","Foreign Investment Liberalization and Incentive Rationalization","Relax foreign equity restrictions, rationalize investment incentives, and promote job-creating investments",""],[1,"145","20","Investment Promotion Acceleration","Accelerate investment promotion activities",""],[1,"146","5","Foreign Investment Liberalization and Incentive Rationalization","Relax foreign equity restrictions, rationalize investment incentives, and promote job-creating investments.",""],[1,"147","2","Investment Promotion and Lead Conversion Programme","Accelerate investment promotion activities.",""]],"85":[[1,"7","1","Peace, Security, and Public Order and Safety Measures","the PDP 2017-2022 contains policies and programs to ensure peace, security, and public order and safety;",""],[1,"62","2","Bangsamoro Transition Process Implementation","These can be achieved by implementing a smooth transition process in the Bangsamoro Autonomous Region in Muslim Mindanao, capacitating local governments to undertake localized peace engagements and strengthen convergence of national government agencies to end communist insurgency, and delivering the remaining commitments under closure agreements.",""],[1,"62","2","Local Peace Engagement Capacity Building","These can be achieved by implementing a smooth transition process in the Bangsamoro Autonomous Region in Muslim Mindanao, capacitating local governments to undertake localized peace engagements and strengthen convergence of national government agencies to end communist insurgency, and delivering the remaining commitments under closure agreements.",""],[1,"62","2","Whole-of-Nation Counterinsurgency Coordination","These can be achieved by implementing a smooth transition process in the Bangsamoro Autonomous Region in Muslim Mindanao, capacitating local governments to undertake localized peace engagements and strengthen convergence of national government agencies to end communist insurgency, and delivering the remaining commitments under closure agreements.",""],[1,"62","2","Closure Agreement Commitments Delivery","These can be achieved by implementing a smooth transition process in the Bangsamoro Autonomous Region in Muslim Mindanao, capacitating local governments to undertake localized peace engagements and strengthen convergence of national government agencies to end communist insurgency, and delivering the remaining commitments under closure agreements.",""],[1,"62","2","Conflict-Affected Area Support and Health Protocol Compliance","Interventions in conflict-affected and conflict-vulnerable areas will be sustained while being mindful of new health protocols to ensure that the socioeconomic impacts of the COVID-19 pandemic will not aggravate the fragile situation in these areas.",""],[1,"262","2","Protection and Development Support for Conflict-Affected Communities","Complementary interventions for the continuous protection and development of conflict- affected and conflict-vulnerable communities were also pursued",""],[1,"262","2","Peacebuilding Initiatives","the implementation of other peacebuilding initiatives",""],[1,"262","3","Sustained Interventions in Conflict-Affected and Conflict-Vulnerable Areas","For the remainder of the Plan period, interventions in conflict-affected and conflict-vulnerable areas will be sustained while being mindful of the new health protocols.",""],[1,"262","3","Peacebuilding Support in Conflict-Affected Areas","peace building efforts would contribute towards a healthy and resilient Philippines.",""],[1,"262","4","Bangsamoro Normalization Acceleration","The Bangsamoro normalization process was fast-tracked through the issuance of Executive Order No. 79, s. 2019.",""],[1,"262","4","Moro Peace Agreement Implementation Engagement","The government has likewise continuously engaged the two groups of the Moro National Liberation Front (MNLF) to ensure the implementation of the remaining commitments under the 1996 Final Peace Agreement (FPA).",""],[1,"262","4","Implementation of Peace Agreements with RPMP-RPA-ABB and CBA-CPLA","Efforts to complete the implementation of the peace agreements with the Rebolusyonaryong Partido ng Manggagawa-Pilipinas - Revolutionary Proletarian Army-Alex Boncayao Brigade (RPMP-RPA-ABB) and the Cordillera Bodong Administration- Cordillera People's Liberation Army (CBA-CPLA) were also actively pursued.",""],[1,"262","5","Implementation of the Annex on Normalization under the Comprehensive Agreement on the Bangsamoro","Implementing the Annex on Normalization under the Comprehensive Agreement on the Bangsamoro (CAB)",""],[1,"263","3","Implementation of Signed Peace Agreements","These include the effective implementation of signed peace agreements and continuous delivery of various peace and development interventions in conflict-affected and conflict-vulnerable areas.",""],[1,"263","3","Peace and Development Interventions in Conflict-Affected Areas","These include the effective implementation of signed peace agreements and continuous delivery of various peace and development interventions in conflict-affected and conflict-vulnerable areas.",""],[1,"264","7","Bangsamoro Normalization Program Implementation","Intensify the implementation of the normalization program for the Bangsamoro",""],[1,"264","9","Implementation of Remaining 1996 Final Peace Agreement Commitments","Complete the implementation of the remaining commitments under the 1996 Final Peace Agreement between the Government of the Philippines (GPH) and the MNLF",""],[1,"264","11","MNLF Combatants Transformation Program","Implement a transformation program for the MNLF combatants",""],[1,"264","15","Fast-Track Completion of Closure Agreement Commitments","Fast-track the completion of remaining commitments under the closure agreements with the RPMP-RPA-ABB and the CBA-CPLA",""],[1,"265","2","Bangsamoro Normalization Program Implementation","Intensify the implementation of the normalization program for the Bangsamoro.",""],[1,"265","3","Completion of Remaining 1996 FPA Commitments","Complete the implementation of the remaining commitments under the 1996 FPA between the Government of the Philippines (GPH) and the MNLF.",""],[1,"265","3","Bangsamoro Development Assistance Fund","These include the establishment of the Bangsamoro Development Assistance Fund (BDAF) intended to uplift the conditions of the MNLF and the operationalization of a monitoring mechanism anchored on the results of the Tripartite Review Process (TRP) between the GPH, MNLF, and the Organization of Islamic Cooperation (OIC).",""],[1,"265","3","Tripartite Review Process Monitoring Mechanism","These include the establishment of the Bangsamoro Development Assistance Fund (BDAF) intended to uplift the conditions of the MNLF and the operationalization of a monitoring mechanism anchored on the results of the Tripartite Review Process (TRP) between the GPH, MNLF, and the Organization of Islamic Cooperation (OIC).",""],[1,"265","4","MNLF Combatants Transformation Program","A transformation program for the MNLF combatants, their families, and communities will be implemented through the coordinating committees, beginning in the Province of Sulu.",""],[1,"266","4","Fast-Track Completion of Peace Agreement Commitments","Fast-track the completion of remaining commitments under the agreements with the Rebolusyonaryong Partidong Manggagawa - Pilipinas-Revolutionary Proletarian Army-Alex Boncayao Brigade (RPMP- RPA-ABB) and the Cordillera Bodong Administration-Cordillera People's Liberation Army (CBA- CPLA).",""],[1,"267","1","TPG Normalization and Civilian Transition Plan","These include the full transformation of the TPG from an armed group into a civilian organization through a three-year normalization plan that will facilitate development assistance to its members, their families, and identified communities.",""],[1,"267","1","Engagement with the NDCG under the Peace Agreement","Engagement with the NDCG is also being pursued within the bounds of the 2000 Peace Agreement, with full observance of the ceasefire agreement.",""],[1,"267","2","Socioeconomic Reintegration Program for Former CPLA Members","the completion strategy for the CBA-CPLA focuses on the implementation and sustainability of socioeconomic reintegration programs for former CPLA members, their families, and communities.",""],[1,"267","7","Expanded E-CLIP Reintegration Program","E-CLIP's coverage was expanded through Administrative Order 25, s. 2020: Amending AO 10, s. 2018 \"Centralizing All Government Efforts for the Reintegration of Former Rebels and Creating for the purpose an Inter-agency Task Force.\"",""],[1,"267","7","Community-Based Reintegration Support for Former Rebels and Former Violent Extremists","This provides for a comprehensive, integrated, and community-based national program that is locally implemented to address the economic, social, psychological rehabilitation needs, legal status and security of Former Rebels (FRs) who are members of the CPP-NPA-NDF, former violent extremists, their immediate family members and communities through the E-CLIP.",""],[1,"267","7","Task Force Balik Loob Oversight Mechanism","The Task Force Balik Loob (TFBL) oversees the implementation of the E-CLIP.",""],[1,"269","1","Normalization and Reintegration Support for Former Women Rebels and Violent Extremists","ensuring that former women rebels and violent extremists can benefit from normalization and reintegration programs",""],[1,"270","6","Presidential Amnesty and Reintegration Proclamations","The proposed presidential proclamations on amnesty for various groups aim to accept former combatants back into the fold of the law and eventually provide them access to the government's socioeconomic services as a means to attain peace, reconciliation, and unity in the country.",""]],"86":[[1,"17","1","Revision of Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Plans for Pandemics","At the same time, disaster risk reduction and management plans need to be revised to include the occurrence of pandemics in the whole framework.",""],[1,"36","1","Disaster Risk Reduction and Climate Change Adaptation Investment","the government will continue to invest in disaster risk reduction (DRR), climate change adaptation (CCA) initiatives to reduce vulnerability to multiple hazards.",""],[1,"51","7","Mainstream Disaster Risk Reduction and Climate Change Adaptation in Growth Centers","Mainstream DRR and CCA in identified growth centers, considering the expected increase in population and economic activities in these areas.",""],[1,"52","1","GeoRiskPH Disaster Risk Information System","The Department of Science and Technology (DOST)-Philippine Institute of Volcanology and Seismology is currently implementing its GeoRiskPH program.","Department of Science and Technology | Philippine Institute of Volcanology and Seismology"],[1,"52","2","Scientific Hazard and Disaster Risk Data Platform Enhancement","the continuous data build-up and updating of relevant databases and platforms of DOST and other agencies will be pursued and supported","DOST"],[1,"52","2","Disaster Risk Assessment and Plan Updating","Disaster risk assessments will be undertaken, utilizing more recent information on hazards and elements exposed to it",""],[1,"52","3","LGU Disaster Preparedness and Resilience Capacity-Building","LGUs will be trained and assisted using these for planning and identifying, designing, financing, and implementing the initiatives to increase their resiliency.",""],[1,"52","3","Inter-LGU Disaster Risk Cooperation Mechanism","Inter-LGU cooperation will also be pursued to address the impacts of natural hazards that affect multiple municipalities, cities, and provinces.",""],[1,"52","4","Review and Update of Disaster Risk Reduction and Crisis Management Frameworks","The traditional DRRM and crisis management frameworks will be reviewed and updated to ensure the country's readiness to prepare, mitigate, and respond to public health emergencies, given also the possibility that disease outbreaks can occur simultaneously with natural hazards such as typhoons or floods.",""],[1,"318","8","Climate and Disaster Risk Reduction Capacity Strengthening","Strengthen national and local capacities for climate and disaster risk reduction and management",""],[1,"326","6","Resilience Index and Sectoral Emissions Monitoring System","the government will prioritize the development and adoption of appropriate baseline information and indicators to measure resilience of ecosystems and communities (i.e., resilience index), and set up a systematic database to regularly monitor sectoral emissions reduction.",""],[1,"326","8","Data Protocol for Sharing Climate and Risk Information","Developing a data protocol to facilitate access and sharing of available scientific researches and studies, geospatial information, climate trends and projections, risk estimation models, gender-related variables, and disaggregated loss and damage datasets on vulnerable and affected groups.",""],[1,"326","9","Integrated Climate Change and Disaster Risk Reduction Knowledge Management System","Establishing integrated knowledge management systems to serve as platforms for sharing, managing, and reporting CC/DRR related information.",""],[1,"326","10","Mainstream Climate and Disaster Risk in Public Investment Programming","Integrate CCAM-DRR considerations in public investment programming processes.","NEDA"],[1,"326","11","Guidelines and Standard Quality Assurance Review Tools Development","Fast-track and prioritize the development of guidelines and standard quality assurance review tools and streamline local planning and review mechanisms","DILG | DHSUD | Office of Civil Defense-NDRRMC | Climate Change Commission"],[1,"326","12","Climate and Disaster Risk Budget Tagging Enhancement","Strengthen existing mechanisms to harmonize the monitoring of CCAM and DRRM expenditures at the national and local levels.","Department of Budget and Management | CCC | OCD- NDRRMC"],[1,"327","1","Government Capacity Enhancement for Multidimensional Hazard Risk Management","Enhance the capacity of the government to address the multidimensional risks arising from natural hazard events, including biological hazards by:",""],[1,"327","2","Update Local Disaster Risk Reduction and Climate Change Action Plans","Updating the local disaster risk reduction and management (DRRM) and local climate change action (LCCAP) plans to include public health emergencies, and climate and disaster risk parameters to ensure better preparedness and response to pandemics while mitigating impacts of climate-related disasters;",""],[1,"327","3","Business and Public Service Continuity Planning Support","Sustaining support to promote business and public service continuity planning and ensuring the development of climate and disaster-resilient structures and designs following established measures and standards;",""],[1,"327","4","Technical Assistance for Climate Adaptation and Disaster Risk Financing","Providing technical assistance to NGAs, LGUs, private sector, and community organizations to: (a) maximize access to CCAM and DRRM financing and risk transfer mechanisms; and (b) implement ecosystem-based adaptation (EbA) measures that are risk- informed, gender-responsive, and sensitive to the needs, benefits, and priorities of men and women, while taking into account indigenous knowledge systems.",""],[1,"327","5","Gender Analysis for CCAM and DRRM Participation","Undertaking gender analysis to identify gender issues related to capacity of both men and women, especially in vulnerable communities, to engage in decision-making processes, project development, implementation, and monitoring of CCAM and DRRM actions.",""]],"87":[[1,"7","2","Overseas Filipino Reintegration and Participation Initiative","Special focus is given to their eventual reintegration and active participation into the country's development processes.",""],[1,"63","2","Capacity Scaling for OF-Serving Agencies","the capacity of OF-serving agencies are being scaled up to be able to serve and assist affected OFs.",""],[1,"63","2","OF Skills Retooling and Employment Assistance","the government is conducting skills retooling and upgrading programs, employment assistance, and short-term employment programs to facilitate local re-employment of OFs who have returned.",""],[1,"63","2","Protection and Reintegration Strategy for Overseas Filipinos","the urgency of strategies already being pursued by the government in the first three years of the Plan implementation: (a) protecting the rights and improving the well-being of OFs; (b) facilitating the reintegration of returnees and expanding opportunities for OFs to participate in the country's development; and (c) strengthening OFs' engagement in governance.",""],[1,"71","2","Overseas Filipino Service Delivery Improvement","Effective service delivery to overseas Filipinos will also be pursued (see Chapter 21).",""]],"88":[[1,"81","4","Alternative Dispute Resolution Strengthening Program","ADR will be strengthened at all levels.","Department of Interior and Local Government (DILG) | DOJ - Office of ADR | Public Attorney's Office (PAO) | DOJ | National Prosecution Service"]],"89":[[1,"82","2","Justice Sector Capacity Strengthening for Legal and Victim Assistance","the government will prioritize strengthening of the justice sector agencies' capacity to deliver legal and victim assistance",""],[1,"82","2","Expansion of Legal Aid Staffing and Recruitment","To increase access of the poor, vulnerable, and marginalized sectors to legal aid, plantilla positions will be increased, and the recruitment of investigators, prosecutors, public attorneys, judges, and other legal or court officers will be expedited",""],[1,"82","2","Nationwide Support for Justice Personnel","Support will also be provided to all personnel nationwide",""],[1,"82","3","Legal Aid Program Strengthening","Apart from the regular services of the PAO, other legal aid programs will also be sustained and improved such as the implementation of the Revised Law Student Practice Rule (Rule 138-A) of the SC and the DOJ Action Center Program.",""],[1,"82","3","Legal Internship and Practice Programs","Justice sector agencies will also explore and implement legal internship and practice programs to augment the limited manpower for legal services and facilitate the recruitment of competent personnel.",""],[1,"82","4","Online Legal and Victim Assistance Access Platform","Safe and convenient access to legal and victim assistance will be established through online and other communication platforms.",""],[1,"82","4","Continuity of Free Legal Assistance and Victim Support Services","Moreover, sustained physical access to free legal assistance and victim support services of agencies concerned will be ensured even during pandemics and other public emergency situations.",""],[1,"82","5","Victim Assistance and Support Strengthening","Assistance and support for victims of crimes and human rights violations, including gender-sensitive and child-friendly procedures and facilities, will be improved and strengthened.",""],[1,"82","5","Victim Compensation Increase Through RA 7309 Amendment","These include increasing the compensation of victims of unjust imprisonment and victims of violent crimes through the amendment of Republic Act (RA) No. 7309.",""],[1,"82","5","Integrated Referral Procedures for Legal Assistance and Victim Support","Referral procedures for legal assistance and victim support in relation to applicable frontline services will be integrated into the manuals of operations, Citizen's Charter, and public assistance or complaint desk mechanism of agencies concerned.",""],[1,"82","6","Access to Justice and Human Rights Legal Assistance Programme","The Commission on Human Rights (CHR) will continue its efforts to facilitate access to justice particularly on addressing human rights violations, empowering the marginalized to seek response and remedies for injustice, and improving legal protection awareness and aid, among others.",""],[1,"82","6","Legal Clinic Caravan","Its Legal Clinic Caravan will sustain its developmental and legal assistance and counselling.",""],[1,"82","6","Human Rights Awareness and Capacity Building Initiative","These include increasing human rights awareness, capacity building and training on basic human rights, and raising public awareness on the role, mandate, and services of CHR and other relevant human rights laws.",""],[1,"86","11","Victims Compensation Program Strengthening","Strengthening of the Victims Compensation Program",""],[1,"86","12","Amendment of RA 7309 Compensation Program","Amend its enabling law, RA 7309, to increase compensation for victims of unjust imprisonment or detention and victims of violent crimes; and to increase access to the program and enhance its administration.",""],[1,"86","13","Commission on Human Rights Charter Establishment","Establishment of the Commission on Human Rights Charter",""],[1,"86","14","Strengthen the CHR as a National Human Rights Institution","Strengthen the CHR as a National Human Rights Institution (NHRI), compliant with the requirements of the UN Paris Principles affecting NHRIs worldwide.",""]],"90":[[1,"84","6","National Justice Information System Implementation","The justice sector will sustain the implementation of the National Justice Information System, with the support of the Department of Information and Communications Technology (DICT) and in compliance with the requirements of the Data Privacy Act.","Department of Information and Communications Technology (DICT)"],[1,"84","6","Single Carpeta System Update","The DOJ, as the lead agency, will update the Single Carpeta System to conform to the new IRR of the Expanded GCTA Law.","DOJ"],[1,"84","6","Justice Sector Information Exchange Platform Development","The development of information exchange platform will be pursued with the DICT, towards streamlining inter-agency processes within the justice sector.","DICT"],[1,"84","6","Philippine Crime Index Access for Justice Agencies","The Philippine Crime Index will also be made available initially to justice sector agencies to harmonize crime and criminal justice data for legal research and as reference for policy development.",""],[1,"84","7","Electronic Transmittal and Documentation System for Justice Orders","the SC, Philippine National Police (PNP), BJMP, BUCOR, and the Bureau of Immigration will proceed with the development and implementation of systems and procedures for electronic transmittal and documentation of warrants; hold departure orders; and commitment, mittimus, and/or release orders.","SC | Philippine National Police (PNP) | BJMP | BUCOR | Bureau of Immigration"],[1,"85","6","Enhanced E-Warrant System","The new Enhanced e-Warrant System, aimed to fully automate the issuance of arrest warrants and serve as online database thereof, will be implemented by SC and PNP in all courts and police stations nationwide.",""]],"91":[[1,"90","9","Institutional and Policy Reforms for Cultural Development","Pursue institutional and policy reforms for cultural development",""],[1,"90","11","Platforms and Mechanisms for Filipino Creativity and Collaboration","Create platforms and mechanisms to support Filipino creativity for collaboration and bayanihan",""],[1,"90","14","Cultural Development Coordination and Evaluation Mechanism","Strengthen mechanisms to measure, evaluate, coordinate, and consolidate efforts towards cultural development",""],[1,"93","1","Creative Economy Roadmap Completion","The creative economy roadmap will be completed to serve as a policy framework to strengthen resilience of cultural and creative industries and address specific concerns of creative and cultural workers, especially freelancers in the gig economy.",""],[1,"93","1","Creative Industries Coordination Mechanism","To ensure a whole- of-country approach to develop and promote the creative industries, the establishment of appropriate coordinating mechanisms across different agencies and stakeholders will be supported.",""],[1,"93","2","Creative Enterprise Capacity-Building and Business Continuity Support","For creative enterprises, programs such as business continuity planning, digitizing operations, knowledge transfer and information sharing, will be implemented.",""],[1,"93","2","Creative Worker Skills Retooling and Income Support","For creative workers especially freelancers, skills retooling and upskilling programs, along with continuing income support programs such as the NCCA Assistance Program and the FDCP Disaster/Emergency Assistance and Relief, will be made available.",""],[1,"93","3","Creative Sector Formalization and Social Protection Coordination","Proper interventions to integrate creatives into the formal economy and ensure their welfare will also be pursued.","DOLE | DTI | Social Security System | Bureau of Internal Revenue"],[1,"93","4","Support for UNESCO Creative Cities Network Participation","Philippine cities, which aim to become part of the UNESCO Creative Cities Network, will also be actively and adequately supported.",""],[1,"93","5","Nation Brand Framework","A Nation Brand will also be adopted as a unified framework to promote the Philippines and the Filipino identity to the rest of the world.",""],[1,"94","2","Creative Collaboration Platforms and Mechanisms","Create platforms and mechanisms to support Filipino creativity for collaboration and bayanihan.",""],[1,"94","2","Digital Promotion Platform for Filipino Creatives","programming will focus on ensuring that digital and online platforms are maximized to provide Filipino creatives due exposure through events, fairs, exhibits, shows, and competitions.",""],[1,"94","3","Artistic-Scientific-Technological Collaboration Strengthening","Artistic-scientific-technological collaborations will be strengthened to stimulate innovations for the common good (see Chapter 14).",""],[1,"94","3","Academe and Private Sector Innovation Partnerships","Collaboration and partnerships with the academe and private sector, including startups and creative hubs, will be nurtured to facilitate the sharing of best practices in technological adaption and other innovations within the sector.",""],[1,"94","3","Creative Works Promotion and Distribution Linkages","Where possible, these linkages can also serve as a venue for Filipino creatives to promote and distribute their works and to establish networks with other groups.",""],[1,"94","4","Cultural Governance and Coordination Reform","Existing governance structures and mechanisms for culture and the arts need to be strengthened.",""],[1,"96","2","Cultural Legislation Enactment Initiative","the Planning Committee on Culture will exert its efforts toward the enactment of the following key legislations:",""],[1,"96","4","Amend Republic Act 7356 to Strengthen NCCA Cultural Governance","Amend Republic Act 7356 to improve cultural governance by strengthening and enabling the NCCA to undertake a lead role in the protection, preservation, and promotion of our cultural and natural heritage and in the promotion of the creative arts for inclusive development.",""],[1,"96","10","Film Production and Creative Industry Support Programme","Encourage the production of quality films; strengthen competitiveness of Filipino content and creative outputs in a digital landscape; address concerns on the welfare and capacity building for local film and audiovisual artists, technicians, and workers; and enhance film preservation and archiving.",""],[1,"96","12","Amendment of the Commission on the Filipino Language Act","Amend certain provisions of the Commission on the Filipino Language Act (RA 7104) to strengthen the protection and conservation of intangible heritage (i.e., languages in the Philippines).",""]],"92":[[1,"100","12","Ecosystems-Based Fisheries Management","Pursue an ecosystems approach to fisheries management, including operationalizing fisheries management areas",""],[1,"100","35","Guidelines for Delineation of Municipal Waters","Issuance of the guidelines by the BFAR on the delineation of municipal waters for LGUs with off-shore islands","BFAR"],[1,"101","3","Ecosystems-Based Fisheries Management and Fisheries Management Areas Operationalization","Pursue an ecosystems approach to fisheries management, including operationalizing fisheries management areas (FMA)4 to provide for a science-based, participatory, transparent governance framework, and mechanism to sustainably manage fisheries.","Bureau of Fisheries and Aquatic Resources (BFAR)"],[1,"101","7","Establishment of Fishery Management Areas","for purposes of sustainable fisheries management, 12 FMAs in Philippine waters are established",""],[1,"102","1","Multi-Sectoral Fisheries Management Bodies and Ecosystem-Approach Fisheries Management Plan","efforts in establishing and convening the multi-sectoral Management Bodies (MB)5 in the FMAs, and develop the Ecosystem-Approach to Fisheries Management Plan (EAMP) guided by the result of the National Stock Assessment Program of the National Fisheries Research and Development Institute (NFRDI).",""],[1,"102","1","Scientific Advisory Group for Fisheries Management Bodies","A Scientific Advisory Group (SAG) composed of scientists, researchers, and technical representatives will also be established to provide policy support and technical advice to the MBs",""],[1,"105","3","Guidelines on Delineation of Municipal Waters for LGUs with Offshore Islands","Issuance of the guidelines by the BFAR on the delineation of municipal waters for LGUs with off- shore islands","BFAR"]],"93":[[1,"100","21","Irrigation Development and Farm and Fishery Mechanization","Accelerate irrigation development and intensify provision of appropriate farm and fishery machinery, equipment, and facilities",""],[1,"103","1","Rice Competitiveness Enhancement Fund Implementation","Effectively implement RCEF in a timely manner to assist rice farmers during the transition period given the removal of the quantitative import restrictions (QR) on rice.",""],[1,"103","4","Farm and Fishery Mechanization Support","Intensify the provision of appropriate farm and fishery machineries, equipment, and facilities.",""],[1,"104","1","Agriculture and Fisheries Mechanization Engineering Resource Network Update","the Agriculture and Fisheries Mechanization Engineering Resource Network (AFMechERN) will be regularly updated to provide timely and reliable data on existing agri-fishery machineries, equipment, and facilities, as well as other mechanization-related information.",""],[1,"104","1","Agricultural Machinery Testing and Evaluation Center Capacity Expansion","The Agricultural Machinery Testing and Evaluation Center (AMTEC)9 in Los Baños, Laguna, will be capacitated to expand its services for testing and evaluation of: (a) imported machinery and equipment for domestic distribution; and (b) locally-developed machinery and equipment prior to its commercialization as mandated by the AFMECH Law (See Chapter 9).",""],[1,"104","1","Local Machinery Manufacturer Training and Incentive Support","The local manufacturers of equipment and machinery will also be supported by providing them with training on the design, fabrication, operation, testing, and evaluation of equipment and machinery, and providing appropriate incentives.",""],[1,"104","5","Agricultural and Fisheries Machinery Testing and Standards Support","The law further states that AMTEC shall assist in the formulation of quality, safety, and performance standards of agricultural and fisheries machinery and provide technical assistance in the establishment of testing centers in other parts of the country.",""],[1,"122","2","Farm Mechanization Program","Encourage the local development, manufacturing, and distribution of farm machinery through the government's Farm Mechanization Program (FMP).",""]],"94":[[1,"100","23","Agricultural Research and Development Intensification","Intensify research and development (R&D) activities for AFF",""],[1,"100","29","Agricultural and Fishery Processing and Packaging Technology Development","Develop processing and packaging technologies to prolong shelf-life and improve nutritional content of agriculture and fishery products",""],[1,"103","3","Agricultural R&D and Technology Commercialization Programme","Intensify research and development (R&D) activities for AFF, including the development and commercialization of appropriate technologies to improve productivity, reduce post-harvest losses, and enhance risk resilience.",""],[1,"110","2","Agri-Food Processing and Packaging Technology Development","Develop processing and packaging technologies to prolong shelf-life and improve nutritional content of agriculture and fishery products.",""],[1,"110","2","Agri-Food Innovation Partnerships and Joint Projects","Partnerships and joint projects with DA, DOST, DTI, and the private sector may be explored to develop agri-food processed products with enhanced nutritional content and longer shelf-life.","DA | DOST | DTI"]],"95":[[1,"100","31","Parcelization and Individual Land Titling Program","Fast track and complete the parcelization of collectively-titled awarded lands and generation of individual titles",""],[1,"104","4","Parcelization and Individual Land Titling for Agrarian Reform Areas","Fast track and complete the parcelization10 of collectively-titled awarded lands and generation of individual titles to address investor uncertainty and facilitate investments in agrarian reform areas.",""],[1,"104","6","Parcelization of Landholdings under CCLOA","Parcelization of landholdings with Collective Certificate of Land Ownership Award (CCLOA) is the process of subdividing and determining the exact metes and bounds of the areas, allocation of lots to ARBs in a CCLOA, determination of common use areas, portions with common service facilities, and establishment of areas capable of being alienated and disposed of by the government.",""],[1,"105","1","CARP Parcelization Coordination and Capacity-Building Initiative","To address this, the coordination and collaboration of the Department of Agrarian Reform (DAR) with CARP Implementing Agencies (IA) should be strengthened with the intent of streamlining the parcelization process.","Department of Agrarian Reform (DAR) | CARP Implementing Agencies (IA)"],[1,"105","1","Modern Survey Technology Capacity Building for Land Titling","In addition, the DAR and CARP IAs should be capacitated on the latest modern survey technologies and equipment to fast track the documentation and reconstitution of lost/missing titles and those with erroneous land surveys.","Department of Agrarian Reform (DAR) | CARP Implementing Agencies (IA)"],[1,"105","4","Usufruct Regulatory Framework for AFF Lands","Establish a regulatory framework and formulate specific guidelines on implementing usufruct arrangement for AFF purposes.",""]],"96":[[1,"100","10","Science-Based Decision Support Tools Optimization","Optimize the use of science-based decision support tools and methodologies",""],[1,"100","36","Joint Planning, Monitoring, and Budgeting Coordination Mechanism","Strengthen coordination and convergence of government agencies in undertaking joint planning, and monitoring, and budgeting for priority programs and projects",""],[1,"110","5","Agriculture Management Information Systems Targeting Mechanism","Utilize and regularly update the A&F management information systems as a strategic targeting mechanism for identification and prioritization of beneficiaries and agriculture-related programs and services (e.g., RSBSA, ABEMIS, etc.).",""],[1,"111","1","Registry Updating and Cross-Referencing for Agriculture and Fishery Beneficiaries","The RSBSA will also be regularly updated, harmonized, and cross-referenced with existing registries such as the Municipal Fisherfolk Registry (FishR) of BFAR, Listahanan or the National Household Targeting System for Poverty Reduction (NHTS-PR) of the Department of Social Welfare and Development (DSWD).","Department of Social Welfare and Development (DSWD) | BFAR"],[1,"111","2","Integrated Road for Agriculture Development (IROAD) Platform","The DA initiative on establishing an online platform for transparency, inter-agency data sharing, and a science-based approach to FMR planning and implementation will be enhanced to develop an Integrated Road for Agriculture Development (IROAD) that will store, consolidate, and manage GIS- based data of all FMR projects implemented by the government.",""],[1,"111","2","Agricultural and Biosystems Engineering Management Information System Harmonization","It may further be harmonized with the Agricultural and Biosystems Engineering Management Information System (ABEMIS) of the Bureau of Agricultural and Fisheries Engineering (BAFE) which contains geotagged data on machineries and equipment provided, postharvest and logistics facilities established, and FMRs completed.",""],[1,"111","2","Accessible FMR Data Sharing System","These systems should be made available, accessible and easily understandable by the AFF stakeholders to help them make informed decisions and guide future investments.",""],[1,"112","7","Coconut Farmers and Industry Trust Fund Management Committee","It will create a Trust Fund Management Committee consisting of representatives from oversight agencies, that is distinct from the PCA Board, to remove the conflict of interest in the previous vetoed version of the bill where PCA is both the approving agency and utilizing agency of the proposed trust fund.",""],[1,"112","7","Coconut Industry Development and Rehabilitation Plan","A Coconut Farmers and Industry Development Plan will also be drafted to set the directions and policies for the development and rehabilitation of the coconut industry in the long-term.",""]],"97":[[1,"100","18","Climate- and Disaster-Resilient Production Technology Adoption","Development and adoption of modern, climate and disaster-resilient production technologies intensified",""],[1,"100","38","AFF Value Chain Resilience Enhancement","Intensify activities on enhancing resilience of the AFF value chain to climate and disaster risks",""],[1,"111","3","Permanent El Nino Task Force","Institutionalize the El Nino Task Force as a permanent body rather than an ad-hoc task force, to ensure the preparedness of the AFF sector",""],[1,"111","5","AFF Sector Resilience Strengthening","Intensify activities on increasing resilience of the AFF sector to climate and disaster risks (See Chapter 20).",""],[1,"112","2","Non-Farm Livelihood Diversification and Training Programme","Provide non-farm livelihood options especially to seasonal and disaster-affected farm and fishery workers, SFF, and their families.",""]],"98":[[1,"117","18","Digital Consumer Protection Strengthening","Promote and strengthen consumer protection to cover digital transactions",""],[1,"120","3","Reduction of Online Participation Costs","Reduce online participation costs for businesses and consumers.",""],[1,"120","7","Broadband Cost Reduction Policies and Programs","15 DICT has ongoing policies and programs that aim to reduce costs of broadband and internet services: roll-out of the third telecommunication player's program and Common Tower Policy.","DICT"],[1,"120","8","Cybersecurity Policy Development and Interagency Coordination","DICT has a Cybersecurity Bureau that develops cybersecurity policies and coordinates with other agencies on consumer right's protection of citizens.","DICT"],[1,"132","3","Secure Digital Banking and Cashless Payment Platforms","IT-enabled platforms that allow the financial system to provide secure digital banking and cashless payment systems will be important.",""],[1,"136","3","Digital Financial Infrastructure Development","Develop the country's digital financial infrastructure to ensure the readiness of the financial system to shift towards a cash-lite economy",""],[1,"136","3","MSME Digital Financing Infrastructure","To support MSMEs, financial infrastructures such as digital supply chain financing, online collateral registry, credit risk database, and credit information and guarantee system, should be established to address fundamental issues that constrain sustained private sector involvement in MSME financing.",""],[1,"136","4","Digital Payments Expansion and Governance Support","The government will engage key stakeholders in both public and private sectors to broaden the use of digital payment platforms and ensure that these are supported by robust infrastructure and digital governance standards.",""],[1,"140","5","Financial Sector Cybersecurity and Online Transaction Regulation","Encourage financial institutions to implement better cybersecurity measures and regulations for online transactions.",""],[1,"140","6","Insurance Awareness Information and Education Campaigns","Promote awareness on insurance policies through various information and education campaigns.",""],[1,"140","7","Digital Literacy Program for Digital Financial Services","Promote digital literacy to increase consumer capability and confidence in using digital financial services and e-payments.",""],[1,"147","5","Digital Payments and Open Banking Expansion","Initiatives such as merchant acceptance of digital payments, digital banks, and open banking will be pursued to promote access to and use of digital financial transactions.",""],[1,"147","9","Digital Payments Transformation Roadmap","These initiatives are under the BSP's Digital Payments Transformation Roadmap (DPTR) 2020-2023.",""]],"99":[[1,"135","1","High-Value Services and Supporting Industries Development Support","Support the development of high-value services sectors and backbone/supporting industries to strengthen linkages of the sector into the domestic and global value chains, as well as address agglomeration, economies of scale, and gaps in the supply and value chains.",""],[1,"135","1","Pandemic-Affected Company Diversification Support","Assist companies affected by the pandemic to diversify to more productive and relevant high-value services that can be easily integrated into the global value chain.",""],[1,"135","2","IT-BPM Industry Support and Enabling Environment Measures","Facilitate the growth of the IT-BPM industry through improved access to quality ICT infrastructure, affordable power, and logistics costs, and an enabling regulatory environment, among others.",""],[1,"135","2","Alternative Working Arrangements for Social Distancing","Alternative working arrangements should be adopted to conform to social distancing protocols.",""],[1,"151","4","IT-BPM Sector Survey on MSMEs","The Department of Information and Communications Technology (DICT) is working with the Philippine Institute for Development Studies (PIDS) on an upcoming survey on the IT BPM sector (FY2020) that shall yield data on MSMEs in the sector.","Department of Information and Communications Technology | Philippine Institute for Development Studies"]],"100":[[1,"123","1","Labor Mobility Facilitation under ASEAN Community Vision 2025","Once infection is managed, labor mobility within Southeast Asia, as part of the ASEAN Community Vision 2025, will be pursued.",""],[1,"123","1","Mutual Recognition Arrangements for Professional Mobility","Mutual recognition arrangements (MRAs) will help Filipino professionals acquire new knowledge and experience overseas and create new networks for professional growth.",""],[1,"176","1","Internationalization of Education Guidelines and Regulatory Frameworks","Formulate guidelines on the internationalization of education.",""],[1,"176","2","PQF Operationalization Action Plan","Develop an action plan to operationalize the Philippine Qualifications Framework (PQF).",""]],"101":[[1,"164","3","Sexual and Reproductive Health Service Intensification","Sexual and reproductive health services will be intensified to address adolescent or early pregnancy.",""],[1,"164","3","Comprehensive Sexuality Education in Schools","DepEd will ensure that there will be comprehensive sexuality education in schools, to include adolescent-friendly health service packages.","DepEd"],[1,"164","3","Reproductive Health Demand- and Supply-Side Interventions","POPCOM and DOH will spearhead and intensify demand- and supply-side interventions for improving reproductive health services, including addressing unmet need for modern family planning (FP).","POPCOM | DOH"],[1,"164","3","Community and Facility-Based Demand Generation Scale-Up","These include scaling up community and facility-based demand generation interventions, and ensuring availability of FP commodities at service delivery points by instituting reforms and enhancements in the FP logistics system.",""],[1,"164","3","Family Planning Logistics System Reform","These include scaling up community and facility-based demand generation interventions, and ensuring availability of FP commodities at service delivery points by instituting reforms and enhancements in the FP logistics system.",""],[1,"164","3","Family Planning Competency-Based Training for Health Providers","FP competency-based training for health providers will be continuously provided (see Chapter 13).",""],[1,"164","3","Uninterrupted Family Planning and Reproductive Health Service Delivery","Uninterrupted provision of FP and reproductive health services and commodities, especially in areas under enhanced and general community quarantine, will be pursued.",""],[1,"212","20","Adolescent Pregnancy Reduction and Family Planning Access","The focus will be on reducing adolescent pregnancy and addressing unmet demand for family planning among couples and individuals.",""],[1,"213","2","Population Management and Reproductive Health Policy Strengthening","Population management and reproductive health policies and programs will be strengthened to assist couples and individuals achieve their desired number of children (wanted fertility rate) within the context of responsible parenthood and informed choice.",""],[1,"213","2","Intensified NPPFP Implementation","These include the intensified implementation of the NPPFP, which involves collaborative management between the DOH and the POPCOM; and coordinated efforts among partner government agencies (e.g., Department of Education, Department of the Interior and Local Government, etc.).","DOH | POPCOM | Department of Education | Department of the Interior and Local Government"],[1,"213","2","Local and Multi-Stakeholder Reproductive Health Partnerships","Strengthened participation of local government units (LGUs) and expanded partnerships with civil society organizations (CSOs) will be pursued.",""],[1,"213","2","Reproductive Health Commodity and Service Delivery Partnerships","Development partners and the private sector will also be engaged to allow for effective and efficient delivery of quality reproductive health and family planning commodities and services.",""],[1,"213","3","Family Planning Demand Generation and Advocacy Campaign","A nationwide age-group-focused multimedia campaign will be pursued by the DOH and POPCOM to raise the level of awareness and knowledge on the importance and benefits of family planning - from a health intervention to a means to improve family outcomes.","DOH | POPCOM"],[1,"213","3","Adolescent Sexual and Reproductive Health Information and Counseling Services","To further widen the reach of these activities while adhering to new normal protocols, interactive forms of communication (e.g., telephone hotlines and online platforms) will be employed to provide adolescent sexual and reproductive health information and counseling.",""],[1,"213","3","Integration of Reproductive Health Information in Existing Programs","Adolescent sexual and reproductive health and family planning (RP/FP) information will likewise be continuously incorporated in relevant programs and activities such as pre-marriage orientation and counseling, Pantawid Pamilyang Pilipino Program Family Development Sessions, and other programs for employees or RP/FP in the workplace conducted by the Department of Labor and Employment and Civil Service Commission, among others.","Department of Labor and Employment | Civil Service Commission"],[1,"213","4","Family Planning and Adolescent Reproductive Health Service Expansion","Strengthen provision of family planning services, adolescent sexual and reproductive health commodities and services.",""],[1,"214","1","Interoperable Commodities Tracking System","through interoperable commodities tracking system across national and local facilities.",""],[1,"214","1","Minimum Initial Service Package for Sexual and Reproductive Health in Emergencies","In times of emergencies and other disasters, the Minimum Initial Service Package (MISP)3 for sexual and reproductive health services will be provided.",""],[1,"214","1","Postpartum and Family Planning Outreach and Counseling Services","Postpartum family planning and family planning outreach missions and counseling services will be intensified.",""],[1,"214","2","Local Stakeholder Capacity Building for Family Planning and Reproductive Health Services","there will be continued capacity building of local stakeholders specifically for local chief executives, local health officers, and local health service providers.",""],[1,"214","2","Family Planning Competency-Based Training for Health Providers","Community volunteers, local government health workers, and private sector providers will be capacitated in delivering family planning and reproductive health services (i.e., Family Planning Competency-Based Training for health providers).",""],[1,"214","2","Leadership and Governance Capacity Building for Local Health Systems","Local chief executives will also be provided with leadership and governance capability building programs for health that can improve local health systems and make them more responsive to the health needs of their constituency.",""],[1,"214","3","Adolescent Sexual and Reproductive Health Services","Hence, to prevent unplanned repeat pregnancies, age-appropriate adolescent sexual and reproductive health services, including family planning, will be provided to sexually active adolescents and those who have already given birth.",""],[1,"214","3","Comprehensive Sexual Education Implementation","The focus will be on ensuring the full implementation of the Comprehensive Sexual Education (CSE) in line with the RPRH Law.",""],[1,"214","3","Adolescent-Friendly Health Service Package Development","Adolescent-friendly health service packages will also be developed to address the age group's unique needs in terms of correct information and access to adolescent sexual and reproductive health services, including HIV.",""],[1,"214","3","Teen Center and Adolescent-Friendly Facility Establishment","These activities will be implemented along with the establishment and sustainability of teen centers and adolescent-friendly facilities or spaces in LGUs and schools, and developmental activities for the youth (e.g., sports, socialization, volunteerism, etc.).",""],[1,"214","3","Online Youth Communication and Outreach Strategy","Innovative and interactive forms of communication strategies to reach the youth will also be employed, such as the use of social media and other online media platforms, cellphone applications, and call or text hotlines.",""],[1,"214","3","Youth-Oriented Media Program Development","Youth- oriented TV and other media programs will be developed to reach the youth and encourage them to make productive use of their time.",""],[1,"214","3","Interagency Adolescent Health Coordination and SK Capacity Building","To this end, coordinated efforts among concerned government agencies will be pursued, including the mobilization of and capacity building for the Sangguniang Kabataan (youth council) to promote adolescent sexual and reproductive health and youth development programs among their constituency.",""],[1,"218","4","Establishment and Operation of Population Offices","This will provide for the establishment and operation of population offices to allow for the effective implementation of population management strategies and measures at the local level.",""],[1,"218","4","National Program of Action and Investment Plan for Teenage Pregnancy Prevention","This will facilitate the development of a National Program of Action and Investment Plan for the prevention of teenage pregnancy.",""],[1,"218","4","Interagency and Inter-sectoral Collaboration Framework on Teenage Pregnancy","The program of action will serve as a national framework for interagency and inter-sectoral collaboration at all levels to address the various health, cultural, socioeconomic, and institutional determinants of teenage pregnancy.",""],[1,"218","4","Legal Instrument for Teenage Pregnancy Prevention Policy","The policy may be issued in the form of either an Executive Order or a Republic Act.",""]],"102":[[1,"172","5","Early Childhood Care and Development Strengthening Program","Strengthen the implementation of the Early Childhood Care and Development (ECCD).",""]],"103":[[1,"173","3","Joint TVET Quality Assurance Bodies","Set up joint industry and government bodies for technical and vocational education and training (TVET) quality assurance.",""],[1,"174","3","TVET Standards and Diploma Program Development","The TVET sector will formulate standards and promote TVET programs (diploma courses) that cultivate higher-order thinking skills demanded by the labor market.",""]],"104":[[1,"180","2","Internship, Apprenticeship, and Dual Training Expansion","Strengthen and expand internship, apprenticeship, and dual training programs.",""],[1,"180","2","Government-Industry-Academe Training Linkages","The government will likewise forge stronger government-industry-academe linkages to provide quality workplace-based and/or remote and tech-based training opportunities for the youth by designing academic and training curricula that are responsive to the skills needed by the industry and establishing employer-led learning networks.",""],[1,"184","9","Enterprise-Based Training Harmonization Law","This proposed law aims to integrate and harmonize all existing enterprise- based training modalities like Apprenticeship, Dual Training System, On-the- Job Training, Work Immersion.",""],[1,"185","6","Apprenticeship Program Reform","Specifically, EO No. 111, s. 1986 that sets the maximum duration of apprenticeship programs must be repealed.",""]],"105":[[1,"181","4","Expanded Unemployment Benefits","the unemployment benefits of the SSS will need to be expanded to assist temporarily laid-off workers.",""],[1,"181","4","Comprehensive Unemployment Support Program","the government will seek to design a more comprehensive unemployment support program that will provide workers more flexibility to search for jobs by improving their skills and capacity as they re-enter the labor market",""],[1,"181","4","Review and Strengthen Financial Assistance Programs","financial assistance programs for displaced formal sector and informal sector workers will be reviewed and strengthened for possible institutionalization.",""],[1,"191","27","Unemployment Insurance Access and Related Services Expansion","Enhance peoples' access to unemployment insurance and related services",""],[1,"191","34","Unemployment Insurance Study","Conduct further studies on unemployment insurance",""],[1,"196","4","National Unemployment Insurance Information Drive","The SSS, in partnership with other relevant agencies, will implement an information drive on UI nationwide.",""],[1,"196","4","Unemployment Insurance Digital Application System Upgrade","the SSS will also fast-track systemic upgrade to allow for digital application and transactions.",""],[1,"196","5","Unemployment Insurance Linkage to Active Labor Market Services","the SSS UI will be tightly linked to active labor market policies.","DOLE"],[1,"196","5","Upskilling and Retooling Training for UI Recipients","Simultaneously, upskilling and retooling trainings will be offered by concerned stakeholders including TESDA to UI recipients to improve their skills and qualifications given the new normal.","TESDA"],[1,"196","6","Unemployment Insurance Reform Studies","To further improve the country's unemployment insurance system, studies will be conducted to explore the creation of a separate program fund, UI linkage to active labor market policies, optimal benefits (i.e. higher compensation benefit or longer duration of benefit), and the criteria to avail the benefits, especially during pandemic, among others.",""],[1,"196","6","Actuarial Study for Unemployment Insurance Reforms","Furthermore, to ensure financial viability, the proposed reforms to the unemployment insurance system should be supported by an actuarial study.",""]],"106":[[1,"191","31","Proactive Disaster Preparedness Promotion","Promote proactive disaster preparedness among individuals",""],[1,"197","2","Proactive Disaster Preparedness Information and Advocacy Campaigns","Filipinos will be informed and encouraged to use existing tools such as the DOST's HazardHunterPH12 to understand natural hazards and help mitigate their effects.",""],[1,"197","2","Fire and Earthquake Drill Programme","Fire and earthquake drills will also be conducted in urban and rural areas.",""]],"107":[[1,"191","40","DRRM Stakeholder Capacity Building and Service Coordination","Continue building capacities of DRRM stakeholders and improve coordination of services",""],[1,"197","6","Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Capacity Building and Coordination","Continue building the capacities of disaster risk reduction and management (DRRM) stakeholders and improve coordination of services.",""],[1,"197","6","DRRM Information Campaigns, Trainings, and Drills","The NDRRMC will coordinate and spearhead information campaigns, trainings, and drills for DRRM stakeholders, as well as the purchase of early warning and emergency devices.","NDRRMC"],[1,"197","6","Disaster and Climate Vulnerability Assessment and Hazard Mapping","These efforts will be supported by data and information through the conduct of disaster and climate vulnerability and risk assessments and the production of hazard maps.",""],[1,"198","1","Post-Disaster Needs Assessment Mechanism","the NDRRMC will provide mechanisms for the conduct of post or rapid disaster needs assessment.",""],[1,"198","1","Disaster Response Coordination Framework","Coordination between responders and aid organizations will be clearly defined to avoid inefficiencies and to ensure that all disaster victims are provided with support.",""],[1,"198","1","Disaster IEC, Orientation, and Communication Systems","This entails the production and dissemination of IEC materials, conduct of related orientation seminars, and establishment of communication systems so that concerned service providers, including non-government organizations, have a clear understanding of their roles and responsibilities during disasters and emergencies.",""]],"108":[[1,"201","1","Building Adequate, Livable, Affordable, and Inclusive Filipino Communities (BALAI) Program","The sector will operationalize the Building Adequate, Livable, Affordable, and Inclusive Filipino Communities (BALAI) program.","Department of Human Settlements and Urban Development (DHSUD)"],[1,"203","1","Hazard- and Health-Standard Housing Production Acceleration","Second, housing production that incorporates hazard and health standards will be accelerated.",""],[1,"203","1","Alternative Housing Solutions for Low-Income Households","Third, alternative housing solutions for low-income market will be adopted.",""],[1,"203","6","Alternative Housing Solutions for Low-Income Market","Adoption of alternative housing solutions for low-income market",""],[1,"203","15","Safe, Livable, and Resilient Housing Production","Include production of safe, livable and resilient housing in the COVID-19 recovery and resiliency program",""],[1,"203","17","High-Density Housing Program Expansion","Upscale high-density housing programs in highly urbanized communities (HUCs)",""],[1,"205","2","Accelerated Housing Production Programme","the government will accelerate housing production, following urban development and housing framework, and incorporating hazard and health standards.",""],[1,"206","2","Safe, Livable, and Resilient Housing Production Program","Include production of safe, livable, and resilient housing in the COVID-19 recovery and resiliency program.",""],[1,"206","2","Human Settlements and Urban Development Program Expansion","it is imperative that the government elevate the human settlements and urban development programs as part of the COVID-19 recovery and resiliency plan and ensure its continuous delivery of services.",""],[1,"206","4","High-Density Housing Program Expansion","Upscale high-density housing programs in highly urbanized cities (HUCs).",""],[1,"207","1","Alternative Housing Solutions for Low-Income Households","To make housing more affordable for low-income market, alternative housing solutions will be adopted.",""]],"109":[[1,"201","2","Department of Human Settlements and Urban Development Consolidation","There is a paradigm shift from housing production to management of housing, human settlements, and urban development which catalyzed the creation of the DHSUD, consolidating the functions of the Housing and Urban Development Coordinating Council (HUDCC) and the regulatory functions of the Housing and Land Use Regulatory Board (HLURB).",""],[1,"203","8","National Urban Development and Housing Framework Implementation","Implement the National Urban Development and Housing Framework (NUDHF) 2017-2022",""],[1,"203","10","Mainstream Local Shelter Planning in CLUPs","Mainstream local shelter planning that integrates public health goals in the Comprehensive Land Use Plans (CLUPs) of cities and municipalities",""],[1,"203","11","Whole-of-Government Voluntary Resettlement Mainstreaming","Fully mainstream whole-of-government action in voluntary resettlement initiatives",""],[1,"203","14","Operationalization of the National Resettlement Policy Framework","Operationalize the National Resettlement Policy Framework (NRPF)",""],[1,"204","3","Local Shelter Planning Institutionalization Program","As a tool to address its public housing provision, the DHSUD shall institutionalize local shelter planning through the Local Shelter Program (LSP) in cities and municipalities as provided for in the Local Government Code of 1991 (RA 7160) and the Urban Development and Housing Act (UDHA) of 1992 (RA 7279).","DHSUD"],[1,"204","3","Risk-Informed Local Shelter Planning Guidelines","To operationalize the LSP, implementing guidelines and strategies that will provide technical assistance to LGUs in the formulation of a risk- informed LSP to address resiliency and mitigate impacts of disaster/calamity to households shall be developed.",""],[1,"204","3","Local Shelter Plan Management and Monitoring System","A Local Government Shelter Plan Management and Monitoring System shall be established to ensure efficient delivery of housing, financing, and other housing/shelter interventions to targeted beneficiaries.",""],[1,"204","3","BALAI Seal Compliance Incentive for Approved Local Shelter Plans","To incentivize its formulation, an approved LSP will be a requirement in DHSUD's issuance of the BALAI seal of compliance.","DHSUD"],[1,"205","1","National Resettlement Policy Framework Implementation","Operationalize the National Resettlement Policy Framework (NRPF).","DHSUD"],[1,"205","3","National Urban Development and Housing Framework Implementation","Implement the National Urban Development and Housing Framework (NUDHF) 2017-2022.",""],[1,"205","3","Urban Planning Integration into Local Development Instruments","These will be incorporated in Comprehensive Land Use Plans (CLUPs), Zoning Ordinances, Comprehensive Development Plans, and Local Shelter Plans which will guide urbanization that supports equitable growth and promotes uniquely Filipino cities and municipalities.",""],[1,"205","4","Balik Probinsya, Bagong Pag-asa Program Implementation","To ensure sustainability in the voluntary resettlement initiatives of the government, the Balik Probinsya, Bagong Pag-asa (BP2) program will be fully implemented through complementary initiatives while sustaining established community safety and health standards.",""],[1,"207","4","Community-Led Human Settlements Development Guidelines","The DHSUD will empower stakeholders by institutionalizing community-led/driven development of human settlements as a crosscutting strategy to ensure sustainability of its program implementation.",""],[1,"208","3","National Land Use Act Amendments and NHMFC Charter Passage","Passage of the National Land Use Act (NaLUA) Amendments to the NHMFC Charter",""],[1,"208","4","National Land Use Framework","Establish a national land use framework that will define the indicative priorities for land utilization and allocation across residential, infrastructure, agricultural, and protective uses and integrate efforts, monitor developments related to land use, and evolve policies, regulations and directions of land use planning processes.",""],[1,"208","6","Mandatory Creation of Local Housing Boards","Provide for mandatory creation of Local Housing Boards in every city and first to third class municipality to ensure full cascading of the government housing policies and programs to the local government; and ensure the sustained implementation of national and local housing programs.",""],[1,"208","7","National Housing Authority Charter Renewal and Institutional Strengthening","Renew the NHA Charter and strengthen its organizational structure and functions.",""]],"110":[[1,"236","1","Tax Reform, Spending Efficiency, and Debt Management Measures","the fiscal position also remains sustainable and supportive of growth with the pursuit of tax reforms, improved spending efficiency, and prudent debt management",""],[1,"236","2","Responsive Fiscal Policy Reform","fiscal policy will be made more responsive through enabling budget and policies, enhanced local government units (LGUs) capacity, and improved private sector participation.",""],[1,"242","6","Strategic Revenue Policy and Administrative Measures","Implement strategic revenue policy and administrative measures",""],[1,"242","9","Expenditure Prioritization and Management Reform","Realign expenditure priorities and implement expenditure management reforms",""],[1,"242","21","Strategic Budget Realignment and Expenditure Reprioritization","To facilitate transition and adjustment to the New Normal, the government will implement strategic realignment of its budget and reprioritize its expenditures over the near-term.",""],[1,"243","3","Fast-Track Priority Tax Reform Measures","Fast-track the implementation of priority tax reform measures.",""],[1,"243","3","Digital Taxation Framework Establishment and Institutionalization","the establishment and institutionalization of a digital taxation framework",""],[1,"243","3","Completion of Remaining Tax Reform Packages","the passage of the remaining packages of the tax reform program",""],[1,"243","3","Tax Administration Modernization Measures","These policy reforms will be complemented by tax administration measures, particularly the fuel marking and Electronic Receipt and Invoice System",""],[1,"243","4","Local Revenue Enhancement Measures","Increase local sources of revenue by introducing legislated and non-legislated measures.",""],[1,"243","4","Real Property Valuation Reform","Foremost is the passage of the Real Property Valuation reform, which can help augment property tax collection of LGUs.",""],[1,"243","4","LGU Financing Capacity Building","Legislative measures will also be supplemented with capacity building activities to enable LGUs to access other sources of financing, such as official development grants.",""],[1,"252","3","National Internal Revenue Code Reform","Amend the National Internal Revenue Code of 1997 to achieve a simpler, fairer, and more efficient tax system.",""],[1,"252","3","Corporate Tax and Fiscal Incentives Reform","The measure aims to institute reforms in the corporate tax system (e.g., reduce corporate income tax rate) and the fiscal incentives system, directing them toward strategic growth industries, to attract greater foreign investment and generate more jobs.",""],[1,"252","5","Digital Taxation Framework","There is a need to establish a digital taxation framework given the expected shift of the private sector to online transactions amid the new normal.",""],[1,"252","7","Military and Uniformed Personnel Pension Reform","Introduce reforms in the Military and Uniformed Personnel (MUP)'s pension system, which among others include (a) mandatory contribution scheme and (b) increase in the compulsory retirement age, to curb the ballooning pension costs and to ensure fiscal sustainability.",""],[1,"252","9","Public Financial Management Reform","Institute sound Public Financial Management (PFM) practices to promote transparency, accountability, and efficiency in the use of public resources.",""],[1,"252","11","Exemption of Priority Infrastructure Projects from Election Ban","Amend certain sections of the Omnibus Election Code (OEC) to allow the exemption of key priority infrastructure projects from the ban during the election period in order to ensure the timely implementation of these projects.",""],[1,"252","12","Update the Government Auditing Code","Update the 1976 Government Auditing Code of the Philippines (Presidential Decree 1445)",""],[1,"252","13","Revision of the Government Auditing Code","Revise the outdated provisions of the Government Auditing Code considering the technological advancements, innovations, and other changes in the conduct of government auditing across the globe.",""]],"111":[[1,"236","1","Monetary and Non-Monetary Inflation Management Measures","Headline inflation rate was generally within target with the implementation of appropriate monetary and non- monetary policy measures",""],[1,"236","2","Financial System Supervisory Reform","Targeted supervisory actions and reforms that address the impact of the pandemic remain crucial in fostering the resilience of the country's financial system.",""],[1,"242","7","Flexible Inflation Targeting Framework","Maintain a flexible inflation targeting framework for monetary policy formulation",""],[1,"242","8","Foreign Exchange Reserve and Exchange Rate Management","Maintain adequate foreign exchange reserves and market-determined exchange rate",""],[1,"242","10","Macro-Prudential Financial Stability Measures","Pursue financial stability through macro-prudential measures",""],[1,"242","13","Micro-Prudential Financial Supervision and Consumer Protection Measures","Use micro-prudential measures to promote financial institution soundness and nurture consumer protection",""],[1,"242","15","Capital Market Development Initiative","· Foster capital market development",""],[1,"244","2","Contingent Liability Risk Management Safeguards","In addition, ensuring that risks related to contingent liabilities are well-managed could safeguard resilience of the country's fiscal position to future shocks, such as pandemics.",""],[1,"244","3","Fiscal Recovery Plan Communication Strategy","To manage market expectations and ensure stability, the national government will carefully and clearly communicate its recovery plan, as well as the temporary nature of deviation from the medium-term fiscal program.",""],[1,"244","4","Monetary Operations Refinement and Interest Rate Corridor System","The BSP will continue to refine its monetary operations, including through the interest rate corridor system, to enhance its capacity in guiding short-term market interest rates to move closely with the policy rate.","BSP"],[1,"244","4","BSP Charter Amendment for Securities Issuance","The amendments to the BSP's charter - particularly on allowing it to issue its own securities - will further expand its policy toolkit and give it more flexibility in determining the size and timing of its monetary operations.","BSP"],[1,"244","4","Monetary Policy Easing and Regulatory Relief Measures","The BSP is ready to ease monetary policy settings further and to deploy regulatory relief measures as needed, especially amid the sustained uncertainty brought about by the COVID-19 pandemic.","BSP"],[1,"244","4","Domestic and International Economic Risk Monitoring","It will continue to vigilantly monitor domestic and international developments for any emerging risks to the outlook for both inflation and economic activity.",""],[1,"244","5","Macroprudential Financial Stability Measures","Pursue financial stability through macro-prudential measures.",""],[1,"245","1","Financial Stability Agenda Guidance Framework","underway will provide guidance on how financial authorities will execute the financial stability agenda and handle systemic risks in the Philippine financial system.",""],[1,"246","3","Micro-prudential Regulatory Relief and Supervisory Measures","Amid the COVID-19 crisis, regulatory relief measures have been implemented to support financial institutions and ensure liquidity flow into the economy.",""],[1,"246","3","Financial Sector Transparency and Communication Measures","Communication and transparency between the financial institutions, regulators, and the public will remain essential to provide a true picture of the financial position of an institution and guide regulators in designing appropriate policy responses.",""],[1,"246","4","Insurance Sector Monitoring and Information Campaigns","Strengthen monitoring of insurance sector and expand information campaigns on available products and services.",""],[1,"247","2","Foreign Exchange Reserve Management and Exchange Rate Stability Measures","Maintain adequate foreign exchange reserves and a market-determined exchange rate.",""],[1,"247","2","Operational Relief Measures for Foreign Exchange Transactions","Lastly, amid the COVID-19 pandemic, the BSP implemented operational relief measures for FX transactions to help stabilize market conditions and restore confidence.",""],[1,"253","4","Financial Sector Stability Support","Aims to maintain the financial health of banks and other financial institutions in order to cushion the adverse economic impact of the COVID-19 pandemic.",""]],"112":[[1,"245","4","Capital Market Development and Transparency Measures","Developing the domestic capital market and increasing the efficiency in trading of securities will be facilitated by policies such as the use of forwards in lieu of spot prices, consolidation of the current exposures into fewer but deeper benchmark tenors, transparent and accessible pricing, and expansion of local investment options.",""],[1,"245","4","Timely Disclosure and Investor Confidence Measures","Increased transparency such as through a timely disclosure of delayed payments and contracts with cross-default provisions will help boost investor confidence.",""],[1,"245","4","Collective Investment Schemes Act Passage","Passage of the Collective Investment Schemes (CIS) Act, will harmonize its tax and regulatory framework, provide an even playing field, and the same level of protection to the investing public.",""],[1,"245","4","Corporate Debt Funds Regulatory Framework","The SEC is drafting the rules on Corporate Debt Funds, which will invest primarily in debt papers of large corporations and medium- sized enterprises that need liquidity to support their capital and operating costs to sustain their businesses, especially those affected by the pandemic.","SEC"],[1,"245","4","Package 4 of the Comprehensive Tax Reform Program","the passage of the proposed Package 4 of the Comprehensive Tax Reform Program (CTRP) can level the playing field and remove tax arbitrage between subsectors of finance by reducing and harmonizing withholding taxes across instruments and minimizing friction costs by eliminating the Initial Public Offering tax.",""],[1,"245","6","Domestic Financial Market Development and Consumer Protection Reform","Support reforms and initiatives that aim to develop the domestic financial market and expand consumer protection.",""],[1,"245","6","Financial Consumer Protection Law","The proposed Financial Consumer Protection Law will provide a comprehensive financial consumer protection regime and empower financial regulators to implement specific enforcement actions.",""],[1,"246","2","Islamic Finance Regulatory Framework Development","Develop the regulatory framework for Islamic finance in the country.",""],[1,"246","2","ADB Technical Assistance for Islamic Financial Services Expansion","there is an ongoing technical assistance from the ADB to expand Islamic financial services in the Philippines, which include capacity building programs to discuss Islamic finance.",""],[1,"252","18","Financial Consumer Protection Law Enactment","Enactment of the Financial Consumer Protection Law",""],[1,"252","19","Financial Consumer Protection Regulatory Empowerment","Empower financial regulators to formulate and implement rules and regulations, conduct surveillance and examination, monitor supervised entities, and have enforcement powers relative to financial consumer protection.",""],[1,"252","21","Financial Transparency and Financial Crime Compliance Reform","Make financial institutions comply with international standards on transparency and help facilitate investigations on tax evasion, money laundering and other financial crimes.",""],[1,"252","23","Securities Code Amendment for SEC Enforcement Powers","Amend outdated provisions of the Code to enable SEC to enforce its rules and regulations relative to its supervision over the corporate sector, the capital market participants, the securities and investment instruments market, and the investing public.",""],[1,"252","25","Collective Investment Schemes Regulatory and Legal Framework","Provide a comprehensive regulatory and legal framework for Collective Investment Schemes.",""]],"113":[[1,"254","2","Competition Law Enforcement and Market Entry Reform","The Philippine Development Plan (PDP) 2017-2022 reinforces the Philippine Competition Act (PCA) through strategies that aim to foster an environment that penalizes anti-competitive practices, facilitates entry of players, supports regulatory reforms, and improves trade policies to stimulate investments and innovation and boost competitiveness.",""],[1,"255","1","Administrative Order to Strengthen the National Competition Policy","To this end, the issuance of an Administrative Order by the President is being sought to lend more strength to the Joint Memorandum Circular on the NCP that was signed by the National Economic and Development Authority (NEDA) and the Philippine Competition Commission (PCC).","National Economic and Development Authority (NEDA) | Philippine Competition Commission (PCC)"],[1,"255","1","Regulatory Environment Improvement for MSME Market Entry","Considering the economic consequences of the pandemic, improving the regulatory environment becomes even more crucial to help MSMEs enter or re-enter the market and thrive.",""],[1,"255","1","Enforcement Against Cartels and Anti-Competitive Practices","Strong enforcement against cartels and other anti-competitive practices is also essential to ensure consumer welfare protection.",""],[1,"255","1","Competition Advocacy and Public Awareness Campaign","Awareness of competition, especially in the regions remains low, thus continuous advocacy of the PCA should be pursued to increase public awareness not only of the PCA but also of the vital role of PCC in promoting competition.",""],[1,"256","6","Competition Policy and Regulatory Reform for Economic Recovery","Specifically, it focuses on sustaining promotion of competition and implementation of the PCA and other competition-related issuances to create a level playing field where small business players alongside larger ones may operate and thrive.",""],[1,"256","6","Regulatory Environment Improvement for Firm Re-entry","Improving the regulatory environment to reduce barriers to entry and facilitate the re-entry of firms that may have closed down as a result of the community quarantine restrictions will likewise be pursued.",""],[1,"256","13","Competition Law Enforcement Strengthening","Strengthen investigation, detection and prosecution of conducts and agreements that may substantially prevent, restrict or lessen competition",""],[1,"256","14","Market Scoping Studies for Priority Sectors","Conduct market scoping studies in priority sectors to facilitate competition among MSMEs",""],[1,"256","16","Competition Regulatory Reform","Improve the regulatory environment by addressing restrictive laws and regulations that hamper competition",""],[1,"256","18","Competition Assessment Manual and Toolkit Institutionalization","Institutionalize the use of the Competition Assessment Manual/Toolkit",""],[1,"256","19","National Competition Policy Implementation","Issue and implement the National Competition Policy (NCP)",""],[1,"256","20","Competition Agency Capacity Strengthening","Strengthen capacity of relevant agencies to foster competition",""],[1,"256","22","Competition Violation Reporting Mechanism Expansion","Expand the mechanism for various sectors to report on potential violations on competition",""],[1,"257","1","National Competition Policy Implementation","Issue and implement the NCP.","NEDA | PCC"],[1,"257","2","National Competition Policy Guidelines","The NCP prescribes guidelines to steer regulations and administrative procedures of government agencies to level the economic playing field.",""],[1,"257","4","Pro-Competitive Policy and Regulatory Reform","the government will ensure that all policies, laws, rules and regulations, issuances, and other interventions do not unnecessarily distort competition.",""],[1,"257","5","Competitive Neutrality Reform for GOCCs","To promote competitive neutrality, the Governance Commission for GOCCs (GCG) and Department of Budget and Management (DBM) will continue to review the mandates of GOCCs within their respective jurisdictions and make appropriate recommendations to the President to ensure, among others, the separation of proprietary and regulatory activities.","Governance Commission for GOCCs (GCG) | Department of Budget and Management (DBM)"],[1,"257","5","Guidelines on Subsidies to GOCCs","Moreover, GCG and DBM will lead in the drafting of guidelines on the grant of subsidies in favor of GOCCs based on an assessment of the nature, form, extent, and costs and benefits of these government subsidies and interventions and their impact on the business environment.","Governance Commission for GOCCs (GCG) | Department of Budget and Management (DBM)"],[1,"257","5","Regulatory and Non-regulatory Neutrality Measures","They will also implement regulatory and non-regulatory measures to neutralize any advantage or disadvantage that may accrue due to public sector ownership.","Governance Commission for GOCCs (GCG) | Department of Budget and Management (DBM)"],[1,"257","6","Competition Law Enforcement and Agency Action Alignment","the government will uphold the original and primary jurisdiction of PCC over issues involving cartel agreements, abuse of dominance by firms, anti-competitive mergers and acquisitions, and other anti-competitive behaviors.",""],[1,"257","6","Government Agency Competition Promotion Actions","all government agencies will identify specific actions within their areas of responsibility to promote competition, eliminate competitive behavior, and undue regulatory burdens on competition.",""],[1,"258","1","Competition Agency Capacity-Building Programs","PCC and the Office for Competition (OFC) under the Department of Justice will continue to implement capacity-building programs aimed at strengthening the technical competencies of the government in developing interventions and measures to address anti-competitive and other pernicious practices affecting the supply, distribution, and movement of goods and services, especially during emergencies.","Department of Justice"],[1,"258","2","Market Competition Awareness and Advocacy Campaign","PCC will sustain its grassroots campaign.",""],[1,"258","2","Citizen Complaint Desk for Anti-competitive Practices","PCC will also engage citizens to play an active role in monitoring and reporting anti-competitive practices through a complaint desk via trunkline and online platform.",""],[1,"258","3","Competition Violation Reporting Mechanism Expansion","Expand the mechanism for various sectors to report on potential violations of competition.",""],[1,"258","3","Leniency Program for Competition Law Enforcement","PCC will sustain its implementation of the Leniency Program, which offers immunity from suit or reduction of administrative fines to any entity that participates in an anti-competitive agreement1 but offers to provide information and full cooperation during the investigation and prosecution of the violation.",""],[1,"258","3","Citizen Reporting of Competition Violations","Citizens will also be encouraged to report violations of competition to the said agencies.",""],[1,"258","4","Competition Law Enforcement and Market Surveillance","Strengthen investigation, detection, and prosecution of conducts and agreements that may substantially prevent, restrict, or lessen competition.",""],[1,"258","5","Competition Law Enforcement and Anti-Cartel Monitoring","PCC will strictly monitor the prevalence of acts in violation of the PCA and other competition-related laws and issuances to protect the welfare of firms and consumers.",""],[1,"258","5","Anti-Competitive Practices Enforcement in the New Normal","It will heighten efforts in addressing anti-competitive practices in the new normal to ensure that firms do not engage in cartelistic agreements, abuse of dominance, and other anti- competitive conduct.",""],[1,"259","1","Collaborative Essential Goods and Services Delivery Arrangement","collaborative efforts among competing firms to ensure more effective and efficient delivery of essential services and articles of prime necessity in the new normal may be considered, subject to the PCA and other competition-related laws and issuances.",""],[1,"259","2","Virtual Training Platform for Prosecutors and Investigators","OFC will gear towards a virtual platform for the conduct of training for prosecutors, investigators, and staff to better enhance institutional capacity.",""],[1,"259","2","Implementation of Criminal Provisions Rules under the PCA","OFC will fully implement the recently issued Rules Implementing the Criminal Provisions of the PCA, which includes provisions for electronic filing of complaints and applications for criminal leniency.",""],[1,"259","3","Market Scoping Studies for Priority Sectors","Conduct market scoping studies in priority sectors to facilitate competition among MSMEs.","PCC | NEDA | DTI"],[1,"259","3","Continued Market Scoping Studies for MSMEs","PCC, NEDA, and DTI will continue to conduct market scoping studies in priority sectors that will provide comprehensive market analysis and identify concerns that need to be addressed.","PCC | NEDA | DTI"],[1,"259","4","Competition-Friendly Regulatory Reform","Improve the regulatory environment by addressing restrictive laws and regulations that hamper competition.",""],[1,"260","1","Competition Assessment Manual/Toolkit Adoption and Regulatory Integration","PCC will adopt the Competition Assessment Manual/Toolkit in identifying and reviewing potentially anti-competitive laws and regulations that address several development objectives but have unwarranted consequences on market competition.",""],[1,"261","1","Market Competition Legislation Package","government will work towards the passage of the following key legislation:",""]],"114":[[1,"264","13","National Plan to End Local Communist Armed Conflict Implementation","Effectively implement the National Plan to End Local Communist Armed Conflict 2019-2022 that will operationalize the whole-of-nation approach to address local communist and other armed conflicts",""],[1,"266","1","National Plan to End Local Communist Armed Conflict Implementation","Effectively implement the National Plan to End Local Communist Armed Conflict 2019-2022 that will operationalize the whole-of-nation approach to address local communist and other armed conflicts.",""],[1,"266","1","Inter-Cluster Convergence and Coordination Mechanism","The NTF- ELCAC will ensure inter-cluster convergence of efforts in addressing community armed-conflict issues.",""],[1,"266","1","Barangay Development Program Localization of Interventions","In addition, these task forces and LOEs will support and complement action plans to address the impact of the pandemic at the national, regional, and local levels, including the localization of interventions through the Barangay Development Program (BDP).",""],[1,"266","1","Referral Protocol Streamlining for Monitoring and Response","Referral protocols for monitoring and response will also be streamlined to improve vertical and horizontal connectivity of various cluster mechanisms.",""],[1,"266","6","Regional Task Force Creation","The regional task forces are created through the convergence of the Regional Peace and Order Councils and the Regional Development Councils, and are headed by the Cabinet Officers for Regional Development and Security.",""],[1,"266","8","Barangay Peace and Development Convergence Initiative","The BDP is a peace and development convergence initiative of the NTF-ELCAC which provides socioeconomic interventions, (e.g., farm to market roads, school buildings, health stations, livelihood support, etc.) to communist terrorist groups-cleared barangays.","NTF-ELCAC"],[1,"266","9","Lakbay Kapayapaan Roadmap","The Lakbay Kapayapaan Roadmap aims to institutionalize and champion sustainable peace and development agenda at the grassroots by continuously building strong and capable institutions, strategic partnership of government and non-government organizations, and heightened citizen participation through whole-of-nation approach to establish and sustain peaceful, progressive, and resilient communities.",""],[1,"267","4","Peace and Development Intervention Convergence Mechanism","Strengthen convergence and complementation in the implementation of peace and development interventions.",""],[1,"267","5","Inter-agency Programming and Agency-Level Budget Prioritization Strengthening","Inter-agency programming and agency-level budget prioritization need to be strengthened in light of foreseen priorities towards addressing the impact of the COVID-19 pandemic.",""]],"115":[[1,"264","14","Localized Peace Engagements and Community Dialogue Initiative","Effectively undertake localized peace engagements through community problem solving sessions and local peace dialogues with local insurgent groups",""],[1,"266","2","Localized Peace Engagements and Community Peace Dialogues","Effectively undertake localized peace engagements through community consultations and problem- solving sessions, and local peace dialogues with local insurgent groups.",""],[1,"266","2","Lakbay Kapayapaan Roadmap Mainstreaming","The Lakbay Kapayapaan Roadmap for Peace and Development6 will be mainstreamed as the primary mechanism to support localized peace dialogues in communities based on mutual confidence and trust.",""],[1,"266","2","Capacity Building for Local Peace Dialogue Actors","the government will prioritize the enhancement of capacities of local chief executives and the strengthening of the role of local government units (LGUs) in carrying out peace dialogues, and the complementation and convergence of socioeconomic packages to communities and individual former rebels and their families.",""],[1,"266","3","Community Dialogue and Consultation Mechanisms","face-to-face interactions will still be undertaken especially in local community dialogues, consultations, and problem-solving sessions, albeit in strict compliance with public health standards and protocols.",""],[1,"266","3","Digital Platforms for Community Engagement","Alternative mechanisms such as the use of digital platforms will be utilized only when necessary and feasible.",""],[1,"267","3","Sustain Peace Process Collaboration and Partnerships","collaboration and partnerships through existing peace process mechanisms need to be sustained especially in recalibrating specific strategies in light of the new normal.",""],[1,"267","6","Community Peacebuilding and Conflict-Prevention Support","Strengthening local capacities for addressing peace, conflict, and security issues remains central in sustaining the government's community-based support and peacebuilding programs.",""],[1,"267","6","Inclusive Support for Conflict-Affected and Vulnerable Groups","The government will continue its engagements with severely affected and vulnerable groups in armed conflicts (i.e., women, indigenous peoples, children, elderly, internally displaced peoples [IDPs]) and pursue the application of inclusive and participatory approaches to empower these groups.",""],[1,"267","6","Partnerships with Women, Youth, and Civil Society Organizations","Moreover, partnerships with women and youth sectors and the local civil society organizations (CSOs) will be strengthened in",""],[1,"268","1","Conflict-Sensitive and Peace-Promoting Capacity Development and Advocacy Initiative","the government will sustain its efforts for various capacity development and advocacy initiatives on conflict-sensitive and peace-promoting (CSPP) approaches, providing avenues for dialogues with vulnerable groups and their communities.",""],[1,"268","1","Face-to-Face Peace Conversations","Face-to-face peace conversations will still be conducted, albeit in strict compliance with public health standards and protocols.",""],[1,"268","1","Digital and Mass Media Peace Advocacy Outreach","Use of alternative digital platforms and other forms of mass media such as local radio and television, will also be considered.",""]],"116":[[1,"271","3","Independent and Principled Foreign Policy","For the remainder of the Plan implementation, the government will maintain its independent and principled foreign policy.",""],[1,"271","3","Security Force Capability Strengthening","The government will strengthen the capabilities of its security forces to ensure that Philippine territories and sovereignty is defended.",""],[1,"272","1","ASEAN-China Code of Conduct Negotiation Process","Successful negotiations for the formulation of the \"ASEAN-China Code of Conduct in the South China Sea\" have been pursued to ensure security and stability in the region.",""],[1,"273","8","Rules-Based West Philippine Sea Dispute Settlement Measures","Promote respect for a rules-based regime in the West Philippine Sea including legal and diplomatic processes, as well as confidence-building measures for the peaceful settlement of disputes",""],[1,"273","15","Bilateral Relations and Strategic Partnerships Expansion","Promote greater amity and cooperation with all nations by enhancing bilateral relations, strengthening alliances and strategic partnerships, and developing new security or cooperation arrangements",""],[1,"273","18","Regional and International Cooperation Expansion","Expand and enhance engagements and cooperation with regional and international organizations, particularly in areas of interest to the country",""],[1,"273","24","Defense Modernization Programs","Pursue and sustain modernization programs for a credible and self-reliant defense posture including the AFP Modernization Program and AFP Capability Upgrade Program",""],[1,"278","1","Border Security Interdiction and Enforcement Strengthening","Protection of our porous borders will be ensured through the enhanced interdiction and strengthened presence and capability of the Bureau of Immigration, Bureau of Customs, and other agencies mandated to enforce border security.","Bureau of Immigration | Bureau of Customs"],[1,"278","1","Maritime Security Patrol Intensification","The PCG and BFAR will intensify the conduct of maritime security law enforcement patrols within Philippine territory.","PCG | BFAR"],[1,"278","1","Maritime Detection Systems and Vessel Traffic Management System","The PCG will also pursue the development of maritime detection systems and operationalize the Vessel Traffic Management System to secure the country's maritime jurisdiction.","PCG"]],"117":[[1,"272","1","Philippine Anti-Illegal Drugs Strategy","A holistic approach, involving community and civil society groups, to the campaign against illegal drugs was introduced through the issuance of Executive Order 66, s. 2018, which institutionalized the Philippine Anti-Illegal Drugs Strategy.",""],[1,"273","14","Holistic Anti-Illegal Drugs Campaign","Strengthen commitment to a holistic campaign against the use of illegal drugs and abuse of dangerous drugs",""],[1,"278","3","Integrated Anti-Drug Abuse Campaign","The government will continue to strengthen the conduct of its intensive and unrelenting campaign against the trafficking and use of dangerous drugs and other similar substances through an integrated system of planning, implementation, and enforcement of anti-drug abuse policies, programs, and projects.",""],[1,"278","3","Balanced National Drug Control Program","In doing so, the government will aim to achieve a balance in its national drug control program so that people with legitimate medical needs will still have access to dangerous but licit drugs, subject to the prescription of appropriate medication.",""],[1,"278","4","Philippine Anti-Illegal Drugs Strategy","Central to the government's campaign is to address the country's illegal drug use problem through the Philippine Anti-Illegal Drugs Strategy (PADS).",""],[1,"278","5","Agency Drug-Free Workplace Implementation Plans","all government agencies, including government owned and controlled corporations and state universities and colleges, are mandated to formulate their respective implementing and operational plans.",""],[1,"278","5","Strengthening of Anti-Drug Abuse Councils","the strategy also calls for the support of LGUs through the strengthening of Anti-Drug Abuse Councils, conducting barangay drug clearing operations, and appropriating funds for anti-illegal drugs programs and projects.",""],[1,"278","5","National Drug Abuse Prevalence Survey","The EO also prescribes the conduct of a nationwide survey to determine the extent and magnitude of drug abuse prevalence in the country.",""],[1,"278","5","Dangerous Drugs Operations Database System","the establishment of an age- and sex-disaggregated database and secure database for dangerous drugs operations will ensure transparency and enable an effective monitoring of the implementation of the government's fight against dangerous drugs.",""],[1,"279","1","Random Drug Testing in the Transportation Sector","The Philippine Drug Enforcement Agency (PDEA) will also intensify the random drug testing in the transportation sector as a preventive effort against drug-related road traffic accidents.","Philippine Drug Enforcement Agency (PDEA)"],[1,"279","1","Integrated Anti-Illegal Drugs Campaign Coordination","It will enjoin all government agencies through the Inter-Agency Committee on Anti-Illegal Drugs, as created through EO 15, s. 2017, to ensure that the anti-illegal drugs campaign is implemented in an integrated and synchronized manner.","Inter-Agency Committee on Anti-Illegal Drugs"],[1,"283","7","Institutionalization of Anti-Drug Abuse Councils","This will institutionalize the creation of Anti-Drug Abuse Councils in every local government unit.",""],[1,"283","9","Mandatory Drug Testing and Drug Law Enforcement Reform","This will allow for the mandatory drug testing of students in the secondary and tertiary level and the forfeiture of properties involved in drug cases in favor of PDEA.",""],[1,"283","9","Stronger Penalties and Drug Evidence Destruction Measures","The amendment will also prescribe stronger penalties to those found guilty of trafficking dangerous drugs; provide for the destruction of seized dangerous drugs and controlled precursors and essential chemicals; and restore plea bargaining and probation laws.",""],[1,"283","9","PDEA Institutional Strengthening and Personnel Benefits","It will also strengthen the PDEA as an organization, including the provision of benefits for personnel, among others.",""]],"118":[[1,"302","4","Integrated Flood Management Coordination Mechanism","Pending the creation of an apex body for the water sector, DPWH, as the de facto lead agency for flood control and management, and other relevant agencies will intensify coordination between flood management efforts and undertakings in other sectors, such as solid waste management, reforestation, and housing, among others, under the general framework of IWRM and river basin and land-use planning.","DPWH"],[1,"302","4","Floodwater Storage and Multi-Use Flood Management Infrastructure","In this regard, storage of excess floodwaters will be prioritized in the context of water conservation and efficiency measures: flood management infrastructure that will also serve as potential source for domestic water supply, irrigation, and/or hydropower generation, among other possible uses, will be implemented, where feasible.",""],[1,"302","4","Flood Management Master Plan Financing and Maintenance Support","Meanwhile, in anticipation of the completion of flood control master plans and studies for the major river basins, timely financial support for the full implementation and maintenance of flood management and mitigation measures under said master plans will be provided through the inclusion of the priority projects in the investment program of the national government.",""],[1,"302","4","National Water-Related Data Database","Under the proposed creation of an apex body for the water sector, a comprehensive database of all water-related data including flood-related information, will be established and regularly updated.",""]],"119":[[1,"302","5","Spatially Enhanced Philippine Energy Plan","The Philippine Energy Plan (PEP) will be enhanced by adding a spatial dimension that informs investors on where to invest their energy projects.",""],[1,"303","1","Renewable Energy Zone Identification and Development","Renewable energy (RE) zones will continue to be identified and developed to facilitate connection to the transmission and distribution facilities.",""],[1,"303","1","Energy Sector Logistics and Fuel Supply Support","Other fuel resources and existing logistical facilities will be supplied to encourage the investments that will improve the operations of the energy service and goods providers.",""],[1,"303","2","Energy Sector Policy Reform and Competition Promotion","Implement policy reforms to promote competition and encourage investment in the energy sector.","Department of Energy (DOE)"],[1,"303","4","Strengthened Competitive Selection Process for Power Supply Contracts","The strengthened Competitive Selection Process (CSP) in securing power supply contracts of all distribution utilities' (DU) procurement of power supply agreements for their captive market will also be sustained.",""],[1,"303","5","Wholesale Electricity Spot Market Commercialization and Enhancement","The full commercialization of the Wholesale Electricity Spot Market (WESM) in Mindanao will be pursued to provide a competitive market for buying and selling of electricity that is not covered by bilateral contracts, and at the same time, promote efficiency in the scheduling and dispatch of generation capacities in the region.",""],[1,"303","5","WESM Systems and Procedures Enhancement","Meanwhile, new market features and enhancements to systems and procedures will be introduced to improve the existing WESM in Luzon and Visayas, including the transition into the five-minute WESM replacing the current one-hour trading interval.",""],[1,"303","6","Enhanced Energy Virtual One-Stop Shop Permitting System","Phase 1 of the enhanced EVOSS system is targeted to be carried out by end of third quarter of 2020 in an effort to promote faster and simplified permitting process of power projects.",""],[1,"304","1","Energy Resource Development Exploration","DOE will continue to explore the development of all the available energy resources, including nuclear energy option.","DOE"],[1,"304","1","National Smart Grid Policy Framework Implementation","The National Smart Grid Policy Framework and Roadmap for distribution utilities (DOE DC 2020-02-0003) will likewise be implemented.","DOE"],[1,"304","2","Power Plant Asset Privatization Acceleration","Further, the privatization of power plant assets, which include the capacity of government-owned generating plants and contracted capacity of independent power producer (IPP) contracts, will be accelerated.",""],[1,"304","2","Third-Party Advisory Study for Power Asset Privatization","To ensure the success of asset privatization, the Power Sector Assets and Liabilities Management (PSALM) Corporation will engage third-party advisors to conduct an extensive study that will serve as basis for formulating options and structures for the privatization of IPP-contracted capacity and real estate assets.",""],[1,"304","2","Streamlined Power Asset Bidding Procedures","PSALM will also streamline and simplify bidding procedures to attract more bidders.",""],[1,"304","2","Virtual and Blended Platform Use for Privatization Processes","Further, it will observe protocols and make use of applicable virtual and blended platforms in the privatization or disposal process to ensure that public bidding schedules will push through under the new normal.",""],[1,"304","3","Hydroelectric Power Plant Rehabilitation and Uprating Programme","major hydroelectric power plants under government ownership will be rehabilitated and uprated.",""],[1,"304","3","Regulated Electricity Supply from Undisposed Power Assets","Electricity generated from undisposed power assets throughout the country will continue to be provided to distribution utilities and other power customers at regulated rates.",""],[1,"312","13","EPIRA Amendment and Implementation Strengthening","Amendments to the EPIRA aim to improve the implementation of the law's provisions and enhance its effectiveness to address high cost of electricity, alleged market collusion, and insufficient power supply.",""]],"120":[[1,"292","3","Accelerated Off-Grid Electrification","Moreover, the electrification efforts will be accelerated, particularly in off-grid areas, to support the energy requirements under the digital economy and contribute to providing security and promoting lasting peace.",""],[1,"305","2","Transmission and Distribution Network Expansion and Grid Interconnection","Continue to develop transmission and distribution facilities, and projects that will transmit electricity efficiently to various load centers and interconnect the entire grid and other areas.",""],[1,"305","2","One Grid Philippines Interconnection Program","Under the One Grid Philippines, the three major grids will be able to share excess supply.",""],[1,"305","2","Integrated Power Development Plan Harmonization","To further improve the delivery of power services, the government will harmonize the Power Development Plan by integrating the Transmission Development Plan, Distribution Development Plan, and the Missionary Electrification Development Plan with the corresponding RE targets under the National Renewable Energy Program.",""],[1,"305","2","Philippine Smart Grid Development Support","It will also support the development of the Philippine Smart Grid.",""],[1,"305","2","Power Line Integration in Inter-Island Bridge Design","The National Transmission Corporation, its concessionaire, the National Grid Corporation of the Philippines, and the DUs will coordinate with concerned agencies (e.g., DPWH) to explore the possibility of including the future installation of power transmission or distribution lines to connect island grids and other areas in the design of proposed inter-island bridges.",""],[1,"305","3","Electrification Program Acceleration","Ensure timely implementation of electrification programs, especially for remaining unelectrified off- grid islands, geographically-isolated and depressed areas, and last-mile communities.","DOE"],[1,"305","4","House Wiring Subsidy for Unenergized Households","house- wiring subsidy will be provided for unenergized households in areas with distribution facilities through the DOE's Nationwide Intensification of Household Electrification.",""],[1,"305","4","Distribution Line Extension to Unserved Areas","Distribution line facilities will also be extended to unserved areas through the National Electrification Administration's Expanded Sitio Electrification Program, Barangay Line Enhancement Program, and Expanded Household Electrification Program.",""],[1,"305","5","Off-grid Solar Home Systems Installation","Under the Off-grid Electrification Program, individual PV Solar Home Systems will be installed by DUs via DOE's Access to Sustainable Energy Program's PV Mainstreaming Program.",""],[1,"305","5","Private Sector Mini- and Micro-Grid Expansion","In addition, the entry of the private sector in the Mini/Micro-Grid System will be allowed and encouraged through Qualified Third Party (QTP) schemes, joint ventures, and the National Power Corporation-Small Power Utilities Group Mini-Grid Scheme.",""],[1,"305","5","Renewable Energy-Diesel Hybrid Power System Development","Further, RE-diesel hybrid power systems will also be developed to provide reliable electricity services at more affordable rates in off-grid areas.",""],[1,"305","6","Private Sector Participation Guidelines Streamlining for Electrification","To facilitate private sector participation in the achievement of the total electrification target of the government, existing guidelines on the participation of QTPs will be further streamlined and enhanced.",""]],"121":[[1,"306","1","Alternative Fuel Roadmap Implementation","The Alternative Fuel Roadmap will be implemented to promote a technology-responsive energy sector.",""],[1,"306","2","Implement Energy Efficiency and Conservation Act and Roadmap","Implement the Energy Efficiency and Conservation (EE&C) Act (RA 11285) and the Energy Efficiency and Conservation Roadmap.",""],[1,"306","3","Government Energy Management Program","the government will take the lead through the Government Energy Management Program involving efficiency and conservation measures in the government's use of electricity and fuel.",""],[1,"306","4","Local Energy Efficiency and Conservation Planning","the law also requires the development of local energy efficiency and conservation plans for incorporation in the local development plans.",""],[1,"306","5","Philippine Conventional Energy Contracting Program","DOE will continue to promote the Philippine Conventional Energy Contracting Program, which offers 14 pre-determined areas for upstream development, with an option for investors to nominate their own prospective exploration area.","DOE"],[1,"306","6","Natural Gas Industry Development and Regulation","Pursue the development of the natural gas industry.",""],[1,"306","7","Strategic Petroleum Reserve Establishment","Pursue the establishment of a strategic petroleum reserve.",""],[1,"306","8","Energy Resiliency Policy Adoption","The government will institutionalize the development, promotion and implementation of a comprehensive Resiliency Plan (RCP), as well as incorporation of mitigation improvements into the reconstruction and rehabilitation of damaged infrastructures in accordance with the Build Back Better principles.","DOE"],[1,"310","7","Energy Resiliency Policy","The Energy Resiliency Policy, issued to institutionalize disaster resiliency efforts, aims to strengthen energy systems and facilities such that these can quickly restore power and provide alternative sources of energy in times of emergency.",""],[1,"312","15","Natural Gas Industry Enabling Law","Enactment of an enabling law for the natural gas industry",""],[1,"312","16","Natural Gas Industry Legal and Regulatory Framework","This provides an enabling legal and regulatory framework for the natural gas industry to guide investments in the sector.",""]],"122":[[1,"292","3","Blended Learning and Education Facility Improvement","to continue the delivery of quality education through blended learning and improvement of our education facilities;",""],[1,"308","4","Completion of Abandoned and Unfinished School Projects","The Department of Education (DepEd), in coordination with DPWH, will endeavor to complete by 2022 all programmed school projects under the Basic Educational Facilities Fund which have been abandoned or unfinished since 2014.","Department of Education (DepEd) | DPWH"],[1,"308","6","Education Infrastructure Backlog Reduction Programme","Efforts to address backlogs in the provision of education facilities will resume.","DepEd | DPWH"],[1,"308","6","Education Infrastructure Backlog Reduction in Conflict-Affected and Isolated Areas","DepEd, in coordination with DPWH, will continue to address its current backlog in education infrastructure, especially in geographically isolated and conflict-affected areas.","DepEd | DPWH"],[1,"308","6","Revision of Education Facility Design Standards","DepEd may need to revisit its existing design standards and minimum specifications for education facilities (e.g., classroom size and class size).","DepEd"],[1,"308","8","Off-Grid School Renewable Electrification","Off-grid schools may be equipped with alternative sources of renewable energy through installation of solar panels, among others;",""],[1,"308","9","School Clinic Multi-Service Hub Development","Clinics that will also serve as multi-service hubs catering to the various health, nutrition, and medical needs of learners;",""],[1,"309","1","Streamlined Disaster Relief Warehouse Scheme","Efficient disaster response through a streamlined warehouse scheme for storage and inventory of supplies and for easier deployment and delivery of materials and equipment, such as temporary learning spaces or classroom tents, to replace those damaged by calamities.",""],[1,"309","2","Education Sector Convergence Initiative","DepEd will facilitate convergence initiatives with the DPWH, Department of Health (DOH), Department of Social Welfare and Development, and other agencies in all governance levels, including LGUs, to address the broader needs of the education sector.","DepEd | DPWH | Department of Health (DOH) | Department of Social Welfare and Development"]],"123":[[1,"319","5","Water Conservation and Efficiency Measures","Enhance water conservation and efficiency measures to avert water shortage.",""],[1,"319","6","Comprehensive Water Resource Assessment Scale-Up","Continue and scale up the conduct of comprehensive water resource assessment in groundwater critical areas and major river basins for sustainable water supply.",""],[1,"324","6","Pollution Source Regulation Strengthening","· Strengthen the regulation of point sources (e.g., discharges from industries and treatment plants) and nonpoint sources (e.g., agricultural farms and residential areas) of pollution by:",""],[1,"324","7","Nationwide Waterbody Inventory and Classification","Expediting the nationwide inventory and classification of waterbodies, and establishment :unselected: of water management systems in priority waterbodies;",""],[1,"324","7","Water Management Systems for Priority Waterbodies","Expediting the nationwide inventory and classification of waterbodies, and establishment :unselected: of water management systems in priority waterbodies;",""],[1,"324","8","Environmental User Fee System Expansion and Refinement","Refining and expanding the Environmental User Fee System (EUFS) to cover all pollution sources (i.e., domestic, industrial, commercial, and agricultural), and to properly reflect the value of environmental damages;",""],[1,"324","9","Designation of Non-Attainment Areas for Waterbodies","Designating the non-attainment areas1 for waterbodies where pollutants exceed the water :unselected: quality guidelines to prevent new sources of effluent concentration and discharge from adversely affecting water quality;",""],[1,"324","10","Water Quality Management Area Designation and Operationalization","Designating and operationalizing the required number of Water Quality Management Areas (WQMAs), including updating of its Action Plans; and",""],[1,"324","11","Marine Pollution Regulation Strengthening and Shore Reception Facility Expansion","Strengthening marine pollution regulations and expanding shore reception facilities in seaports for the collection and disposal services of wastes generated from ships through collaboration among concerned agencies (e.g., DOTr, PCG, MARINA, PPA, and CPA) ..",""],[1,"324","12","Domestic Wastewater Treatment and Conveyance Facilities","Accelerate the establishment of domestic wastewater treatment facilities and its conveyance system.",""],[1,"324","12","Institutional and Technical Capacity Support for Sewerage and Septage Projects","The DPWH, DENR, and DOH will continue to enhance the institutional and technical capacities of LGUs, water districts, and concerned entities to implement sewerage and septage projects under the NSSMP, and mobilize other financial support on wastewater treatment.","DPWH | DENR | DOH"],[1,"324","13","Water Quality Monitoring System Modernization","Modernize water quality monitoring systems by:",""],[1,"324","14","Ambient Water Quality Monitoring Station Upgrade and Expansion","Repairing, upgrading, and increasing the number of fully-operational ambient water quality monitoring stations;",""],[1,"324","15","Laboratory Analysis Capacity and Water Quality Monitoring Technology Upgrade","Enhancing capacity for laboratory analysis and exploring the use of advanced remote sensing and UAV technologies in monitoring water quality.",""],[1,"324","16","Designation of Non-Attainment Waterbody Areas","the DENR in coordination with the LGUs, shall designate these non-attainment areas of waterbodies where pollutants have exceeded water quality guidelines to prevent new effluent concentration and discharges.","DENR | LGUs"],[1,"326","3","Wastewater Reclamation, Recycling, and Reuse Support","Support wastewater reclamation/recycling and reuse for next intended use (e.g., indoor use and irrigation purposes);",""],[1,"326","5","Research Collaboration for Water Pollution Abatement","Establish synergies with research and development institutions to undertake studies on technological solutions and water pollution abatement measures.",""]],"124":[[1,"332","2","Financial Inclusion Initiatives for Overseas Filipinos and Families","Financial inclusion initiatives for OFs and their families will also be strengthened.",""],[1,"336","8","Financial Inclusion Initiatives for Overseas Filipinos and Their Families","Strengthen financial inclusion initiatives for OFs and their families",""],[1,"339","5","Financial Inclusion Initiatives for Overseas Filipinos and Families","Strengthen financial inclusion initiatives for OFs and their families.",""],[1,"340","1","Full Operationalization of PhilSys for Financial Access","access to financial products and services will be supported by the full operationalization of the PhilSys which will address issues on lack of identity documents for opening bank accounts and verifying financial transactions.",""]],"126":[[1,"147","1","Whole-of-Nation Peacebuilding Approach","A whole-of-nation approach in attaining inclusive and sustainable peace will also be pursued",""],[1,"161","45","Leadership, Management, and Coordination Capacity Strengthening","· Strengthen leadership, management, capacities, coordination and support mechanisms",""]],"128":[[1,"179","2","Expansion of Employment Facilitation Services","Boost and expand employment facilitation services.",""],[1,"179","2","Capacity Strengthening for Public Employment Service Offices","To this end, capacities of Public Employment Service Offices (PESOs) in LGUs will be strengthened.",""],[1,"179","2","Strengthening Local Employment Service Delivery Mechanisms","creating stronger mechanisms to effectively deliver services, boost employment, and generate jobs at the local level is needed",""],[1,"179","3","Institutionalization of Public Employment Service Offices","Efforts to intensify the institutionalization of PESOs across localities nationwide will be pushed to ensure availability of funds and resources.",""],[1,"179","3","PESO Staffing, Facilities, and Jobseeker Database Upgrade","In particular, it is crucial to have adequate and well-trained staff as well as up-to-date facilities and to keep an updated and expanded database of jobseekers and available jobs that may be accessed by other PESOs nationwide.",""],[1,"179","3","Economic and Financial Literacy Programs for Vulnerable Sectors","Moreover, PESOs will also strengthen the delivery of economic and financial literacy programs for the vulnerable sectors, through intensified partnership with the regional offices of the National Economic and Development Authority and Bangko Sentral ng Pilipinas.","National Economic and Development Authority | Bangko Sentral ng Pilipinas"],[1,"179","3","Local Hiring Incentives for Firms","More importantly, firms will be encouraged to hire workers residing in the communities where they operate to reduce vulnerability to transport disruptions and community quarantine restrictions.",""],[1,"179","5","PESO Labor Market Database Updating and Skills Mapping","PESOs should regularly update their database on the labor needs of businesses, especially in emerging industries, and supply of labor.",""],[1,"179","5","Barangay-Level Skills Mapping","skills mapping in the barangay level needs to be done regularly.",""],[1,"179","5","Targeted Skills Development Programs","PESOs can then organize better- designed and targeted skills development programs.",""],[1,"179","6","PESO Cooperative Formation and Market Linkage Support","PESOs may also assist unorganized wage employees in forming cooperatives, link microfinance institutions with those with livelihood activities, and develop market linkages for micro, small, and medium enterprises.",""],[1,"179","6","Inter-LGU and Overseas Jobseeker Referral Support","PESOs may also link job seekers with PESOs in other LGUs and/or relevant agencies for those aspiring to work abroad.",""],[1,"179","7","Labor Market Center One-Stop Employment Service","the PESO partnered with the LGU Center for Excellence and City Women's Council in coming up with a Labor Market Center, which works as a one-stop shop for all employment-related concerns including training/skills development and wage employment and livelihood facilitation",""],[1,"179","7","Local College Continuing Education and Skills Development Partnership","LGUs partnered with local colleges for continuing education and skills development of the workforce",""],[1,"180","1","Labor Market Information System Enhancement","The PhilJobNet - the government's web-based job search, matching, and referral portal along with the PESO Employment Information System (PEIS) will be enhanced through intensified promotion among stakeholders and improved collection of data.",""],[1,"180","1","Expansion of Online and Home-Based Job Listings","These platforms will also be expanded to highlight online and home-based job openings.",""],[1,"180","1","E-Recruitment Guidelines and Anti-Illegal Recruitment Advocacy","Development of e- recruitment guidelines and intensified advocacy against online illegal recruitment and trafficking will also be pursued.",""]],"129":[[1,"161","15","Employment Facilitation Services Expansion","Boost and expand employment facilitation services",""],[1,"161","41","Income Support and Emergency Employment Enhancement","Enhance income support and emergency employment",""]],"130":[[1,"215","1","Youth and Women Employment Expansion","Labor force participation and employment opportunities in all regions will be enhanced, focusing on the youth and women towards countryside development.",""],[1,"216","1","Youth Employment Transition Support Mechanisms","To ease the youth's transition from school to work - internships, apprenticeships, and dual-training programs will be strengthened and expanded.",""],[1,"216","1","Government-Industry-Academe Linkage for Youth Employment","Stronger government-industry-academe linkage will be forged and sustained to achieve these.",""],[1,"216","1","Youth Employment Facilitation Services","Employment facilitation for this age cohort will also be improved by providing assistance such as coaching, career advocacy, and counseling.",""],[1,"216","1","Online Delivery of Employment Assistance","These will be offered through online platforms to make it accessible during the pandemic.",""],[1,"216","1","Labor Market Program Utilization and PhilJobNet Promotion","Promoting the use of existing labor market programs including technology-based mechanisms such as the PhilJobNet can also help in their employment.",""],[1,"216","1","Employee and Enterprise Capacity Building","Upon employment, their productivity can be further improved by building and strengthening employee and enterprise capacities.",""],[1,"216","1","Workplace Psychosocial Risk and Stress Support Mechanisms","Health and safety in the workplace will also be promoted by crafting support mechanisms to address psychosocial risks and work-related stress, and providing reproductive health and modern family planning services to workers (see Chapter 10).",""],[1,"216","2","Women's Labor Force Participation and Retention Measures","Female labor force participation will be increased by intensifying monitoring and ensuring compliance of corporations to laws, policies, and programs that foster women's participation and retention in the workforce (e.g., Expanded Maternity Leave Act and the Family Welfare Program).",""],[1,"216","2","Women's Access to Formal Employment and E-Commerce Entrepreneurship","Women's access to formal employment opportunities will also be advanced, including entrepreneurship through e-commerce.",""],[1,"216","2","Flexible Work Arrangements","Flexible work arrangements such as compressed workweek and alternative worksites will likewise be explored.",""],[1,"216","2","Childcare Support Mechanisms","There will also be a continuous push for affordable and accessible childcare support mechanisms like daycare and child-minding facilities and services (see Chapter 10).",""]],"131":[[1,"125","2","Industry Roadmap Collaboration and Monitoring","Strengthen collaboration and monitoring of the implementation of various industry roadmaps.",""],[1,"125","3","Business Continuity Planning Capacity Building","Build capacity in preparing Business Continuity Plans (BCPs) across industries.",""],[1,"125","7","Productivity Toolbox Implementation for BCPs","National Wages and Productivity Commission (NWPC) commits to implement the Productivity Toolbox to sharpen the productivity perspective of BCPs",""],[1,"145","22","Monitoring and Evaluation Framework for Flagship Enterprise Programs","Create an M&E framework on government flagship programs for startups, MSMEs, and cooperatives",""],[1,"145","24","Business Continuity Planning and Capacity Building","Undertake business continuity planning (BCP) and capacity building to enhance resilience",""],[1,"151","1","Monitoring and Evaluation Framework for Flagship MSME and Cooperative Programs","Create an M&E framework on government flagship programs for startups, MSMEs, and cooperatives.",""],[1,"151","3","Business Continuity Planning and Capacity-Building Support for Enterprises","Undertake business continuity planning (BCP) and capacity building to enhance resilience.",""],[1,"161","28","Capacity Building for Productivity-Based Incentive Schemes and Business Continuity Plans","Enhance delivery of capacity building for productivity-based incentive schemes and business continuity plans",""],[1,"180","4","Capacity Building for Productivity-Based Incentive Schemes","Enhance delivery of capacity building for productivity-based incentive schemes and business continuity plans.",""],[1,"181","1","Business Continuity Plan Expansion","The productivity toolbox will be expanded to include the preparation of Business Continuity Plans.",""],[1,"185","9","Amendment of RA 6971 to Liberalize Productivity Incentives","To accelerate the adoption of productivity improvement and gainsharing schemes, RA 6971 needs to be amended to liberalize its restrictive provisions while (a) making the establishment of productivity incentives committees mandatory in large private business enterprises; (b) reiterating that gainsharing will be contingent on gains from productivity improvement; and (c) easing the requirements for availing tax incentives by business enterprises for granting productivity incentives and grants to employees and workers.",""]],"132":[[1,"124","6","Halal Industry Financing and Technical Assistance Support","Financing and technical assistance for Halal firms'",""],[1,"125","1","Halal Industry Compliance and Common Service Facilities Support","The implementation of the Philippine Halal Export Development and Promotion Act of 2016 (RA 10817) will provide assistance to Halal industries to ensure compliance with Halal technical standards and provide common service facilities in strategic production areas.",""],[1,"125","1","Halal Market Research and Intelligence through Foreign Service Posts","Further, the Department of Foreign Affairs (DFA) Foreign Service Posts will be utilized in conducting market research and intelligence for potential opportunities for the development of the Philippine Halal industry and other relevant information to expand market access.","Department of Foreign Affairs (DFA)"],[1,"135","10","Halal Industry Development and Tourism Promotion","Boost tourism from the Middle East and other Muslim-majority countries by supporting the development of the halal industry and promoting business partnerships with companies from",""],[1,"136","1","Halal Seminars and Webinar Training Programme","Increase the conduct of halal-related seminars and training via webinars to strengthen the Philippine halal industry and continue exploring the potential of incorporating halal in other sectors.",""]],"133":[[1,"4","5","Strategic Industry Location Reform Package","This pandemic also lends urgency to crucial reform initiatives that will encourage strategic industries to locate in the country (e.g., amendments to the Foreign Investment Act, Public Service Act, Retail Trade Liberalization Act, and the Corporate Recovery and Tax Incentives for Enterprises or CREATE)",""],[1,"10","5","Telecommunications Market Liberalization","The entry of a third telecommunications player, meanwhile, will create a more competitive environment to help ensure affordable and reliable internet services in the country.",""],[1,"10","5","Public Service and Foreign Investment Reform","Further reforms in the Public Service Act and Foreign Investments Act will open the sector more.",""],[1,"17","5","Amend Investment and Liberalization Laws","Some of these restrictions can be addressed by amending laws or regulations such as the Public Service Act, Foreign Investment Act, and the Retail Trade Liberalization Act.",""]],"134":[[1,"216","3","Financial Inclusion and Digital Payments Expansion","The government will provide effective access to a wide range of financial products and services for all.",""],[1,"216","3","Digital Financial Literacy and Economic Literacy Training","During the pandemic, online courses, webinars, and e-conferences will be employed to improve the population's economic and financial literacy (see Chapter 15).",""],[1,"242","17","Inclusive Digital Finance Ecosystem Development","Develop a more inclusive digital finance ecosystem",""],[1,"242","19","Microfinance and Microinsurance Efficiency and Innovation Promotion","Encourage efficiency and innovation in microfinance and microinsurance",""],[1,"242","20","Islamic Banking and Finance Regulatory Framework Development","Develop the regulatory framework on Islamic banking and finance",""],[1,"245","2","Inclusive Digital Finance Ecosystem Development","the country's digital financial infrastructure will be developed, including the regulatory frameworks and platforms that facilitate the scope, scale and reach of DFS.",""],[1,"245","3","Microfinance Efficiency and Digital Financial Services Enhancement","Encourage efficiency and innovation in microfinance and microinsurance for the domestic market.",""],[1,"245","3","Agricultural Microinsurance Expansion","Private insurance providers will be encouraged to engage in the delivery of microinsurance for agriculture, in addition to the existing micro-health and pre-need services.",""],[1,"246","1","Digital MSME Financing Infrastructure","The establishment of digital supply chain financing, credit risk database, and online collateral registry will enhance MSME access to finance.",""],[1,"246","1","Agricultural Insurance and Guarantee Mechanisms","Lastly, agriculture insurance, guarantee programs, and other mechanisms that address risks in the agriculture sector will be put in place to strengthen agricultural financing",""],[1,"253","2","Amendment of the Agri-Agra Reform Credit Act","Seeks to amend the Agri-Agra Reform Credit Act of 2009 (RA 10000) to strengthen rural development by providing for a holistic approach that takes into account the broader agriculture financing ecosystem and rural community development requirements.",""],[1,"253","6","Financial Assistance for Strategically Important Firms","Provide financial assistance to firms that are strategically important to economic recovery, in view of their role in providing employment and supporting the",""],[1,"259","3","Financial and Technical Support for MSMEs","government will provide financial and technical support to MSMEs to enable them to thrive in a market participated in by larger and more established foreign and domestic players.",""],[1,"261","11","MSME Growth and Financing Support Measure","The measure will promote the growth and development of MSMEs by addressing challenges such as limits to entrepreneurship and lack of access to finance and markets, among others.",""]],"135":[[1,"94","2","Cybersecurity and Copyright Protection Mechanisms","mechanisms to address cybersecurity concerns such as copyright infringement, especially of film and audiovisual content, will be established.",""]],"136":[[1,"318","11","Innovative Pollution Abatement Solutions","Adopt and implement innovative pollution abatement solutions",""],[1,"326","3","Cleaner Production Techniques Promotion","and promote other cleaner production techniques to control the discharge of pollutants (e.g. use of organic fertilizers and biopesticides).",""],[1,"326","4","Public-Private Partnership Support for Cleaner Technologies","Strengthen public-private partnerships to create opportunities for low-cost pollution-control and treatment technologies.",""]],"137":[[1,"100","13","Online Marketing Channels for Agriculture and Fishery Products","Strengthen online marketing of agriculture and fishery products, including establishment of online or digital channels for transactions and delivery services",""],[1,"106","4","Online Marketing and Digital Delivery Channels for Agriculture and Fishery Products","Strengthen online marketing of agriculture and fishery products, including the establishment of online or digital channels for transactions and delivery services.",""],[1,"106","4","Expansion of eKadiwa to Urban Areas Outside Metro Manila","The DA can expand the reach of the recently launched eKadiwa14 to urban areas outside Metro Manila and expand the mode of payment and delivery service providers.","DA"],[1,"106","4","Online Pabili Service Delivery System","In areas where food and grocery deliveries are not available, an online service delivery system where buyers send a list of items to buy to a pabili service provider may be explored as an option.",""],[1,"106","4","Registry System for Online Sellers and Deliveries","Parallel to this, a registry system for online sellers or deliveries should be established to monitor and regulate the movement of people engaged in such transactions.",""],[1,"106","4","Digital Payment Adoption for Farmers and Fisherfolk","Farmers and fisherfolk should likewise be encouraged to make use of digital payment systems (i.e., online or app-based financial technologies), particularly in receiving/accessing payments for their produce.",""]],"138":[[1,"161","8","Life-Course Nutrition and Health Care Interventions","Provide quality nutrition and health care interventions at all life stages",""],[1,"161","27","Nutrition and Health Investment and Resource Efficiency Initiative","Secure sustainable investment on nutrition and health and ensure efficient and equitable use of nutrition and health resources",""],[1,"161","40","Multi-sector Nutrition and Health Support Mobilization","Elicit multi-sector, multi-stakeholder support for nutrition and health",""],[1,"163","18","Nutrition and Health Care Interventions Across All Life Stages","Provide quality nutrition and health care interventions at all life stages.",""],[1,"164","1","First 1,000 Days Nutrition and Health Services","Nutrition Council (NNC), will ensure that appropriate nutrition and health-related interventions and services will be given for the first 1,000 days of life",""],[1,"164","2","Whole-of-Government Nutrition Program Strengthening","Implementation of nutrition-specific interventions at the local level such as Nutrition in Emergencies, Overweight and Obesity Management Prevention Program, Supplementary and School-Based Feeding Program, Food Fortification, National Dietary Supplementation Program will be strengthened through intensified coordination and collaboration of LGUs with implementing agencies given new normal conditions.","LGUs | DOH | NNC | DepEd | Department of Social Welfare and Development (DSWD) | Department of Agriculture (DA) | Department of Science and Technology - Food and Nutrition Research Institute (DOST-FNRI)"],[1,"164","2","Malnutrition Reduction Program Continuation","The implementation of Malnutrition Reduction Program of the DOST-FNRI, which provides age-appropriate complementary foods for babies and other vulnerable groups, will be continued.","DOST-FNRI"],[1,"164","2","Production and Consumption of Nutritious Complementary Foods","Further, nutritious complementary foods, snack foods and meals will continue to be produced and consumed.",""],[1,"164","2","Fortified Staples Integration into Social Safety Net Programs","Fortified staples will be produced and included in all social safety net programs, such as dietary supplementation among pregnant women, 6-23 months old children, and children in child development centers and public elementary schools.",""],[1,"164","2","Expanded Partnerships for Nutrition Scale-Up","This will be scaled up through expanded partnerships with agrarian reform beneficiaries, organizations, cooperatives, small and medium-sized enterprises, among others (see Chapter 11).",""],[1,"209","2","Nutrition and Health Service Delivery Reforms","major reforms to improve the delivery of nutrition and health services, and transformative education have been put in place in the past three years",""],[1,"209","2","COVID-19 Impact Mitigation Programs","the government will implement programs that will mitigate the pandemic's short and long-term effects",""],[1,"209","2","Malnutrition Reduction and Health Access Improvement","continuing to address persistent issues on malnutrition, access to health services, and quality of graduates for employment",""],[1,"213","1","Universal Healthcare Implementation","Universal healthcare will be pursued with the implementation of the UHC Act to maintain the downward trend in mortality rates, particularly among neonates, infants, and under-five children.",""],[1,"213","1","First 1,000 Days Nutrition and Health Services","This will be complemented by the provision of appropriate nutrition and health services for the first 1,000 days of life which includes appropriate care for mothers during pregnancy, labor, and childbirth; essential care for the newborn; optimal infant and young child care and nutrition; immunization; and vitamin supplementation for children, among others.",""],[1,"213","1","Strengthening of Local Health Systems and Primary Care Networks","As mandated by the UHC Act, local health systems will be strengthened, specifically the primary care provider networks.",""],[1,"213","1","Integration of Province- and City-Wide Health Systems","There will be improved integration of province- and city-wide health systems and networks under the stewardship of the provincial and city health boards, which will manage the special health fund.",""],[1,"213","1","Local Health Investment for Service Access and Resilience","Adequate local investment to improve access to quality health services and resilience to any threats and health emergencies will also be provided.",""],[1,"215","1","Human Capital Improvement Initiative","Thus, it entails the improvement of health and nutrition, education, and total well-being of the human capital.",""],[1,"215","2","Maternal, Newborn, and Child Health Services Expansion","For health and nutrition outcomes, the focus will be on providing maternal, newborn, and child health services, and school and community nutrition programs.",""],[1,"215","2","First 1,000 Days Nutrition and Health Intervention Expansion","Health and nutrition interventions for mothers, infants, and young children will be expanded in line with the implementation of the First 1,000 Days Law.",""],[1,"215","2","Universal Health Care Law Implementation and Health System Reform","Reforms in the country's healthcare system will be pursued with the implementation of the UHC Law and the introduction of innovative measures to make it more resilient and accessible.",""]],"139":[[1,"169","4","Multi-stakeholder Nutrition and Health Partnership Mobilization","Elicit multi-sector, multi-stakeholder support for nutrition and health.",""],[1,"169","4","Civil Society Participation in Nutrition and Health Planning and Monitoring","Civil society organizations (CSOs), including volunteers will be mobilized to participate in budget development, service delivery, and monitoring and evaluation through their involvement in local development councils and other special bodies.",""],[1,"169","4","Official Development Assistance for Nutrition and Health","development partners can be tapped to provide official development assistance aligned with the nutrition and health agenda.",""],[1,"169","4","Private Sector Engagement in Health and Nutrition Service Delivery","Improved health and nutrition outcomes can be achieved with the help and involvement of private sector in the provision of health care and nutrition services.",""],[1,"169","4","Scaling Up Nutrition Multisectoral Partnership Strengthening","the NNC will strengthen the existing country, regional and global multisectoral partnerships with CSOs, academe, business, and development partners through the Scaling Up Nutrition Movement networks with the \"engage-inspire-invest\" slogan.",""],[1,"169","4","Integration of Nutrition and Health Components in Flagship Programs","There will also be integration of nutrition and health components in all major flagship programs of the government.",""],[1,"169","5","Nutrition and Health Sector Regulatory and Monitoring Measures","This will be done by: (a) developing innovative regulatory and monitoring mechanisms to promote adequately fortified staples and food products, and equitable distribution of quality and affordable health goods and services; (b) establishing a performance monitoring unit to track the progress of reforms and medical audits and to oversee third-party monitoring; (c) adopting responsive organizational structure, staffing patterns, and skill-mix at all levels of the health system; and (d) monitoring and evaluating health and nutrition",""],[1,"170","1","Local Level Plan Monitoring and Evaluation for Nutrition","programs such as through the Monitoring and Evaluation of Local Level Plan Implementation being conducted by NNC member agencies to ensure compliance and improvement of nutrition status at the local level.",""],[1,"170","1","LGU Transparency and Accountability Incentive and Guidance System","The DILG will also continue to offer incentives and provide guidelines to ensure transparency and accountability among LGUs in delivering nutrition and health care services, especially during health emergencies (e.g., pandemics).","DILG"],[1,"170","6","Technical Assistance for Local Health and Nutrition Service Delivery","The national government will provide technical assistance to LGUs to improve the delivery of health and nutrition services at the local level.",""],[1,"170","6","Local Government Nutrition and Health Programs","LGUs may also initiate their own local programs and projects that will supplement the programs of the national government to ensure nutrition and health for all.",""],[1,"170","6","Strengthened Coordination for Nutrition and Health Programs","This will further strengthen the coordination and collaboration among national and local government agencies in implementing nutrition and health programs in the country.",""],[1,"170","6","Implementation of the Mandanas Ruling for Local Health and Nutrition Capacity","By 2022, the implementation of the Mandanas ruling would further strengthen the capacity of the LGUs in delivering health and nutrition services, especially that some of the functions of the national government will be shifted to the LGUs.",""],[1,"182","10","Local Nutrition Program Strengthening through Nutrition Action Officer Positions","Strengthening the Local Nutrition Program through the creation of plantilla Nutrition Action Officer position",""],[1,"182","11","Plantilla Nutrition Action Officer Position","The creation of a plantilla nutrition action officer (NAO) position will ensure that the tasks of planning, implementing, and monitoring projects/activities to guarantee adequate food supply, livelihood, health and nutrition caring, and food stability during emergencies among the most vulnerable population are provided.",""],[1,"182","11","Local Government Nutrition Policy and Program Implementation","The full-time NAO will ensure that LGU nutrition policies and programs, as well as national laws on nutrition, are executed to promote good nutrition of the people.",""]],"140":[[1,"191","4","Food Demand-Supply Linkage Strengthening","Strengthen efforts to link food demand and supply",""],[1,"192","2","Zero Hunger Policy and Program Support","The Inter-agency Task Force on Zero Hunger8 ensures that these strategies are supported with policies and programs that will end hunger, achieve food security, improve nutrition, and promote sustainable agriculture.",""],[1,"192","3","Food Demand-Supply Linkage Strengthening","Strengthen efforts to link food demand and supply.",""],[1,"192","6","Inter-Agency Task Force on Zero Hunger","8 Executive Order No. 101: Creating an Inter-agency Task Force on Zero Hunger",""]],"141":[[1,"191","18","Disability Information Campaign","Conduct information campaign on disability",""],[1,"191","19","Accessibility Improvement for Social Protection Services for Persons with Disabilities","Improve the accessibility of social protection services for persons with disabilities",""],[1,"195","3","Disability Information and Education Campaigns","The government, with the leadership of the National Council on Disability Affairs (NCDA), will continue conducting information and education campaigns among stakeholders to improve their understanding of disability, as well as increase people's awareness of the rights of persons with disabilities.",""],[1,"195","4","Disability-Inclusive Social Protection Access Improvement","Improve the accessibility of social protection services for persons with disabilities.",""]],"142":[[1,"203","9","Innovative Housing Finance Modalities","Implement innovative housing finance modalities",""],[1,"203","13","Primary and Secondary Mortgage Market Development","Strengthen primary mortgage markets and develop more secondary ones",""],[1,"203","18","Viable Land Acquisition Approaches","Adopt viable land acquisition approaches",""],[1,"206","5","Land Banking Expansion for Socialized Housing","Land banking, especially for urban socialized housing, will be scaled up as government prioritizes in-city and near city approaches to resettlement.",""],[1,"206","5","Expanded Land Tenure Modalities for Affordable Housing","the use of the modalities of usufruct or long-term use of land will be expanded to enhance affordability of socialized and low-cost housing programs due to lower land development cost.",""],[1,"207","2","Housing Microfinance Reform and Expansion","the DHSUD will formulate institutional and policy reforms to accelerate housing microfinance as the primary pro-poor housing finance strategy.","DHSUD"],[1,"207","2","Housing Voucher and Public Rental Housing Pilot","A feasibility study and pilot implementation of the housing voucher and public rental housing modalities will be pursued by the DHSUD.","DHSUD"],[1,"207","2","Balanced Housing Compliance Partnership","Partnership with the private sector for incentivized compliance with the Balanced Housing provision under Republic Act No. 7279 as amended by Republic Act No. 10884 to mobilize funds for public housing of LGUs as an offshoot of the private developer's compliance with these laws shall be continuously explored.",""],[1,"207","3","Primary and Secondary Mortgage Market Strengthening","Strengthen primary mortgage markets and develop more secondary ones.",""],[1,"208","4","Expanded NHMFC Secondary Mortgage Market Mandate","Strengthen and broaden NHMFC's mandate to include the development of a secondary mortgage market for housing-related financial instruments/assets and issuance of housing related asset- backed securities as well as invest in housing-related financial instruments and other investment vehicles.",""]],"143":[[1,"161","49","Accessible Sporting Culture Development","Develop an accessible sporting culture",""],[1,"176","3","Accessible Sporting Culture Development","A sporting culture accessible to all Filipinos will be developed as an instrument to promote human development and improve quality of life.",""],[1,"176","3","Sports Facilities Development and Upgrading","Sports facilities will be developed and upgraded to be at par with global standards.",""],[1,"176","3","Philippine Sports Commission Capacity Strengthening","The PSC's human resources, management and research capacities will be improved to enhance its ability to lead, manage, and assess the country's sports programs.",""],[1,"176","3","Philippine Sports Institute Institutionalization","The Philippine Sports Institute will be institutionalized to direct the development and linkages of the grassroots and high-performance sports programs and the professional development of sports practitioners.",""]],"144":[[1,"167","4","Human Resources for Health Equity and Deployment Measures","The DOH will ensure that there will be equitable distribution of HRH, including allied health professionals (e.g., dietitians, nutritionists, therapists, medical technologists), and continuous improvement of their working conditions by: (a) continuing the provision of pre-service full scholarship program (with return service contract) to students in medical-related fields (including virology, microbiology, among others) offered by both national and local governments; (b) continuing augmentation, redistribution, and retention of health workers in challenged priority provinces, far-flung municipalities, and geographically isolated and disadvantaged areas (GIDA) through the DOH HRH Deployment Program; (c) monitoring and revisiting the implementation of Magna Carta of Public Health Workers by LGUs; (d) providing appropriate/competitive salaries, benefits, and incentives to public and private health workers, among others; and (e) progressively increasing the number of permanent positions for health workers (e.g., provincial/city/municipal nutrition action officers, barangay nutrition scholars, barangay health workers) to achieve the appropriate health worker-to- population ratio.","DOH | LGUs"],[1,"167","5","National Health Human Resource Master Plan","a National Health Human Resource Master Plan will be formulated and implemented.","DOH"],[1,"167","5","Health Workforce Recruitment and Deployment Improvement","The DOH will also improve the recruitment and deployment process.","DOH"],[1,"167","5","Community Health Volunteer Network","a network of community health volunteers who will assist in providing health surveillance and health information dissemination services during health emergencies will be established.",""],[1,"170","4","National Health Human Resource Master Plan","a National Health Human Resource Master Plan will be implemented to provide appropriate health workforce based on population needs.","DOH"],[1,"170","4","Multi-Stakeholder HRH Network","The DOH will lead and institutionalize a multi-stakeholder HRH Network, composed of both public and private organizations and agencies, to formulate and oversee the sustainable implementation, monitoring, periodic evaluation, and reformulation of the Master Plan for the management and development of HRH.","DOH"],[1,"170","4","National Health Workforce Support System","Moreover, a National Health Workforce Support System will be established to assist LGUs in human health resource needs.",""],[1,"170","4","Priority Deployment of Health Professionals in GIDAs","Deployment of health professionals and health workers in GIDAs will be prioritized.",""],[1,"170","4","Expansion of Allied and Health-Related Degree and Training Programs","Existing and new allied and health-related degree and training programs will be expanded and all allied and health-related government-funded scholars must enter into a return service agreement with both the training institution/facility and DOH for at least three years with compensation.","DOH"],[1,"182","8","Barangay Nutrition Scholar Program Law Amendment","Amendment of the law (Presidential Decree 1569) on the Barangay Nutrition Scholar (BNS) Program",""],[1,"182","9","Barangay Nutrition Scholar Qualification and Tenure Reform","This will upgrade the qualifications standards, incentives, and benefits and will ensure the security of tenure of BNS.",""],[1,"183","10","Public Health Workers Benefits and Incentives Reform","The proposed measure will provide appropriate benefits to public health workers across LGUs, regardless of LGU income classification, to promote equity in benefits/incentives received, among others.",""],[1,"185","15","Equitable Hazard Allowance Reform for Public Health Workers","A more equitable hazard allowance of public health workers across salary grades will be pursued.",""]],"145":[[1,"168","1","Epidemiological and Infectious Disease Surveillance Capacity Improvement","Epidemiological and surveillance capacities for COVID-19 and other infectious diseases will be improved at the national, regional, provincial, and municipal levels, focusing on areas at or near major points of entry and strategic LGUs in a region.",""],[1,"168","1","Regional Biosafety Laboratory Expansion","Specifically, an operational Level 2 Biosafety Laboratory must be present in every region, stocked with adequate number of testing kits.",""],[1,"168","1","Digital Contact Tracing and Real-Time Surveillance Tools","Technology such as mobile applications can be utilized to facilitate contact tracing and real-time surveillance of infectious diseases particularly COVID-19.",""],[1,"168","1","Local and Regional Centers for Disease Control Establishment","Moreover, local or regional Centers for Disease Control (CDC) will be established under the supervision of a national CDC or the Research Institute for Tropical Medicine (RITM).",""],[1,"168","2","Mandatory Disease Reporting and Surveillance System Implementation","the DOH and LGUs should also ensure strict implementation of the Mandatory Reporting of Notifiable Diseases and Health Events of Public Health Concern Act (RA 11332), especially the provisions on establishing and maintaining functional disease surveillance and response systems.","DOH | LGUs"],[1,"168","2","National Infection Prevention and Control Guidelines Formulation","Accordingly, the DOH will spearhead the formulation of a national infection prevention and control guidelines/strategies, including quarantine and disinfection protocols that will guide national and local implementers, both in the public and private sectors (e.g., hospitals, health facilities).","DOH"],[1,"183","8","National and Local Health Emergency Preparedness Strengthening","This aims to strengthen the national and local response and preparedness during health emergencies (e.g., pandemic, epidemic).",""],[1,"183","8","National and Local CDC Institutionalization","The proposed measure may institutionalize national and local/regional CDC.",""],[1,"183","8","Medical Reserve Corps for Disasters and Health Emergencies","It may also cover establishing medical reserve corps for disasters and health emergencies; and providing social assistance (i.e., social amelioration) during pandemics.",""],[1,"219","2","Pandemic Response Technology Rollout","This will include the rollout of technologies that will help address the pandemic.",""],[1,"220","4","Pandemic Health Technology Development","Similar to the development of COVID-19 testing kits by local scientists, there will be greater efforts to find ways to manage pandemic situations via STI.",""],[1,"220","4","Mass Testing and Medical Equipment Production","Among these are means by which mass testing can be facilitated, including the design and manufacture of medical equipment that can aid in the treatment of patients such as ventilators, among others.",""],[1,"220","4","Digital Health and Pandemic Response Technologies","Moreover, the demand for health-related technologies (i.e., sanitation booths, contact-tracing applications, and other researches related to the treatment or response to the pandemic) is seen to increase.",""],[1,"224","1","Technology Rollout and Scale-Up for Pandemic and Emergency Response","Intensify the rollout of available technologies that can be used during pandemic, state of calamities, emergencies, and the transition to the new normal.",""],[1,"224","1","Research and Development Support for Medical Countermeasures","Moreover, the government will incentivize, subsidize, and support researchers and research institutions that will engage in R&D related to development of test kits, medical equipment, vaccines (e.g., COVID-19 vaccine), medicine, and others.",""],[1,"235","3","Virus Research Institute Establishment","This will establish a Research Institute that will delve into the study of viruses.",""],[1,"235","4","Center for Disease Control and Prevention Establishment Act","An Act Creating the Center for Disease Control and Prevention, Providing Mechanisms for Epidemic Control, and for Other Purposes",""],[1,"235","5","Communicable Disease Control and Prevention Center","This aims to establish a center that will be the principal agency tasked with developing and applying communicable disease control and prevention initiatives.",""]],"146":[[1,"271","3","Human Rights Protection in Crisis and Emergency Response","The protection of human rights, as enshrined in the Constitution, will be ensured, especially during the implementation of policies and measures in times of crisis and emergencies.",""],[1,"273","17","Human Rights Violations Investigation and Remedy Support","Intensify investigation and resolution of human rights violations cases and empower the poor, marginized, vulnerable and disadvantaged to seek response and remedies for injustice",""],[1,"280","1","Strengthened Investigation and Prosecution of Human Rights Violations","Intensify investigation and resolution of human rights violations cases.",""],[1,"280","1","Client-Based Human Rights Education and Training Programme","The Commission on Human Rights will pursue efforts to empower the poor, marginalized, vulnerable, and disadvantaged to seek response and remedies for injustice through the development of client-based education and training programs.","The Commission on Human Rights"],[1,"280","1","Human Rights Partnership Mechanism","Partnerships with state and non-state duty bearers in addressing human rights violations cases will also be pursued.",""],[1,"280","1","National Action Plan on Women, Peace, and Security","Furthermore, the National Action Plan on Women, Peace, and Security (NAP-WPS) will pursue the protection of human rights of women and girls at all times and the prevention of gender- based violence.",""],[1,"280","2","Human Rights-Based Implementation of Emergency Laws and Protocols","a human-rights based approach will be followed in the implementation of relevant laws, policies, protocols, and guidelines.",""]],"147":[[1,"273","11","Border Control Capacity-Building and International Partnership Measures","Strengthen border control measures to protect OFs against human and drug trafficking through capacity-building and effective partnership with destination countries",""],[1,"273","19","Monitoring Mechanism for Socioeconomic and Political Conditions of OFs","Establish mechanism to monitor the socioeconomic and political conditions of OFs",""],[1,"273","21","Migrant-Serving Agency and Consular Crisis Preparedness Capacity Building","Enhance the capability of migrant-serving agencies and consular offices on crisis preparedness and contingency planning",""],[1,"278","2","Air and Maritime Border Security and Health Screening Upgrade","The threat of global pandemics calls for intensified air and maritime border security and strict imposition of health protocols and quarantine procedures for arriving passengers and visitors.",""]],"148":[[1,"282","8","Local Defense Industry Incentive Scheme","This will promote and stimulate the local defense industry, as in-country enterprises will be entitled to avail incentives under the Omnibus Investments Code (EO 226, s. 1987).",""],[1,"282","8","Promotion of Defense Materiel Exports","The government will promote the export of locally made defense materiel and the in-country enterprises to other countries.",""]],"149":[[1,"283","11","BFP Modernization and Fire Code Enforcement Reform","This will modernize the BFP and enable it to become a fire and emergency medical and rescue services agency capable of responding to hazards such as destructive fires, accidents, and other natural and human-induced disasters.",""],[1,"283","11","Department of Disaster Resilience Establishment","This will establish a Department of Disaster Resilience with sufficiently high level of authority to lead the coordination, monitoring, oversight, and implementation of disaster risk reduction and management efforts.",""]],"151":[[1,"308","2","Acceleration of Social Infrastructure Projects","The implementation of social infrastructure projects will have to be ramped up to make up for the slow progress in the first three years of the Plan implementation.",""],[1,"308","3","Strengthening Local Government Delivery of Devolved Social Services","LGUs must also be able to step up in the provision of devolved social services, including education, health, and sanitation.",""]],"152":[[1,"200","9","Permanent and Resilient Evacuation Center Construction Program","This will establish permanent and resilient (i.e., to earthquake and hydro- meteorological hazards) evacuation centers with the necessary facilities to avoid the practice of using classrooms as evacuation centers during calamities.","NDRRMC"]],"153":[[1,"103","2","Climate-Resilient Irrigation Development and Modernization","Accelerate irrigation development, especially the construction of disaster- and climate-resilient small-scale irrigation systems and retrofitting of existing ones, to be guided by a National Irrigation Master Plan (NIMP).",""],[1,"103","2","Irrigation System Modernization and Maintenance Financing","This includes the financing of the modernization of priority irrigation systems, quick response for restoration works in disaster-prone areas, and regular preventive operations and maintenance for optimal production for the year-round cropping (See Chapter 19).",""],[1,"103","2","Water-Saving and Water-Harvesting Technology Promotion","In addition, to support sustainable consumption and production (SCP) initiatives, proper use of water-saving and water-harvesting technologies such as alternate wetting and drying (AWD), rotational method, rainwater harvesting, and solar-powered irrigation8 will also be promoted in areas where it is applicable.",""],[1,"103","2","Critical Watershed Protection and Rehabilitation","The protection, rehabilitation, and management of critical watersheds for irrigation are critical counterpart interventions to ensure sustainable water supply (See Chapter 20).",""],[1,"111","6","Climate and Disaster Risk Integration in Agricultural Programs","Integrate climate and disaster risks in the design of AFF programs and projects.",""],[1,"292","3","Irrigation Facilities Development and Maintenance","The development and maintenance of irrigation facilities will also be necessary to support the food security goals of the country.",""],[1,"302","2","Irrigation Fund Optimization and Technical Capacity Strengthening","Optimize funds for irrigation development and strengthen technical capacities for the development and maintenance of irrigation facilities guided by the National Irrigation Master Plan.",""],[1,"302","2","Irrigation System Operation, Maintenance, Rehabilitation, and Restoration Shift","Specifically, the government will shift its focus in the short term towards funding the operation and maintenance, rehabilitation, and/or restoration of existing irrigation systems across the regions, instead of funding for the construction of multi- year large irrigation systems.",""],[1,"302","3","Irrigation Sector Master Plan Direction Setting","Other developments in the agricultural sector, such as RCEF and support for diversified, non-traditional, and high-value crop farming, will also be taken into consideration in setting the direction for the irrigation sector under the said master plan.",""],[1,"302","3","Irrigation Operations and Maintenance Capacity Building","Likewise, to ensure effective and sustainable operations and maintenance of irrigation facilities, there will be capacity-building activities to improve the technical skills and workforce of LGUs, National Irrigation Administration, Department of Agriculture-Regional Field Offices, Bureau of Soils and Water Management, Irrigators' Associations, and Small Water Irrigation System Associations.","LGUs | National Irrigation Administration | Department of Agriculture-Regional Field Offices | Bureau of Soils and Water Management"]],"154":[[1,"127","1","Energy Virtual One Stop Shop and Energy Investment Coordinating Council Implementation","Speed up implementation of Energy Virtual One Stop Shop (EVOSS) (RA 11234) and the Energy Investment Coordinating Council (EO 30) to address delays in the implementation of energy infrastructure projects.",""]],"155":[[1,"147","1","Energy and Water Sector Reform Programme","improving quality and reducing the cost of utilities, particularly through energy and water sector reforms ... will be implemented",""]],"156":[[1,"223","8","Commercialization and Utilization of Publicly Funded R&D Technologies","Promote commercialization and utilization of technologies from publicly funded R&D",""],[1,"225","1","Filipinnovation Portal Establishment and Operation","The government will fast-track the establishment of the Filipinnovation portal which will serve as a repository of government and academic research and innovation outputs.",""],[1,"225","2","Interactive STI Communication Platform","the government will launch an interactive communication strategy or platform where STI results, initiatives, and efforts are highlighted and communicated to Filipinos for their feedback.",""],[1,"225","3","R&D Public Awareness and Technology Promotion Campaign","To become more effective in communicating and raising awareness on R&D, investments in promotions and communications will be increased.",""],[1,"225","3","ICT-Based Technology Transfer and Commercialization Program","The government will maximize the use of ICT/online platforms in the conduct of technology transfer and commercialization programs such as science fairs, exhibits, invention contests, and technology transfer days, among others, to help publicize and commercialize the existing technologies from the government, academe, and the industry.",""],[1,"225","3","Face-to-Face Technology Transfer and Commercialization Continuation","Face-to-face/physical technology transfer and commercialization programs will still be continued but in accordance with appropriate social distancing measures.",""],[1,"225","4","Non-Exclusive Public Technology Transfer Policy","Ensure that the transfer or distribution of technologies as a public good will be on a non-exclusive and non-competitive basis.",""],[1,"225","4","Free Technology Access for Target Users","The provision of free technologies to target users such as farmers, fisherfolks, and small-scale industries, among others intends to upgrade their processes and operations for improved productivity.",""],[1,"232","3","Harmonized STI Communication and Advocacy Plan","Government will consolidate all its existing communication advocacy and campaigns and turn it into a comprehensive/harmonized advocacy plan to promote better public appreciation and understanding of STI.",""],[1,"232","3","Private Media Incentives for STI Public Education","Privately owned mass media networks will be incentivized to undertake mass education and promotion of science-responsive communities.",""],[1,"232","4","Public Science Communication Campaign","Aggressively promote to the public the importance and benefits of science in helping resolve national issues.",""],[1,"234","10","Public Technology Adoption Requirement","The bill also seeks to require NGAs, LGUs, and SUCs to adopt publicly funded and generated technologies whenever feasible and practicable.",""]],"157":[[1,"223","12","Human Resource Development Funding Increase","Increase funding for human resource development",""],[1,"223","18","STI Infrastructure Strengthening","Strengthen STI infrastructure",""],[1,"226","4","Science for Change Program Institutionalization","Institutionalize the implementation of the Science for Change Program (S4CP).",""],[1,"226","5","CRADLE Challenge Innovation Support Programme","The CRADLE Challenge has four thematic areas: (a) sustainable supply and logistics, (b) products for the new normal, (c) reinventing the workplace, and (d) services that transcend boundaries.",""],[1,"228","6","Regional RD&E Capacity-Building Programme","This will be complemented by sustained and aggressive capacity-building activities particularly for R&D institutions in the regions to spur regional R&D that addresses local concerns, expands opportunities for growth, and brings about significant",""],[1,"229","3","Public-Private Partnership for Research and Development","The NIC will intensify the undertaking of PPP on R&D, including innovation, to encourage the private sector to deepen their R&D activities while at the same time accelerating the public sector's efforts.",""],[1,"229","6","Human Resource Development Plan for Researchers in Higher Education","Formulate a Human Resource Development Plan for Researchers in Higher Education.",""],[1,"229","7","Regular Revision of Faculty Promotion Guidelines for RD&E and Innovation","the national budget circular guidelines for promoting faculty members in SUCs and institutions supervised by the Technical Education and Skills Development Authority (TESDA) will be revisited regularly to ensure that those who are engaged in RD&E and innovation under the Philippine Innovation Act are given the proper recognition and commensurate points.",""],[1,"230","2","Scholarship Program Expansion","The government will continue and expand the provision of scholarship programs such as the Expanded Specialized Science Secondary Education Scholarships, Expanded Undergraduate S&T Scholarships for Inclusive Development, and Expanded S&T Graduate (Masters/Ph.D.) Scholarships, among others to further encourage students to pursue STI courses.",""],[1,"230","2","Scholarship Applicant Information Drive","This will be complemented with an intensive information drive to further increase the number of scholarship applicants.",""],[1,"230","3","Expansion of Entrepreneurship-Related Courses in Engineering and Allied Disciplines","Expand the implementation of entrepreneurship-related courses to engineering and the other allied disciplines.",""],[1,"231","5","STI-Aligned Higher Education Program Expansion","SUCs will invest in the enhancement of quality of program offerings and will explore offering engineering and science programs to increase the number of scientists and engineers.",""],[1,"231","7","Balik Scientist Program Participation Expansion","The government will aggressively promote the enhanced benefits and incentives under the Balik Scientist Act to encourage wider participation, particularly in sectors and areas where expertise is lacking.",""],[1,"231","9","Science, Technology, and Innovation Facilities Expansion","The government will engage with the academe and industry to build more makerspace, innovation hubs, innovation centers, FabLabs, laboratory facilities, R&D centers, and prototyping facilities, as well as science and technology parks in strategic locations throughout the country to support the innovation and technology requirements of the MSMEs and startups.",""],[1,"231","9","OneLab Network Expansion","Moreover, the OneLab Network, a platform which integrates DOST analytical and testing laboratories and other",""],[1,"232","1","STI Laboratory and Innovation Hub Strengthening","laboratories in the Philippines and ASEAN countries, will be strengthened to provide easy access to testing and calibration services.",""],[1,"234","10","Expansion of Science and Technology Programs","This aims to expand various S&T programs of the DOST (e.g., R&D programs, technology business incubation, foreign scholarships) and prescribes the R&D areas to be considered under the S4C Program.","DOST"],[1,"235","11","Provincial Centers for Science and Technology Conversion to Office","This seeks to strengthen the existing Provincial Centers for Science and Technology (PSTCs) under RA 6959 by converting them into an Office so that the development and transfer of technologies in the rural areas can be vigorously pursued and implemented.",""]],"158":[[1,"169","3","Health Research and Evidence-Based Decision-Making Capacity Strengthening","Capacity to conduct evidence-based policymaking, decision-making, program planning, and implementation in the health and nutrition sector will be strengthened.",""],[1,"169","3","Institutional Capacity Building for Health and Nutrition Research Institutes","Concerned agencies, including health and nutrition research institutes (e.g., DOH, RITM, NNC, DOST-FNRI, DOST-Philippine Council for Health and Research Development, among others) will enhance their internal capacity to produce high quality health and nutrition studies and researches.","DOH | RITM | NNC | DOST-FNRI | DOST-Philippine Council for Health and Research Development"],[1,"169","3","Support for Local Health Scientists and Health Research Investment","There will be increased support for local healthcare scientists and higher investments in health researches especially on vaccine and drug discovery and development (e.g., COVID-19 vaccine) and on zoonotic diseases and risk factors.",""],[1,"169","3","Health Impact Assessment Implementation","A Health Impact Assessment (HIA) will likewise be conducted following the UHC Act.",""],[1,"195","6","COVID-19 Vaccine Research, Regulation, and Procurement Plan","The IATF for Emergency Infectious Diseases Sub-Technical Working Group (sTWG) on Vaccine Development will continue to spearhead the research and development, testing/trials, regulation, and accreditation of the potential COVID-19 vaccines entering the country.",""]],"159":[[1,"90","13","Cultural Diplomacy and Overseas Promotion Initiative","Strengthen cultural diplomacy and promotions overseas",""],[1,"92","4","Cultural Diplomacy and Overseas Promotion Programme","Strengthen cultural diplomacy and promotions overseas.","Department of Foreign Affairs | DTI | Department of Tourism | culture agencies"],[1,"92","5","Overseas Cultural Diplomacy and Promotion Program","the government will carry out cultural diplomacy and promotions overseas through digital means as a way for OFs to maintain their connection to their culture",""],[1,"92","5","Cultural Diplomacy Awareness Response for Migrant Communities","In cases where racism and discrimination against migrant communities escalate abroad, cultural diplomacy programs will become vehicles in raising awareness and understanding of Philippine culture and cultural diversity among non-Filipinos",""],[1,"93","4","Accession to UNESCO 2005 Convention on Cultural Expressions","The Philippines' accession to the United Nations Educational, Scientific and Cultural Organisation (UNESCO) 2005 Convention on the Protection and Promotion of the Diversity of Cultural Expressions will be hastened.",""],[1,"93","4","Creative Economy International Linkages Promotion","Industry linkages with international stakeholders will likewise be promoted as a venue for the Philippine creative economy to be apprised of global trends and to optimize opportunities for marketing and distribution of creative content, products, and services.",""],[1,"96","6","Ratification of the Convention on the Protection of the Diversity of Cultural Expressions","Ratifying this Convention will further promote and protect the works of the creatives in the country.",""]],"160":[[1,"93","6","STEM to STEAM Program Transformation","the transformation of the Department of Education's (DepEd) Science, Technology, Engineering, and Mathematics (STEM) Program to Science, Technology, Engineering, Arts, and Math (STEAM) is a welcome development.","Department of Education"],[1,"93","6","Secondary School Arts Facilities and Teacher Support","Secondary level schools that offer special program for the arts will also be equipped with facilities and well-trained teachers while establishing regional arts academies.",""],[1,"93","6","Cultural Education and Arts Specialization Pathways","At the tertiary level, young people will be encouraged to take specialized programs on cultural education and arts to become future culture and arts managers.",""],[1,"93","7","Culture-Related NC II Qualifications Development","TESDA, in collaboration with the NCCA, has developed culture-related NC II qualifications in nine areas: (1) handloom weaving (upright loom); (2) handloom weaving (backstrap loom); (3) beadworks and accessories making; (4) mat weaving and diversified product making; (5) basket weaving; (6) embroidery; (7) wood carving; (8) paper mache making; and (9) pottery.","TESDA | NCCA"],[1,"94","1","TESDA Industry and Market Linkage Initiative","Technical Education and Skills Development Authority (TESDA) will also be connected to industries and markets to promote creative excellence and for them to enjoy income security.",""]],"161":[[1,"269","6","Peace Education Mainstreaming and Culture of Peace Promotion","The government will continue and expand the mainstreaming of peace education and promote a culture of peace and non-violence in both formal and non-formal settings.",""],[1,"269","6","Integration of Peace Education Across Education Levels","These include the integration of peace education in basic, higher, and technical and vocational education and integration of Mindanaoan narratives from indigenous peoples, Bangsamoro Filipinos, and Filipino Christian migrants into the",""],[1,"270","1","Peace Studies Advocacy and Capacity-Building Programme","This will be coupled with advocacy programs, capacity building for faculty, and development of syllabi and training materials for peace studies in higher education.",""],[1,"270","1","Online Learning Materials and Peace Education Mainstreaming Modules","Development of online learning materials and capacity building modules for COP and peace education mainstreaming will also be pursued as part of the new normal situations.",""],[1,"270","1","COP Sessions Under Health Protocols","Other COP sessions will be conducted, firmly adhering to prescribed health standards and protocols.",""],[1,"270","2","Social Healing, Reconciliation, and Peacebuilding Programs","The government will actively undertake social healing, reconciliation, and peacebuilding programs.",""],[1,"270","2","Reintegration and Rehabilitation Program for Former Violent Extremists","the implementation of reintegration and rehabilitation programs for former violent extremists (FVEs) through the Task Force Balik Loob (TFBL) will be conflict-, gender-, and culture-sensitive.",""],[1,"270","2","Safe Spaces for Healing and Reconciliation","These will also include various programs and projects such as provision of safe spaces for healing and reconciliation of SVEs and their families, families of survivors and victims of conflict-related violence, and the communities.",""],[1,"270","2","Community Relationship-Building for IDPs and Stakeholders","Furthermore, the building and rebuilding of relationships of the IDPs with their community leaders, sectoral representatives, NGAs, LGUs, CSOs, and all stakeholders is expected to build social cohesion, resilience, and sustainable peace towards the recovery and rehabilitation of Marawi and its nearby municipalities.",""]],"162":[[1,"128","3","Consumer Act Amendment for Stronger Consumer Protection","Amend the Consumer Act to strengthen protection for consumers.","DTI"],[1,"128","4","Consumer Welfare Organization Engagement and Dialogue Mechanism","Regular engagement and continuous dialogue among the government, non-profit consumer organizations, and other relevant non-profit private organizations will be established.",""],[1,"129","2","E-commerce Policy Framework and Consumer Protection Guidelines","Formulate and enforce policy framework/guidelines for online sellers and buyers to spur e- commerce growth.","DTI | DA | DOH"],[1,"130","16","Consumer Protection Law Update","The law needs to be updated to efficiently and effectively address consumer concerns and align existing business and industry practices to be at par with international standards and best practices and to cover the use of technology applications (e.g. e-commerce).",""],[1,"130","18","Consumer Act Amendments for Product Safety and Digital Commerce","Among the Consumer Act amendments being considered are: (a) stronger measure to give DTI the authority to close down establishments caught in the act of manufacturing, distributing, selling, producing, displaying, or importing hazardous and defective products; (b) coverage on e- commerce and ICT; (c) protection from deceptive and misleading online or digital advertisements; (d) real-time consumer hotline to be made mandatory for all manufacturers/suppliers/final producers to respond to consumer complaints/suggestions and a stronger policy for return and refund options; (e) requirement for foreign products with labels to have English or Filipino translation before being allowed entry into the country; and (f) exemption of businesses offering price-discounted rates for single or bulk-purchase of products or services from the requirement to secure sales promotion permit from DTI to facilitate growth of e-commerce, among others.","DTI"],[1,"138","4","E-commerce Dispute Settlement Mechanism","Strengthen consumer/producer rights' protection in e-commerce transactions by establishing an effective dispute settlement mechanism to govern and streamline processes for the resolution of complaints, which may involve fraud, cyber-crime, payment security issues, and security of websites, among others.",""],[1,"138","9","Secure E-Payment Systems and Online Consumer Protection","Establish secure e-payment systems and ensuring consumer protection online.",""],[1,"140","2","Consumer Protection Act Amendment","Amend the Consumer Act to broaden protection for consumers.",""],[1,"140","3","Financial Consumer Protection Framework Implementation and Monitoring","Implement and monitor compliance with the Financial Consumer Protection Framework (FCP) by BSP Supervised Financial Institutions (BSFIs).",""],[1,"140","4","Consumer Protection Standards and Market Monitoring","Strictly enforce standards and regulations to protect and empower consumers against unfair trade practices and fraudulent schemes.",""],[1,"141","1","Financial Consumer Protection Bill","Pursue the passage of the Financial Consumer Protection Bill, which aims to provide the regulatory framework for financial services and products offered by financial institutions, including digital financial services, to protect the interest of financial consumers and invigorate confidence in the financial markets.",""],[1,"141","10","E-Commerce Legal and Consumer Protection Reform","The law needs to be revisited to make it more comprehensive in detailing e-commerce transactions, specifying the rights of consumers, strengthening the imposition of penalties on service providers, and requiring service providers to provide high-security measures to ensure safety from possible breaches on data processing and money handling.",""],[1,"142","2","E-Commerce Regulatory Framework","Defines the scope and coverage of internet transactions, apart from the sale or exchange of digital products, and lays down the code of conduct and qualifications for businesses who wish to engage in e-commerce.",""],[1,"142","2","E-Commerce Bureau for Consumer Complaints","Also proposes the creation of an E-commerce Bureau to handle complaints on internet transactions, protect consumers' rights, and facilitate the speedy resolution of complaints, among others.",""]],"163":[[1,"242","12","Exploration of Optimal Financing Schemes","Explore optimal financing schemes including multilateral and market financing",""],[1,"242","16","Medium-Term Debt and Contingent Liability Management Strategy Recalibration","Recalibrate medium term debt and contingent liability management strategy",""],[1,"244","1","Economic Recovery Plan Financing Mobilization","The national government will explore various financing schemes, including multilateral institutions to ensure sufficient resources are available to support the economic recovery plan.",""],[1,"244","1","Domestic and Offshore Debt Issuance for Recovery Funding","Furthermore, the Bureau of the Treasury will tap the local market through local bonds issuance and the offshore commercial markets through issuance of dollar-denominated debt papers, \"panda\" bonds, and \"samurai\" bonds for additional funding sources.",""],[1,"244","2","Debt and Contingent Liability Management Reform","Recalibrate debt and contingent liability management by: (a) continuing to adopt a strategic and sustainable financing mix in favor of domestic sources and optimization of Official Development Assistance resource; (b) further diversifying funding sources and instruments; and (c) improving the liquidity of the government securities market.",""],[1,"244","2","Local Currency Debt Market Development Roadmap","These strategies can be supported by the Local Currency Debt Market Development Roadmap - a reform package that focuses on deepening market liquidity, improving price discovery, and enhancing regulatory oversight and surveillance.",""]],"164":[[1,"15","25","Regional Development through the Balik Probinsya Bagong Pag-asa Program","this updated PDP contains five major programs designed to build the resilience of individuals, families, business, government, and society under the new normal: (5) regional development through the Balik Probinsya Bagong Pag-asa Program",""],[1,"16","8","Balik Probinsya Bagong Pag-asa Program","A major initiative to decongest urban areas is the Balik Probinsya Bagong Pag-asa Program (BP2).",""],[1,"53","2","BP2 Sustainable Rural Development and Voluntary Relocation Program","The program, which will have short-, medium- and long-term components, will provide the mechanism for convergence among regional agencies and local governments in investing in sustainable rural development projects.",""],[1,"53","3","BP2 Program Spatial Planning Support","The NSS will guide the implementation of the BP2 program by providing the trends in settlements development and the roles of various urban centers in the country.",""]],"165":[[1,"60","4","Demographic Transition Acceleration Policies and Programs","Towards this end, policies and programs to accelerate the demographic transition along with improving access to health and education services were instituted.",""]],"166":[[1,"84","5","Justice Sector Business Continuity Plan","A business continuity plan will be drafted to ensure sustained administration of justice.",""],[1,"84","5","Sector-Wide National Emergency Preparedness and Response Framework","This includes the formulation of a sector-wide national emergency preparedness and response framework.",""],[1,"84","5","Justice Sector Emergency Coordination and Guidance Mechanism","Coordination with and guidance from justice sector agencies during emergency situations will be facilitated relative to the legal framework, administration of justice, and protection of human rights.",""]],"167":[[1,"85","8","Judiciary Public Information and Online Access Platform Enhancement","Public information on the justice system, including access to legal remedies and assistance, will be continuously improved through agency websites and other media and communication platforms.",""],[1,"85","8","Online Judiciary Information Platform Maintenance and Expansion","Online judiciary information platforms (i.e., court locator, judicial application scheduler, public assistance helpdesk) will be sustained and maximized, including the accessibility of court details, to ensure easier facilitation of online filing of complaint and grant of bails.",""],[1,"86","10","Judiciary Court Redistribution and Expansion","Where necessary, the existing courts may be redistributed and new courts created as needed.",""]],"168":[[1,"81","2","Witness and Whistleblower Protection Programs","The Witness Protection Program will be strengthened and a whistleblower protection program will be established to facilitate case buildup, investigation, and prosecution, especially on heinous crimes and high profile cases.",""],[1,"81","2","International Criminal Justice Cooperation","International cooperation on criminal justice will also be pursued including mutual legal assistance and transfer of sentence.",""],[1,"86","18","Witness and Whistleblower Protection Programs","Strengthen the Witness Protection Program to encourage more witnesses to be covered and maintained coverage, towards successful prosecution, especially of heinous and high profile crimes; and the Whistleblower Protection Program to encourage and protect whistleblowers.",""]],"169":[[1,"90","10","Cultural Asset Resilience Measures","Adopt resilience measures in the design and use of cultural assets across the country, including historic and cultural infrastructures, to address the new normal",""],[1,"90","15","Heritage Conservation and Management Mainstreaming","Institutionalize and intensify heritage conservation and management in cultural and tourism development plans and programs",""],[1,"91","6","Resilient Reconfiguration of Cultural Assets","Adopt resilience measures in the design and use of cultural assets across the country, including historic and cultural infrastructures, to address the new normal.",""],[1,"91","7","Health and Sanitation Guidelines for Cultural Spaces","To ensure safe reopening of cultural spaces and eventual resumption of cultural and creative activities, cultural agencies will coordinate with the Department of Health, Department of Labor and Employment (DOLE), and Department of Trade and Industry (DTI) in crafting health and sanitation guidelines.","Department of Health | Department of Labor and Employment (DOLE) | Department of Trade and Industry (DTI)"],[1,"92","1","Establishment and Redesign of Cultural Parks and Hubs","The redesign or establishment of cultural structures, especially open-space cultural parks or hubs in the regions will be supported.","National Commission for Culture and the Arts (NCCA) | Film Development Council of the Philippines (FDCP) | National Library of the Philippines | Philippine Sports Commission"],[1,"92","1","Culture Hubs Development in Bohol and Davao Region","The establishment of culture hubs in Bohol and Davao Region, and the establishment of open-space cultural parks and hubs in other parts of the country will be pursued in collaboration with LGUs.",""],[1,"94","5","Local Heritage Management Integration in Local Development and Land Use Plans","LGUs are expected to be more proactive in heritage management by incorporating heritage preservation, protection, and promotion efforts into their local development plans.",""],[1,"94","5","Heritage Protection Integration in Land Use Planning","Land use plans should also integrate protection and preservation of heritage.",""],[1,"94","5","Local Culture and Arts Councils Capacity-Building Programme","Capacity-building programs and activities to ensure the full functionality of Local Culture and Arts Councils will also be institutionalized through collaborative work among the NCCA, LGUs, and Regional Development Councils.","NCCA | LGUs | Regional Development Councils"],[1,"94","5","Heritage Documentation and Cultural Mapping Capacity Development","These include developing capabilities for heritage documentation, cultural mapping, planning, policymaking, and development.",""],[1,"94","5","Local Heritage Management Financing Guidance","LGUs are especially encouraged to utilize a portion of their Internal Revenue Allotment based on the Department of Budget and Management's Local Budget Memorandum No. 78, s. 2019 for local heritage management efforts.","Department of Budget and Management"],[1,"94","5","Monitoring of LGU Compliance with the National Cultural Heritage Act","In implementing all these, the NCCA and the Department of Interior and Local Government will be vigilant in the monitoring of LGU compliance with the National Cultural Heritage Act (RA 10066).","NCCA | Department of Interior and Local Government"],[1,"96","1","Heritage Conservation Institutionalization and Management Strengthening","Institutionalize and intensify heritage conservation and management in cultural and tourism development plans and programs.",""],[1,"96","1","Heritage Conservation Management Plan Development and Policy Enforcement","Responsible entities mandated to preserve heritage structures and owners of cultural properties will then ensure the development of conservation management plans and stronger implementation of related policies in preserving heritage structures.",""],[1,"96","1","Heritage Preservation and Conservation Expert Development Programme","Plans and programs on the development of heritage preservation and conservation experts will be initiated.",""]],"170":[[1,"90","6","Filipino Culture Information Development and Access Liberalization","Intensify the development, production, dissemination, and liberalization of access to information on Filiipino culture",""],[1,"90","12","Protection of the Right to Access Cultural Resources","Strengthen the protection of the right to access cultural resources by whole of society, with special attention to the needs of vulnerable sectors (indigenous peoples, women, youth and children, persons with disability, senior citizens, and Muslim Filipinos)",""],[1,"92","2","Cultural Information Development and Dissemination Initiative","Intensify the development, production, dissemination, and liberalization of access to information on Filipino culture.",""],[1,"95","1","Protection of Access to Cultural Resources","Strengthen the protection of the right to access cultural resources by whole of society, with particular attention to the needs of vulnerable sectors of society (indigenous peoples, women, youth and children, persons with disabilities, senior citizens, and Muslim Filipinos).",""],[1,"95","1","Online and Digital Culture, Arts, and Heritage Programs","Online and digital culture, arts, and heritage programs will be designed to inspire bayanihan and support lifelong learning, creative collaboration, mental health and wellbeing, and cultural and heritage tourism, among others.",""],[1,"95","2","Digital and Online Cultural Program Expansion","Existing Knowledge Development Centers (KDCs), Institutes and Schools of Living Traditions (I/SLTs), Sentro Rizal, Arts Centers, museums, and cultural centers will improve on digital and online programs to continue respective work of transmitting knowledge and skills and cultural dissemination.",""],[1,"95","3","Enhanced Programs for Vulnerable Sectors","Programs designed specifically for the needs of vulnerable sectors will be enhanced in line with the principle of respect for cultural diversity and cultural rights, notwithstanding community quarantine protocols that limit social gatherings.",""],[1,"95","4","Community-Based Skills Development Program for Indigenous Peoples and Indigenous Cultural Communities","The Community-Based Skills Development Program for indigenous peoples and indigenous cultural communities under the TESDA and NCCA will be supported under a blended learning modality, as it enhances existing SLTs by developing trainers from different regions.","TESDA | NCCA"],[1,"95","4","Cultural Access Improvement for Muslim Filipinos","Access to cultural resources for Muslim Filipinos will be improved, so they can participate in cultural life without fear of prejudice.",""],[1,"95","4","Accessible Cultural Infrastructure and Resource Materials Initiative","Cultural infrastructure and resource materials will be made accessible to persons with disabilities through technology and innovative design.",""],[1,"95","4","Repackaging of Inclusive Sports Programs for Community Quarantine","Programs that are responsive to this strategy such as the Philippine Sports Commission's Children's Games, Differently-Abled Sports for Life, Indigenous Peoples' Games, and Women in Sports will have to be repackaged in light of community quarantine guidelines.","Philippine Sports Commission"],[1,"96","8","National Library Charter and Public Library Standardization Reform","Establish the charter of the National Library of the Philippines to promote full intellectual and cultural development of the Filipino.",""]],"171":[[1,"92","3","Interagency Heritage Research and Documentation Initiative","Documentation and research on both tangible and intangible heritage will be improved through interagency research initiatives.",""],[1,"92","3","Research Consolidation Mechanism for Heritage Documentation","Mechanisms to consolidate research works by relevant government agencies and independent organizations will be established to ensure that all documentations are captured and used as bases for government interventions.",""],[1,"92","3","Indigenous Knowledge Systems Documentation Partnerships","The involvement of the academe and other research institutions in partnering with indigenous cultural communities and indigenous peoples (ICCs/IPs) as primary participants in indigenous knowledge systems and practices (IKSP) documentation initiatives will also be encouraged.",""],[1,"92","3","NCIP Guidelines Review and Enhancement for IKSP Documentation","the National Commission on Indigenous Peoples (NCIP) will continuously review and enhance the guidelines on research and documentation of IKSPs, as well as the FPIC process to balance the protection of IPs while implementing projects.","National Commission on Indigenous Peoples (NCIP)"],[1,"92","3","NCIP Cultural Integrity Safeguards Reform Coordination","NCIP will continue to work with agencies and other partner-stakeholders to facilitate and implement necessary reforms to safeguard cultural expressions and uphold the cultural integrity of ICCs/IPs.","NCIP"],[1,"95","5","Philippine Cultural Statistics Framework Implementation","The Philippine Cultural Statistics Framework (PCSF) will be implemented as this generates the needed cultural statistics and indicators for evidence-based planning, policymaking, and programming.",""],[1,"95","5","Ethnographic Studies of Indigenous Peoples","Given the vulnerability of IP culture, the conduct of ethnographies of Philippine indigenous peoples will be a priority.",""],[1,"95","5","Statistics Development for Muslim Filipinos","Similarly, statistics on Muslim Filipinos will be developed.",""],[1,"95","5","Cultural and Creative Industry Mapping and Training","Cultural and creative industry mapping will be intensified by DTI and NCCA to better inform planning and programming for the sector through adequate funding and LGU-level trainings.","DTI | NCCA"],[1,"95","6","Sector Registries for Vulnerable Groups Improvement","agencies such as the NCIP, National Commission on Muslim Filipinos, NCCA, DTI-DCP, and FDCP, will improve the generation of registries for IPs, Muslim Filipinos, creative and cultural workers, and freelancers, and coordinate the same with other social protection programs of the government","NCIP | National Commission on Muslim Filipinos | NCCA | DTI-DCP | FDCP"]],"172":[[1,"100","34","Land Reclassification and Conversion Law Enforcement","Strictly enforce and monitor the implementation of existing laws, rules, and regulations on land reclassification and conversion",""],[1,"105","2","Land Reclassification and Conversion Enforcement and Monitoring Reform","Strictly enforce and monitor the implementation of laws, rules, and regulations on land reclassification and conversion.",""],[1,"112","5","Prime Agricultural Land Protection and Land Use Enforcement","Under this bill, prime agricultural lands shall be protected through proper and rational delineation, classification or reclassification, allocation, establishment, utilization and management of these lands.",""],[1,"113","3","Progressive Idle Land Tax","Impose a progressive idle land tax",""]],"173":[[1,"114","2","Inclusive Innovation and Industrial Strategy Operationalization","the industry sector needs to rapidly operationalize the strategies under the Inclusive Innovation and Industrial Strategy (i3s, pronounced eye- cube-s).",""],[1,"114","2","Human Resource Development for Technology Use","the i3s underscores the need to build up our human resource to utilize technologies;",""],[1,"114","2","Inclusive Business Model Linkages for Domestic Firms","adopt inclusive business models to link smaller domestic-based firms to larger enterprises;",""],[1,"114","2","Startup Ecosystem Strengthening for Tech-Based Startups","strengthen the startup ecosystem to assist tech-based startups, particularly those inclined to develop health or industrial solutions in response to the current pandemic;",""],[1,"114","2","Business Continuity Planning for Supply Chain Resilience","formulate business continuity plans (BCPs) for enhanced supply and value chain resilience.",""],[1,"114","2","Cross-Sector Structural Reform for Digital Transformation","The urgent passage of structural reforms that cut across multiple sectors is needed to fast-track a national digital transformation responsive to the current crisis.",""],[1,"117","2","Digital Economy Partnership and Innovation Strategy","reformulated strategies in the medium term will harness the ability of the academe, the private sector, and the government to maximize the opportunities of the digital economy.",""],[1,"117","2","Technology Access and Innovation Capacity Building","This will require accessing new technology and innovation, building innovative talent, and encouraging entrepreneurship that uses technology-enabled business models to leverage opportunities and growth of budding small-scale enterprises.",""],[1,"117","16","Technology-Enabled Entrepreneurship Promotion","Encourage entrepreneurship leveraging technology-enabled business models",""],[1,"117","20","Digital Transformation for Ease of Doing Business","Improve ease of doing business to boost industry expansion through digital transformation",""]],"174":[[1,"117","1","Business and Consumer Confidence Revival Measures","Under the new normal, the focus will be to revive business and consumer confidence in the immediate term.",""],[1,"117","1","Essential Goods Manufacturing Support","In the manufacturing sector, production of merchandise goods will favor necessities such as food, beverages, medicine, pharmaceutical and other chemical products, and other essential and complementary goods.",""],[1,"117","1","Health Facility Construction and Rehabilitation","Construction will now include building quarantine and other health facilities and rehabilitating existing ones to increase the capacity of the health care system.",""],[1,"117","14","Manufacturing Production Repurposing Support","Support the re-purposing of manufacturing production",""],[1,"119","2","Registry of Essential Goods Manufacturers","Establish a registry of firms that are or will be engaged in the manufacture of essential goods.",""],[1,"119","3","Workplace Reconfiguration and Health Protocol Support","Provide assistance in re-configuration of production areas, taking into consideration minimum public health standards for COVID-19 mitigation.",""],[1,"119","3","Private Sector Dialogue and Business Health Protocol Facilitation","The government will regularly conduct dialogues with the private sector to understand and respond to industry needs.",""],[1,"119","3","ICT Capacity and Health System Investment","Adequate investments to enhance the country's ICT capabilities (see Chapter 19) and strengthen the country's healthcare system (see Chapter 10) will also be prioritized.",""],[1,"119","4","Business Regulatory Streamlining for Essential Goods Production","Reduce transaction costs by streamlining complex rules and regulations affecting business operations of companies that are repurposing.",""],[1,"119","4","Streamlined Licensing and Certification Procedures","Clear and transparent rules and guidelines will be drafted and implemented in the process of obtaining licenses and certificates.",""],[1,"119","4","Regulatory Framework for Essential Goods Production","a regulatory framework for the production of these essential goods (e.g., PPEs) will also be formulated and enforced.",""],[1,"119","6","Expansion of the Manufacturer Registry for Basic Necessities and Prime Commodities","The DTI Consumer Protection and Advocacy Bureau (CPAB) already has a registry of manufacturers of basic necessities and prime commodities which can be expanded.","DTI Consumer Protection and Advocacy Bureau (CPAB)"]],"175":[[1,"117","10","Regional Business-Matching Platform","Facilitate business-matching activities across regions utilizing technology-enabling platforms",""],[1,"118","1","Regional Business-Matching Platform","Facilitate business-matching activities across regions via technology-enabling platforms.",""],[1,"118","3","Value Chain Mapping and Business Continuity Support","Provide technical assistance in mapping out value chains across primary, secondary, and tertiary industries to determine alternative suppliers and address production bottlenecks.",""],[1,"118","3","MSME and Large Enterprise Supplier Partnership Facilitation","the government will facilitate partnerships between MSMEs and large enterprises (LEs) in the process of identifying alternative domestic suppliers in lieu of external ones for enhanced value chain resilience",""],[1,"118","3","Digital Platform Market Access Expansion","Utilizing digital platforms will reduce transaction costs as it enables farmers, manufacturers, and suppliers to also gain access to domestic and external markets.",""],[1,"118","4","Domestic Investment Promotion and Business-Matching Support","Strengthen domestic investment promotion and support business-matching activities at the local level.",""],[1,"118","5","Local Investment and Incentives Code Adoption and Implementation","Encourage LGUs to adopt and implement their Local Investment and Incentives Code (LIICs) (see Chapter 9C)",""],[1,"118","7","Supplier Development Program","The implementation of the Supplier Development Program (SDP) of the DTI-BOI and World Bank-IFC for the automotive, electronics, and aerospace sectors is a concrete example of how government can facilitate partnerships between local auto parts and electronics suppliers and the automotive and aerospace industry.","DTI-BOI | World Bank-IFC"],[1,"118","8","Investment Promotion Coordination and Outreach","On investment promotion, the following requires close coordination of the DTI-BOI and various IPAs with the LGU, (a) identify investment opportunities; (b) invite local investors to participate in investment-related activities; (c) disseminate investment-related information; and, (d) invite local proponents to participate in the organized missions and matching.","DTI-BOI | various IPAs | LGU"],[1,"121","5","Startup and MSME Linkage to Cooperatives and Large Enterprises","Promote linking startups and MSMEs to cooperatives and large enterprises (LEs) to enhance value and supply chain resilience and spur innovation.",""]],"176":[[1,"120","2","Public-Private Partnership Investment in Urban Basic Resource Infrastructure","Public-private partnerships will be encouraged to invest ahead using available technologies.",""],[1,"120","2","Real-Time Water Quality Monitoring and Small-Scale Water Recycling","real-time water quality monitoring as well as small-scale water recycling systems in the interim will be explored to effectively service households and businesses in major urban areas.",""],[1,"120","2","Expansion of Dependable Power Generation Capacity","the government will ensure continuous supply of power through increasing the country's dependable capacity (in megawatt).",""]],"177":[[1,"121","6","Sustainable Consumption and Production Integration","Integrate sustainable consumption and production (SCP) processes.",""],[1,"121","6","Sustainability Incentive Program","In the construction sector, the Sustainability Incentive Program will be promoted to reduce greenhouse gas emissions in built environments, and for construction of",""]],"178":[[1,"126","1","Technopreneurship in Balik Probinsya Bagong Pag-asa Program","Technopreneurship will also be considered in the implementation of the Balik Probinsya Bagong Pag- asa Program, to address livelihood and job scarcity as support to regional growth and development.",""],[1,"129","3","Rural Special Economic Zones Development","Administrative Order No. 18 series of 2019, \"Accelerating rural progress through robust development of Special Economic Zones in the countryside,\" and Executive Order No. 114, the \"Balik Probinsya Bagong Pag-asa Program,\" are perceived as complementary measures.",""],[1,"129","5","Regional Transportation and Logistics Hub Development","Encourage PPP, joint ventures (JVs), and other modes of partnership in building a Transportation and Logistics Hub in every region to encourage countryside investment.",""],[1,"145","10","Digital Value and Supply Chain Mapping","Utilize digital platforms in mapping out value and supply chains",""],[1,"149","1","Digital Value and Supply Chain Mapping Platform","Utilize digital platforms in mapping out value and supply chains to find alternative suppliers and address production bottlenecks.",""],[1,"149","1","Digital Technical Assistance for Enterprise Supply Chain Linkages","In providing technical assistance to enterprises, digital platforms will be useful in linking farmers, producers, suppliers, distributors, and retailers to consumers.",""],[1,"149","1","Integration of Existing GIS Platforms","Integration of all relevant existing GIS platforms of relevant agencies will also be pursued (see Chapter 9A).",""],[1,"149","2","Startup and Enterprise Linkage Promotion","Create linkages between startups, MSMEs, cooperatives, and other large enterprises (LEs) to spur innovation and create new markets.",""],[1,"149","2","Social Enterprise and Inclusive Business Promotion","Social enterprises and inclusive business (IB) models will be promoted.",""],[1,"149","2","Micro and Small Supplier Linkage and Market Access Support","The government will also facilitate linking micro and small suppliers to cooperatives for purposes of facilitating access to finance, and to medium and large enterprises to access/diversify markets and enhance supply chain resilience, leveraging digital platforms, as appropriate.",""]],"179":[[1,"138","8","Microinsurance Product Expansion and Business Continuity Planning","Expand microinsurance products to include non-life business insurance and increase business owners' awareness on insurance.",""],[1,"138","8","MSME Microinsurance Uptake and Business Continuity Support","Encourage businesses, especially MSMEs, to avail of microinsurance to protect their businesses and investments and to craft business continuity plans that take into account possibilities of multiple crises including pandemics.",""],[1,"143","2","Urgent Consumer and Business Confidence Revival Measures","In response, the government has formulated urgent interventions to revive consumer and business confidence.",""],[1,"143","2","Digital Economy and Antifragility Measures","Focusing on laying down a healthy and resilient Philippines, the medium-term strategies will leverage the digital economy and put in place antifragility measures.",""],[1,"148","4","Enterprise Rehabilitation Fund and Business Adjustment Support","Establish an Enterprise Rehabilitation Fund (ERF) and implement adjustment measures to startups, MSMEs, and cooperatives severely affected by calamities and national emergencies.",""],[1,"148","4","Debt Relief and Loan Fee Suspension Program","Ongoing debt relief programs are being implemented, including suspension of imposition of non-interest fees and charges on loans incurred.",""],[1,"148","4","Post-Quarantine Payment Deferment, Tax Relief, and Concessional Lending Measures","In the post-community quarantine period, the following interventions will be monitored and extended if needed: (a) payment deferment to government (e.g., deferment of tax remittance such as withholding tax, VAT, SSS, PhilHealth); (b) payment deferment to debtor (e.g., rent, banks, utility companies); (c) tax discounts or tax credits; (d) low-interest loans from government; and (e) low - interest loans from banks.",""],[1,"148","8","MSME Financing Support in Economic Stimulus Programs","Sufficient government support for MSME financing, to be funded under the General Appropriations Act or relevant legislation, will be considered in all forms of economic stimulus programs.",""],[1,"148","8","Livelihood Seeding Program - Negosyo sa Barangay","Some of these programs which target micro and small enterprises are: (a) Livelihood Seeding Program - Negosyo sa Barangay;",""],[1,"148","8","Pondo sa Pagbabago at Pag-asenso Program","Some of these programs which target micro and small enterprises are: (c) Pondo sa Pagbabago at Pag-asenso Program;",""],[1,"148","8","Small Business Corporation Financing Programs","Some of these programs which target micro and small enterprises are: (d) Small business corporation financing programs;",""],[1,"148","8","Go Lokal! Support Program","Some of these programs which target micro and small enterprises are: (e) Go Lokal !.",""],[1,"152","5","Enterprise Rehabilitation Fund for Calamity-Stricken MSMEs","The bill will establish an Enterprise Rehabilitation Fund for calamity-stricken MSMEs.",""],[1,"152","5","Free and Discounted MSME Selling Space Support","It will also provide MSMEs with free selling space in government buildings, structures, and open areas, as well as free selling areas or discounted rent in private malls and other commercial selling establishments.",""],[1,"152","7","Strategic Firm Financial Assistance Program","Provide financial assistance to firms that are strategically important to economic recovery in view of their role in providing employment and supporting the Philippine economy.",""]],"180":[[1,"138","10","Digital Taxation Framework Reform","Establish and institutionalize a clear and simple digital taxation framework that is efficient and fair.",""],[1,"141","5","Regulatory Governance Baseline Survey","and a comprehensive baseline survey on regulatory governance and substance.",""],[1,"152","10","Tax Incentives Management and Transparency Act Amendment","Amendment of the Tax Incentives Management and Transparency Act (TIMTA)",""],[1,"152","11","Mandatory Submission of Data for Economic Cost-Benefit Analysis","Amend existing provision to require/mandate various Registered Business Entities (RBEs) and Investment Promotion Agencies (IPAs) to submit to NEDA relevant information needed to conduct economic cost-benefit analysis (CBA) and to have the flexibility to refine scope of data requirement and data tools that will adequately capture information relevant to the conduct of this CBA.","NEDA"]],"181":[[1,"142","4","Legal Framework for the Gig Economy","Seeks to establish a legal framework for the \"gig economy\" that will map out strategies to promote and strengthen digital careers, as well as provide the needed institutional support.",""],[1,"142","4","Extension of Social Protection for Digital Platform Workers","requires the government to extend the social protection system appropriate to this new mode of work, especially in times of economic downturns caused by calamities and public emergencies.",""],[1,"161","21","Flexible Work Arrangements Policy","Ensure that flexible work arrangements allow members of the workforce to balance their household and work duties",""],[1,"161","32","Workplace Safety and Health under Flexible Working Arrangements","Ensure safety and health in the workplace amid intensified adoption of flexible working arrangements",""]],"182":[[1,"164","4","Communicable Disease Case-Finding and Response Services","The DOH will continue to intensify COVID-19, TB, and HIV case-finding activities.","DOH"],[1,"164","4","COVID-19 Contact Tracing, Testing, Isolation, and Treatment","There will be continuous contact tracing, timely testing, isolation, and treatment of persons affected by COVID-19.",""],[1,"164","4","Tuberculosis Treatment and HIV Co-Infection Services","Adequate TB services will be provided for TB-infected patients, especially for those drug-resistant TB cases and people living with HIV (PLHIV).",""],[1,"164","4","Anti-Retroviral Therapy Provision for PLHIV","Anti-Retroviral Therapy for PLHIV will continuously be provided.",""],[1,"164","4","Integrated HIV Care Service Expansion","Integrated services for HIV care will be expanded by establishing social hygiene clinics, sundown clinics, and HIV care facilities.",""],[1,"164","4","TB and HIV Education and Promotion Campaigns","Moreover, TB and HIV education and promotion programs will be enhanced to increase public awareness and reduce stigma.",""]],"183":[[1,"165","2","Non-Communicable Disease Risk Reduction Measures","the implementation of policies and programs will be intensified to reduce the prevalence of behavioral risks factors such as tobacco use, harmful use of alcohol, physical inactivity, and unhealthy diet.",""],[1,"165","2","Excise Taxes on Sweetened Beverages, Alcohol, and E-Cigarettes","The Department of Finance (DOF) will continue to impose excise tax on sweetened beverages along with taxes for alcohol products and e-cigarettes, and strategies to reduce salt consumption.","Department of Finance (DOF)"],[1,"165","2","Whole-of-Government Wellness and Work-Life Balance Programs","The whole of government will implement and encourage wellness and fitness programs as well as activities to promote work-life balance to avoid NCDs, stress, and other mental health effects.",""],[1,"165","2","Healthy Lifestyle and Diet Promotion Policies","Policies to promote healthy lifestyle and diet will be pursued and implemented both in the public (i.e., government offices, public schools) and private sectors.",""],[1,"166","1","Healthy Lifestyle Promotion Strategy","The strategies to promote a healthy lifestyle will first improve nutrition and health literacy, and then, the health-seeking behavior of Filipinos.",""]],"184":[[1,"165","3","Substance and Drug Abuse Treatment Benefit Packages","PhilHealth will offer packages for substance and drug abuse management, rehabilitation, and treatment services.",""],[1,"165","3","Expansion of Medical Detoxification Benefit Package","Existing PhilHealth benefit package such as medical detoxification will be expanded.",""],[1,"165","3","Expansion of Balay Silangan Facilities","More Balay Silangan facilities initiated by Philippine Drug Enforcement Agency (PDEA)11 will also be established.",""],[1,"165","7","Balay Silangan Drug Reformation Program","Balay Silangan is a national drug reformation program initiated by PDEA.",""]],"185":[[1,"165","4","Community-Based Mental Health Care Facilities","national government, through DOH, will fund the establishment, and assist in the operation, of community-based mental health care facilities.","DOH"],[1,"165","4","Local Mental Health Program Development and Implementation","LGUs and academic institutions will create and implement mental health programs, which will be in accordance with the general guidelines set by the Philippine Council for Mental Health.",""],[1,"165","4","Mental Health Prevention, Treatment, and Psychosocial Support Services","These services include prevention, promotion, treatment, and rehabilitation, including psychosocial support, especially during the time of pandemic.",""]],"186":[[1,"165","6","Elderly Palliative and Hospice Care Services","Elderly health will also be given priority through specific interventions, including palliative and hospice care.",""]],"187":[[1,"166","2","Integrated Nutrition and Health Promotion in Local and Education Programs","Various stakeholders such as LGUs, DepEd, DSWD, among others, will be tapped to ensure that nutrition and health promotion is integrated in their programs.","LGUs | DepEd | DSWD"],[1,"166","2","Local Health and Nutrition Campaign Intensification","LGUs will be enjoined to intensify health and nutrition campaigns.","LGUs"],[1,"166","2","Health Literacy and Health Rights Curriculum Modules","DepEd will formulate modules on health literacy and health rights to be integrated in the school curricula and activities.","DepEd"],[1,"166","2","Health Modules in Family Development Sessions","More health modules can be incorporated in the Family Development Sessions of the Pantawid Pamilyang Pilipino Program of DSWD.","DSWD"],[1,"166","2","Public Health Education and Risk Communication Campaign","Government instrumentalities will be mobilized for aggressive public health education campaigns, including effective risk communication through various media (i.e., television, radio, and social media) to encourage social distancing, better hygiene, self-isolation, and health-seeking behavior at the first sign of infectious disease symptoms (e.g., COVID-19).",""],[1,"166","2","Minimum Public Health Standards Enforcement","With the new normal, the minimum public health standards (i.e., for COVID-19 mitigation) through non-pharmaceutical interventions such as physical distancing, ensuring proper ventilation, regular and thorough disinfection, provision of alcohol/sanitizers/soap, temperature check, use of personal protective equipment (PPE), among others, will be strictly implemented.",""],[1,"191","22","Minimum Health Standards Implementation","Continue the implementation of minimum health standards",""],[1,"194","1","Health Information, Education, and Communication Campaign","Strengthen the information, education, and communication (IEC) campaign on health and the available insurance and benefits.","DOH | DepEd | LGUs | PhilHealth"],[1,"196","1","Minimum Public Health Standards Implementation and Monitoring","The prescribed minimum public health standards in transport, workplaces and public places will be continuously implemented and monitored by the LGUs and national government agencies in partnership with the private sector to prevent and reduce the spread of COVID-19 as well as ensure the safe re-opening of the economy.",""],[1,"196","1","Minimum Health Standards for Social Protection Delivery","Further, the NGAs need to ensure that the minimum health standards are observed in the delivery of social protection projects and services to avoid the spread of COVID-19.",""]],"188":[[1,"166","3","Expanded PhilHealth Preventive and Diagnostic Service Packages","PhilHealth will work with private service providers to offer preventive services, diagnostics, laboratory, medicines, dental and other medical services, as well as packages for regular annual check-up for all employees - public and private.",""],[1,"191","5","PhilHealth Coverage and Benefit Package Expansion","Ensure financial risk protection through improved PhilHealth coverage and benefit packages",""],[1,"191","8","Health Insurance and Benefits IEC Campaign","Strengthen IEC campaign on health and the available insurance and benefits",""],[1,"193","6","Expanded PhilHealth Benefit Packages","PhilHealth will develop new or enhance existing health benefit packages as recommended by the Health Technology Assessment process.",""],[1,"193","6","Universal Outpatient Benefit Package Provision","Outpatient benefit packages including diagnostics, laboratory, dental, medicines, and other preventive services will be provided to all Filipinos.",""],[1,"193","6","Case Rate Coverage for Emerging Diseases","PhilHealth should also guarantee the availability of case rate packages for emerging and re-emerging diseases.",""],[1,"193","6","No Co-payment Policy Implementation","Moreover, implementation of the No Co-payment Policy, wherein no other fees or expenses will be charged to those who will be admitted to basic or ward accommodations, will be ensured.",""]],"189":[[1,"166","5","Telehealth System Strengthening and Expansion","the country's telehealth system will be strengthened and expanded by the DOH in coordination with other agencies including DICT and DOST.","DOH | DICT | DOST"],[1,"166","5","Telemedicine for Primary Care Consultations","Telemedicine, including primary care consultations, will be established, so that during emergencies (e.g., COVID-19 pandemic), the number of patients going to hospitals and health facilities will be reduced.",""],[1,"166","5","Institutionalization of Health Technology Assessment Process","Health technology assessment (HTA) process 12 will also be institutionalized.",""],[1,"183","12","National eHealth System Establishment","This measure will establish a national eHealth System that will direct, institutionalize, and regulate the practice of eHealth in the country.",""]],"190":[[1,"167","1","Emergency Health Supply Management and Logistics System","DOH will institute an emergency supply management and logistics system, with an adequate national stockpile of medicines, medical supplies, PPEs, ventilators, and related resources including FP commodities, for use during a public health emergency.","DOH"],[1,"167","1","Expedited Procurement Procedures for Health Supplies","The DBM and Government Procurement Policy Board (GPPB) will work on policies and procedures to expedite procurement of these necessary equipment and health supplies.","DBM | Government Procurement Policy Board (GPPB)"]],"191":[[1,"167","2","Emergency Nutrition Advisory Issuance","the Nutrition Cluster will issue advisories to guide LGUs and relevant partners on appropriate nutrition response.",""],[1,"167","2","Nutritious Relief Food Recipe Advocacy","the NNC and DOST-FNRI will also continue advocating for recipes that would help transform relief goods (i.e., canned goods, instant noodles) into more nutritious meals.","NNC | DOST-FNRI"]],"192":[[1,"172","8","Learning Environment Improvement for Schools and Classrooms","Improvement of the learning environment by ensuring that schools, classrooms, and other learning facilities promote productive learning experiences.",""],[1,"172","8","Inclusive Education Program Expansion","Improved learning environments will utilize best practices in inclusive education such as the Madrasah, Special Education, and Indigenous Peoples' Education Programs",""],[1,"172","8","Comprehensive Sexuality Education Intensification","the intensified implementation of the Comprehensive Sexuality Education Program to address early pregnancy.",""],[1,"184","3","Government Assistance Expansion for Private School Learners and Teachers","Expansion of government assistance to K to 6 learners in private schools through GASTPE and expansion of the TSS to elementary and SHS teachers",""],[1,"184","4","Government Assistance to Students and Teachers in Private Education","The GASTPE (Government Assistance to Students and Teachers in Private Education) is an education assistance program for students and teachers in private schools.",""]],"193":[[1,"172","10","Stakeholder Engagement for Education Policy Support","Engagement of stakeholders for support and collaboration towards better research, analysis, and high-level advice for strategic policy, planning, and programming for delivering quality education for all.",""],[1,"175","5","Government-Academe-Industry and International Education Partnerships","Maximize government-academe-industry collaborations and international partnerships to ensure alignment of competencies and labor requirements.",""]],"194":[[1,"173","4","Student Financial Assistance Program Implementation Enhancement","Enhance the implementation of Student Financial Assistance Programs, especially the Universal Access to Quality Tertiary Education Act (UAQTE).",""],[1,"174","1","Tertiary Education Voucher and Student Loan Reform","The Unified Financial Assistance System for Tertiary Education (UniFAST) Board will consider implementing a voucher system and improve the loan system to give students a choice in school (whether public or private) and educational tracks (whether TVET or higher education) prior to the enrollment period.",""],[1,"174","1","Quality Assurance and Monitoring for Subsidized Tertiary Institutions","Further, support interventions and adequate monitoring activities will be done to ensure that quality of education is not sacrificed in the course of policy implementation through: (a) strong monitoring of tuition and other school fees being charged by HEIs and TVIs to the government; (b) stricter quality assurance in HEIs, especially those enjoying government subsidies; (c) pursuit of per student normative cost budgeting; and (d) career guidance and financial counseling for student beneficiaries14.",""]],"195":[[1,"178","5","Human Resource Quality and Workforce Adaptability Strengthening","the government will further strengthen efforts to raise the quality of human resources and ensure that current and future workforce will be able to adapt to the changing demands of the labor market.",""],[1,"178","5","Digital Work Adaptation and Job Quality Strategy","Strategies that will improve the ability of individuals to operate and thrive in a digital environment, while at the same time ensuring job quality and income security, will be pursued.",""]],"196":[[1,"180","3","Flexible Work Arrangements for Work-Life Balance","Ensure that flexible work arrangements allow members of the workforce to balance their household and work duties.",""],[1,"180","3","Gender Bias Reduction in Basic Education Materials","addressing gender bias and gender role stereotype in basic education curriculum materials",""],[1,"180","3","Women’s Entrepreneurship and Digital Economic Opportunity Support","promoting entrepreneurship and advance economic opportunities for women through the use of digital technology.",""]],"197":[[1,"181","2","Review and Update Flexible Work and Occupational Safety Rules","The current rules and guidelines on flexible/alternative work arrangements both in the private and public sectors, as well as the observance of occupational safety and health (OSH) will need to be revisited in light of the new normal.",""],[1,"181","2","Institutionalize Employer Provision of PPE for Physical Reporting Work","the provision of PPEs by employers to prevent the spread of COVID-19 and other viruses needs to be institutionalized.",""],[1,"181","2","Expand Employees' Compensation Coverage for Pandemic Risks","promoting awareness and expanding coverage of the Employees' Compensation Program by including pandemic-related risks as a valid criterion to avail of such program will be pushed.",""],[1,"181","2","Review Public Sector Hazard Pay Guidelines","guidelines on the provision of hazard pay for workers in the public sector will be reviewed, or formulated where there is none.",""],[1,"181","2","Strengthen Bilateral Labor Agreements for Overseas Workers","Protection of Filipinos working overseas, especially the low-skilled workers, can be improved through strengthening bilateral labor agreements with host countries (see Chapter 21).",""],[1,"181","3","Labor and Employment Education Services Information Dissemination and Workplace Harmony Modules","the government will intensify information dissemination of the recalibrated Labor and Employment Education Services (LEES) of the Department of Labor and Employment (DOLE), which includes Labor Relations, Human Relations and Productivity, Continuing Labor Education Seminars, and Labor Education for Graduating Students.","Department of Labor and Employment (DOLE)"],[1,"185","12","Five-Day Workweek Amendment and Alternative Work Arrangements Guidelines","Amendment to the five-day workweek prescribed by the Labor Code would need to be pursued, accompanied by more specific guidelines on the implementation of alternative work arrangements for both private and public sector.",""],[1,"185","12","Part-Time Work Legal Framework","Creation of a legal framework on part-time work to increase flexibility for employers while integrating workers' protection needs to be established under the law.",""],[1,"185","17","Employees Compensation Program Amendment for Pandemic-Related Workplace Risks","The guidelines and benefits of the Employees Compensation Program need to be amended to include compensations for pandemic-related risks at work.",""]],"198":[[1,"181","5","Minimum Wage Policy Implementation Enhancement","current efforts towards enhancing the implementation of minimum wage policies ... will be continued to protect vulnerable workers from undue low wages.",""]],"199":[[1,"182","6","National Program of Action and Investment Plan for Teenage Pregnancy Prevention","This will facilitate the development of a National Program of Action and Investment Plan for the prevention of teenage pregnancy.",""]],"200":[[1,"182","6","Fireworks Safety Regulation and Enforcement Reform","The policy may be in the form of either an Executive Order or a Republic Act.",""]],"201":[[1,"183","4","Anti-Counterfeiting Law Modernization","This aims to make the 22-year-old law responsive to the changes in the industry and in anti-counterfeiting technologies.",""],[1,"183","6","Drugs and Medicines Price Regulation Board","creation of the Drugs and Medicines Price Regulation Board that will regulate the pricing of any or all drugs enumerated in Section 23 of RA 9502",""],[1,"183","6","Mandatory Drug Price Display Requirement","mandating of the display of prices fixed and approved by the Board for drugs and medicines on a clearly printed poster conspicuously placed within the retail outlet",""],[1,"183","6","VAT Exemption Expansion for Essential Medicines","extension of the VAT exemption coverage to all essential ethical medicines listed in the Philippine National Formulary",""],[1,"183","6","Generic Prescription Requirement","prescription of all physicians should be in generic terminology without any specific brand",""],[1,"183","6","Central Pharmaceutical Procurement Agency Designation","designation of the Philippine Pharma Procurement, Incorporated as DOH's and PhilHealth's central procurement agency for drugs, medicines, and common medical supplies",""]],"202":[[1,"191","6","Food Fortification Program Strengthening","Strengthen the food fortification program",""],[1,"191","9","Implementation of the Masustansyang Pagkain para sa Batang Pilipino Act and Nutritious Food Pack Provision","Fully implement RA 11037 (Masustansyang Pagkain para sa Batang Pilipino Act) and provide nutritious food packs to children through SFP and SBFP",""],[1,"192","4","Food Fortification Program Enhancement","The Department of Health (DOH) in coordination with other concerned agencies such as the National Nutrition Council (NNC), Department of Science and Technology- Food and Nutrition Research Institute (DOST-FNRI), and the Food and Drug Authority, among others, will enhance the country's food fortification program, a complementary intervention to micronutrient supplementation, to produce fortified staples and raw materials for use in disasters and safety net programs.","Department of Health | National Nutrition Council | Department of Science and Technology- Food and Nutrition Research Institute | Food and Drug Authority"],[1,"193","1","Implementation of the Masustansyang Pagkain para sa Batang Pilipino Act","Fully implement the Masustansyang Pagkain para sa Batang Pilipino Act (RA 11037) and provide nutritious food packs to children through the Supplemental Feeding Program and School-Based Feeding Program.","DSWD | Department of Education"],[1,"193","1","Emergency Nutrition Supplementation for Children","To address emerging nutrition concerns during emergencies, food supplementation through the Supplemental Feeding Program and School-Based Feeding Program can be enhanced.",""],[1,"193","1","Nutritious Food Pack Distribution System for Students","Instead of hot meals, day care and elementary school students will be provided with nutritious food packs, which may include vegetable noodles (malunggay/squash/carrots), iron fortified rice, enhanced nutribun, among others.",""]],"203":[[1,"191","7","Small-Scale Household and Community Planting Support","Encourage small-scale planting for the consumption of the households and community",""],[1,"192","5","Household and Community Backyard Gardening Support","Encourage small-scale planting for the consumption of the households and community.",""],[1,"192","5","Backyard Gardening Technology and Indigenous Knowledge Initiative","To foster effective backyard gardening and ensure access to healthy food, the DOST and the National Commission on Indigenous Peoples will be engaged to explore and implement not only new technologies but also indigenous knowledge systems and processes.","DOST | the National Commission on Indigenous Peoples"]],"204":[[1,"191","11","Study on Establishing a Government Body for Filipino Families","Study the necessity of establishing a governmental body on Filipino families",""],[1,"194","4","Governmental Body for Filipino Families","The NEDA Social Development Committee (SDC) may therefore look into the creation of a governmental body that will lead in the development of policies and programs aimed at promoting the wellbeing of families.","NEDA Social Development Committee (SDC)"]],"205":[[1,"191","13","Violence Against Women and Children Prevention Advocacy Program","Conduct advocacy programs aimed at preventing the occurence of VAWC",""],[1,"191","15","Community-Based VAWC Response Program","Implement community-based programs to address VAWC, including the development of a standardized VAWC manual",""],[1,"191","33","Protective Services Access for POCs","Provide POCs with access to protective services",""],[1,"194","5","Violence Against Women and Children Advocacy and Education Program","Conduct advocacy programs aimed at preventing the occurrence of VAWC.",""],[1,"194","6","Community-Based VAWC Response Programs","Implement community-based programs to address VAWC, including the development of a standardized VAWC manual.","DSWD | PNP"],[1,"194","6","Standardized VAWC Manual of Operations and Protocol","A standardized VAWC manual of operations/protocol will be developed by the IACVAWC to better assist abused women and children, as well as improve the referral system between the DSWD and the institutions where the cases are being reported.","IACVAWC | DSWD"],[1,"194","6","Strengthening Local Councils and VAW Desks","Among others, the document will help (a) improve the functionality of Local Councils for the Protection of Children and the VAW desks; and (b) harmonize existing VAWC databases (i.e. PNP, DSWD) to ensure that all victims are provided the needed support services.","PNP | DSWD"],[1,"195","1","24/7 Helplines and Digital Reporting Platforms for Child and Women Protection","it is important to ensure the availability of 24/7 helplines as well as the adoption of mobile and online platforms for reporting child and women protection issues and accessing government assistance and services.",""]],"206":[[1,"191","28","Rapid Assistance and Insurance for Farmers and Fisherfolk","Provide rapid assistance and insurance for farmers and fisherfolks",""],[1,"197","1","Rapid Disaster Assistance for Farmers and Fisherfolk","Provide rapid assistance and insurance for farmers and fisherfolk.","DA | DSWD"]],"207":[[1,"191","32","Household Resilience and Savings Mobilization","Encourage proactive resilience of households, including savings mobilization",""]],"208":[[1,"203","16","Unified Digital Housing Transaction Processing System","Implement unified seamless digitalized housing development transactions processing for homebuyers and developers",""],[1,"206","3","Unified Digital Housing Transactions Processing System","Implement unified seamless digitalized housing development transactions processing for homebuyers and developers.",""],[1,"206","3","Housing One-Stop Processing Centers","Housing One-Stop Processing centers will be established in every region to fast-track processing of housing-related permits, clearances, and licenses issued by the national government agencies (NGAs) and LGUs.",""]],"209":[[1,"212","17","Population and Development Data Integration in Planning","Improve build-up and utilization of population and development data in development planning and programming",""],[1,"212","20","Strategic Interventions for Demographic Dividend Achievement","full and intensified implementation of strategic interventions will be pursued to enable all regions to reach the demographic dividend.",""],[1,"212","20","Human Capital Development Support Measures","Efforts to prepare the country's human capital will likewise be sustained along with supportive strategies for improving savings build-up and ensuring the integration of population and demographic factors in development planning and programming.",""],[1,"215","1","Population and Development Planning Integration","Finally, to ensure that the demographic transition will be planned for, there will be continuous integration of population and development, along with health and environment aspects, in the development planning and programming at the national and local levels.",""],[1,"217","1","Population and Development Integration Capacity-Building Programme","Integration of population factors in development initiatives, planning, and programming will be pursued through various channels - specifically in localizing and teaching population and development concepts (including the demographic dividend) to local chief executives.",""],[1,"217","1","Interagency Coordination for Demographic Dividend Strategies","There will be continuous interagency collaboration for synergized implementation of key strategies identified in the PDP 2017-2022 towards achieving the demographic dividend.",""],[1,"217","1","Population and Development Integration Capacity Building and Mentoring Support","Various support such as the provision of capacity building and mentoring will also be extended to national government agencies and LGUs in integrating population and development in their sectoral and local development plans.",""],[1,"217","1","Integrated Population, Health, Nutrition, and Environment Approach","Sustainable development will be pursued through an integrated population, health and nutrition, and environment approach in carrying out initiatives for reaping the demographic dividend (see Chapter 20).",""],[1,"217","2","Local Migration and Information System Institutionalization","a harmonized and interoperable Local Migration and Information System will be institutionalized, maintained, and utilized for planning and programming, especially in urban areas.",""],[1,"217","2","Community-Based Monitoring System Support for LGU Data Collection","LGUs will also be supported in the collection of population and development-related data through the Community-Based Monitoring System7 and other local data collection mechanisms.",""],[1,"217","2","Local Data-Driven Planning and Shock Response Mechanism","These mechanisms will provide local- level data that will guide the implementation of national programs targeted at developing LGUs (e.g., Balik Probinsya, Bagong Pag-asa Program).",""],[1,"217","4","Integrated Population-Health-Environment Community Projects","The integrated Population-Health-Environment (PHE) approach in community projects will be promoted and supported in this time of pandemic, when a lot of Filipinos lost their jobs and most are returning to their places of origin.",""],[1,"218","1","Youth Data Access and Evidence-Based Policy Support","data will be made available and accessible for crafting the most relevant, appropriate, and effective policies and programs for this age group.",""],[1,"218","1","Youth Participation in Policy and Programme Design","Their active, meaningful, and holistic participation in society will also be strengthened by involving them in the conceptualization and implementation of programs and policies across the following sectors: health, education, economic empowerment, social inclusion and equity, peace-building and security, governance, citizenship, environment, and global mobility.",""],[1,"218","1","Youth Crisis and Public Health Emergency Mobilization","With the right information and training, they can be mobilized to assist in government response - in the case of pandemics, to help break the chain of infection.",""]],"210":[[1,"219","2","STI Procurement Process Review and Refinement","Moreover, the procurement process of STI programs, projects, and activities (PPAs) will be reviewed and refined for timely implementation and greater impact.",""],[1,"219","2","National Innovation Council Establishment","The establishment of the National Innovation Council, which is seen to guide the country towards long-term STI development, will also be fast-tracked.",""],[1,"223","10","Research and Development Agenda Support","Support research and development agenda",""],[1,"223","17","Implementation of STI Statistics Scoping Study Recommendations","Implement the recommendations of the Scoping Study on STI Statistics",""],[1,"228","3","National Innovation Agenda Strategy Document","The government, through the NIC, will craft the NIASD that will establish the country's vision and long-term goals for innovation, consistent with global and regional commitments and with AmBisyon Natin 2040 and the PDP.",""],[1,"228","3","Innovation Governance Roadmap","This document will also provide a roadmap consisting of strategies and action plans for improving innovation governance (e.g., identifying and addressing the absorptive capacities of government agencies doing R&D).",""],[1,"228","4","National Innovation Priority Areas and Resource Allocation Framework","The NIASD will contain innovation priority areas ... the strategies to be used to realize these priorities, and for which resources and budget will be provided.",""],[1,"228","5","STI Foresight Studies and Evidence-Based Planning Framework","the government will support the conduct of long-term STI foresight studies and development of evidenced-based planning framework to complement the NIASD, taking into consideration the whole STI ecosystem.",""],[1,"228","5","Capacity Building on Foresight Planning Tools","Increasing capacities on planning tools such as foresight techniques will also be pursued.",""],[1,"228","6","RD&E Theme Development and Relevance Criteria Framework","The government, guided by the country's innovation agenda and development goals, will develop RD&E themes.",""],[1,"228","6","Publicly Funded RD&E Program Selection Criteria","A \"relevance criteria\" will also be applied by the agencies concerned in the selection of RD&E programs or projects for funding.",""],[1,"228","6","National RD&E Institutions and Capacity Inventory","The government will likewise conduct an inventory of academic or educational and RD&E institutions, as well as their resources and capacities to undertake RD&E programs and projects.",""],[1,"228","6","Expansion and Alignment of the National RD&E Agenda","The research areas under the Harmonized National Research and Development Agenda 2017- 2022 will be expanded and aligned with RD&E themes of the government.","Harmonized National Research and Development Agenda 2017- 2022"],[1,"229","4","STI Monitoring and Evaluation System Strengthening","Strengthen monitoring and evaluation system for all STI-related programs and projects.",""],[1,"233","2","National Innovation Council Establishment and Operationalization","Establish and operationalize the National Innovation Council (NIC).",""],[1,"233","3","Interim NIC Secretariat Establishment","NEDA will constitute an interim Secretariat through the temporary detail of personnel from the NIC member agencies, pursuant to RA 11293.","NEDA"],[1,"233","6","National Innovation Council and Innovation Strategy Framework","The law establishes the NIC which will develop the country's innovation goals, priorities, and long-term national strategy.",""],[1,"234","2","Inter-Agency STI Statistics Coordination Committee","The results of the scoping study on STI statistics will feed into the work of and will be implemented by the Inter-Agency Committee (IAC) on STI Statistics.",""],[1,"234","2","Regional STI Indicator Monitoring System","The government will also identify indicators with available regional data to enable the concerned regional offices to effectively monitor their STI sector.",""],[1,"234","3","Research and Development Data Reporting and Sharing Mechanism","The government will also require various stakeholders (e.g., SUCs) to submit data that will be recommended under the scoping study (e.g., R&D data) and encourage private corporations to participate voluntarily in sharing relevant data.",""],[1,"234","3","Unified Accounts Code Structure for R&D Spending","The DBM and the DOST will work closely to develop the Unified Accounts Code Structure (UACS) for the R&D spending in the public sector.","DBM | DOST"]],"211":[[1,"223","16","International STI Cooperation Intensification","· Intensify international cooperation in STI",""],[1,"229","5","Operationalization of the Philippine Space Agency and Space Development Policy","Operationalize the Philippine Space Agency and implement the Philippine Space Development and Utilization Policy.",""],[1,"233","4","Open Science and International Research Collaboration Initiative","Encourage open science and collaboration to combat public health issues and emerging diseases such as COVID-19.",""],[1,"233","5","International STI Collaboration","The Philippines will continue to actively participate and figure more prominently in regional and international discussions on STI.",""],[1,"233","5","New and Emerging Scientific Cooperation Areas","it will continue to explore new and emerging areas of scientific cooperation where the country and its partner governments and institutions may mutually benefit from (e.g., vaccine development, space and satellite technology, artificial intelligence, security and defense, etc.).",""],[1,"233","5","Improvement of STI Standing","The government will also intensify its efforts in improving the country's STI standing in the",""],[1,"234","1","International STI Partnership Promotion and Exchange Programme","international community through information dissemination on potential STI partners in the Philippines, promoting international activities related to STI, and fostering exchanges on STI activities.",""],[1,"234","1","Strategic STI Partnership and Technology Transfer Initiative","strategic partnerships will be built with other countries through activities such as joint research and development, exchange of scientists, building researchers networks, joint seminars/workshops, technology transfer, and capacity building.",""],[1,"234","1","Foreign Technology Acquisition for COVID-19 and New Normal Adaptation","Bilateral and multilateral partnerships will also be used to acquire new and existing foreign technologies (e.g., those that may be used to address the COVID-19 pandemic and adopt to the new normal).",""]],"212":[[1,"229","2","Renewable Energy R&D and Innovation Promotion","The government will explore and conduct R&D studies on renewable energy technologies, including the viability of new technologies to expand the share of renewables in the energy supply mix to fuel the country's industrialization and urbanization, while simultaneously being mindful of its environmental responsibility.",""],[1,"229","2","Renewable Energy Innovation Culture Promotion","Moreover, the government will promote an innovation culture that supports new and emerging renewable technologies, as well as innovative business models in the renewable energy industry (see also Chapter 19).",""]],"213":[[1,"235","7","Independent Regulatory Framework Legislation","This aims to legislate an independent regulatory framework that will decide on issues affecting public health and safety, protection of the environment, and nuclear security and safeguards, that is beyond the reach of entities with self-motivated interests.",""],[1,"235","8","National Measurement Infrastructure System Strengthening","Strengthening the National Measurement Infrastructure System (NMIS), Amending RA 9236 also known as the National Metrology Act of 2003",""],[1,"235","9","Establishment of the National Metrology Institute","This aims to establish the National Metrology Institute under the DOST.","DOST"],[1,"235","9","Metrology Competency Training and Capacity Building Program","It also seeks to provide capacity building programs through competency training to strengthen the local metrology authorities at the local level and foster a metrology culture that will instill a keen appreciation of the importance of metrology.",""],[1,"235","16","National Defense Industry Development Policy Environment","This intends to provide the required policy environment for the development of a national defense industry through the strengthening and revitalizing of the self-reliant defense posture program, incentivizing in-country enterprises, rationalizing defense acquisition, and institutionalizing a functional office for defense technology research and industry development under the Department of National Defense.","Department of National Defense"]],"214":[[1,"242","22","Institutional Reforms for Timely Project Execution","Pursue institutional reforms to ensure timely execution of projects.",""],[1,"243","1","Procurement Delay Review","Act will be further reviewed to address procurement delays.",""],[1,"243","1","Election-Period Infrastructure Exemption Amendments","To minimize undue delay in the implementation of crucial infrastructure projects during election periods, amendments to the exemption provisions under the Omnibus Election Code will be pursued.",""],[1,"243","1","Emergency Budget Flexibility Reform","institutional reforms to increase flexibility in the emergency use of funds, such as the LGU development fund, will be considered.",""]],"215":[[1,"245","5","Green, Social, and Sustainable Bond Regulation","The SEC has issued regulations and guidelines on the issuance of green, social, and sustainable bonds that are aligned with ASEAN standards.","SEC"],[1,"245","5","Green Finance Market Development Collaboration","Further, it has collaborated with multinational corporations such as the Asian Development Bank (ADB) to seek assistance in developing the market.","SEC"],[1,"245","5","Transition and Sustainability-Linked Bond Guidance Development","the agency is currently studying the possible publication of guidance for issuing transition and sustainability-linked bonds to provide direction for issuers and assurance for both domestic and foreign investors.","SEC"]],"216":[[1,"246","1","Personal Property Security Registry Development","To implement the Personal Property Security Act, a personal property security registry will be developed by the Land Registration Authority.","Land Registration Authority"],[1,"246","1","Electronic Warehouse Receipts Registry System","The amendments to the Warehouse Receipts Law of 1912 seek to establish an online registry system where all electronic warehouse receipts can be lodged and accessed.",""],[1,"249","3","Electronic Warehouse Receipts Registry System","The present warehouse receipt system will be overhauled to include the creation of an online electronic warehouse receipts registry system.",""],[1,"252","27","Warehouse Receipt System Overhaul and Online Registry","Overhaul the present warehouse receipt system and provide an online registry system where all electronic warehouse receipts can be registered and accessed.",""]],"217":[[1,"247","5","Strengthening Trade Agreement Negotiation Governance","The existing governance structure on negotiations for international trade agreements will be strengthened.",""],[1,"248","2","Regional Stockpiling and Essential Goods Logistics Scheme","Regional stockpiling and operationalizing of a logistics scheme to ensure supply of essential goods will be explored.",""],[1,"250","4","Holistic Communication Management System","Develop a holistic communication management system and increase market intelligence responsive to dynamic consumer preferences.",""],[1,"250","4","Crisis Communication Management System","Strengthening the lines of communication between the national government, LGUs, and the private sector through the establishment of a crisis communication management system will enable the immediate dissemination of critical information during emergencies.",""],[1,"250","4","Crisis Standard Operating Procedures Compendium","The development of a compendium of standard operating procedures in times of crisis will be a useful resource for the crisis management system.",""],[1,"250","5","Implementation of Enabling and Investment-Related Law Amendments","Pursue full implementation of enabling laws, support amendments to investment-related laws, and ensure timely implementation of trade facilitative platforms.",""],[1,"250","5","TradeNet Acceleration and Digital Trade Facilitation","Implementation of the TradeNet will be accelerated to ensure efficient government services and a robust monitoring and evaluation framework that will facilitate the movement of cargo through the digitalization of processes and payments.",""],[1,"250","5","Trade Cost Reduction and Trade Document Simplification","The new system shall also curb trade costs and create ease in securing trade documents.",""],[1,"250","7","Regulatory Tracking and Alignment Mechanism","Development of mechanisms to track initiatives related to regulations will enable the country to align regulations with other countries and identity necessary capacity building initiatives and norm-setting.",""],[1,"250","7","Strengthening of Science-Based SPS Protocol Enforcement","The enforcement of science-based sanitary and phytosanitary (SPS) protocols will be strengthened to guard against various diseases that may be brought in through imports.",""],[1,"251","1","Quarantine Agency Detection Equipment and Staffing Upgrade","Quarantine and other regulatory agencies shall be equipped with detection equipment and the hiring of properly trained personnel.",""],[1,"251","2","ICT and Logistics Infrastructure for Trade Connectivity","The government will also provide adequate Information and Communications Technology and logistics infrastructure to achieve connectivity and facilitate the movement of traded goods",""],[1,"251","3","Philippine Trade Facilitation Committee","The Philippine Trade Facilitation Committee will also be established to improve coordination of trade facilitation regulations and procedures in line with the country's WTO commitments.",""],[1,"253","8","Amendment of the Customs Modernization and Tariff Act","Amendment of the Customs Modernization and Tariff Act (RA 10863)",""],[1,"253","9","Expedited Tariff Modification Mechanism for Essential Medical Supplies","Allow for the expeditious process of tariff modifications in times of crisis in order to augment local supply and ensure that essential medical supplies are stable",""]],"218":[[1,"249","3","National Quality Infrastructure Law","The issuance of a National Quality Infrastructure Law will be pursued to establish the country as a provider of quality products (see Chapter 9).",""],[1,"249","3","Export Sector Business Continuity Planning Support","To ensure supply chain resilience, better business continuity planning in the export sector will be supported.",""],[1,"249","3","Strategic Warehousing and Cold Chain Logistics Reforms","Logistics reforms such as strategic warehousing as well as cold chain systems will be prioritized.",""],[1,"249","4","Production Process Upgrading and Digitalization Initiative","Upgrading of production processes will be pursued to integrate automation of operations as well as put in place innovative and alternative business processes that will become the new standard on engaging clients, buyers, and suppliers.",""],[1,"249","5","Inclusive Innovation Industrial Strategy","Through the Inclusive Innovation Industrial Strategy (i3S), a competition-innovation-productivity relationship will be pursued to address a highly-liberalized market environment by growing innovative and globally-competitive manufacturing, agriculture, and services sectors to combat challenges as a result not only of globalization but also of rising regional economic integration.",""],[1,"249","6","Skills Development Investment for Higher-Value Services","The government will encourage investments in skills development to tap into higher-value services like animation, data analytics, and cloud computing by strengthening its industry-academe linkages.",""],[1,"249","6","Shared Service Facilities Project","The Shared Service Facilities Project of the DTI will improve the competitiveness of MSMEs","DTI"],[1,"250","1","Private Sector Investment in Agro-Based Industries","Engaging the private sector to invest and set up more agri-based industries will also help in developing agricultural products for exports (see Chapter 8).",""],[1,"250","1","MSME Linkages to Large Companies Programme","Programs that link MSMEs to large companies that are part of or operate their own global supply and/or value chains will be sustained (see Chapter 9).",""],[1,"250","2","Logistics Reform and Strategic Warehousing Development","The government will prioritize logistics reforms that will rationalize the freight system, establish strategic warehousing, as well as cold chain systems.",""],[1,"250","2","Enterprise Production and Storage Adjustment Support","Enterprises will be encouraged to rethink and adjust production and storage facilities to ensure optimum access with the least disruptions.",""],[1,"250","2","Local Supplier Partnership Development","Development of partnerships with local suppliers to reduce vulnerabilities will be supported.",""],[1,"250","2","Supply Chain and Logistics Committee","The formation of a Supply Chain and Logistics Committee which will be responsible for identifying and implementing programs that will improve the flow of goods will be considered.",""],[1,"250","3","Customs Tariff Modification Acceleration Amendments","Amendments to the Customs Modernization and Tariff Act (RA 10863) to allow for the expeditious process of tariff modifications in times of crises will be considered to augment local supply.",""],[1,"250","3","Special Economic Zone Emergency Export Requirement Flexibility","Likewise, amendments to the Special Economic Zone Act of 1995 (RA 7916) may be considered to relax export requirements pertaining to threshold values for domestic sales in cases of emergency as declared by the President and subject to applicable laws, rules or regulations.",""],[1,"251","5","Industry Roadmap and Business Continuity Planning Development","Industry roadmaps that will include the development of business continuity plans for promising export- oriented industries will be developed to better prepare firms for the challenges of the New Normal.",""],[1,"251","5","Board of Investments Industry Recovery and Roadmap Support","The Board of Investments will continue to work with the industry, specifically for export-oriented and priority industries, in coming up with recovery plans and preparing/updating of industry roadmaps to prepare and assist firms for changes brought about by the new normal.",""],[1,"259","6","Construction Sector Regulatory Reform","the government will address public restraints by reviewing regulations that hinder competition such as the nationality-based distinction, which creates an uneven playing field between local and foreign contractors.",""],[1,"259","6","Construction Industry Regulatory Quality Improvement","The subsequent strengthening of regulatory quality within the industry will effectively reduce the formal and informal costs of doing business that held back sector efficiency and performance far below its inherent potential for so long.",""],[1,"259","7","Research and Development Support for Technological Advancement","the government will continue to support research and development efforts to further pursue technological advancements in the country.",""],[1,"261","10","Amendment of the Magna Carta for MSMEs","Amendment of the Magna Carta for Micro, Small and Medium Enterprises (MSMEs) (Republic Act No. 9501, amending Republic Act No. 6977)",""]],"219":[[1,"249","3","Integrated Cargo and Supply Tracking Website","An integrated website tracking real-time information on cargo release, availability of supply, production, and inventory is useful for the national government, LGUs, as well as the private sector to avoid disruptions and uncoordinated supply flow.",""],[1,"249","3","Importer and Trader Registry Database","A registry or database of importers and traders will also be developed for seamless issuance of permits and necessary travel documents to ensure a steady supply and keep track of inventories particularly during emergencies.",""],[1,"261","8","E-commerce Regulation and Digital Economy Support Measure","The measure will facilitate the growth of e-commerce and ensure that firms respond to the requirements in the new normal and thrive in the digital economy.",""],[1,"261","8","E-commerce Fraud Protection Regulation","It will regulate e- commerce to protect both firms and consumers from fraudulent schemes.",""]],"220":[[1,"264","6","Peace and Development Intervention Coordination","Strengthen convergence and complementation in the implementation of peace and development interventions",""],[1,"264","10","Strengthen Peace and Development Institutions and Mechanisms","Strengthen government peace and development institutions and mechanisms to increase their accountability and responsiveness to peace and human security issues",""],[1,"268","2","Strengthening Peace and Development Institutions and Accountability Mechanisms","Strengthen government peace and development institutions and mechanisms to increase their accountability and responsiveness to peace and human security issues.",""],[1,"268","3","Peace and Development Program Planning, Implementation, and Monitoring","Planning, implementation, and monitoring and evaluation of peace and development programs will likewise be undertaken to ensure streamlined and harmonized government response to various peace and security issues.",""],[1,"268","3","Mainstreaming CSPP in Government Plans and Programs","Mainstreaming of CSPP approaches in the plans and programs of government and various stakeholders will be institutionalized.",""],[1,"268","3","CSPP Mainstreaming in Comprehensive Development Plans","This includes mainstreaming CSPP in the Comprehensive Development Plans (CDPs) to highlight the important role of LGUs and local special bodies in conflict prevention and peacebuilding.",""],[1,"268","3","Online CSPP Knowledge Products Development","The Office of the Presidential Adviser on the Peace Process, with the Department of the Interior and Local Government will develop various online knowledge products, including the facilitators' manuals and guidebooks on mainstreaming CSPP in the CDPs of conflict-affected and conflict-vulnerable LGUs.","The Office of the Presidential Adviser on the Peace Process | the Department of the Interior and Local Government"],[1,"268","3","Online Reporting Scheme for CSPP Mainstreaming","LGUs will explore online schemes of reporting their CSPP mainstreaming and coaching efforts to the national government.",""]],"221":[[1,"268","4","Action Plans for Women, Youth, and Children Protection in Conflict and Against Extremism","The government will develop and continuously implement action plans to ensure the protection and promotion of rights of women, youth, and children in conflict situations and against radicalization and violent extremism.",""],[1,"268","5","Women, Peace and Security Action Plan Implementation","For the remainder of the Plan period, the National Steering Committee on Women, Peace, and Security, through its member agencies and local stakeholders, will target the implementation of the action points identified in the Agency Strategic Action Plans.",""],[1,"269","1","Localization of the National Action Plan on Women, Peace and Security","the localization of the NAP-WPS through the crafting of respective regional action plans",""],[1,"269","1","Gender-Based Violence Response in Emergencies","the development and implementation of programs to address gender-based violence in emergencies (e.g., those affected by the Marawi crisis)",""],[1,"269","2","National Action Plan on Youth, Peace and Security","The NAP-YPS will outline the country's YPS agenda based on the recommendations from the Youth Peace Tables",""],[1,"269","3","Implementation of the Special Protection of Children in Armed Conflict Act","Implementation of RA 11188.",""],[1,"269","4","Children in Situations of Armed Conflict Work Plan Development","For the remainder of the Plan period, all activities for the development of a work plan for this law will proceed, utilizing alternative strategies in consideration of the current public health situation.",""],[1,"269","4","Online Policy Advocacy and Community Engagement for Children in Armed Conflict","These activities include policy advocacy and dissemination, risk communications, and community engagements through online platforms;",""],[1,"269","4","Online Coordination Meetings for CSAC Work Plan Finalization","conduct of regular online coordination meetings to enhance and finalize the work plan;",""],[1,"269","4","Partnerships to Update CSAC Protocols","increasing partnerships with NGAs and international development partners particularly in updating and enhancing CSAC protocols on the handling and management of children involved in armed conflict.",""]],"222":[[1,"270","7","Autonomous Cordillera Regional Government Establishment","The purpose of establishing the Autonomous Region of the Cordillera is to establish a political entity and provide the structure of its government",""],[1,"270","8","National Transitional Justice and Reconciliation Commission for the Bangsamoro","Enabling law creating the National Transitional Justice and Reconciliation Commission for the Bangsamoro (NTJRB)",""],[1,"270","9","National Transitional Justice and Reconciliation Commission Establishment","The proposed law will create the NTJRCB which shall design and supervise the implementation of a TJR program.",""]],"223":[[1,"271","3","Whole-of-Security-Sector Health Emergency Response","During times of health emergencies, the whole of the security sector will be mobilized to adequately respond to needs of the people, including the provision of support to sectors that bring food, basic necessities, and essential services to them.",""],[1,"273","23","Fire Protection Services Capacity Improvement","Improve capability of the fire protection services to respond to fire and other related emergencies",""],[1,"273","25","Security Sector Humanitarian Assistance and Disaster Response Capacity Enhancement","Enhance the capability of the security sector for humanitarian assistance and disaster response",""],[1,"275","4","Security Sector Disaster Response Capacity-Building Programs","the National Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Council (NDRRMC) through the Office of Civil Defense (OCD), will continue to provide capacity-building programs for disaster responders such as the National Urban Search and Rescue Capacity Building.","National Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Council (NDRRMC) | Office of Civil Defense (OCD)"],[1,"275","4","Safe Philippines Project Phase I","the DILG is expected to implement by the fourth quarter of 2020 the Safe Philippines Project Phase I which will provide police, public safety institutions, and emergency response units with the latest technologies and equipment on surveillance and monitoring, with its own integrated operations and command center, and a remote back-up center.","DILG"],[1,"275","4","Security Sector INSARAG Classification Capacity Development","The security sector shall also continue to build its capacities to qualify for International Search and Rescue Advisory Group's (INSARAG's) external classification, to be recognized for international response support.",""],[1,"275","5","Health Human Resources Mobilization and Capacity Building","the OCD will augment the Human Resources for Health through the establishment and mobilization of a pool of medical and allied health professionals and volunteers from the security sector.",""],[1,"275","5","Security Sector Medical Support Capacity Building","Duty bearers in the security sector will be capacitated on providing medical/paramedic services to enable and intensify the conduct of contact tracing and early detection.",""],[1,"275","6","Coordination and Harmonization of Women’s Protection and Rehabilitation Initiatives","the government will strengthen the coordination and harmonization of protection and rehabilitation initiatives for women and girls in various emergencies.",""],[1,"275","6","Gender- and Culturally-Sensitive Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Programme","It will also develop comprehensive, gender- and culturally-sensitive disaster risk reduction and management programs that specifically highlight the context and vulnerabilities of women during emergencies, including women in frontline agencies.",""],[1,"275","7","Department of Disaster Resilience Establishment Bill","the passage of the bill to establish the Department of Disaster Resilience will be actively pursued in Congress.",""],[1,"275","7","Emergency Response Coordination Strengthening","The bill will strengthen the coordination among agencies in providing response during emergencies and disasters.",""],[1,"275","7","National Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Plan Revision","Meanwhile, the National Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Plan will be revisited to reflect the aforementioned aspects, among others.",""],[1,"276","1","Fire Protection Services Modernization and Capability Upgrade","This includes fast-tracking the modernization of fire protection services and the implementation of the BFP service upgrade and capability upgrade programs.",""],[1,"276","2","Fire Code Enforcement and Emergency Response Strengthening","The capacity of the BFP to enforce the Fire Code and respond to fire and other related emergencies will be further strengthened.",""],[1,"276","2","Road Obstruction Clearing for Emergency Access","roads will be cleared of obstructions to ensure the smooth and quick access of responders.",""]],"224":[[1,"277","4","Child Protection and Anti-Trafficking Policy Measures","Moreover, the DILG will lay down policies to protect and rehabilitate children at risk and children in conflict with the law.","DILG"],[1,"277","4","Manual on Handling Children at Risk","This will include developing a manual on handling and treatment of children at risk, as well as on preventing trafficking in persons, especially of women and children.","DILG"]],"225":[[1,"279","2","Whole-of-Nation Counterterrorism Implementation","To address communist terrorist groups, the National Task Force to End Local Communist Armed Conflict will intensify the implementation of the whole-of- nation approach at the regional and local levels.",""],[1,"279","2","Regional and Local Peace and Order Coordination","This will require strong coordination between regional and local development and peace and order councils, as well as the commitment and support of local chief executives and the communities.",""],[1,"279","3","Agency and Local Government PCVE Plan Capacity-Building","Following the adoption of the National Action Plan on Preventing and Countering Violent Extremism (NAP PCVE),2 various national government agencies will be capacitated particularly on the formulation of their respective agency's PCVE plans that are aligned with the NAP.",""],[1,"279","3","Local PCVE Planning and Translation of National Strategies","In the same manner, LGUs will be capacitated on the preparation of their local plans that will adopt and translate national strategies into concrete action at the grassroots level, taking into consideration the current health crisis and other emerging threats to peace and order and public safety.",""],[1,"279","3","Comprehensive People-Centered Radicalization Prevention Programme","These plans will include programs aimed at addressing the political, economic, cultural, psychosocial, and religious factors of radicalization that lead to violent extremism.",""],[1,"279","4","Violent Extremism and Terrorism Prevention Intensification","The government's efforts to prevent violent extremism and terrorism will be further intensified to maintain community resilience, especially during pandemics and other public health emergencies.",""],[1,"279","4","PCVE Multi-Stakeholder Cooperation Framework","The cooperation of the citizens, private sector, and non-government organizations with the government's efforts on PCVE will build a strong and solid front against violent extremists, which may lead to their possible containment and neutralization.",""]],"226":[[1,"279","5","International Legal and Law Enforcement Cooperation Mechanisms","The government will continue to deepen partnerships with the international community through multilateral and bilateral mechanisms such as mutual legal assistance agreements, global cooperation, and international law enforcement arrangements (e.g., International Criminal Police and joint law enforcement operations).",""],[1,"279","5","Anti-Trafficking Partnership and Coordination Efforts","This will also include intensified government and multisectoral efforts against domestic and transnational trafficking in persons through international partnerships and the Inter-Agency Council Against Trafficking.",""]],"227":[[1,"280","4","Rules-Based Maritime Dispute Resolution and Diplomacy","The government will sustain efforts that promote respect for legal and diplomatic processes in clarifying issues and resolving disputes on maritime jurisdictions, in accordance with international law, particularly the 1982 United Nations Convention on the Law of the Sea (UNCLOS).",""],[1,"280","4","ASEAN-China South China Sea Code of Conduct Initiative","Central to this is the push for an effective and substantive ASEAN-China COC that will guide actions of claimant-states to avoid activities that raise tension or threaten security and stability in the SCS.",""],[1,"280","4","Diplomatic Intervention to Protect National Maritime Rights","the Philippines remains committed to taking necessary diplomatic interventions against actions that run counter to international laws and principles, including the UN Charter, the 1982 UNCLOS, and the 2002 ASEAN-China Declaration on the Conduct of Parties in the South China Sea, to preserve national security and maintain peace and stability in the region.",""],[1,"280","4","Bilateral Relations Enhancement with Claimant Countries","The government will continue to enhance its relations with other claimant countries such as China, but with the consciousness of the need to protect the country's rights and interests in the WPS, as recognized under the foregoing international instruments and the 2016 Award of the Arbitral Tribunal on the South China Sea arbitration case.",""],[1,"280","5","Maritime Boundary Delimitation Negotiations","the government will pursue negotiations of maritime boundary delimitation agreements with countries the Philippines shares borders with",""],[1,"280","5","International Maritime Dispute Settlement Mechanisms","dispute settlement mechanisms consistent with international law will be pursued for the settlement of maritime border delineation and outstanding territorial claims",""],[1,"281","1","Bilateral and Multilateral Diplomatic Engagement Strengthening","The country will continue to enhance and strengthen existing bilateral relations, alliances, strategic partnerships, and defense cooperation, while expanding our bilateral diplomatic engagements.",""],[1,"281","1","Alternative Diplomatic Platform Utilization","The government will maximize existing platforms and pursue alternative platforms to maintain diplomatic engagements with its bilateral and multilateral partners to strengthen cooperation towards addressing the impact of public health emergencies such as pandemics.",""],[1,"281","2","Expanded Diplomatic Engagement and Regional Cooperation","Expand and enhance diplomatic engagements and cooperation in regional and international fora.",""],[1,"281","2","ASEAN Security and Maritime Cooperation","the Philippines will continue to engage ASEAN through its various platforms towards promoting joint patrols, maritime exercises, intelligence cooperation, regional security, and stability.",""],[1,"281","2","Pandemic Cooperation Strengthening","It will also strengthen cooperation to effectively manage the current and avoid future pandemic situations.",""]],"228":[[1,"281","3","Armed Forces Modernization and Capability Upgrade Program","the government will fully implement the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) Modernization Program and the AFP Capability Upgrade Program by ensuring continued budgetary support to these programs.",""],[1,"281","3","Air and Maritime Domain Awareness Enhancement","Air and maritime domain awareness will likewise be intensified through the conduct of law enforcement patrols and operations in Philippine maritime jurisdiction, as well as the establishment of domain awareness platforms.",""],[1,"281","3","Territorial Defense and Marine Resource Protection Infrastructure","Various structures that can be used for territorial defense operations, marine resource protection, information gathering, and civilian purposes will be established to strengthen the AFP's presence in Philippine-owned islands and features.",""],[1,"281","3","Reserved Forces and ROTC Strengthening","Moreover, the AFP will strengthen the Reserved Forces and the Reserved Officers Training Corps (ROTC) Program to augment its numbers, especially during crisis situations.",""],[1,"284","1","Re-establishment of Mandatory Basic ROTC Program","The re-establishment of mandatory basic ROTC Program will form part of the basic curricula for Senior High School (Grades 11 and 12) in public and private schools and a requisite for graduation.",""]],"229":[[1,"282","4","National Defense Policy Codification and Reform Package","This will update and define key national defense policies, principles, and concepts.",""],[1,"282","5","Defense Procurement Exemption","This will exempt all acquisition of defense equipment, materiel, ordinance and integrated military systems of the Department of National Defense and its attached bureaus from the regular procurement process bounded by the Government Procurement and Reform Act.","Department of National Defense"],[1,"282","6","National Security Planning Process Institutionalization","This will institutionalize the national security planning process.",""],[1,"282","8","Maritime Zones Legal Framework Act","This will serve as a general declaration of the maritime zones under the sovereignty and jurisdiction of the Philippines.",""],[1,"282","11","Archipelagic Sea Lanes Establishment Law","The proposed law will establish archipelagic sea lanes in Philippine archipelagic waters and the adjacent territorial sea.",""]],"230":[[1,"283","3","PNP Infrastructure, Facilities, and Equipment Upgrading","This will enhance the capabilities of the PNP through infrastructure and facilities development as well as equipment acquisition and upgrading.",""],[1,"283","5","DNA Database System for Law Enforcement","The bill will give way for the establishment of a DNA database system for the collection, storage, and maintenance of genetic identification information for law enforcement purposes.",""]],"231":[[1,"303","3","Use of ER 1-94 Funds for COVID-19 Response Mechanisms","the DOE Department Circular (DC) 2020-04-00085 issued on 6 April 2020, authorizing host LGUs to utilize the Energy Regulation (ER) 1-94 Funds for COVID-19 related response mechanisms.","DOE Department"],[1,"303","7","Rationalization of ER 1-94 Fund Use by Host Local Government Units","Rationalizing the Utilization of ER 1-94 Fund by Host Local Government Units in Response to COVID-19 Public Health Emergency.",""]],"232":[[1,"292","3","Housing and Resettlement Support for Balik Probinsya","as well as to provide appropriate housing and resettlement in support of the Balik Probinsya, Bagong Pag-asa Program.",""]],"233":[[1,"318","1","Innovative Wildlife and Habitat Enforcement Monitoring Technologies","accelerate the adoption of innovative technologies for enforcement and monitoring of wildlife and habitat",""],[1,"318","9","Wildlife and Habitat Monitoring Technology Scale-Up","Scale up adoption of innovative technologies for enforcement and monitoring of wildlife and habitat integrity",""],[1,"319","2","Natural Resources Data and Monitoring Capacity Enhancement","Capacities and competencies for data generation, assessment, and tracking of the state of natural resources, including its ecosystem services, will be enhanced.",""],[1,"319","2","Research, Development, and Innovative Wildlife Monitoring Investment","Complementing these are the necessary investments for research and development as well as innovative monitoring technologies that will support habitat and wildlife protection and help safeguard the country from zoonotic diseases arising from unsustainable and illegal wildlife consumption and trade",""],[1,"322","7","Enhanced Wildlife and Fisheries Enforcement Surveillance","Strengthen law enforcement and intensify the use of technological innovations for improved surveillance activities to combat illegal wildlife trade, and deter illegal, unreported, unregulated fishing (IUUF).",""],[1,"322","8","Habitat Monitoring and Impact Evaluation Modernization","Modernize habitat monitoring and impact evaluation of management interventions.",""],[1,"323","1","Geospatial Monitoring of Terrestrial and Coastal Marine Habitats","geospatial mapping) will be utilized for regular and real-time monitoring of terrestrial and coastal and marine habitats.",""]],"234":[[1,"321","1","Environmental and Social Safeguards Compliance for Mineral Resources Development","Improve compliance with environmental and social safeguards for mineral resources development.","DENR"],[1,"321","2","Regulatory Enforcement and Monitoring, Evaluation, and Reporting Strengthening","Strengthen regulatory enforcement, monitoring and evaluation (M&E), and reporting mechanisms through the:",""],[1,"321","3","Science-Based Review of Mining Operations","conduct of objective, science-based, and fact-finding reviews of large- and small-scale mining operations, including mineral processing plants;",""],[1,"321","4","Mining Industry Participation in EITI","enhancement of the participation of the mining industry in the Extractive Industries Transparency Initiative to ensure greater transparency and accountability in the management of natural resources;",""],[1,"321","5","Mining Compliance Monitoring Scorecard","development and adoption of a more stringent monitoring instrument (e.g., scorecard) for assessing compliance of mines under exploration, production, and care and maintenance.",""],[1,"321","6","Alignment of Mining Plans with Local Land Use and Development Plans","Ensure that plans and programs for large-scale mining operations (e.g., Safety and Health Program, Final Mine Rehabilitation and/or Decommissioning Plan, Social Development and Management Program and Environmental Protection and Enhancement Program) and small- scale mining operations (e.g., Community Development and Management Plan and Potential Environmental Impact Management Plan) are aligned with the local land use and development plans;",""],[1,"321","7","Mercury Contamination Rehabilitation and LGU Turnover","Continue research and development to determine the appropriate strategies that will address the mercury contamination of Palawan Quicksilver Mine, Inc. as part of the rehabilitation (i.e., bio-remediation), and facilitate the smooth turnover of management (i.e., protection and maintenance) to the LGU at the end of the project;",""],[1,"321","8","Strengthen the Minahang Bayan Scheme","Strengthen the Minahang Bayan scheme to avoid proliferation of illegal small-scale mining activities and ensure that operations are undertaken only under legitimate contracts/permits and within legitimate/designated areas by:",""],[1,"321","9","Review of the People's Small-Scale Mining Act Implementation","Revisiting the implementation of the People's Small-scale Mining Act of 1991 (RA 7076) particularly the definition and coverage of small-scale mining;",""],[1,"321","10","Minahang Bayan Application Requirement Easing","Easing the application requirement of Minahang Bayan scheme;",""],[1,"321","11","Strengthened Penalties and Anti-Illegal Mining Enforcement","Increasing the penalty provisions to approximate the value of environmental and health damages and intensify the anti-illegal mining efforts.",""]],"235":[[1,"318","1","Resilience and Livelihood Support for Resource-Dependent Communities","The resilience of resource-dependent communities and their livelihood will be enhanced by strengthening capacities to undertake CCAM-DRRM actions and expanding sustainable economic opportunities from natural capital",""],[1,"327","6","Sustainable Livelihood and Economic Opportunity Development for Upland and Coastal Communities","the development of more sustainable livelihood and other economic opportunities will be pursued in cooperation with relevant agencies (e.g., DTI, DSWD) to increase their socioeconomic resilience.","DTI | DSWD"],[1,"327","7","Agroforestry and Commercial Forest Plantation Development","Intensify agroforestry development and establishment of commercial forest plantations.",""],[1,"327","7","Community and Family-Based Agroforestry Enterprise Development","Community and family-based agroforestry farms, and related biodiversity- friendly enterprises will be established.",""],[1,"327","7","Forest Registry and Certification System Institutionalization","To ensure sustainability and international competitiveness of the country's forest-based products, registry and forest certification systems will be institutionalized.",""],[1,"328","3","Green Jobs Assessment, Certification, and Monitoring Framework","Fast track adoption and implementation of (a) green jobs assessment and certification criteria/guidelines, (b) green jobs human resource development plan, and (c) tools to monitor and account green jobs.",""]],"236":[[1,"336","12","Health Insurance and Social Security Enhancement for OFWs","Enhance health insurance and social security for OFWs",""],[1,"337","4","Health Insurance and Social Security Enhancement for OFWs","Enhance health insurance and social security for OFWs.",""],[1,"337","5","Health Insurance and Social Security Information Campaigns for OFWs","Information campaigns on the importance and benefits of health insurance and social security for OFWs and their families will be intensified.",""],[1,"337","5","Enhanced E-Payment Services for PhilHealth and SSS","With the urgent need for convenient and contactless transactions, e-payment services for PhilHealth and Social Security System (SSS) will be continuously enhanced and expanded.",""],[1,"337","5","Flexible PhilHealth Premium Payment Scheme for Departing OFWs","Payment schemes for PhilHealth premiums for departing OFWs will be enhanced to enable more flexible payment terms.",""],[1,"338","1","Bilateral Labor Agreement Social Security Provisions for OFWs","In line with RA 11199, the requirement for foreign employers of land-based OFWs to pay SSS contributions, similar to foreign principals of sea-based OFWs, and portability of social security entitlements and earned benefits will be included in the bilateral labor agreements and their implementing administrative arrangements.",""]],"237":[[1,"336","9","Mainstream Migration into Local Development Planning","Mainstream migration into local development planning",""],[1,"336","11","Migrant-Receiving Country Policy Direction Framework","Establish clear policy direction as a migrant-receiving country",""],[1,"336","22","Enhanced Overseas Filipinos Migration Framework","For this update, the framework has been enhanced in line with the new normal and the commitments under the Global Compact for Safe, Orderly, and Regular Migration (GCM).",""],[1,"337","3","Facilitation of OFW Mobility and Recruitment Industry Recovery Support","Concurrently, the government will facilitate the movement of OFWs, especially essential workers needed by the global economy, without compromising the needs of the local economy.",""],[1,"337","3","Recruitment Industry Recovery Support","The government will also explore options to support the recovery of the recruitment industry.",""],[1,"337","6","Bilateral Labor Agreement Negotiation and Protection Enhancement","Negotiation of bilateral labor agreements (BLAs) with migrant- receiving countries will be intensified, especially with those practicing the Kafala system.",""],[1,"340","5","Mainstream Migration into Local Development Planning","The government will facilitate the inclusion of programs/projects for repatriated OFWs in the Rehabilitation and Recovery Plans of local government units (LGUs).",""],[1,"340","5","Local Migration Committees and Councils","Committees, subcommittees, or councils on IMD will be created in key regions to provide a proper venue to discuss migration issues at the local level.",""],[1,"341","2","Immigration Act Amendment and Migration Management Reform","The swift passage of amendments to the Philippine Immigration Act to enhance the control and regulation of the entry of foreign citizens into the Philippines is a crucial step towards improving immigration policy and management.",""],[1,"341","2","Single Work Permit Provider Transition","the government will look into the eventual transition to a single provider of all work permits for foreign nationals.",""],[1,"341","2","Protection and Basic Services for Foreign Nationals","the government will uphold international treaties on the rights of migrants and guarantee that foreign nationals in the Philippines are not denied basic services on the basis of their status as migrants.",""],[1,"341","2","Legal Framework for Asylum Seekers, Refugees, and Stateless Persons","The legal framework for the protection of asylum seekers, refugees, and stateless persons, including children, will be developed, including institutionalization of their access to social services.",""],[1,"341","10","Legal and Institutional Framework Strengthening for Foreign Nationals Management","The amendments aim to strengthen legal and institutional framework; border control at ports of entry; and regulation and registration of foreign nationals within the country.",""]],"238":[[1,"338","2","Mobile Overseas Government Service Offices","Deploying mobile government representative offices overseas will improve the provision of basic services to OFs.",""],[1,"338","2","Onsite Scholarships, Training Assistance, and Competency Assessment Support","To help empower the OFs onsite, scholarships, training assistance, and competency assessments shall be provided.","Technical Education and Skills Development Authority | Professional Regulation Commission"],[1,"338","2","Online Transaction Simplification for Overseas Workers","Moreover, government transactions that cater to OFs will be simplified.","Philippine Overseas Employment Administration"],[1,"338","2","Online Psychosocial Support Platforms for Overseas Workers","Further, the government will provide online platforms for psychosocial intervention and psychological first aid to bring together trained professionals to address the psychological needs of OFs.",""],[1,"338","2","International Migration Statistics Framework Operationalization","expediting the operationalization of the international migration statistics framework is necessary.",""],[1,"338","2","Integrated Inter-Agency Referral and Case Tracking System","An integrated inter-agency referral and case tracking system will also be introduced (see Chapter 5).",""],[1,"338","6","Migrant Worker Online Service Systems","This includes e-Registration of OFWs and Seafarers; Balik Manggagawa (BM) Online; POEA Online Processing System; and further developing Online Direct Hire; Online Continuing Agency Education Program (CAEP); and Online Licensing and Legal Assistance.",""]],"239":[[1,"338","5","Migrant Orientation Seminar Enhancement","The pre-employment, pre-departure, and post-arrival orientation seminars will be improved in terms of conduct and content.",""],[1,"338","5","Expanded Orientation Seminar Curriculum","Enriching the orientation seminar modules to include cultural diversity, benefits and costs of migration, economic and financial literacy, and overseas voting and reintegration would better prepare OFs throughout the migration cycle.",""],[1,"338","5","Pre-Migration Orientation for Migrants and Families","Pre-migration orientation seminars that include not only the prospective migrants but also the families left behind will also be implemented.",""],[1,"338","5","Standardized Orientation Content Across Agencies","Content will be standardized across agencies conducting the orientation seminars.",""],[1,"338","5","Local Government Integration in Pre-Migration Education","Further, local governments will be integrated as service providers in the conduct of pre-migration education training.",""],[1,"339","1","Expansion of BaLinkBayan Online Presence","The online presence of existing programs such as the BaLinkBayan may be expanded to reach a larger audience",""],[1,"339","1","Mobile Pre-departure Orientation Seminars","The conduct of mobile Pre-departure Orientation Seminars (PDOS) in more areas as well as the expansion of the Community Education Program and Peer Counseling Program of the Commission on Filipinos Overseas (CFO) would help prospective emigrants make informed decisions on working or settling abroad","Commission on Filipinos Overseas"],[1,"339","1","Handbook for OFWs Completion and Distribution","The Handbook for OFWs (RA 11227) will be completed and regularly distributed to serve as an important reference for migrants",""],[1,"339","1","Institutionalization of Cultural Initiatives in Embassies","embassies will continue to strengthen regular engagement of Filipinos abroad by institutionalizing cultural initiatives","embassies"],[1,"340","4","Overseas Experts Knowledge-Sharing Mechanisms","Mechanisms through which overseas-based experts are able to share their knowledge and specializations with the academe, industry, and government will be strengthened.",""],[1,"340","4","Diaspora Research and Capacity-Building Linkages","Likewise, institutional linkages will be fostered through Filipino professionals and experts abroad to induce more collaborations in research and development and capacity-building activities.",""],[1,"340","4","OF Remittance Investment Mobilization","The potential of OF remittances will be effectively harnessed and channeled into productive investments, through localization of the BaLinkBayan Portal and replication of the Overseas Filipino Remittances for Development3 (OFReD) project.",""],[1,"341","1","Overseas Voter Registration Center Expansion","More strategic locations of overseas registration centers abroad will be explored.",""],[1,"341","1","Overseas Voter Information Campaigns","Massive information campaigns, especially through social media, to encourage OFs to register and vote will be also pursued.",""]],"240":[[1,"336","20","Monitoring Mechanisms for Overseas Filipinos' Socioeconomic and Political Conditions","Improve mechanisms to monitor the socioeconomic and political conditions of OFs",""],[1,"339","3","Overseas Filipino Monitoring and Status-Checking Mechanisms","Existing mechanisms to monitor the conditions of OFs, such as ATN Mappings and connections with Filipino communities will be complemented by mechanisms to facilitate regular gatherings to enable embassies to check the status of OFs, particularly OFWs, on a regular basis",""],[1,"339","3","Regular Threat and Environmental Scanning","The OPRT will also conduct threat and environmental scanning regularly",""]],"241":[[1,"339","4","Technology-Enabled Pre-Departure Payment Platform Enhancement","Technology-enabled platforms such as online payment systems will be enhanced to address the issue of requiring payments in bulk.",""],[1,"339","4","Recruitment Fee Compliance Monitoring","To ensure that OFWs are not charged more than the regulations allow, recruitment agencies will be strictly monitored.",""],[1,"341","7","Maritime Labor Standards Implementation Framework","This provides the legislative framework on the implementation of the standards set by international conventions and agreements such as the Maritime Labor Convention 2006 on the working and living conditions and occupational safety and health, among others, for seafarers.",""]]}});